hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2297","(2297) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahm narrated — and Abū Aḥmad informed us; Ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us; Azhar ibn Jamīl narrated — both saying: Ḥajjāj ibn Farrūkh al-Tamīmī al-Wāsiṭī narrated to us; al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥawshab narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When Bilāl said \Qad qāmat al-ṣalāh","\"" the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would spring up and say the takbīr.\n\nThis is narrated only by Ḥajjāj ibn Farrūkh. And Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn used to deem him weak."""
"2298","(2298) Abū Saʿd al-Zāhid narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Bundār ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ṣūfī narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Firyābī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us; ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, from Bilāl (may Allah be pleased with him), that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said: \Do not precede me in saying Āmīn.\"""""
"2299","(2299) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Abū Zakariyyā al-Ḥināʾī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us; ʿĀṣim narrated from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: Bilāl (may Allah be pleased with him) said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): \Do not precede me in saying Āmīn.\"" This is how ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated it from ʿĀṣim"," as a mursal narration.\n\nIt was also narrated through a weak chain from ʿĀṣim"," from Abū ʿUthmān"," from Salmān"," who said: Bilāl said — but this is nothing. Rather"," the narration of the reliable group from ʿĀṣim is without the mention of Salmān. And Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated it from ʿĀṣim with different wording."""
"2300","(2300) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us in the Musnad; ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us; ʿĀṣim narrated from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: Bilāl said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not precede me in saying Āmīn.\""\n\nAnd Shuʿbah narrated from ʿĀṣim and said: From Bilāl that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Do not precede me in saying Āmīn.\""\n\nThus the hadith indicates that Bilāl used to say Āmīn before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said Āmīn"," so he said: \""Do not precede me in saying Āmīn.\"" And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best."""
"2301","(2301) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-Ḥusaynī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam raise his hands when he commenced the ṣalāh, aligning them with his shoulders, and when he bowed (rukūʿ), and when he raised his head from the rukūʿ — but he did not do that in the sujūd.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others from Sufyān, and al-Bukhārī extracted it through other chains from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī extracted it (703)]"
"2302","(2302) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us in Makkah: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us: ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us: Ḥammād narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar: that the Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam, when he entered into the ṣalāh, would raise his hands level with his shoulders, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from the rukūʿ.\n\nḤammād is Ibn Salamah, and al-Bukhārī used this as evidence. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik extracted it (196)]"
"2303","(2303) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz al-Baṣrī in Baghdad narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʬāʾ informed me, saying: I heard Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī, in the presence of ten Companions of the Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam, among them Abū Qatādah al-Ḥārith ibn Ribʿī — Abū Ḥumayd said: The Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam, when he stood for the ṣalāh, would raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then he would say the takbīr. And he mentioned the remainder of the hadith, describing the raising of his hands at the rukūʿ, and at raising his head from it, and when he stood up from the two rakʿahs, and he said regarding each of them: \until they were level with his shoulders.\"" And this is also the case in the narration of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭābillāh raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu from the Prophet ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah extracted it (1/235/2438)]"""
"2304","(2304) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī al-Ṭustarī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān al-Bazzāz narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Hāshimī narrated to us: Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from Mūsā — and he is Ibn ʿUqbah — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Faḍl al-Qurashī, from al-Aʿraj, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī raḍiyallāhu taʿālā ʿanhu, who said: The Prophet ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam, when he commenced the ṣalāh, would raise his hands level with his shoulders, and when he intended to bow, and when he raised his head from the rukūʿ — and he did not do that in any of his prostrations, and when he stood up from the two prostrations, he did likewise. And this is also the case in one of the two narrations from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tirmidhī extracted it (3423)]"
"2305","(2305) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb, who said: I heard my father saying — Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr narrated to me, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam — when he commenced the ṣalāh, he would raise his hands level with his shoulders, and when he bowed, and after he raised his head from the rukūʿ.\n\nWāʾil said: Then I came to them in the winter, and I saw them raising their hands beneath their cloaks (al-barānis).\n\nAnd al-Ḥumaydī and others narrated it similarly from Ibn ʿUyaynah, and it was also narrated from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād from ʿĀṣim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shāfiʿī extracted it in his chain (1/176)]"
"2306","(2306) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Nakhaʿī, from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil, from his father: that he saw the Prophet ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam when he stood for the ṣalāh — he raised his hands until they were opposite his shoulders, and he aligned his thumbs with his ears, then he said the takbīr.\n\nAnd al-Thawrī, Shuʿbah, Abū ʿAwānah, Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah, Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal, and a group narrated it from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb, and they said in the hadith: \He raised his hands until they were opposite his ears","\"" and some of them said: \""level with his ears.\"" And Sharīk narrated from ʿĀṣim"," saying: \""He raised his hands opposite his ears.\""\n\nAnd this is also the case in the established narration from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil from Wāʾil"," and in another established narration from Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith from the Prophet ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam: \""until they were opposite his ears","\"" and in yet another established narration: \""until they were opposite the upper parts of his ears.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd extracted it (724)]"""
"2307","(2307) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated from Saʿīd — (ḥ) and Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us: Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from Naṣr ibn ʿĀṣim al-Laythī, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith, who said: The Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam, when he said the takbīr, would raise his hands until they were opposite the upper parts of his ears, and when he bowed, he did likewise, and when he raised his head from the rukūʿ, he did likewise.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā.\n\nAnd Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, and he said at its beginning: \He raised his hands and placed them close to his ears.\"" And Hishām al-Dastawāʾī said similarly from Qatādah in one of his two narrations from him"," and in the other narration he said: \""to the upper parts of his ears.\"" And Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah"," saying: \""until they were opposite the upper parts of his ears","\"" and in another narration: \""level with his shoulders.\""\n\nWhen these narrations differ"," then either all may be taken and a choice made between them"," or the narration of the one about whom there is disagreement may be abandoned"," and the narration of the one about whom there is no disagreement may be adopted.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī raḥimahullāh said: Because its chains of narration are more established"," and because it is a hadith of a number"," and a number is more deserving of being preserved than a single narrator.\n\nThe Shaykh raḥimahullāh said: Along with their narrations is the practice of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim extracted it (589)]"""
"2308","(2308) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from al-Zubayr ibn ʿAdī, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad: that ʿUmar raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu used to raise his hands to the level of his shoulders.\n\nThe Shaykh raḥimahullāh said: And ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Abū Hurayrah used to do likewise. [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq extracted it (2/71)]"
"2309","(2309) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī informed us dictating: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Dalwīyah al-Daqqāq narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us: Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, who said: The Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam, when he commenced the ṣalāh, would raise his hands until they were level with his ears.\n\nYazīd ibn Abī Ziyād is not strong (ghayr qawī). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"2310","(2310) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah al-Qurashī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī said: Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam — when he commenced the takbīr in the ṣalāh, he would raise his hands as he said the takbīr, until he placed them level with his shoulders. Then when he said the takbīr for the rukūʿ, he did likewise. Then when he said \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","\"" he did likewise and said: \""Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd.\"" And he did not do that when he prostrated"," nor when he raised his head from the prostration.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān.\n\nAnd in the narration of Mālik and Ibn ʿUyaynah from al-Zuhrī: \""When he commenced the ṣalāh"," he raised his hands.\"" And it is in the meaning of the narration of Shuʿayb"," except that the narration of Shuʿayb is more explicit. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī extracted it (738)]"""
"2311","(2311) ʿAlī ibn Bashrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Khalīl al-Barjalānī informed us, Abū al-Naḍr informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Masʿūdī said: I heard ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil say: My household narrated to me from my father Wāʾil that when he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he saw him raising his hands along with the takbīr, placing his right hand upon his left hand during the Ṣalāh, and prostrating between his two palms. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿĀmir al-Yaḥṣubī also narrated it from Wāʾil. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/316]"
"2312","(2312) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed me, Muḥammad ibn Ribḥ al-Sammāk informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Shuʿbah informed us, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Abū al-Bakhtarī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Yaḥṣubī, from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he said the takbīr, he raised his hands along with the takbīr, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head—or he said, when he prostrated—and I saw him giving salām on his right and on his left. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Aḥmad 18369]"
"2313","(2313) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original source, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ibn Shihāb informed me, from Sālim, that Ibn ʿUmar used to say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stood for the Ṣalāh, raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then he said the takbīr. And he narrated the ḥadīth at length. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been referenced previously in 1310]"
"2314","(2314) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ibn Shihāb informed me, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stood for the Ṣalāh, raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders, then he said the takbīr. And when he intended to bow, he did likewise, and when he raised his head from bowing, he did likewise, and he did not do it when he raised his head from prostration.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī also narrated it from Ibn Shihāb, and likewise ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ from Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī. And in the narration of Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ from Abū Ḥumayd in this ḥadīth: I saw him, when he said the takbīr, he placed his hands opposite his shoulders. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been referenced previously in the one before it]"
"2315","(2315) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, from Khālid, i.e., al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, that he saw Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith: when he prayed, he said the takbīr, then raised his hands, and when he intended to bow, he raised his hands, and when he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands. And he narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do this.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Shāhīn al-Wāsiṭī from Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh, and he said: When he prayed, he said the takbīr and raised his hands. The narrations that indicate raising the hands along with the takbīr are more established and more numerous; therefore, they are more deserving of being followed. And with Allah is the success. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 737]"
"2316","(2316) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us, from Saʿīd ibn Simʿān, who said: Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us in the Mosque of the Zurqiyyīn and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he entered the Ṣalāh, raised his hands fully, then remained silent for a brief moment, asking Allah for His bounty, and he would say the takbīr when he lowered and when he bowed. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī 2495]"
"2317","(2317) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq al-Baṣrī in Egypt informed us, Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us, from Saʿīd ibn Samʿān, who said: Abū Hurayrah came to us in the Mosque of Banī Zurayq and said: There are three practices that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform which the people have abandoned. When he stood for the Ṣalāh, he would do like this—and Abū ʿĀmir gestured with his hand without spreading his fingers apart and without closing them together. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been referenced previously in the one before it]"
"2318","(2318) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, Abū ʿAlī al-Raffāʾ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Yamān informed us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʾb, from Saʿīd ibn Samʿān, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he opened the Ṣalāh, he spread his fingers open. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been referenced previously in the one before it]"
"2319","(2319) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raising his hands fully, meaning during the Ṣalāh. It has also been said in this narration that this was before the takbīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 2/375/8862]"
"2320","(2320) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Sawwār informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr informed us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr informed us, Ibn Isḥāq informed us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand in an obligatory or voluntary prayer except that he raised his hands toward the sky, supplicating, and then said the takbīr thereafter.\n\nJarīr corroborated it from Ibn Isḥāq. And it has been narrated in a ḥadīth that he said: When one of you opens the Ṣalāh, let him raise his hands and turn their inner side toward the Qiblah—however, it is weak, so I set it aside. [Munkar. Narrated by Abū Nuʿaym in al-Ḥilyah 9/238]"
"2321","(2321) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnazī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmī narrated to us; he said: My father informed me that Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr informed him, he said: I said to myself, \I shall certainly watch the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) to see how he performs the prayer.\"" He said: So I looked at him; he stood and pronounced the takbīr"," and raised his hands. And he mentioned the hadith and said at the end of it: Then I came after that during a time of cold"," and I saw the people wearing heavy garments"," their hands moving from beneath the garments. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/318]"""
"2322","(2322) Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from ʿĀṣim and said in the hadith: \Then I came to them in the winter"," and I saw them raising their hands beneath the cloaks (al-barānis).\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ reported it to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān informed us"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī with his chain 852]"""
"2323","(2323) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil, a freedman of theirs, that both of them narrated to him from his father Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr: That he saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) when he entered into the prayer, he pronounced the takbīr — Abū ʿUthmān said: Hammām described [the raising] to the level of his ears — then he wrapped himself in his garment, then he placed his right hand upon his left hand. When he intended to bow, he brought his hands out from the garment and raised them, then pronounced the takbīr. When he said, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","\"" he raised his hands. When he prostrated"," he prostrated between his two palms. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from ʿAffān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 401]"""
"2324","(2324) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Mūsā ibn ʿUmayr al-ʿAnbarī narrated to us; ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil narrated to me from his father: That the Prophet (peace be upon him), when he stood in prayer, would grasp his left hand with his right hand. And I saw ʿAlqamah doing it. Yaʿqūb said: Mūsā ibn ʿUmayr is a Kūfan, trustworthy (thiqah). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 723]"
"2325","(2325) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnazī informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb al-Jarmī narrated to us; he said: My father informed me that Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr informed him, he said: I said to myself, \I shall certainly watch the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) to see how he performs the prayer.\"" He said: So I looked at him; he stood and pronounced the takbīr"," and raised his hands until they were level with his ears. Then he placed his right hand upon the back of his left hand"," and the wrist from the forearm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned in 321]"""
"2326","(2326) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq and Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan both said: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik from Abū Ḥāzim from Sahl ibn Saʿd that he said: The people were commanded that a man should place his right hand upon his left arm in the prayer. Abū Ḥāzim said: And I do not know except that he attributed that [statement] to the Prophet (peace be upon him), or a word similar to it. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī, and he said: Abū Ḥāzim said: \And I do not know except that he attributed it to the Prophet (peace be upon him).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik 1/376]"""
"2327","(2327) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Bikkār ibn al-Rayyān narrated to us from Hushaym ibn Bashīr from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Abī Zaynab from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī from Ibn Masʿd (may Allah be pleased with him): That he was praying and had placed his left hand upon his right hand. The Prophet (peace be upon him) saw him, so he placed his right hand upon his left hand. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 755]"
"2328","(2328) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Qabīṣah ibn Hulb from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) placing his right hand upon his left hand in the prayer. Hulb's name is Yazīd ibn Qunāfah. And it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥārith ibn Ghuḍayf al-Kindī and Shaddād ibn Sharḥabīl al-Anṣārī that each one of them saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) do that. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 5/226/22313]"
"2329","(2329) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Aḥmad al-Khuzāʿī in Makkah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd ibn Sālim al-Qaddāḥ narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rawwād narrated to us from his father from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Indeed"," we"," the company of prophets"," have been commanded with three things: hastening the breaking of the fast"," delaying the pre-dawn meal (suḥūr)"," and placing the right hand upon the left hand in the prayer.\"" ʿAbd al-Majīd is alone in narrating it. It is only known through Ṭalḥah ibn ʿAmr — who is not strong — from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and once from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace be upon him). However"," the authentic narration is from Muḥammad ibn Abān al-Anṣārī from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," who said: \""Three things are from prophethood","\"" and she mentioned them from her own statement. [Shādh. Narrated by al-ʿUqaylī in al-Ḍuʿafāʾ 1/383/343]"""
"2330","(2330) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed it to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Shujāʿ ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; he said: Manṣūr — we were narrated to from Muḥammad ibn Abān al-Anṣārī from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \Three things are from prophethood: hastening the breaking of the fast"," delaying the pre-dawn meal (suḥūr)"," and placing the right hand upon the left hand in the prayer.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2331","(2331) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl informed us; Hishām ibn ʿAlī and Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb both said: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Jaḥdarī from ʿUqbah ibn Ṣuhbān from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the verse: \So pray to your Lord and sacrifice\"" [Al-Kawthar: 2]. He said: It means placing your right hand upon your left hand in prayer. Thus said our shaykh: ʿĀṣim al-Jaḥdarī from ʿUqbah ibn Ṣuhbān. [Weak. Al-Ḥākim narrated it"," 2/586/3980]"""
"2332","(2332) Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Tārīkh in the biography of ʿUqbah ibn Ẓabyān, from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, who heard ʿĀṣim al-Jaḥdarī from his father from ʿUqbah ibn Ẓabyān from ʿAlī regarding the verse: \So pray to your Lord and sacrifice\"" [Al-Kawthar: 2]: He placed his right hand upon the middle of his left forearm upon his chest.\n\nAbū Bakr al-Fārisī informed us; Abū Isḥāq al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Mūsā informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\nHe said: And al-Bukhārī said: Qutaybah narrated to us from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Yazīd ibn Ziyād ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from ʿĀṣim al-Jaḥdarī from ʿUqbah"," one of the companions of ʿAlī"," from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): He placed them both upon the elbow. [Weak. It was preceded in the one before it]"""
"2333","(2333) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣīr al-Khuldī informed us, dictating; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muslim informed us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Abī Ḥāzim narrated to us; Ghazwān ibn Jarīr narrated from his father: that he was a close companion of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him). He said: When ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) stood for prayer and pronounced the takbīr, he would strike his right hand upon his left wrist, and he would remain in that state until he went into rukūʿ, unless he needed to scratch his skin or adjust his garment. When he gave the salām, he gave it from his right side: \Alaykum al-salām","\"" then he would turn from his left side and move his lips"," and we did not know what he was saying. Then he would say: \""Lā ilāha illā Allāhu waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā bi-Allāh"," lā naʿbudu illā iyyāh.\"" Then he would turn his face toward the people"," and he did not mind whether he turned from his right side or from his left side.\n\nThis is a ḥasan isnād. [Weak. Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Bishrān narrated it]"""
"2334","(2334) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Naṣr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Ṣāliḥ from Zurʿah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: Aligning the feet and placing the hand upon the hand are from the Sunnah. [Weak. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, 754]"
"2335","(2335) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibn Ṣāʿid informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥujr al-Ḥaḍramī informed us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil narrated to me from his father from his mother from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, who said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He went to the mosque and entered the miḥrāb, then raised his hands with the takbīr, then placed his right hand upon his left hand upon his chest. [Weak]"
"2336","(2336) Muʾammal ibn Ismāʿīl also narrated it from al-Thawrī from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wāʾil: that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) place his right hand upon his left hand, then place both of them upon his chest.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā informed us; Muʾammal narrated it. [Weak]"
"2337","(2337) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh, informed us; Abū al-Ḥarīsh al-Kilābī informed us; Shaybān narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us; ʿĀṣim al-Jaḥdarī narrated to us from his father from ʿUqbah ibn Ṣuhbān — thus he said — that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding this verse: \So pray to your Lord and sacrifice\"" [Al-Kawthar: 2]: It means placing his right hand upon the middle of his left hand"," then placing both of them upon his chest. [Weak. It was preceded in 2331"," 2332]"""
"2338","(2338) He said: And Abū al-Ḥarīsh narrated to us; Shaybān narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated to us; ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated from a man from Anas, similarly, or he said: from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). [Weak]"
"2339","(2339) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb ibn al-Bukhārī informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me; ʿAmr ibn Mālik al-Nukrī narrated to me from Abū al-Jawzāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the word of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: \So pray to your Lord and sacrifice\"" [Al-Kawthar: 2]. He said: It means placing the right hand upon the left hand in prayer at the level of the chest. [Weak]"""
"2340","(2340) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; Zayd informed us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Abī al-Zubayr, who said: ʿAṭāʾ commanded me to ask Saʿīd: Where should the hands be placed in prayer — above the navel or below the navel? So I asked him, and he said: Above the navel. He meant by that Saʿīd ibn Jubayr.\n\nAnd Abū Mijlaz Lāḥiq ibn Ḥumayd said the same. The most authentic narration reported in this topic is the narration of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and Abū Mijlaz. [Weak]"
"2341","(2341) It is narrated from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): \Beneath the navel.\"" And in its chain of narration there is weakness.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā informed us; Abū Kurayb informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq; Ziyād ibn Zayd al-Suwāʾī narrated to me; from Abū Juḥayfah; from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""Indeed"," among the Sunnah in prayer is placing the palm upon the palm beneath the navel.\""\n\nAnd Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated it similarly from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. And Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān as well. [Weak]"""
"2342","(2342) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim informed us; Abū Kurayb informed us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq; from al-Nuʿmān ibn Saʿd; from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that he used to say: \Indeed"," among the Sunnah of prayer is placing the right hand upon the left beneath the navel.\""\n\nThis ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq is al-Wāsiṭī al-Qurashī. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," al-Bukhārī"," and others criticized him.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān also narrated it from Sayyār"," from Abū Wāʾil"," from Abū Hurayrah"," similarly.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq is abandoned (matrūk). [Weak. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2343","(2343) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah informed me; my uncle al-Mājishūn ibn Abī Salamah narrated to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us; Yūsuf al-Mājishūn informed me; my father narrated to me; from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj; from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ; from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him); from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that when he stood for prayer, he said:\n\n\I have turned my face toward Him who created the heavens and the earth"," as a ḥanīf"," and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed"," my prayer"," my sacrifice"," my living"," and my dying are for Allah"," Lord of the worlds. He has no partner"," and by that I have been commanded"," and I am of the Muslims. O Allah"," You is the King; there is no god but You. You is my Lord"," and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself"," and I acknowledge my sin"," so forgive me all my sins. Indeed"," none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character"," for none guides to the best of it but You. Turn away from me its evil"," for none turns away its evil but You. Here I am"," at Your service. All good is in Your hands"," and evil is not attributed to You. I am with You and to You. Blessed are You and Exalted. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.\""\n\nWhen he bowed (rukūʿ)"," he said: \""O Allah"," to You I have bowed"," and in You I have believed"," and to You I have submitted. My hearing"," my sight"," my brain"," my bones"," and my nerves are humble to You.\""\n\nWhen he raised his head"," he said: \""O Allah"," to You is praise filling the heavens and the earth and what is between them"," and filling whatever You will beyond that.\""\n\nWhen he prostrated"," he said: \""O Allah"," to You I have prostrated"," and in You I have believed"," and to You I have submitted. My face has prostrated to Him who created it and fashioned it"," and opened its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah"," the Best of creators.\""\n\nThen among the last things he would say between the tashahhud and the salām was: \""O Allah"," forgive me for what I have advanced and what I have delayed"," what I have concealed and what I have made public"," and what You know of me better than I. You are the One who brings forward and the One who puts back. There is no god but You.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Abī Salamah. And in the narration of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he commenced the prayer"," he said the takbīr"," then he said","\"" and he said: \""And I am the first of the Muslims.\"" And he said: when he raised his head: \""Allah hears those who praise Him. Our Lord"," to You is praise filling the heavens"," filling the earth"," filling what is between them"," and filling whatever You will beyond that.\"" And he said: \""And He fashioned it and perfected its form"," and opened its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah"," the Best of creators.\"" When he said the salām"," he said… and he mentioned the supplication"," but he did not mention his words: \""And what I have transgressed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr"," and he narrated it from two other routes from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Salamah"," and he mentioned his words: \""And what I have transgressed.\"" [Authentic. Narrated by Aḥmad 1/93"," 717]"""
"2344","(2344) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Anmāṭī informed us — and I asked him — Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī informed us; Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad narrated from Ibn Jurayj; Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed me; from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Faḍl; from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj; from Ibn Abī Rāfiʿ; from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he commenced the obligatory prayer, he said:\n\n\I have turned my face toward Him who created the heavens and the earth"," as a ḥanīf"," a Muslim"," and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed"," my prayer"," my sacrifice"," my living"," and my dying are for Allah"," Lord of the worlds. He has no partner"," and by that I have been commanded"," and I am of the Muslims. O Allah"," You is the King; there is no god but You. Glorified are You and praised. You is my Lord"," and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and acknowledged my sin"," so forgive me all my sins. Indeed"," none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to the best of it but You. Turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil but You. Here I am"," at Your service. All good is in Your hands"," and the guided one is whom You have guided. I am with You and to You. Blessed are You and Exalted. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You.\""\n\nHe said: And when he bowed"," he said: \""O Allah"," to You I have bowed"," and in You I have believed"," and to You I have submitted. You is my Lord. My hearing"," my sight"," my brain"," my bones"," and what my foot stands upon are humble to You"," Allah"," Lord of the worlds.\""\n\nAnd when he raised his head from the bowing in the obligatory prayer"," he said: \""O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise filling the heavens"," filling the earth"," and filling whatever You will beyond that.\"" [Authentic. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2345","(2345) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me; Ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated to me; from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah; from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Faḍl al-Hāshimī; from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj; from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ; from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him); from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that when he stood for the obligatory prayer, he said the takbīr and raised his hands level with his shoulders. Then he mentioned the ḥadīth. He said: And he would say when commencing the prayer after the takbīr: \I have turned my face…\"" Then he mentioned it and said: \""And I am of the Muslims. O Allah"," You is the King; there is no god but You. Glorified are You. You is my Lord"," and I am Your servant.\"" Then he mentioned it and did not mention his words: \""Guide me…\"" up to his words: \""Here I am.\"" Then he said: \""Here I am"," at Your service. I am with You and to You. There is no refuge from You except to You. I seek Your forgiveness and then repent to You.\"" Then he mentioned the remainder with the meaning of the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," and the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz is more complete. [Authentic. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2346","(2346) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl al-Shaʿrānī informed us; my grandfather informed me; ʿAmr ibn ʿAwn informed us; Hushaym narrated from Shuʿbah; from Abī Isḥāq; from al-Ḥārith; from ʿAlī, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when he commenced the prayer, he said: \There is no god but You; glorified are You. I have wronged myself and done evil"," so forgive me. Indeed"," none forgives sins but You. I have turned my face toward Him who created the heavens and the earth"," as a ḥanīf"," and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed"," my prayer"," my sacrifice"," my living"," and my dying are for Allah"," Lord of the worlds. He has no partner"," and by that I have been commanded"," and I am of the Muslims.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī narrated it from Hushaym"," not directly"," from some of his companions"," from Abī Isḥāq"," from Abī al-Khalīl"," from ʿAlī. If it is preserved"," then it is possible that Abū Isḥāq heard it from both of them"," and Allah knows best.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah: \""And I am the first of the Muslims.\"" And likewise in some narrations from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah"," and in some of them: \""And I am of the Muslims.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He makes the place of \""And I am the first of the Muslims\"" to be \""And I am of the Muslims.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir and a group of the jurists of Madīnah commanded that.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; he said: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb say: I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And evil is not attributed to You\"" — its interpretation is: \""Evil is not done to draw near to You.\"" [Authentic]"""
"2347","(2347) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us; Ṭalq ibn Ghannām informed us; ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb al-Mulāʾī narrated from Budayl ibn Mayṣarah; from Abū al-Jawzāʾ; from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he commenced the prayer, he said: \Glorified are You"," O Allah"," and praised. Blessed is Your name"," and exalted is Your majesty. There is no god but You.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; he said: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: This ḥadīth is not well-known from ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb; no one narrated it except Ṭalq ibn Ghannām. And a group narrated the story of the prayer from Budayl"," and they did not mention anything of this.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And it was narrated from another weak route from ʿĀʾishah. [Denounced (munkar). Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 776]"""
"2348","(2348) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ghaḍāʾirī informed us; they said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Ḥārithah ibn Muḥammad; from ʿAmrah; from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he commenced the prayer, raised his hands level with his shoulders, then said: \Glorified are You"," O Allah"," and praised. Blessed is Your name"," and exalted is Your majesty. There is no god but You.\"" And we did not record this except from the ḥadīth of Ḥārithah ibn Abī al-Rijāl. And he is weak. And it was narrated in the ḥadīth of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah 470]"""
"2349","(2349) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us from the original of his book; Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Raffāʾ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān informed us; Zakariyyā — that is Ibn ʿAdī — narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān; from ʿAlī ibn ʿAlī; from Abī al-Mutawakkil; from Abū Saʿīd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he stood at night and commenced the prayer, he said: \Glorified are You"," O Allah"," and praised. Blessed is Your name"," and exalted is Your majesty. There is no god but You.\"" He said: Then he said the tahlīl three times: \""There is no god but Allah. There is no god but Allah. There is no god but Allah.\"" Then he said the takbīr three times: \""Allah is the Greatest. Allah is the Greatest. Allah is the Greatest. I seek refuge in Allah"," the All-Hearing"," the All-Knowing"," from the accursed Satan — from his madness"," his poetry"," and his pride.\"" Jaʿfar said: His madness is epilepsy"," his poetry is verse"," and his pride is arrogance.\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; he said: Abū Dāwūd said: This ḥadīth — they say it is from ʿAlī ibn ʿAlī from al-Ḥasan. The error is from Jaʿfar.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And in the opening with \""Glorified are You"," O Allah"," and praised","\"" another ḥadīth was narrated from Layth"," from ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," from his father"," raised (marfūʿ)"," and it is not strong.\n\nAnd that was narrated as marfūʿ from Ḥumayd"," from Anas"," and it was narrated from another route from ʿĀʾishah. And the most authentic of what was narrated in it is the narration of the stopped (mawqūf) tradition attributed to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). [Denounced (munkar). Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah 467]"""
"2350","(2350) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us; Yazīd — meaning Ibn Hārūn — informed us; Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam; from Ibrāhīm; from al-Aswad, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) when he commenced the prayer, he said the takbīr, then said: \Glorified are You"," O Allah"," and praised. Blessed is Your name"," and exalted is Your majesty. There is no god but You.\"" [Authentic. And the discussion on it has been mentioned recently.]"""
"2351","(2351) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ibn Nājiʿah informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Yaʿqūb al-Jūzajānī informed us: ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥimṣī informed us: Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed us: his father informed him: Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir informed him that Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) informed him that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commenced the prayer, he said: \Subḥānaka Allāhumma wa bi-ḥamdika"," tabāraka ismuka"," wa taʿālā jadduka"," wa lā ilāha ghayruka. Wajjahtu wajhiya lilladhī faṭar al-samāwāt wa al-arḍa ḥanīfan wa mā ana min al-mushrikīn. Inna ṣalātī wa nusukī wa maḥyāya wa mamātī lillāhi Rabb al-ʿālamīn"," lā sharīka lahu.\"" [Weak. Al-Dhahabī said in Naṣb al-Rābiṭah 2/204]"""
"2352","(2352) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū Sahl al-Isfarāyinī informed us: Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Yaʿqūb al-Jūzajānī, Abū Isḥāq, narrated it with a similar chain, except that he said: \Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us","\"" and he said: \""Tabāraka ismuka.\"" The remainder is the same. It was also narrated by ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir al-Aslamī—and he is weak—from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from Ibn ʿUmar. [Weak]"""
"2353","(2353) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: ʿAmr ibn Murrah informed me: he heard ʿĀṣim al-ʿAnazī narrating from Ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim from his father that when the Prophet (ﷺ) entered into prayer, he said the takbīr and then said: \Allāhu Akbar kabīrā\""—he said it three times; \""Wa al-ḥamdu lillāhi kathīrā\""—he said it three times; \""Wa subḥān Allāhi bukratan wa aṣīlā\""—he said it three times; \""Aʿūdhu billāhi min al-shayṭān al-rajīm"," min nafkhihi wa nafthihi wa hamzihi.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/82"," 16882]"""
"2354","(2354) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: Shuʿbah narrated it with the same meaning, except that he said: \Allāhumma innī aʿūdhu bika min al-shayṭān al-rajīm.\"" ʿAmr added: \""Nafkhuhu is al-kibr (arrogance)"," hamzuhu is al-mawtata (the fainting seizure that takes the son of Ādam)"," and nafthuhu is al-shiʿr (poetry).\"" Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated it from Misʿar and Shuʿbah from ʿAmr from a man from ʿAnazah whose name was ʿĀṣim"," from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim from his father from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," with the meaning of the ḥadīth of Abū Dāwūd"," and he added the explanation"," except that he did not attribute it to ʿAmr; rather he said: \""It was asked: 'What is hamzuhu?' He said: 'The seizure that takes the son of Ādam.' It was asked: 'What is nafkhuhu?' He said: 'Al-kibr (arrogance).' It was asked: 'What is nafthuhu?' He said: 'Al-shiʿr (poetry).'\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed me: al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Misʿar and Shuʿbah narrated it. [Weak. Previously mentioned in the one before it]"""
"2355","(2355) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Muṭahhar informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAlī al-Rifāʿī informed us: Abū al-Mutawakkil al-Nājī informed us: Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood at night, he would say the takbīr and then mention his opening supplication with \Subḥānaka Allāhumma","\"" and after it the tahlīl and takbīr three times"," then: \""Aʿūdhu billāh al-Samīʿ al-ʿAlīm min al-shayṭān al-rajīm"," min hamzihi wa nafkhihi wa nafthihi.\"" Then he would recite. It was also narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," both marfūʿ and mawqūf. [Denounced. Previously mentioned 2349]"""
"2356","(2356) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūh al-Shaybānī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Abī Ḥabībah informed us: Warqāʾ informed us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib informed us. (H) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl informed us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered into prayer, he would say—and in the ḥadīth of Warqāʾ it is: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to teach us to say: 'Allāhumma innī aʿūdhu bika min al-shayṭān al-rajīm"," wa hamzihi wa nafkhihi wa nafthihi.'\"" ʿAṭāʾ said: \""Hamzuhu is al-mawtata (the fainting seizure)"," nafthuhu is al-shiʿr (poetry)"," and nafkhuhu is al-kibr (arrogance).\"" Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ and stopped it (as mawqūf). [Weak. Narrated by Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl in al-Duʿāʾ 119]"""
"2357","(2357) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated it to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah informed us: ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib informed us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us: Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He used to seek refuge in Allah during prayer from al-shayṭān al-rajīm, from nafkhihi and nafthihi and hamzihi. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī 1/49/371]"
"2358","(2358) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāyinī informed us: Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad al-Kātib informed us: Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād al-Khuzāʿī informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth informed us: al-Aʿmash informed us: Ibrāhīm informed us: al-Aswad ibn Yazīd informed us that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), when he entered into prayer, would say: \Allāhu Akbar","\"" then he would say: \""Subḥānaka Allāhumma wa bi-ḥamdika"," tabāraka ismuka wa taʿālā jadduka"," wa lā ilāha ghayruka.\"" Then he would seek refuge in Allah from al-shayṭān al-rajīm"," then he would recite whatever was easy for him from the Qurʾān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned 2350]"""
"2359","(2359) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad informed us: from Rābiʿah ibn ʿUthmān from Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ that he heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) leading the people in prayer, raising his voice: \Rabbanā innā nʿūdhu bika min al-shayṭān al-rajīm\"" in the obligatory prayer when he finished Umm al-Qurʾān. Abū Saʿīd added in his narration: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to seek refuge silently"," and whichever one does is sufficient. Some of them would seek refuge when opening the prayer before Umm al-Qurʾān"," and that is my position.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The aḥādīth in the chapter before it indicate that one seeks refuge before the recitation.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And one should say it in the first rakʿah.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Al-Ḥasan"," ʿAṭāʾ"," and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī held this same view.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""And it has been said that if one says it at the opening of every rakʿah before Umm al-Qurʾān"," it is good.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It is narrated from Ibn Sīrīn that he used to seek refuge in every rakʿah.\"""""
"2360","(2360) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Muḥammad ibn Khallād al-Bāhilī informed us: Yaḥyā, that is Ibn Saʿīd, informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh informed us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd informed me: from his father, from Abū Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the mosque, and a man entered and prayed, then came and greeted the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned his greeting and said: \Go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" The man went back and prayed as he had prayed"," then came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \""And upon you be peace. Go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" He did this three times. The man said: \""By the One Who sent you with the truth"," I cannot do better than this"," so teach me.\"" He said: \""When you stand for prayer"," say the takbīr"," then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qurʾān"," then bow until you are at ease in rukūʿ"," then raise up until you stand upright"," then prostrate until you are at ease in sujūd"," then raise up until you are at ease sitting"," then do that throughout all your prayer.\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 793]"""
"2361","(2361) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us — Qabīṣah narrated to us — Sufyān narrated from Jaʿfar, Abū ʿAlī, the seller of al-Anmāṭ, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to announce: \There is no ṣalāh except with the Qurʾān — with the Opening of the Book (Fātiḥat al-Kitāb) and whatever more (one adds).\"""""
"2362","(2362) Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah informed us — Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us — Yaʿlā and ʿUbaydullāh narrated from al-Aʿmash, from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr, from Abū Maʿmar, who said: We asked Khabbāb: \Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in the first (rakʿah) and the ʿAṣr prayer?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" We asked: \""By what means did you know that?\"" He said: \""By the movement of his blessed beard.\"""""
"2363","(2363) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣbahānī informed us orally — Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no ṣalāh for the one who does not recite the Opening of the Book (Fātiḥat al-Kitāb).\"""""
"2364","(2364) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us — Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated — al-Zuhrī said: \I heard Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ narrating from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no ṣalāh for the one who does not recite therein the Opening of the Book (Fātiḥat al-Kitāb).'\"" And likewise al-Shāfiʿī and al-Ḥumaydī narrated from Sufyān: \""There is no ṣalāh for the one who does not recite therein the Opening of the Book (Fātiḥat al-Kitāb).\"""""
"2365","(2365) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us — they said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān (ḥ) — and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us — Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to me — al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿqūb narrated from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Every ṣalāh in which the Mother of the Book (Umm al-Qurʾān) is not recited is deficient (khidāj)"," then deficient"," then deficient.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""O Abū Hurayrah"," sometimes I am behind the imam.\"" He said: \""O Persian"," recite it within yourself"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," said: I have divided the ṣalāh between Me and My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks. When the servant says {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi al-ʿālamīn}"," Allah says: My servant has praised Me. And when he says {al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}"," Allah says: My servant has extolled Me. And when he says {māliki yawmi al-dīn}"," Allah says: My servant has glorified Me — or he said: My servant has entrusted himself to Me. And when he says {iyyāka nabudu wa iyyāka nastaʿīn}"," Allah says: This is between Me and My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks. And when him says {ihdina al-ṣirāṭa al-mustaqīma ṣirāṭa alladhīna anʿamta ʿalayhim ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā al-ḍāllīn}"," then this is for My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks.'\"" Sufyān said: \""I entered upon al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān in his house while he was ill"," and I asked him"," and he narrated this ḥadīth to me.\"""""
"2366","(2366) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik. And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated from Mālik ibn Anas, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that he heard Abū al-Sāʾib, the freed slave of Hishām ibn Zuhrah, saying: I heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever prays a ṣalāh in which he does not recite the Mother of the Qurʾān (Umm al-Qurʾān)"," it is deficient (khidāj)"," it is deficient"," it is deficient — incomplete (ghayru tāmm).\"" He (the narrator) said: \""O Abū Hurayrah"," sometimes I am behind the imam.\"" He said: \""He squeezed my arm and said: 'Recite it within yourself"," O Persian"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," said: I have divided the ṣalāh between Me and My servant into two halves: one half is for Me and one half is for My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""When the servant recites"," he says {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi al-ʿālamīn}"," Allah says: My servant has praised Me. And the servant says {al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}"," Allah says: My servant has extolled Me. The servant says {māliki yawmi al-dīn}"," Allah says: My servant has glorified Me. The servant says {iyyāka nabudu wa iyyāka nastaʿīn}"," then this verse is between Me and My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks. The servant says {ihdina al-ṣirāṭa al-mustaqīma ṣirāṭa alladhīna anʿamta ʿalayhim ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā al-ḍāllīn}"," then these are for My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Qutaybah. And in the ḥadīth of al-Qaʿnabī: \""The servant says {māliki yawmi al-dīn}"," Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," says: My servant has glorified Me"," and this verse is between Me and My servant.\"" And the remainder is similar."""
"2367","(2367) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammil ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us — and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Fāmī, the righteous shaykh, from his original book, narrated to us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammil said — they both said: al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me — my father narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: I heard from my father and from Abū al-Sāʾib together, and they were both sitting with Abū Hurayrah, who said — and Abū Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever prays a ṣalāh in which he does not recite the Opening of the Book (Fātiḥat al-Kitāb)"," it is deficient (khidāj)"," it is deficient — incomplete (ghayru tāmm).\"" The ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh ends here. And Abū Naṣr al-Fāmī mentioned the remainder of the ḥadīth in a manner similar to the narration of al-Qaʿnabī from Mālik. (b) And ʿAbdullāh ibn Ziyād ibn Samʿān narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father from Abū Hurayrah"," and he added the tasmiyah (Basmalah) therein."""
"2368","(2368) Abū Ḥāzim ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me — Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdūn al-Dhuhlī, who wrote it for me in his own hand — Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Naṣr al-Muqriʾ narrated to us — Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated from Ibn Samʿān, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Allah"," Blessed and Exalted"," says: I have divided this sūrah between Me and My servant into two halves. When the servant says {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}"," Allah says: My servant has remembered Me. When he says {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi al-ʿālamīn}"," Allah says: My servant has praised Me. When he says {al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}"," Allah says: My servant has extolled Me. When he says {māliki yawmi al-dīn}"," Allah says: My servant has glorified Me. And when he says {iyyāka nabudu wa iyyāka nastaʿīn}"," Allah says: This is for My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks.\"""""
"2369","(2369) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Bakr al-Azraq Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq ibn Bahlūl narrated to us — my grandfather narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Ibn Samʿān narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \Whoever prays a ṣalāh in which he does not recite the Mother of the Book (Umm al-Kitāb)"," it is deficient (khidāj).\"" Then he mentioned something similar to the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah at its beginning"," and he added the tasmiyah (Basmalah). And at the end of the ḥadīth he said: \""And this verse is between Me and My servant into two halves"," and the end of the sūrah is for My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks.\"" ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Ibn Samʿān is ʿAbdullāh ibn Ziyād ibn Samʿān"," whose ḥadīth is abandoned (matrūk).\"" And a group of trustworthy narrators narrated this ḥadīth from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — among them Mālik ibn Anas"," Ibn Jurayj"," Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim"," Ibn ʿUyaynah"," Ibn ʿAjlān"," al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr"," and Abū Uways and others — with differences among them in the chain of narration"," but agreement among them on the text. Not one of them mentioned {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm} in his ḥadīth"," and their agreement is upon the correctness of what is other than the narration of Ibn Samʿān"," and Allah knows best."""
"2370","(2370) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām said — they both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated from Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim, from Aṭāʾ, who said: Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \In every ṣalāh there is a recitation. Whatever the Prophet ﷺ made audible for us"," we have made audible for you"," and whatever he concealed from us"," we have concealed from you. Whoever recites the Mother of the Book (Umm al-Kitāb)"," it suffices him; and whoever adds more"," it is more meritorious.\"""""
"2371","(2371) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ḥakīm al-Awdī narrated to us; Sahl ibn ʿĀmir al-Bajalī narrated to us; Huraym ibn Sufyān narrated to us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid, from Qays ibn Abī Ḥāzim, who said:\n\nI prayed behind Ibn ʿAbbās in Baṣrah. In the first rakʿah he recited {Al-ḥamdu lillāh} [Sūrat al-Fātiḥah] and the first verse of Sūrat al-Baqarah, then he made rukūʿ. Then he stood for the second rakʿah and recited {Al-ḥamdu lillāh} and the second verse of Sūrat al-Baqarah, then he made rukūʿ. When he finished, he turned toward us and said: Indeed, Allah, the Most High, says {So recite what is easy of it} [al-Muzzammil: 20].\n\nʿAlī ibn ʿUmar, may Allah have mercy on him, said: This is a ḥasan isnād. And in it there is evidence for the one who says that the meaning of His statement {So recite what is easy of it} [al-Muzzammil: 20] is that this is after the recitation of Fātiḥat al-Kitāb. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"2372","(2372) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī informed me; my grandfather narrated to us; Abū Thābit Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd ibn al-Sabbāq, from Zayd ibn Thābit, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nAbū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sent for me at the time of the battle of Yamāmah, and ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, was with him. Abū Bakr said: ʿUmar came to me and said: Indeed, the killing has become rampant on the day of Yamāmah among the reciters of the Qurʾān, and I fear that the killing may become rampant among the reciters of the Qurʾān in all places, and much of the Qurʾān will be lost. I think that you should command the collection of the Qurʾān. I said: How can I do something that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do? ʿUmar said: By Allah, it is good. ʿUmar kept discussing this with me until Allah expanded my chest for that which He expanded ʿUmar's chest, and I came to see in this what ʿUmar saw.\n\nZayd said: Abū Bakr said: You are a young, intelligent man; we do not suspect you. You used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So seek out the Qurʾān and collect it. Zayd said: By Allah, had they tasked me with moving a mountain from among the mountains, it would not have been more burdensome upon me than what they tasked me with of collecting the Qurʾān. I said: How can you two do something that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do? Abū Bakr said: By Allah, it is good. He kept discussing this with me until Allah expanded my chest for that which He expanded the chest of Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, and I came to see in this what they both saw. He said: So I sought out the Qurʾān to collect it from palm stalks, thin stones, leather patches, and the memories of men. I found the last verses of Sūrat al-Tawbah — {There has come to you a messenger from among you} [al-Tawbah: 128] to the end of the sūrah — with Khuzaymah or Abū Khuzaymah, and I appended it to the sūrah. The ṣuḥuf remained with Abū Bakr during his lifetime, then with ʿUmar during his lifetime until Allah took him, then with Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Thābit. [Sound. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, no. 7191]"
"2373","(2373) Abū Sahl Muḥammad ibn Naṣrūyah ibn Aḥmad al-Kushmayhanī narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, dictating; Abū Isḥāq Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us. He said: And Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us; al-Zuhrī narrated to us, from ʿUbayd ibn al-Sabbāq, from Zayd ibn Thābit, and he mentioned something similar to it. And he added: Ibn Shihāb said: And Khārijah ibn Zayd informed me, from Zayd ibn Thābit, who said: I was missing a verse from Sūrat al-Aḥzāb that I had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting. I searched for it and did not find it with anyone except with Khuzaymah al-Anṣārī, whose testimony the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had equated with the testimony of two men, due to the statement of Allah, the Most High: {Among the believers are men who were true to what they pledged to Allah} [al-Aḥzāb: 23]. [Sound. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, no. 2807]"
"2374","(2374) And with this isnād, from al-Zuhrī, who said: Anas ibn Mālik informed me that Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān during his caliphate. He had been raiding with the people of Iraq toward Armenia and Azerbaijan in their campaign — that frontier — together with the people of Shām and the people of Iraq. They disputed regarding the Qurʾān, until Ḥudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, was alarmed by what he heard of their disagreement regarding it. So Ḥudhayfah rode until he came to ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: O Commander of the Faithful, take heed of this nation before they disagree regarding the Qurʾān as the Jews and Christians disagreed regarding the scriptures.\n\nʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, was alarmed by that and sent to Ḥafṣah bint ʿUmar: Send us the ṣuḥuf in which the Qurʾān was collected. Ḥafṣah sent them to him. ʿUthmān commanded Zayd ibn Thābit, Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām to copy them into maṣāḥif. He said to them: If you and Zayd ibn Thābit disagree regarding any Arabic expression of the Qurʾān, write it in the tongue of Quraysh, for the Qurʾān was revealed in their tongue. They did so until the maṣāḥif were written. Then ʿUthmān returned the ṣuḥuf to Ḥafṣah, and he sent to every military district of the Muslims a muṣḥaf, and he commanded them to burn every muṣḥaf that contradicted the muṣḥaf that was sent. That was the time when the maṣāḥif were burned.\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah, and the ḥadīth of Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd carries the same meaning, except that in the narration of Abū al-Walīd he said \al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām","\"" and in the narration of Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamzah he said \""ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith.\"" The return of the ṣuḥuf to Ḥafṣah was not mentioned in the narration of Abū al-Walīd"," but it was mentioned in the narration of Ibn Ḥamzah. And at the end of it he said: So they wrote the ṣuḥuf into maṣāḥif"," and he sent a muṣḥaf to every region"," and he commanded that whatever other readings there were on every sheet should be erased or burned.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd"," and he said in both narrations: {Among the believers are men who were true to what they pledged to Allah} [al-Aḥzāb: 23]. [Sound. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 2807]"""
"2375","(2375) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us; Ḥusayn, meaning Ibn ʿAlī al-Juʿfī, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abān — and he was the brother-in-law of Ḥusayn — narrated to us, from ʿAlqamah ibn Marthad, from al-ʿAyzār ibn Jirwal, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nThe people differed regarding the Qurʾān during the time of ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him. A man would say to another man: \My recitation is better than your recitation.\"" When this reached ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," he gathered the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: Indeed"," the people have differed today regarding recitation"," and you are among them. I think that I should unite them upon a single recitation. He said: Our opinion agreed with his opinion on that. ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: Had I been entrusted with what he was entrusted with"," I would have done what he did. [Sound. Ibn ʿAsākar narrated it in Tārīkh Dimashq"," 39/245]"""
"2376","(2376) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us; ʿAwf narrated to us, from Yazīd al-Fārisī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\nI said to ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him: What compelled you to take Sūrat al-Barāʾah, which is among the sūrahs of around two hundred verses, and Sūrat al-Anfāl, which is among the sūrahs of around eighty verses, and join them together, without placing between them a line containing {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}, and you placed it among the seven long sūrahs? What compelled you to do that?\n\nʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ — when sūrahs would be revealed to him in which such-and-such was mentioned — and when verses would be revealed to him, he would say: \Place these verses in such-and-such a place.\"" And when a sūrah would be revealed to him"," he would say: \""Place this sūrah in such-and-such a place.\"" Sūrat al-Anfāl was among the first to be revealed to him in Madīnah"," and Sūrat al-Barāʾah was among the last of the Qurʾān in its revelation"," and its story resembled its story. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away and did not clarify its matter. So I thought that it was part of it; for that reason I joined them together"," and I did not place between them a line containing {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}"," and I placed it among the seven long sūrahs.\n\nIn this is evidence that it was written in the maṣāḥif of the Companions based on direct observation.\n\nAnd we have narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that which indicates that it was written at the beginnings of the sūrahs due to its revelation"," and at the time of its revelation it would be known that a sūrah had ended and another had begun. [Weak. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 786]"""
"2377","(2377) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us in the book of the Sunan; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī, and Ibn al-Sarḥ all said: Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿAmr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr. Qutaybah said: from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not know the separation of a sūrah until {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} was revealed to him.\n\nIbn Jurayj narrated it from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār. [Sound. Abū Dāwūd narrated it, no. 669]"
"2378","(2378) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-ʿAdl narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Ghuzī narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated to us, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\nThe Muslims would not know the ending of a sūrah until {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} was revealed. When {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} was revealed, they would know that the sūrah had ended.\n\nAnd likewise Ḥuṣaym ibn al-Naʿīm narrated it from al-Walīd ibn Muslim, except that he shortened it and did not mention Saʿīd ibn Jubayr in his isnād. [Sound. Al-Ṭaḥāwī narrated it in Mushkil al-Āthār, 3/406]"
"2379","(2379) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us from the original of his book; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī narrated to us in Khusrawjird from his original; ʿĪsā ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Marwazī and Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī both said: ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Mushhir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtār ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:\n\nWhile the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one day among us in the mosque, he nodded off briefly, then raised his head and recited: {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm — Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar, so pray to your Lord and sacrifice. Indeed, your enemy is the one cut off} [al-Kawthar: 1–3]. Then he said: \Do you know what al-Kawthar is?\"" We said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""It is a river that my Lord has promised me in Paradise. Its vessels are more numerous than the number of stars. My Ummah will come to it"," and a servant will be snatched away from among them"," and I will say: 'O Lord"," he is from my Ummah.' And it will be said: 'You do not know what he innovated after you.'\"" [Sound. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it"," 6/305/31655]"""
"2380","(2380) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Mushhir narrated to us; al-Mukhtār ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:\n\nWhile the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one day among us, he nodded off briefly, then raised his head smiling. We said: \What has made you laugh"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""A sūrah has just been revealed to me.\"" Then he recited: {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm — Indeed"," We have granted you al-Kawthar} [al-Kawthar: 1] to the end of it"," and he mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and from ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr"," following the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Bakr.\n\nAnd with his wording also ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād and Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated it from al-Mukhtār ibn Fulful"," though some of them did not say \""just now\"" (ānifan). And the well-known position among the people of tafsīr and maghāzī is that this sūrah is Makkan. And the wording of the ḥadīth of ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr does not contradict their statement"," and it is perhaps the more preferable of the two. [Sound. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2381","(2381) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qaṭan ibn Nusayr narrated to us; Jaʿfar narrated to us; Ḥumayd al-Aʿraj al-Makkī narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), in the narration of the Incident of the Slander (al-Ifk), she said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sat and uncovered his face and said: 'I seek refuge in the All-Hearing' — or he said"," 'I seek refuge in Allah"," the All-Hearing"," the All-Knowing"," from the accursed Satan: {Indeed"," those who came with falsehood…}' [Sūrat al-Nūr"," 11].\"" Abū Dāwūd said: \""I fear that the matter of seeking refuge may be from the words of Ḥumayd.\""\n\nThe Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} at the opening of a sūrah"," but he did not recite it at the opening of verses that were not the beginning of a sūrah. In that is a confirmation of what we have narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," and that it was written in the muṣḥafs only where it was revealed. And Allah knows best.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 783]"""
"2382","(2382) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Baghdādī in Harāt informed us; Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us; Khallād ibn Yaḥyā informed us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rāwād narrated to us; Nāfiʿ narrated from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both): \When he commenced the prayer"," he would say the takbīr"," then recite {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful. All praise is due to Allah…} And when he finished"," he would recite {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful}.\"" He (Nāfiʿ) said: \""And he (Ibn ʿUmar) would say: 'Why was it written in the muṣḥaf if it is not to be recited?'\"" [Strong]"""
"2383","(2383) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā al-Umawī narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Mulaykah from Umm Salamah: \She mentioned — or a word other than it — the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful. All praise is due to Allah"," Lord of the worlds. The Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful. Master of the Day of Judgment.} He would separate his recitation"," verse by verse.\"" [Shādh. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/352]"""
"2384","(2384) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us; Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her): \The recitation of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was: {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful. All praise is due to Allah"," Lord of the worlds} — that is"," word by word.\""\n\nAnd similarly did Ḥafṣ ibn Ghayyāth narrate it from Ibn Jurayj with its meaning. And ʿUmar ibn Hārūn narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"," though he is not strong"," and added to it. [Shādh. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2385","(2385) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Khālid ibn Khidāsh narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Hārūn narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from Umm Salamah: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited in the prayer {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} and counted it as one verse; {All praise is due to Allah"," Lord of the worlds} as two verses; {The Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} as three verses; {Master of the Day of Judgment} as four verses; and thus {You alone we worship"," and You alone we ask for help} as the fifth"," and he gathered his five fingers.\"" Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his book from al-Ṣaghānī. [Shādh. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2386","(2386) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, among others, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Ḥajjāj narrated to us. And ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bushrān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad al-Aʿwar narrated, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: \My father informed me that Saʿīd ibn Jubayr informed him"," and he said to him: {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated verses} [Sūrat al-Ḥijr: 87]. He said: 'It is the Mother of the Qurʾān (Umm al-Qurʾān).'\""\n\nMy father said: \""And Saʿīd ibn Jubayr recited to me {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} until he completed it"," then said: '{In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} is the seventh verse.'\""\n\nSaʿīd ibn Jubayr said to my father: \""And Ibn ʿAbbās recited it to me just as I recited it to you"," then said: '{In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} is the seventh verse.'\""\n\nIbn ʿAbbās said: \""Allah has treasured it for you"," and He did not reveal it to anyone before you.\"""""
"2387","(2387) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghayyāth narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Jurayj from his father from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of the Most High: {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated verses}. He said: \The Opening of the Book (Fātiḥat al-Kitāb).\"" It was said to Ibn ʿAbbās: \""Then where is the seventh?\"" He said: \""{In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful}.\""\n\nAnd that has been narrated from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Weak]"""
"2388","(2388) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Wāṣil narrated to us; Khallād ibn Khālid al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Asbāṭ ibn Naṣr narrated from al-Suddī from ʿAbd Khayr, who said: \ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the seven oft-repeated verses (al-Sabʿ al-Mathānī). He said: '{All praise is due to Allah}' — meaning Sūrat al-Fātiḥah.\"" It was said to him: \""It is only six verses.\"" He said: \""{In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} is a verse.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him)"," both as a marfūʿ and a mawqūf narration"," and the mawqūf is more authentic. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī in his Sunan"," 1/313]"""
"2389","(2389) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Saʿd ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar al-Anṣārī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Thābit narrated from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar; Nūḥ ibn Abī Bilāl narrated to me from Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \He used to say: '{All praise is due to Allah"," Lord of the worlds} — seven verses"," one of which is {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful}"," and it is the seven of the oft-repeated verses"," the great Qurʾān"," the Mother of the Qurʾān"," and the Opening of the Book.'\"" [Munkar. Ibn al-Jawzī said in al-Taḥqīq"," 1/346]"""
"2390","(2390) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid and Muḥammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn Mukram narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated to me; Nūḥ ibn Abī Bilāl informed me from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When you recite {All praise is due to Allah}"," then recite {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful}. Indeed"," it is the Mother of the Qurʾān"," the Mother of the Book"," the seven oft-repeated verses"," and {In the name of Allah"," the Most Gracious"," the Most Merciful} is one of them.\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Ḥanafī said: \""Then I met Nūḥ"," and he narrated to me from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī from Abū Hurayrah the same"," but he did not raise it (to the Prophet).\"" [Munkar. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2391","(2391) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Ḥassān ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: al-Mufaḍḍal, meaning Ibn Faḍālah, narrated from Abī Ṣakhir, from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, regarding the verse {sabʿan min al-mathānī} — he said: It is Umm al-Kitāb (the Mother of the Book), and it is seven verses including {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}. [Ḥasan]"
"2392","(2392) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿĀṣim al-Kilābī narrated to us: Hammām and Jarīr said: Qatādah narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked: \How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""It was elongated (maddan).\"" Then he recited {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}"," elongating (al-Raḥmān) and elongating (al-Raḥīm).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr ibn ʿĀṣim from Hammām"," except that he said: \""He elongated {Bismillāh} and elongated {al-Raḥmān} and elongated {al-Raḥīm}.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Without mention of the Basmalah"," al-Bukhārī narrated it (5045)]"""
"2393","(2393) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: Hammām and Jarīr, meaning Ibn Ḥāzim, said: Qatādah narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Mālik was asked: \How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""It was elongated.\"" Then he recited {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}"," elongating {Bismillāh} and elongating {al-Raḥmān} and elongating {al-Raḥīm}. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Without mention of the Basmalah; it was preceded in the one before it]"""
"2394","(2394) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Miṣrī narrated to us: My father and Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth said: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us, saying: And Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdād informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us: Khālid ibn Yazīd narrated to me from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl from Nuʿaym al-Mujmir, who said: I was behind Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he recited {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}, then he recited Umm al-Qurʾān until he reached {wa lā ḍ-ḍāllīn}. He said: \Āmīn","\"" and the people said: \""Āmīn.\"" And he would say whenever he prostrated: \""Allāhu Akbar","\"" and when he stood from sitting he would say: \""Allāhu Akbar","\"" and when he said the salām he said: \""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," I am the most similar among you in ṣalāh to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nIn the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam: \""I prayed behind Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him).\""\n\nAnd likewise Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ al-Miṣrī narrated it from Khālid ibn Yazīd with this isnād"," and it is in the book of al-Dāraquṭnī"," and it is a ṣaḥīḥ isnād"," and it has corroborating narrations"," including what… [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it (688)]"""
"2395","(2395) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Fārisī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Khurrādhādh narrated to us: Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim narrated to us: Abū Uways narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿqūb from his father from Abū Hurayrah: that the Prophet (ﷺ) would, when he led the people in prayer, recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}. [Ṣaḥīḥ for others]"
"2396","(2396) Abū Bakr informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Ṭālib al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim narrated to us: My grandfather narrated it with its isnād: that the Prophet (ﷺ), when he recited while leading the people, he would open with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\n\nAbū Hurayrah said: \It is a verse from the Book of Allah"," Mighty and Majestic. Recite"," if you wish"," the opening chapter of the Qurʾān"," for it is the seventh verse.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2397","(2397) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Sarrāj narrated to us: ʿUqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Miʿsar from Muḥammad ibn Qays from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to recite aloud in the prayer {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}"," but the people abandoned that.\"" Thus al-Sarrāj said it from ʿUqbah from Yūnus from Miʿsar.\n\nAnd al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated it from ʿUqbah ibn Mukram from Yūnus from Abī Maʿshar from Muḥammad ibn Qays ibn Makhramah"," and this is the correct version. [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Rajab said in al-Fatḥ (5/197)]"""
"2398","(2398) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawayh al-ʿAskarī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us: Muʿtamir narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān from Abī Khālid from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to open the recitation with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\n\nAnd Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated it from Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān, and he said: \I heard Ismāʿīl ibn Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān narrate from Abī Khālid from Ibn ʿAbbās: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} in the prayer"," meaning he used to recite it aloud.\""\n\nAbū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Tamīmī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Māsarjisī narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī informed us: al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān narrated it. And there are corroborating narrations from Ibn ʿAbbās which we have mentioned in al-Khilāfiyāt. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2399","(2399) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī informed us: Abū al-Muwajjih informed us: ʿAbdān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh — and Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥurayth narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ṭālaqānī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Ibn Jurayj from his father from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding al-Sabʿ al-Mathānī — he said: \It is the opening chapter of the Book.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās recited it with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} — seven (verses). Ibn Jurayj said: \""I said to my father: 'Did Saʿīd ibn Jubayr inform you from Ibn ʿAbbās that he said {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} is a verse from the Book of Allah?'\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" Then he said: \""Ibn ʿAbbās recited it with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} in both rakʿahs aloud.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2400","(2400) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us, saying: It was recited to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad while I heard: Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd narrated to us: Ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: ʿUmar ibn Dharr narrated from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzā from his father, who said: \I prayed behind ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," and he recited aloud {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2401","(2401) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Zīqī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Zīqī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from ʿUmar ibn Saʿīd ibn Masrūq, from his father, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \I saw ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib and I prayed behind him"," and I heard him recite aloud {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\"""""
"2402","(2402) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated, saying: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Usāmah ibn Zayd informed you, from Nāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, that he would begin the Mother of the Book with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}. This is the correct version, and it is mawqūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"2403","(2403) Abū Saʿd al-Zāhid narrated to us, saying: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: ʿAtīq ibn Yaʿqūb al-Zubayrī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, saying: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḍabbī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yaḥyā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us, saying: ʿAtīq ibn Yaʿqūb al-Zubayrī narrated to me, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from his father and from his paternal uncle ʿUbayd Allāh, meaning Ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when he commenced the prayer, would begin with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}. In the narration of al-Zāhid, the word \he would recite\"" is used instead of \""he would begin","\"" and he added in his narration: \""And ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," when he commenced the prayer"," would recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} in the Mother of the Book and in the sūrah that follows it.\"" And the correct version is that it is mawqūf.\n\nLikewise"," Ayyūb"," Ibn Jurayj"," and others narrated it from Nāfiʿ. [Ḍaʿīf. al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Awsaṭ"," 1/257]"""
"2404","(2404) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), that he would commence the prayer with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}. [Ḥasan]"
"2405","(2405) He said: And Saʿīd narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), that he would say: \Recitation is to be commenced with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"2406","(2406) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us in Baghdad, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with both of them) would commence the recitation in the prayer with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} and would say: 'Nothing prevents them from it except arrogance.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2407","(2407) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ informed us in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us, he said: it was recited to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad while I was listening: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I prayed behind Ibn al-Zubayr, and he recited and pronounced aloud {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abū Hurayrah with a sound isnād from him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"2408","(2408) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us among others; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, from ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym informed me that Abū Bakr ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar informed him that Anas ibn Mālik said: Muʿāwiyah prayed in Madīnah a prayer in which he recited aloud. He recited {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} with Umm al-Qur'ān, but he did not recite it with the surah that followed it until he completed that recitation. He did not say the takbīr when he bowed until he completed that prayer. When he gave the salām, those of the Muhājirūn who had witnessed that called out to him from every place: \O Muʿāwiyah"," have you stolen the prayer or have you forgotten?\"" Then when he prayed after that"," he recited {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} with the surah that followed Umm al-Qur'ān"," and he said the takbīr when he bowed into prostration. ʿAbd al-Razzāq likewise narrated it from Ibn Jurayj.\n\n[Shādh. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in his Musnad"," 1/36]"""
"2409","(2409) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Yaḥyā al-Jurjānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us. ʿAlī said, and Abū Bakr narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, and he mentioned it, except that he said: \He did not recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} with Umm al-Qur'ān"," nor did he recite it with the surah that followed it.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith and added the Anṣār. Then he said: \""He did not pray after that without reciting {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} with Umm al-Qur'ān and the surah that followed it"," and he said the takbīr when he bowed into prostration.\"" It is as though he reconciled the wording of al-Shāfiʿī's hadith with the wording of ʿAbd al-Razzāq's hadith without clarifying"," and the wording of al-Shāfiʿī's hadith is as we have narrated it. He likewise narrated it in al-Mabsūṭ. Shādh"," and it has been mentioned in the one before it."""
"2410","(2410) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah, from his father, that Muʿāwiyah, may Allah be pleased with him, came to Madīnah and prayed with them, and he did not recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}, and he did not say the takbīr when he lowered or when he raised. The Muhājirūn and the Anṣār called out to him when he gave the salām: \O Muʿāwiyah"," have you stolen your prayer? Where is {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}"," and where is the takbīr when you lower and when you raise?\"" So he prayed with them another prayer and did in it that which they had criticized him for. [Shādh"," and it has been mentioned in the one before it]"""
"2411","(2411) With his isnād, he said: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym informed us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym, from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah, from his father, from Muʿāwiyah and the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār, similar to it or similar in meaning.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, said: \I consider this isnād to be better preserved than the first isnād.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated it from Ibn Khuthaym"," from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah"," from his father"," from his grandfather"," that Muʿāwiyah came to Madīnah. And it is possible that Ibn Khuthaym heard it from both of them"," and Allah knows best.\"" [Shādh"," and it has been mentioned in the one before it]"""
"2412","(2412) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Imām Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd both said: ʿUqayl ibn Khālid narrated to us, from Ibn Shihāb, that he said: \It is from the Sunnah of the prayer that one recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}"," then the Opening of the Book"," then {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}"," then a surah.\"" Ibn Shihāb used to recite at times a surah along with the Opening of the Book"," opening each surah from among them with {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}. He used to say: \""The first to recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} quietly in Madīnah was ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," and he was a modest man.\""\n\nAnd the recitation of it aloud has been narrated to us from the jurists of Makkah: ʿAṭāʾ"," Ṭāwūs"," Mujāhid"," and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Dhahabī in Tārīkh al-Islām"," 8/236]"""
"2413","(2413) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād: Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam informed us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Kathīr informed me: ʿUmar ibn Dharr narrated to me, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that he said: \Indeed"," the Shayṭān stole from the people of the Qur'ān the greatest verse in the Qur'ān: {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\"" Thus it was in my book"," from his father"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and it is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)."""
"2414","(2414) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us in al-Fawāʾid; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd, meaning Ibn Ziyād, informed me: my father informed me; he said: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: Qatādah ibn Daʿāmah wrote to me: Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me: \I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ"," and behind Abū Bakr"," ʿUmar"," and ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with them"," and they used to open the recitation with {al-Ḥamdu lillāhi Rabb al-ʿĀlamīn}"," not mentioning {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} at the beginning of the recitation or at its end.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Mihrān"," from al-Walīd ibn Muslim"," from al-Awzāʿī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 399]"""
"2415","(2415) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Sulamī narrated to us: Badl ibn al-Muḥabbir, Abū al-Munīr al-Yarbūʿī, narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Qatādah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Mālik say: \I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and behind Abū Bakr"," ʿUmar"," and ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with them"," and I did not hear any of them say {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Mūsā and Bundār"," from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar Ghundar"," from Shuʿbah"," and he said: \""I did not hear any of them recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\"" And with this wording a group narrated it from Shuʿbah.\n\nWakīʿ and Aswad ibn ʿĀmir narrated it from Shuʿbah: \""They did not recite aloud {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}.\""\n\nZayd ibn Ḥubāb narrated it from Shuʿbah: \""They used not to recite it aloud.\""\n\nAnd likewise ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated it from Shuʿbah and Hammām"," from Qatādah.\n\nYazīd ibn Hārūn"," Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān"," Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī"," and a group narrated it from Shuʿbah: \""They used to open the recitation with {al-Ḥamdu lillāhi Rabb al-ʿĀlamīn}.\"" And with this wording al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ"," and it has been mentioned in the one before it]"""
"2416","(2416) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Abū ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Anas: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," Abū Bakr"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with both of them"," used to open the recitation with {al-Ḥamdu lillāhi Rabb al-ʿĀlamīn}.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿUmar Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar.\n\nAnd this wording is more deserving of being the preserved one"," for the generality of Qatādah's companions narrated it from Qatādah with this wording"," among them Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl"," Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"," Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"," Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," Abān ibn Yazīd al-Aṭṭār"," Ḥammād ibn Salamah"," and others.\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī said: \""It is the preserved narration from Qatādah and others from Anas.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And likewise Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah and Thābit al-Bunānī narrated it from Anas ibn Mālik.\""\n\nAnd likewise Abū al-Jawzāʾ narrated it from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," from the Prophet ﷺ: \""He used to open the prayer with the takbīr and the recitation with {al-Ḥamdu lillāhi Rabb al-ʿĀlamīn}.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 743]"""
"2417","(2417) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, among the last of them, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān informed us, from Ayyūb, from Qatādah, from Anas — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Prophet ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with them — used to begin the recitation with {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi l-ʿālamīn}.\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh and Abū Saʿīd added in their narration that al-Shāfiʿī said: That is, they would begin with the recitation of Umm al-Qur'ān before what they recited after it. And Allah knows best. And he did not mean that they omitted {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}. [Ṣaḥīḥ. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"
"2418","(2418) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzzakī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from Anas ibn Mālik, that he said: I prayed behind Abū Bakr, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with them — and none of them used to recite {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm} when he opened the prayer. Thus narrated Mālik, and the companions of Ḥumayd differed with him in its wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it in al-Muwaṭṭāʾ, 1/81.]"
"2419","(2419) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed it to us: Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us: Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh informed us, from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from Anas ibn Mālik — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: I prayed behind Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with them — and they used to open their recitation with {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi l-ʿālamīn}. Thus is the narration of the group from Ḥumayd, and some of them mentioned the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, except that they mentioned it with the wording of opening with {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi l-ʿālamīn}.\n\nḤarmalah said: al-Shāfiʿī said, in the narration of Mālik from Ḥumayd, Sufyān ibn ʿUaynah, al-Fazārī, al-Thaqafī, and a number whom I met — seven or eight — agreed in contradicting him, and the large number is more deserving of being preserved than a single one. Then he gave precedence to their narration over the narration of Ayyūb from Qatādah from Anas, and it has already passed. [Ṣaḥīḥ. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"
"2420","(2420) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān, and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: Rūḥ informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Ghiyāth informed us: Abū Naʿāmah al-Ḥanafī informed us, from Ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Mughaffal, from his father, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar, and I did not hear any of them recite {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}.\n\nAnd likewise narrated al-Jurayrī from Abū Nuʿāmah Qays ibn ʿAbāyah al-Ḥanafī, and he added in its text: ʿUthmān — may Allah be pleased with them — except that he said: \I did not hear any of them recite it aloud.\""\n\nAnd Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ contradicted them both"," so he narrated it from Abū Naʿāmah"," from Anas ibn Mālik. [Ḥasan. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it"," 2600.]"""
"2421","(2421) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd informed us, from Sufyān, from Khālid al-Ḥadhdāʾ, from Abū Naʿāmah al-Ḥanafī, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar did not recite — meaning, they did not recite aloud — {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}. Thus is it in the hadith.\n\nAnd al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated it from Sufyān, and he said: \They did not recite aloud","\"" and he did not say \""they did not recite.\""\n\nAnd Abū Naʿāmah is Qays ibn ʿAbāyah; the two Shaykhs (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) did not use him as evidence. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. And it has preceded recently.]"""
"2422","(2422) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us: ʿAffān and Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, they said: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim informed us: Qatādah informed us, he said: I asked Anas about the recitation of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: He used to elongate (the voice) with a prolonged elongation.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, 4045.]"
"2423","(2423) ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: ʿAffān informed us: Hammām informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, from Umm Salamah, that the recitation of the Prophet ﷺ was {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}, and ʿAffān described (it as) letter by letter, and he elongated the sound of each letter. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"2424","(2424) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawayh al-ʿAskarī in Baṣrah informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī informed us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: Abū Iyās, meaning Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah, informed us, he said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon his she-camel — or upon his camel — and it was carrying him along, and he was reciting Sūrat al-Fatḥ with a gentle recitation, or from Sūrat al-Fatḥ, and he was chanting (with tarjīʿ).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it, 4281.]"
"2425","(2425) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Bāghandī informed us: Abū Nuʿaym informed us: Sufyān informed us.\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā al-Ḥīrī informed us: Musaddad ibn Qaṭan informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Wakīʿ ibn al-Jarrāḥ informed us, from Sufyān, from ʿĀṣim ibn Abī al-Najūd, from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr — may Allah be pleased with them both — from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \It will be said to the companion of the Qur'ān on the Day of Resurrection: 'Recite and ascend"," and chant (with tartīl) as you used to chant in the worldly life. For indeed"," your station shall be at the last verse you recite.'\""\n\nTheir two meanings are one"," and Wakīʿ is the more complete of the two in hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it"," 2/192/6799.]"""
"2426","(2426) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī in al-Kūfah and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī in Naysābūr informed us, they said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-ʿAbsī informed us: Wakīʿ informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwsajah, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Adorn the Qur'ān with your voices.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it"," 4/283.]"""
"2427","(2427) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Shuʿbah informed us. And Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr the Faqīh informed us, Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawārīrī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us from Shuʿbah, who said: Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif narrated to me from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwsajah from al-Barāʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Adorn the Qurʾān with your voices.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \""I had forgotten this word until al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Muzāḥim reminded me of it.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of Abū Dāwūd from Shuʿbah: \""I had forgotten this phrase until al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Muzāḥim reminded me of it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2428","(2428) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — he read it to him in Shawwāl of the year thirty-five and three hundred — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq ibn Hammām informed us, Maʿmar informed us from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Shādhān and Muḥammad ibn Naṣr both said: Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad informed us from Yazīd ibn al-Hād from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Allah has not permitted anything as He has permitted a Prophet with a beautiful voice to chant the Qurʾān.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm added in his hadith: \""raising his voice with it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from another route from Yazīd"," and they both narrated it from other routes from al-Zuhrī."""
"2429","(2429) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād informed us, ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-Ward informed us, who said: I heard Ibn Abī Mulaykah say: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Yazīd said: \Abū Lubābah passed by us"," so we followed him until he entered his house"," and we entered upon him. There was a man of shabby appearance and shabby dwelling"," and I heard him say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'He is not of us who does not chant the Qurʾān.'\""\n\nHe said: \""So I said to Ibn Abī Mulaykah: 'O Abū Muḥammad"," what if one does not have a beautiful voice?' He said: 'He should beautify it as much as he is able.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," no. 1471.]"""
"2430","(2430) ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, al-Ḥasan al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ḥammād informed us from Abū Jamrah, who said: \I said to Ibn ʿAbbās: 'Indeed"," I am quick in my recitation; I rush through the Qurʾān.'\""\n\nIbn ʿAbbās said: \""That I should recite Sūrat al-Baqarah and recite it with measured deliberation is more beloved to me than that I should recite the entire Qurʾān in haste.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"2431","(2431) Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us, Abū Saʿīd informed us, al-Zaʿfarānī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us from al-Mughīrah from Ibrāhīm, who said: \ʿAlqamah recited before ʿAbdullāh"," and he had a beautiful voice"," so he said: 'Recite with measured deliberation — may my father and mother be your ransom — for indeed it is the adornment of the Qurʾān.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in Khalq Afʿāl al-ʿIbād"," 1/69.]"""
"2432","(2432) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us, Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Baṣrī informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd informed us, al-Aʿmash informed us from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr from Abū Maʿmar ʿAbdullāh ibn Sakhbarah, who said: \We asked Khabbāb: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recite in the first two rakʿahs and in al-ʿAṣr?' He said: 'Yes.' We said: 'How did you know that?' He said: 'By the movement of his beard.'\""\n\nIt is narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of al-Aʿmash. (Q) And in it is evidence that it is necessary to move the tongue during recitation.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 746.]"""
"2433","(2433) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muʾazzī informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd and Abū Salamah, both of whom informed him from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the imām says 'Āmīn","' then say 'Āmīn","' for indeed"," the one whose saying of 'Āmīn' coincides with the saying of 'Āmīn' by the angels"," his past sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nIbn Shihāb said: \""And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: 'Āmīn.'\""\n\nAnd Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us"," Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us"," Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us"," who said: \""I read it over Mālik"," and he mentioned it with its meaning.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 780.]"""
"2434","(2434) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb informed us, Sufyān informed us from al-Zuhrī.\n\n(H) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī informed us, Sufyān informed us — he said: \We memorized it from al-Zuhrī","\"" and on another occasion he said: \""He narrated it to us\"" — from Saʿīd from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," who said: \""When the reciter says 'Āmīn","' then say 'Āmīn","' for the angels say 'Āmīn.' So the one whose saying of 'Āmīn' coincides with the saying of 'Āmīn' by the angels"," his past sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it"," and it is in al-Bukhārī"," no. 6402.]"""
"2435","(2435) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us among others, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed me, Sumayy informed me.\n\n(H) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbdullāh — that is, al-Qaʿnabī — informed us from Mālik from Sumayy, the freedman of Abū Bakr, from Abū Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the imām says {ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā ḍ-ḍāllīn}"," then say 'Āmīn","' for indeed"," the one whose saying coincides with the saying of the angels"," his past sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: \""Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr followed it up from Abū Salamah.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 796.]"""
"2436","(2436) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed him, Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Marwazī informed us, al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr informed us from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When the reciter says {ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā ḍ-ḍāllīn}"," and those behind him say 'Āmīn","' and that coincides with the saying of the people of the heavens — 'Āmīn' — his past sins will be forgiven.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it"," no. 410"," 416.]"""
"2437","(2437) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from what he read to Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Sarrāj narrated to us among others, and they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When one of you says 'Āmīn","' the angels in the sky say 'Āmīn","' and if one of them coincides with the other"," his past sins are forgiven.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," from Abū al-Zinād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 781.]"""
"2438","(2438) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us, by dictation; Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Bālawayh al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar informed us, from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abū Hurayrah narrated to me. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When one of you says 'Āmīn' and the angels in the sky say 'Āmīn","' and if one of them coincides with the other"," his past sins are forgiven.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\nThat is also established from the ḥadīth of Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Mujmir and Abū Yūnus Sulaym ibn Jubayr"," from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 3232.]"""
"2439","(2439) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us; al-Dabarī narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from Sufyān, from ʿĀṣim, meaning al-Aḥwal, from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: Bilāl, may Allah be pleased with him, said to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \Do not precede me with 'Āmīn.'\""\n\nWakīʿ narrated it from Sufyān"," and he said: from Bilāl that he said: \""O Messenger of Allah.\"" The narration of ʿAbd al-Razzāq is more authentic. ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād also narrated it from ʿĀṣim.\n\nShuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it from ʿĀṣim as well. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 937.]"""
"2440","(2440) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us.\n\nHe said: And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed me; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim ibn Sulaymān. He said: And in the ḥadīth of Rūḥ, he said: ʿĀṣim ibn Sulaymān wrote to me that Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī narrated to him, from Bilāl, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Do not precede me with 'Āmīn.'\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Fuḍayl also narrated it from ʿĀṣim in the same manner."""
"2441","(2441) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us in the Musnad; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; my father narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us; ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: Bilāl, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Do not precede me with 'Āmīn.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: It is as though Bilāl used to say \""Āmīn\"" before the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said \""Āmīn","\"" so he said: \""Do not precede me with 'Āmīn","'\"" just as he said: \""When the Imām says 'Āmīn","' then you say 'Āmīn.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2442","(2442) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Kathīr informed us, from Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAmr ibn Qays, from Muḥammad ibn al-Ashʿath, who said: I entered upon ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and she narrated to me, saying: While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, three Jewish men came, and one of them sought permission. And she mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Do you know what they envied us for?\"" I said: \""Allah and His Messenger know best.\"" He said: \""They envied us for the qiblah to which we were guided and they went astray from it"," and for the Jumuʿah to which we were guided and they went astray from it"," and for our saying 'Āmīn' behind the Imām.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/136/25073.]"""
"2443","(2443) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī informed us; ʿAbd al-Bāqī ibn Qāniʿ al-Qāḍī narrated to us in Baghdād; Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maysarah narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥurrah narrated to us, from Mujāhid, from Muḥammad ibn al-Ashʿath, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The Jews do not envy us in anything as much as they envy us in three things: the salām"," the saying of 'Āmīn","' and 'Allāhumma rabbanā laka al-ḥamd.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2444","(2444) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and others narrated to us, and they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; he said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas and Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to me that Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: \When the Imām says 'Āmīn","' then you say 'Āmīn","' for the angels say 'Āmīn.' So whose saying of 'Āmīn' coincides with the saying of the angels"," his past sins are forgiven.\""\n\nIbn Shihāb"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: And the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," used to say \""Āmīn.\""\n\nYūnus said: And Ibn Shihāb used to say that. Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā"," from Ibn Wahb"," from Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. And it has preceded under no. 2433 and what follows it.]"""
"2445","(2445) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original copy; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadbādhī narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Ḥafarī narrated to us, from Sufyān al-Thawrī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us; Khallād ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Sufyān informed us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Ḥujr ibn al-ʿAnbas, from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, who said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said \Āmīn","\"" he raised his voice with it. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Faqīh. And in the narration of al-Sulamī"," he said: I heard the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," when he said {"""
"2446","(2446) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us; Yazīd ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth narrated to us; al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us, from Sufyān, and he mentioned with its isnād something similar.\n\nAnd he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, when he said {"
"2447","(2447) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to me: Salamah ibn Kuhayl informed me. He said: I heard Hujr, Abu al-'Anbas, say: I heard 'Alqamah ibn Wa'il narrating from Wa'il — and I also heard it directly from Wa'il — that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he recited {Not of those who have earned [Your] anger nor of those who are astray}, he said: \Amin","\"" lowering his voice therewith.\n\nAbu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi informed us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Faris narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari said: Shu'bah was contradicted in this narration in three respects. It was said [that the narrator is] Hujr Abu al-Sakin"," who is Ibn 'Anbas"," and he added 'Alqamah in the chain when he is not [actually] in it"," and he said \""he lowered his voice","\"" when in fact it is \""he raised his voice.\"" And it has reached me from Abu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi"," from al-Bukhari"," that he mentioned it and said: The hadith of Sufyan al-Thawri from Salamah on this topic is more authentic than the hadith of Shu'bah"," and Shu'bah erred in it. Abu Zur'ah al-Razi said likewise.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: As for his error in the matn"," it is clear. As for his statement that Hujr is Abu al-'Anbas"," Muhammad ibn Kathir likewise narrated it from al-Thawri. As for his statement regarding 'Alqamah"," he clarified in his narration that Hujr heard it from 'Alqamah"," and he also heard it directly from Wa'il himself. Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated it from Shu'bah in a manner similar to the narration of al-Thawri.\n\n[Rejected (Munkar). Narrated by al-Tirmidhi"," 248.]"""
"2448","(2448) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us in al-Fawa'id al-Kabir li-Abi al-'Abbas, and in the hadith of Shu'bah: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Marzuq al-Basri narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl. He said: I heard Hujr Abu 'Anbas narrating from Wa'il al-Hadrami that he prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and when he said {nor of those who are astray}, he said: \Amin","\"" raising his voice therewith. It has also been narrated from two other routes from Wa'il ibn Hujr"," in a manner similar to the narration of al-Thawri.\n\n[Sahih. And it was mentioned previously.]"""
"2449","(2449) Abu Siddiq Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fawaris al-Saydalani informed us from his original copy: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us: al-Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us: Sharik narrated from Abu Ishaq from 'Alqamah ibn Wa'il from his father, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite \Amin\"" aloud.\n\nAnd Abu Siddiq informed us: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us: al-Aswad ibn 'Amir narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated from Abu Ishaq from 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il from his father"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," similarly.\n\nZayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated it from Abu Ishaq from 'Abd al-Jabbar"," and he said: \""He extended his voice with it.\"" And 'Ammar ibn Zurayq narrated it from Abu Ishaq from 'Abd al-Jabbar"," and he said: \""He raised his voice with it.\""\n\n[Sahih. And it was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2450","(2450) And Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran informed us: Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-'Utaridi narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Nahshali, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu 'Abdullah al-Yahsabi, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said {Not of those who have earned [Your] anger nor of those who are astray} [al-Fatihah: 7], say: \My Lord"," forgive me. Amin.\""\n\n[Weak (Da'if). Narrated by al-Tabarani in al-Kabir"," 22/42.]"""
"2451","(2451) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Isbahani narrated to us: 'Abdan narrated to us: 'Abd al-Malik ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir, who said: Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, led us in prayer. He said {In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful}, then he recited Umm al-Qur'an until he reached {Not of those who have earned [Your] anger nor of those who are astray}. He said: \Amin.\"" Then he said: \""By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," I am the one among you whose prayer most closely resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 688.]"""
"2452","(2452) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bashran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya ibn 'Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Zubaydi informed me: 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Salim narrated from al-Zubaydi, who said: Al-Zuhri informed me from Abu Salamah and Sa'id that Abu Hurayrah said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished reciting Umm al-Qur'an, he raised his voice and said: \Amin.\""\n\nAnd likewise Abu al-Ahwas al-Qadi narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-'Ala' al-Zubaydi.\n\nAnd Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us. He said: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz said: This is a good (hasan) isnad — meaning the isnad of this hadith.\n\n[Hasan. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 571.]"""
"2453","(2453) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us: Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Thabit from Abu Rafi' that Abu Hurayrah used to give the adhan for Marwan ibn al-Hakam, and he stipulated that Marwan should not say {nor of those who are astray} before he knew that he had entered the row. So when Marwan said {nor of those who are astray}, Abu Hurayrah would say: \Amin","\"" prolonging his voice with it"," and he said: \""When the tamin of the people of the earth coincides with the tamin of the people of the heavens"," they will be forgiven.\""\n\n[Sahih. And it was mentioned previously"," no. 2436.]"""
"2454","(2454) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated from Ibn Jurayj from 'Ata', who said: I used to hear the imams — Ibn al-Zubayr and those after him — say \Amin","\"" and those behind them would say \""Amin","\"" until the mosque would resound with a clamor.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," that he would raise his voice with it"," whether he was an imam or a follower (ma'mum).\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari in a ta'liq (suspended) form.]"""
"2455","(2455) And Abu Ya'la Hamzah ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Saydalani informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us: Abu Hamzah narrated from Mutarrif from Khalid ibn Abi Ayyub from 'Ata', who said: I came upon two hundred of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ in this mosque. When the imam said {Not of those who have earned [Your] anger nor of those who are astray}, I would hear from them a clamor of \Amin.\"" Ishaq al-Hanzali narrated it from 'Ali ibn al-Hasan"," and he said: \""They raised their voices with 'Amin.'\""\n\n[Hasan.]"""
"2456","(2456) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bashran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz narrated to us: Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Qabisah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Ja'far, Abu 'Ali, the seller of mats, from Abu 'Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to announce: \There is no prayer without the recitation of the Opening of the Book"," and what is beyond that [is additional].\""\n\n[Sahih in other respects. And it was mentioned previously"," no. 2361.]"""
"2457","(2457) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Muhammad 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamdan in Hamadan informed us; Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Jazzar narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Sulaiman narrated to us; Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he used to recite in the two rak'ahs of Zuhr: in every rak'ah, the Opening of the Book (Surah al-Fatihah) and a surah. He would lengthen the first rak'ah and shorten the second, and he would sometimes let us hear a verse.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Nu'aym from Shayban, and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Yahya.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari, 759]"
"2458","(2458) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, and Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid al-Muqri', and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us; Hajjaj said: Ibn Jurayj said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abbad ibn Ja'far say:\n\n(And) 'Ali ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Shafi'i narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us; Hajjaj said: Ibn Jurayj said: I heard Muhammad ibn 'Abbad ibn Ja'far say: Abu Salamah ibn Sufyan, 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr ibn al-'As, and 'Abdullah ibn al-Musayyab al-'Abadi informed me from 'Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: The Prophet ﷺ prayed the morning prayer in Makkah and began Surah al-Mu'minun. When he reached the mention of Musa and Harun — or the mention of 'Isa (Muhammad ibn 'Abbad was uncertain, or they differed concerning it) — a cough overtook the Prophet ﷺ, so he went into ruku'. And Ibn al-Sa'ib was present.\n\nMuslim likewise narrated it in his Sahih from Harun al-Jamal from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, and al-Bukhari said: It is mentioned from 'Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib with this.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Muslim, 455]"
"2459","(2459) 'Ali ibn Ahmad al-Muqri', known as Ibn al-Hammami, in Baghdad informed us; Ahmad ibn Salman informed us; it was recited to Ahmad ibn Mula'ib; 'Affan narrated to us. And it was recited to 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad while I heard; 'Amr ibn 'Amir and Abu al-Walid said: Hammam ibn Yahya, the companion of al-Basri, narrated from Qatadah from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to recite the Opening of the Book (Surah al-Fatihah) and whatever is easy (from the Qur'an).\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad, 3/110, 113]"
"2460","(2460) Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmawayh al-'Askari in Basrah informed us; Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi narrated to us; Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from 'Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il say: A man came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: \I recited the Mufassal in one rak'ah last night.\"" Ibn Mas'ud said: \""Is this like the recitation of poetry? I know the pairs of surahs that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to combine together.\"" He then mentioned twenty surahs from the beginning of the Mufassal"," two surahs in one rak'ah.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Adam"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shu'bah.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 775]"""
"2461","(2461) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zurai' narrated to us; al-Jurayri narrated from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I asked 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ combine between surahs?\"" She said: \""From the Mufassal.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 1292]"""
"2462","(2462) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, both narrated from Sa'id al-Jurayri, and he mentioned it, except that he said: \Between the two surahs.\""\n\n[Sahih. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2463","(2463) Abu Ahmad al-Mihranjani al-'Adl informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Ibn Shihab from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah: that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) recited to them {By the star when it descends} (Surah al-Najm) and performed prostration in it, then stood up and recited another surah.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Malik in al-Muwatta', 481]"
"2464","(2464) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated from al-Walid ibn Kathir; Nafi' informed me: that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar used to combine two or three surahs from the Mufassal in a single rak'ah of the obligatory prayer.\n\n[Sahih]"
"2465","(2465) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; al-Qadi Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Khurrazadh informed us; Musa ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us; Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Darawardi narrated from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar from Thabit al-Bunani from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man from the Ansar used to lead them in prayer in the Mosque of Quba'. Whenever he began a surah to recite to them in the prayer from what is recited, he would begin with {Say: He is Allah, the One} (Surah al-Ikhlas) until he finished it, then he would recite another surah along with it. He would do that in every rak'ah. His companions spoke to him and said: \You begin with this surah"," then you do not consider it sufficient until you recite another with it. Either recite it alone"," or leave it and recite another.\"" He said to them: \""I will not leave it. If you wish"," I will lead you in prayer with that"," and if you dislike it"," I will leave you.\"" They considered him the best among them"," and they disliked that anyone else should lead them. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them"," they informed him of the matter. He said: \""O so-and-so"," what prevents you from doing what your companions ask you? And what compels you to adhere to this surah in every rak'ah?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I love it.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," your love for it will admit you to Paradise.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari in ta'liq form"," Kitab al-Adhan"," chapter on combining two surahs in one rak'ah...]"""
"2466","(2466) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtawayh informed us; 'Ali ibn al-Saqr narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated it with the same meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhari said: And 'Ubaydullah narrated from Thabit from Anas, and he mentioned this hadith.\n\n[Sahih. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"
"2467","(2467) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: it was read to Ibn Wahb: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you, from Ibn Shihāb, from Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Mother of the Qurʾān (Sūrat al-Fātiḥah).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah"," from Ibn Wahb"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It was previously cited under no. 2363.]"""
"2468","(2468) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \In every prayer there is recitation. Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud for us"," we have recited aloud for you"," and whatever he concealed from us"," we have concealed from you.\"" A man said: \""What is your opinion if I do not add anything beyond the Mother of the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""If you add to it"," that is better"," and if you confine yourself to it"," it will suffice you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī cited it as no. 772.]"""
"2469","(2469) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us — reading to him — ʿAffān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us: Ḥanẓalah narrated to us, from ʿIkrimah, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs in which he recited nothing except the Opening of the Book (Sūrat al-Fātiḥah).\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad cited it in al-Musnad, 1/282.]"
"2470","(2469) And ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated it similarly from Ḥanẓalah al-Sadūsī, except that he said: \He prayed a prayer in which he recited nothing except the Opening of the the Book.\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān narrated it to us in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adami narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Ramlī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to us: Ḥanẓalah al-Sadūsī narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. It was previously cited in the hadith before it.]"""
"2471","(2471) And others narrated it from Ḥanẓalah: Shahr ibn Ḥawshab narrated to us, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs and did not add to them anything beyond the Opening of the Book.\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated it to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Bakrāwī narrated to us: Ḥanẓalah al-Sadūsī narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd it was narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās as his own statement regarding the permissibility of confining oneself to the Opening of the Book.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. It was previously cited in the hadith before it.]"
"2472","(2472) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāʾinī narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar: Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated to me, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ entered the mosque. A man entered and prayed, then came and greeted the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \And upon you be peace. Go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" He did this three times. The man said: \""By the One Who sent you with the truth"," I cannot do better than this"," so show me and teach me.\"" He said: \""When you stand for prayer"," say the takbīr"," then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qurʾān"," then bow until you are at ease in rukūʿ"," then raise your head until you stand upright"," then prostrate until you are at ease in sujūd"," then raise your head until you are at ease sitting"," then do that throughout all your prayer.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī cited it as no. 757.]"""
"2473","(2473) Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated it from Abū Usāmah, from ʿUbaydullāh, from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, and he said at its end: \Then do likewise in every rakʿah and every sajdah.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Abū Naṣr al-Khaffāf narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī cited it in al-Qirāʾah khalf al-Imām"," no. 74.]"""
"2474","(2474) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Muḥammad al-Nāqid narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \When you are the imām"," then make it light"," for among the people there are the elderly"," the weak"," and those with needs. And when you pray alone"," then make it as long as you wish. In every prayer there is recitation. Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud for us"," we have recited aloud for you"," and whatever he concealed from us"," we have concealed from you.\"" A man said to him: \""What is your opinion if I do not add anything beyond the Mother of the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""If you add to it"," that is better"," and if you confine yourself to it"," it will suffice you.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr al-Nāqid"," without what is at its beginning regarding the command to make the prayer light. Al-Bukhārī narrated it as mentioned above.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī cited it as no. 772.]"""
"2475","(2475) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — dictating — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us: Hammām and Abān ibn Yazīd narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the first two rakʿahs of Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr the Opening of the Book and a sūrah, and he would sometimes let us hear a verse, and he would recite in the last two rakʿahs the Opening of the Book.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah, from Yazīd ibn Hārūn, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl, from Hammām.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī cited it as no. 776.]"
"2476","(2476) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdād: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Miʿsar narrated to us, saying: Yazīd al-Faqīr narrated to me, saying: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, saying: \In the two rakʿahs — meaning the first two — one recites the Opening of the Book and a sūrah"," and in the last two"," the Opening of the Book.\"" He said: \""And we used to say that there is no prayer except with the Opening of the Book and what is beyond that\"" — or he said: \""and more than that.\""\n\nAnd we have been narrated what indicates this from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd"," and ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with them.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah cited it as no. 3633.]"""
"2477","(2477) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlāʾ ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾinī informed us — Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad ibn Bishr informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī al-Dhuhlī narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Hushaym narrated from Manṣūr, from al-Walīd ibn Muslim.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Hushaym ibn Bashīr narrated from Manṣūr ibn Zādhān, from al-Walīd Abī Bishr, from Abī al-Ṣiddīq, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: We used to estimate the length of the standing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr prayers. We estimated his standing in the first two rakʿahs of the Ẓuhr to be the length of the recitation of {Alif Lām Mīm Tanzīl} — al-Sajdah. And we estimated his standing in the last two rakʿahs to be half of that. And we estimated his standing in the first two rakʿahs of the ʿAṣr to be equal to his standing in the last two rakʿahs of the Ẓuhr, and in the last two rakʿahs to be half of that. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. And in the ḥadīth of Musaddad it states: \equal to the length of thirty verses","\"" and the remainder carries the same meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (7755)"," Muslim.]"""
"2478","(2478) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed me — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ ibn al-Sindī narrated to us — Shaybān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah narrated from Manṣūr ibn Zādhān, from al-Walīd Abī Bishr, from Abī al-Ṣiddīq al-Nājī, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, from the Prophet ﷺ: He used to recite in the Ẓuhr prayer, in the first two rakʿahs, approximately thirty verses in each rakʿah, and in the last two rakʿahs approximately fifteen verses — or he said, half of that — and in the ʿAṣr, in the first two rakʿahs, approximately fifteen verses in each rakʿah, and in the last two rakʿahs, half of that.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim (452).]"
"2479","(2479) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Abī Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-ʿAdl informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated from Abī ʿUbayd, the mawlā of Sulaymān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, that ʿUbadah ibn Nusayy informed him that he heard Qays ibn al-Ḥārith say: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣunābīḥī informed me that he came to Madīnah during the caliphate of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, and he prayed the Maghrib behind Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq. Abū Bakr recited in the first two rakʿahs Umm al-Qurʾān and a short sūrah from al-Mufaṣṣal. Then he stood up for the third rakʿah. He (the narrator) said: I drew close to him until my garments were nearly touching his garments, and I heard him reciting Umm al-Qurʾān and this verse: {Our Lord, let not our hearts deviate after You have guided us and grant us from Yourself mercy. Indeed, You are the Bestower.} [Āl ʿImrān: 8]. Abū Saʿīd added in his narration that al-Shāfiʿī said, and Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said: When ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz heard this from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: \I was not upon this practice until I heard this"," and so I adopted it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," and from him al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm (7/207"," 228).]"""
"2480","(2480) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, when he prayed alone, would recite in all four rakʿahs, in each rakʿah, Umm al-Qurʾān and a sūrah. And sometimes he would recite two or three sūrahs in a single rakʿah in the obligatory prayer. And he would recite in the two rakʿahs of the Maghrib likewise — Umm al-Qurʾān and a sūrah in each. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Bukayr, and al-Shāfiʿī did not mention the Maghrib. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Muwaṭṭāʾ (175).]"
"2481","(2481) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us — Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us — Abū ʿAmr Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from Abī ʿAwn Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from Jābir ibn Samurah, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, may Allah be pleased with him: \Indeed"," the people of Kūfah have complained about you in everything"," even in the prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (770).]"""
"2482","(2482) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us — Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb, Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl, and ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us, and the wording is that of Sulaymān — Shuʿbah narrated from Abī ʿAwn, who said: I heard Jābir ibn Samurah say: ʿUmar said to Saʿd, may Allah be pleased with them both: \They have complained about you in everything"," even in the prayer.\"" He said: \""As for me"," I lengthen the first two rakʿahs and shorten the last two"," and I do not fall short of what I followed from the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He said: \""You have spoken truly; that is what I thought of you.\"" In the ḥadīth of Shabābah it states: \""I lengthen them in the first two rakʿahs and shorten them in the last two.\"" And at the end of it he said: \""That is what I thought of you"," O Abū Isḥāq.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to in the preceding ḥadīth.]"""
"2483","(2483) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us — ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, and the wording is his — Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh in Ṭabarān informed us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us — Abū ʿAwānah narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr narrated from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: The people of Kūfah complained about Saʿd to ʿUmar, so he removed him and appointed ʿAmmār over them. They complained about him until they mentioned that he could not pray properly. So he sent for him and said: \O Abū Isḥāq"," these people claim that you cannot pray properly.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I used to pray with them the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," without omitting anything from it. I would pray the ʿIshāʾ prayer and make the first two rakʿahs long and shorten the last two.\"" He said: \""That is what I thought of you"," O Abū Isḥāq.\""\n\nSo he sent with him a man or men to the people of Kūfah to ask about him. He did not leave a mosque without asking about him"," and they spoke only good of him"," until he entered the mosque of Banī ʿAbs. A man from among them stood up — he was called Usāmah ibn Qatādah"," known as Abū Saʿdah — and said: \""Since you have adjured us"," indeed Saʿd used not to go out on military campaigns"," nor distribute equally"," nor judge fairly.\""\n\nSaʿd said: \""By Allah"," I will supplicate against him with three things: O Allah"," if this servant of Yours is a liar"," having stood for show and reputation"," then prolong his life"," prolong his poverty"," and expose him to tribulations.\"" Afterwards"," when he was asked about his condition"," he would say: \""An old man"," afflicted — the supplication of Saʿd has befallen me.\"" ʿAbd al-Malik said: \""I later saw him"," his eyebrows having fallen over his eyes due to old age"," and he would expose himself to young women in the pathways"," winking at them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (755).]"""
"2484","(2484) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us — Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us — Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us — Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the first two rakʿahs of the Ẓuhr prayer, lengthening the first and shortening the second, and he would do the same in the Fajr prayer.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (779).]"
"2485","(2485) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us — Ibn Rajāʾ narrated to us — Hammām narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr prayers, in the first two rakʿahs, Umm al-Kitāb and two sūrahs, and in the last two rakʿahs, Umm al-Kitāb alone. And he would sometimes let us hear a verse. And he would lengthen the first rakʿah and not lengthen the second, and likewise in the ʿAṣr, and likewise in the Fajr.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Hammām ibn Yaḥyā, and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hammām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously referenced as no. 2475.]"
"2486","(2486) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated from Yaḥyā, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father: \We thought that he intended by this that the people might catch the first rakʿah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (2675).]"""
"2487","(2487) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us; Jaʿfar, meaning Ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir, and Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr both said: ʿAffān narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Juḥāda narrated from a man from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā that the Prophet ﷺ used to stand in the first rakʿah of Ẓuhr until no footfall could be heard. It is said that this man is Ṭarfa al-Ḥaḍramī. [Weak. Narrated by Aḥmad 4/356/19359]"
"2488","(2488) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbbās al-Asfaṭī and Aḥmad ibn al-Haytham al-Shaʿrānī both said: al-Ḥimmānī narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq al-Ḥumaysī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Juḥāda narrated from Ṭarfa al-Ḥaḍramī from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Awfā, who said: The Prophet ﷺ used to pray Ẓuhr with us when the sun passed its meridian, when the heat was so intense that if one placed a side on the burning sand, it would cook it. He would lengthen the first rakʿah of Ẓuhr, continuing to stand reciting so long as he could hear the clatter of the people's sandals. He would make the second rakʿah shorter than the first, the third shorter than the second, and the fourth shorter than the third. He would pray ʿAṣr with us for a duration in which a traveller could cover two or three farsakhs. He would lengthen the first rakʿah of ʿAṣr, the second shorter than the first, the third shorter than the second, and the fourth shorter than the third. He would pray Maghrib with us at the time when one person would say, \The sun has set","\"" while another would say"," \""It has not yet set.\"" He would lengthen the first rakʿah of Maghrib"," the second shorter than the first"," and the third shorter than the second. He would delay ʿIshāʾ slightly. [Weak. The ḥadīth has been previously mentioned.]"""
"2489","(2489) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Sahl narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Rushayd narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz from ʿAṭiyya ibn Qays from Qazaʿa from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Ẓuhr prayer would be announced for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a person would go to al-Baqīʿ, relieve himself, perform wuḍūʾ, and then come, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would still be in the first rakʿah, owing to how much he would lengthen it. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Dāwūd ibn Rushayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 454]"
"2490","(2490) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Manṣūr ibn Zādhān narrated from al-Walīd ibn Muslim from Abī al-Ṣiddīq from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: We used to estimate the standing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the first two rakʿāt of Ẓuhr to be approximately the recitation of thirty verses, equivalent to the recitation of {Alif Lām Mīm Tanzīl} (al-Sajdah), and in the last two rakʿāt, half of that. We estimated his standing in the first two rakʿāt of ʿAṣr to be equal to the last two rakʿāt of Ẓuhr, and the last two rakʿāt of ʿAṣr to be half of that. Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Hushaym. And Abū ʿAwāna narrated it from Manṣūr, and he said in the ḥadīth: In each rakʿah, approximately thirty verses. Muslim has narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ as previously mentioned. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned under no. 2477]"
"2491","(2491) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated, and among the last he said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated, he said: I read to Mālik from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Salama ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that Abū Hurayra used to lead them in prayer. He would say the takbīr whenever he lowered and raised himself. When he had completed the prayer, he said: By Allah, I am the one among you whose prayer most closely resembles the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. In the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā: \When he had completed.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 785]"""
"2492","(2492) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Mukram narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that he heard Abū Hurayra say: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he would say the takbīr upon standing. Then he would say the takbīr when he bowed. Then he would say, \Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah","\"" when he raised his back from the rukūʿ. Then"," while standing"," he would say"," \""Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd.\"" Then he would say the takbīr when he went down into prostration. Then he would say the takbīr when he raised his head. He would do this throughout the entire prayer until he completed it"," and he would say the takbīr when he stood up from the two rakʿāt after sitting. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from Ḥujayn ibn al-Muthannā from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 789]"""
"2493","(2493) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated; it was read to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas and Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you from Ibn Shihāb from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say the takbīr whenever he lowered and raised himself. He said: This remained his prayer until he met Allah, the Mighty and Majestic. It is a ḥasan mursal ḥadīth. This last wording has also been narrated in the connected ḥadīth from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Abū Salama from Abū Hurayra, may Allah be pleased with him. [Weak. Narrated by Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭāʾ 166]"
"2494","(2494) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsa narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us; my father and Baqiyya narrated from Shuʿayb from al-Zuhrī, who said: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Abū Salama informed me that Abū Hurayra would say the takbīr in every prayer, obligatory and otherwise. He would say the takbīr when he stood, then say the takbīr when he bowed, then say, \Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah","\"" then say"," \""Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd","\"" before he prostrated. Then he would say"," \""Allāhu Akbar","\"" when he went down into prostration. Then he would say the takbīr when he raised his head. Then he would say the takbīr when he prostrated. Then he would say the takbīr when he raised his head. Then he would say the takbīr when he stood from the sitting of the two rakʿāt. He would do this in every rakʿah until he finished the prayer. Then"," when he had completed it"," he would say: By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," I am the closest of you in resemblance to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Indeed"," this was his prayer until he departed this world. Abū Dāwūd"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: This last statement is narrated by Mālik"," al-Zubaydī"," and others from al-Zuhrī from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn. And ʿAbd al-Aʿlā agreed with Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamza from al-Zuhrī from Maʿmar. The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: al-Bukhārī has narrated the ḥadīth of Shuʿayb from Abū al-Yamān from Shuʿayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad 2/270/7645]"""
"2495","(2495) And Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Muqriʾ informed us with the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Aʿlā; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated from Maʿmar from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salama and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: Both of them prayed behind Abū Hurayra. When he bowed, he said the takbīr. When he raised his head, he said, \Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah"," Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd.\"" Then he prostrated and said the takbīr. Then he raised his head and said the takbīr. Then he said the takbīr when he stood from the two rakʿāt. Then he said: This remained the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he departed this world. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned in the one before it]"""
"2496","(2496) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥusayn al-Dārimī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Shāhīn narrated to us; Khālid narrated from al-Jurayrī from Abū al-ʿAlāʾ from Muṭarrif from ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, who said: He prayed with ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, in Baṣra. ʿImrān said: This man reminded us of a prayer that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray with us. He mentioned that he would say the takbīr whenever he raised and whenever he placed down. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Shāhīn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 786]"
"2497","(2497) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz in Naysabur and Abu al-Qasim 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali al-Fami al-Faqih in Baghdad informed us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us; Ja'far al-Tayalisi narrated to us; 'Affan and Abu Salamah narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us; Qatadah narrated from 'Ikramah, who said: I prayed behind an old man in Makkah, and he pronounced twenty-two takbirs in the Zuhr prayer. So I came to Ibn 'Abbas and said: \I prayed behind a foolish old man who pronounced twenty-two takbirs in the Zuhr prayer.\"" He said: \""May your mother lose you! That is the prayer of Abu al-Qasim (ﷺ).\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Salamah. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 787"," 788.]"""
"2498","(2498) Abu al-Qasim Zayd ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Husayni in Kufah informed us; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Hunayn narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abu 'Awanah narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman al-Asam, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about the takbir in prayer. He said: \He (the Prophet ﷺ) would say takbir when he bowed (ruku')"," when he prostrated (sujud)"," when he raised his head from prostration"," when he prostrated again"," and when he stood up in the two rak'ahs.\"" Khatim asked him: \""From whom do you preserve this?\"" He said: \""From the Prophet (ﷺ)"," Abu Bakr"," and Umayd (may Allah be pleased with them both).\"" Khatim then asked him: \""'Uthman as well?\"" He said: \""And 'Uthman.\""\n\nThis is the correct form with the letter kha' (خ)"," though it has also been said as Hutaym with the letter ha' ("""
"2499","(2499) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu 'Uthman al-Basri and Abu al-Fadl al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Quhyar said: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Sufyan narrated.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu al-Qasim Zayd ibn Abi Hashim al-'Alawi informed us; Abu Ja'far ibn Duhaym narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated from Sufyan, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-Asam, who said: I heard Anas saying: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," Abu Bakr"," 'Umar"," and 'Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them all) would complete the takbir when they raised and when they lowered.\""\n\nAnd this and what precedes it are more preferable. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Maqdisi in al-Mukhtarah"," 6/406/15426.]"""
"2500","(2500) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Abu Muslim narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Ka'bi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from al-Hasan ibn 'Imran from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abzi from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would not complete the takbir.\""\n\nAnd in the hadith of 'Amr"," from Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abzi from his father: \""He prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he would not complete the takbir.\""\n\nIt may be that he said the takbir but it was not heard"," or it may be that he omitted it once to demonstrate permissibility. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Da'if. Narrated by Ahmad"," 3/406/15426.]"""
"2501","(2501) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī (by way of recitation) and Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isfahani (by way of dictation) informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik informed us.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us; Isma'il al-Qadi narrated to us; 'Abdullah narrated from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn 'Abdillah, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commenced the prayer"," he would raise his hands level with his shoulders"," and when he raised his head from ruku'"," he would raise them likewise"," and he would say: 'Sami' Allahu liman hamidah"," Rabbana wa lak al-hamd.' And he would not do that in prostration.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of al-Qa'nabi.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi"," and 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated it from Malik"," adding therein: \""And when he said takbir for ruku'.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 735.]"""
"2502","(2502) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us; it was read to Ibn Wahb: \Malik ibn Anas informed you","\"" and he mentioned it.\n\nLikewise"," 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi"," Khalid ibn Mukhallad"," and a group narrated it from Malik. [Sahih. And it was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2503","(2503) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar and Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz narrated to us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr al-Mukharrami narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): when he commenced the prayer"," he would raise his hands until they were level with his shoulders; and when he intended to bow into ruku'"," and after he raised his head from ruku'; but he would not raise them between the two prostrations.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya and a group from Ibn 'Uyaynah. [Sahih. And it was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2504","(2504) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; al-Hasan ibn Halim al-Marwazi narrated to us; Abu al-Muwajjah narrated to us; 'Abdan informed us; 'Abdullah informed us.\n\n(Chain variant) And Abu 'Abdillah informed us; Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan in Marw informed us — and the wording is his — he said: Ibrahim ibn Hilal narrated to us; 'Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Butani narrated to us; 'Abdullah informed us; Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrated from al-Zuhri, who said: Salim ibn 'Abdillah informed me from Ibn 'Umar, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): when he stood in prayer"," he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders"," then he would say takbir.\"" He said: \""And he would do that when he said takbir for ruku'"," and he would do that when he raised his head from ruku'"," and he would say: 'Sami' Allahu liman hamidah.' And he would not do that in prostration.\"" He said: \""And Ibn al-Mubarak used to raise his hands likewise in the five prayers"," the voluntary prayers"," the two Eids"," and the funeral prayer.\"" [Sahih. And it was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2505","(2505) Abu 'Abdillah informed us through it in another place; Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan al-Sayrafi narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Hilal narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated from Yunus, and he mentioned something similar to it, but he did not mention the action of Ibn al-Mubarak.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn Muqatil from 'Abdullah, and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Qahzad from Salamah ibn Sulayman from 'Abdullah. [Sahih. And it was mentioned in the one before it.]"
"2506","(2506) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Saffar narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman al-Hakim ibn Nafi' narrated to us; he said: Abu Bishr Shu'bayb ibn Dinar informed me from Abu Hamzah, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn 'Ubaydillah ibn Shihab al-Zuhri; he said: Salim ibn 'Abdillah informed me from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): when he commenced the takbir for the prayer"," he raised his hands when he said takbir"," until he placed them level with his shoulders. Then when he said takbir for ruku'"," he did likewise. Then when he said: 'Sami' Allahu liman hamidah","' he did likewise"," and he said: 'Rabbana wa lak al-hamd.' And he did not do that when he prostrated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Yaman. [Sahih. And it was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2507","(2507) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk and Ibn Milḥān narrated: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated: al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood for prayer"," he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders"," then he pronounced the takbīr. When he intended to bow"," he did likewise. When he raised his head from rukūʿ"," he did likewise. And he did not do so when he raised his head from sujūd.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Rāfiʿ from Ḥujayn from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ; it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2508","(2508) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Ibn Jurayj narrated: Ibn Shihāb narrated to me, and he mentioned it with the same wording.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ; it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"
"2509","(2509) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Samnānī narrated: Naṣr ibn ʿAlī al-Jahḍamī informed me: ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from Nāʿim, from Ibn ʿUmar, that: \When he entered into prayer"," he raised his hands; and when he bowed; and after he raised his head from rukūʿ; and when he stood up from the two rakʿahs"," he raised his hands.\"" And he attributed that to the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAyāsh from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā. [Ṣaḥīḥ; it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2510","(2510) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated: ʿAffān narrated: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated: Ayyūb narrated: Nāʿim narrated from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered into prayer"," he raised his hands level with his shoulders; and when he bowed; and when he raised his head from rukūʿ.\""\n\nAnd likewise Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated it from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah and Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī from Nāʿim"," as a musnad narration. And al-Bukhārī cited all of that as supporting evidence. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī narrated it (739).]"""
"2511","(2511) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Razīn al-Sulamī, Abū al-ʿAbbās, narrated: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah and Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from Nāʿim, from Ibn ʿUmar, that: \He used to raise his hands when he commenced the prayer"," and when he bowed"," and when he stood upright from his rukūʿ"," level with his shoulders. And he said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do that.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2512","(2512) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb al-Dīnawarī and Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm both narrated: Abū Bashr Isḥāq ibn Shāhin narrated — and al-Dīnawarī said: Isḥāq ibn Abī ʿImrān al-Wāsiṭī — Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, who said: \I saw Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith: when he prayed"," he pronounced the takbīr and raised his hands; and when he intended to bow"," he raised his hands; and when he raised his head from rukūʿ"," he raised his hands. And he narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray in this manner.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Shāhin"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī narrated it (737).]"""
"2513","(2513) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Burhān, Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān, and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdad informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated: Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith al-Hujaymī al-Baṣrī narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, who said: Qatādah informed us from Naṣr ibn ʿĀṣim, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith, that he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) raising his hands in his prayer when he bowed and when he raised his head from rukūʿ"," until he brought them in line with the upper parts of his ears.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2514","(2514) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated: Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated: Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, and he mentioned it with its chain and its meaning, and added: \He raised the hands when he pronounced the takbīr.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā.\n\nAnd Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj"," Abū ʿAwānah"," Hammām ibn Yaḥyā"," Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"," and others narrated it from Qatādah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2515","(2515) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated: ʿAffān narrated: Hammām narrated: Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah narrated from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil, from ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil and a mawlā of theirs, that both of them narrated to him from his father Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, that: \He saw the Prophet (ﷺ) when he entered into prayer"," he pronounced the takbīr\"" — Abū ʿUthmān said: \""And Hammām described: 'in the direction of his ears","' meaning he raised the hands — then he wrapped himself in his garment"," then he placed his right hand upon his left hand. When he intended to bow"," he brought his hands out from the garment and raised them"," then pronounced the takbīr. When he said 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' he raised his hands. When he prostrated"," he prostrated between his two palms.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from ʿAffān. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Muslim narrated it (826).]"""
"2516","(2516) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated: Musaddad narrated: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid, meaning Ibn Ziyād, narrated: ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb narrated from his father, from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr al-Ḥaḍramī, who said: \I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'I shall certainly observe how he prays.' He faced the qiblah"," pronounced the takbīr"," and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. Then he took his left hand with his right hand. When he intended to bow"," he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. When he bowed"," he placed his hands upon his knees. When he intended to raise his head"," he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. When he prostrated"," he placed his hands on that part of his face. When he sat"," he spread out his left foot"," placed his left hand upon his left thigh"," and placed the edge of his right elbow upon his right thigh. He clasped two fingers and formed a ring with one"," and he pointed with the index finger.\""\n\nAnd Sufyān al-Thawrī"," Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj"," Abū ʿAwānah"," Ghaylān ibn Jāmiʿ"," Abū al-Aḥwaṣ"," Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah"," Ibn ʿUyaynah"," and a group narrated it from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb"," except that some of them said \""opposite his ears\"" instead. And Ibn ʿUyaynah agreed with ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād regarding the shoulders. [Ṣaḥīḥ; it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2517","(2417) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, among the last [narrators], they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān informed us from Ayyūb, from Qatādah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ), Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them) used to begin the recitation with {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi l-ʿālamīn}.\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh and Abū Saʿīd added in their narration: al-Shāfiʿī said, meaning they would commence with the recitation of Umm al-Qur'ān before what they recited after it. And Allah knows best. And he did not mean that they omitted {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm}."
"2518","(2418) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik informed us from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl from Anas ibn Mālik, that he said: I prayed behind Abū Bakr, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them), and none of them used to recite {bismillāhi al-raḥmāni al-raḥīm} when they commenced the prayer. Thus narrated Mālik, and the companions of Ḥumayd differed with him in its wording."
"2519","(2519) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār al-Zāhid narrated to us, dictating from the original of his book; he said: Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī said: I prayed behind Abū al-Nuʿmān Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl, and he raised his hands when he commenced the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing. So I asked him about that, and he said: I prayed behind Ḥammād ibn Zayd, and he raised his hands when he commenced the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing. So I asked him about that, and he said: I prayed behind Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, and he would raise his hands when he commenced the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing. So I asked him, and he said: I saw ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ raising his hands when he commenced the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing. So I asked him, and he said: I prayed behind ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, and he would raise his hands when he commenced the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing. So I asked him, and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr said: I prayed behind Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him), and he would raise his hands when he commenced the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing. And Abū Bakr said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he would raise his hands when he commenced the prayer, and when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing. Its narrators are trustworthy."
"2520","(2520) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; the Imam Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn ʿAbdillāh Abū Jaʿfar al-Kīlānī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Salamah ibn Shabīb narrated to us; he said: I heard ʿAbd al-Razzāq say: The people of Makkah learned the prayer from Ibn Jurayj, and Ibn Jurayj learned it from ʿAṭāʾ, and ʿAṭāʾ learned it from Ibn al-Zubayr, and Ibn al-Zubayr learned it from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him), and Abū Bakr learned it from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nSalamah said: and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, and added in it: and the Prophet (ﷺ) learned it from Jibrīl, and Jibrīl (peace be upon him) learned it from Allah, the Blessed and Most High. ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Ibn Jurayj used to raise his hands."
"2521","(2521) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī al-Asadiyyān in Hamadhān narrated to us; they said: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dīzīl al-Hamadhānī narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us; al-Ḥakam narrated to us; he said: I saw Ṭāwūs raise his hands to the level of his shoulders at the time of the takbīr, and at the time of bowing, and at the time of raising his head from bowing. So I asked a man among his companions, and he said: He relates it from Ibn ʿUmar, from ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Both ḥadīths are preserved from Ibn ʿUmar, from ʿUmar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), and from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet (ﷺ), for Ibn ʿUmar saw the Prophet (ﷺ) do it and saw his father do it, and he narrated it from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"2522","(2522) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to us; Ibn Abī al-Zinād informed me from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Faḍl al-Hāshimī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): that when he stood for the obligatory prayer, he would say the takbīr and raise his hands to the level of his shoulders, and he would do the same when he completed his recitation and intended to bow, and he would do it when he raised his head from bowing. And he would not raise his hands in any part of his prayer while he was seated. And when he stood up from the two prostrations, he would raise his hands likewise and say the takbīr. And we have narrated this ḥadīth from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī, Abū Hurayrah, and Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"2523","(2523) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Mūsā al-Bukhārī in Naysābūr narrated to us; Maḥmūd ibn Isḥāq ibn Maḥmūd al-Bukhārī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: And we have narrated from seventeen persons among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) that they used to raise their hands at the time of bowing. Among them were: Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī, Abū Usayd al-Sāʿidī al-Badrī, Muḥammad ibn Muslimah al-Badrī, Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib al-Hāshimī, Anas ibn Mālik the servant of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), Abū Hurayrah al-Dawsī, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām al-Qurashī, Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr al-Ḥaḍramī, Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith, Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, and Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī al-Anṣārī (may Allah the Most High be pleased with them).\n\nThe Shaykh said: And we have narrated it from these, and from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī, ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī, and ʿAbdullāh ibn Jābir al-Bayāḍī (may Allah be pleased with them all)."
"2524","(2524) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Minhāl narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated to us from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to raise their hands when they bowed and when they raised their heads from bowing, as if their hands were fans."
"2525","(2525) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Akram narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān informed us from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr: that he was asked about raising the hands in prayer, and he said: It is something by which a man adorns his prayer. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to raise their hands at the opening, and at the time of bowing, and when they raised their heads."
"2526","(2526) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Mūsā al-Bukhārī narrated to us; Maḥmūd ibn Isḥāq al-Bukhārī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl said: And it is narrated from a number of the people of Makkah, the people of the Ḥijāz, the people of Iraq, al-Shām, al-Baṣrah, and al-Yemen that they used to raise their hands at the time of bowing and at the time of raising the head from it. Among them were: Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, Mujāhid, al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, al-Nuʿmān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh, al-Ḥasan, Ibn Sīrīn, Ṭāwūs, Makḥūl, ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, Nāfiʿ, ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim, Qays ibn Saʿd, and others—a large number.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And we have narrated it from Abū Qilābah, Abū al-Zubayr, then from Mālik ibn Anas, al-Awzāʿī, al-Layth ibn Saʿd, Ibn ʿUyaynah, then from al-Shāfiʿī, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī, and a large number of the people of āthār in the various cities—may Allah the Most High have mercy upon them."
"2527","(2527) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, from dictation: Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān al-Jallāb in Hamadhān narrated to us: Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Rāzī narrated to us: Wahb ibn Abī Marḥūm narrated to us: Isrāʾīl ibn Ḥātim narrated to us, from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān, from al-Aṣbgh ibn Nubātah, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālli رضي الله عنه, who said: When this āyah was revealed upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — {Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar. So pray to your Lord and sacrifice} — the Prophet ﷺ said to Jibrīl: \What is this sacrifice (naḥīrah) that my Lord"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has commanded me with?\"" He said: \""It is not a sacrifice (of an animal); rather"," He commands you that when you commence the prayer"," you raise your hands when you say the takbīr"," and when you bow (rukūʿ)"," and when you raise your head from rukūʿ. For that is our prayer and the prayer of the angels who are in the seven heavens.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""The raising of the hands is from the humility (istikānah) about which Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," said: {And they were not humble before their Lord"," nor did they implore (Him)}.\""\n\nAnd this has been narrated; however"," reliance is upon what has passed. And with Allah is the granting of success.\n\n[Very weak. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān in al-Majrūḥīn 1/177/112]"""
"2528","(2528) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — when he commenced the prayer, he raised his hands. Sufyān said: Then I came to al-Kūfah and met Yazīd, and I heard him narrating this, and he added in it: \Then he does not repeat it (thumma lā yaʿūd).\"" So I thought that they had coached him (laqqanūh). Sufyān said: Thus I heard Yazīd narrating it"," and then later I heard him narrating it thus"," adding in it: \""Then he does not repeat it (thumma lā yaʿūd).\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"""
"2529","(2529) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdawws informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us. He said: I asked Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal about this ḥadīth, and he said: This ḥadīth is not authentic from him (the Prophet ﷺ).\n\nHe said: And I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn weakening (yuḍaʿʿifu) Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād.\n\nAbū Saʿīd al-Dārimī said: Among that which confirms the statement of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah — that they coached him this word — is that Sufyān al-Thawrī, Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah, Hushaym, and others from the people of knowledge did not narrate it (i.e., the addition). Rather, it was only narrated by those who heard from him later in his life.\n\nThe Shaykh"
"2530","(2530) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us. They both said: Ibrāhīm ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated to us in Makkah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ — when he commenced the prayer, he raised his hands; and when he intended to bow (rukūʿ); and when he raised his head from rukūʿ. Sufyān said: Then when I came to al-Kūfah, I heard him saying: \He raises his hands when he commences the prayer"," then he does not repeat it (thumma lā yaʿūd).\"" So I thought that they had coached him.\n\nAnd similarly ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Haytham al-Dayrāqūlī narrated it from Ibrāhīm ibn Bashshār.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And this ḥadīth has been narrated by Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from his brother ʿĪsā"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," from al-Barāʾ"," and he said in it: \""Then he does not repeat it (thumma lā yaʿūd).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," from al-Ḥakam"," from Ibn Abī Laylā; and it has been narrated from him"," from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād"," from Ibn Abī Laylā.\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā — his ḥadīth is not used as a proof (lā yuḥtajju biḥadīthih). He is in a worse condition (aswaʾu ḥālan) in the view of the people of ḥadīth knowledge than Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdawws informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us"," and he mentioned a section on the weakening of the ḥadīth of Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād"," then he said: And no one narrated this from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā who is stronger than Yazīd.\n\n[Sound (ṣaḥīḥ)"," except for his statement \""then he does not repeat it (thumma lā yaʿūd).\"" The discussion on it has been addressed recently.]"""
"2531","(2531) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Aḥmasī narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Āṣim — meaning Ibn Kulayb — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad, from ʿAlqamah, who said: ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — said: \I will most certainly pray with you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" So he prayed"," and he did not raise his hands except once.\n\n[Weak (ḍaʿīf). Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 257]"""
"2532","(2532) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Ibn Idrīs narrated to us, from Āṣim ibn Kulayb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad, from ʿAlqamah, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the prayer.\"" So he said the takbīr and raised his hands. Then when he bowed (rukūʿ)"," he clasped his hands between his knees. He said: This reached Saʿd"," and he said: \""My brother has spoken the truth. We used to do this"," then we were commanded with this\"" — meaning holding (imsāk) upon the two knees.\n\nThe Shaykh said: If the ḥadīth is as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Idrīs narrated it"," then it may be that he (the Prophet ﷺ) did return to raising them (the hands) but he (Ibn Masʿūd) did not mention it. And if it is as al-Thawrī narrated it"," then in the ḥadīth of Ibn Idrīs there is an indication that that was in the early period of Islam"," just as clasping (tadbīq) was in the early period of Islam. Then thereafter the sunnahs were established"," and the legislated rulings were introduced — whoever memorized them memorized them"," and whoever conveyed them conveyed them"," and it became obligatory to adhere to them. And with Allah is the granting of success.\n\n[Sound (ṣaḥīḥ). Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah 595]"""
"2533","(2533) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Jarrāḥī in Marw narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Sāsawayh narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Sukkariyy narrated to us: Wahb ibn Zamʿah informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿAbd al-Malik said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak say: \The ḥadīth of Ibn Masʿūd — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands the first time and then did not repeat it — is not established (lam yathbut) with me. And the ḥadīth of raising the hands is established with me — the one narrated by ʿUbayd Allāh"," Mālik"," Maʿmar"," and Ibn Abī Ḥafṣah"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Sālim"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\"" He said: \""And I consider it broad (and ample).\"" Then ʿAbd Allāh said: \""It is as though I am looking at the Prophet ﷺ raising his hands in the prayer"," due to the abundance of the aḥādīth and the excellence of the chains of narration.\""\n\n[Sound (ṣaḥīḥ). See 2530]"""
"2534","(2534) The Shaykh said: And Muḥammad ibn Jābir narrated it, from Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd رضي الله عنه, who said: \I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ"," Abū Bakr"," and ʿUmar"," and they did not raise their hands except at the opening (iftitāḥ) of the prayer.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Makhlad al-Ḍarīr narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Abī Isrāʾīl narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jābir narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\n(j) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us and said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Muḥammad ibn Jābir is the one who narrated it exclusively (tafarradu bih) — and he was weak (ḍaʿīf) — from Ḥammād"," from Ibrāhīm. And other than Ḥammād narrate it from Ibrāhīm as a mursal narration from ʿAbd Allāh"," from his own action"," not raised (marfūʿ) to the Prophet ﷺ — and that is the correct view (al-ṣawāb).\n\nThe Shaykh said: And similarly Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it"," from Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān"," from Ibrāhīm"," from Ibn Masʿūd"," as a mursal"," mawqūf narration.\n\nAnd Abū Bakr al-Nahshalī narrated from Āṣim ibn Kulayb"," from his father"," from ʿAlī رضي الله"""
"2535","(2535) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him: Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnzī informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Abū Bakr al-Nahshalī narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nʿUthmān al-Dārimī said: So this has been narrated through this weak (wāhī) chain from ʿAlī.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmuz al-Aʿraj narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī: that he saw the Prophet ﷺ raising them (his hands) at the time of rukūʿ and after he raised his head from rukūʿ.\n\nIt is not to be supposed about ʿAlī"
"2536","(2536) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr informed us: Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Zāʾidah narrated to us, from Ḥuṣayn.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl and ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us and said: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Jarīr narrated to us, from Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: \We entered upon Ibrāhīm"," and ʿAmr ibn Murrah narrated to him. He said: 'We prayed in the Mosque of the Ḥaḍramiyyīn"," and ʿAlqamah ibn Wāʾil narrated to me from his father: that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raise his hands when he commenced the prayer"," and when he bowed (rukūʿ).'\"" Ibrāhīm said: \""I do not think that his father saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except on that one day"," so he memorized that"," and ʿAbd Allāh did not memorize it from him.\"" Then Ibrāhīm said: \""The raising of the hands is only at the opening (iftitāḥ) of the prayer.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Jarīr.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh said: This is a flaw (ʿillah) that does not reach the level of its hearing (lā taswī samʿah)"," because the raising of the hands has been authenticated from the Prophet ﷺ"," then from the Rightly Guided Caliphs"," then from the Companions and the Successors. And the forgetting of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd regarding the raising of the hands does not necessitate that these Companions"""
"2537","(2537) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: I asked al-Shāfiʿī: \What is the meaning of raising the hands at the time of rukūʿ?\"" He said: \""It carries the same meaning as raising them at the opening of the prayer — it is an act of veneration of Allah"," a followed Sunnah"," through which the reward of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," is hoped for — and it is like the raising of the hands at al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah and other such occasions.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2538","(2538) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥalīm al-Ṣāʾigh in Marw informed us; Abū al-Muwajjih informed me; Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Khaṭṭāb al-Sulamī — and he was a righteous man — informed me; ʿAlī ibn Yūnus informed us; Wakīʿ said: I prayed in the mosque of Kūfah, and there was Abū Ḥanīfah standing in prayer, and Ibn al-Mubārak beside him praying. Whenever ʿAbd Allāh went into rukūʿ and whenever he raised his head, he raised his hands, whereas Abū Ḥanīfah did not raise them. When they finished the prayer, Abū Ḥanīfah said to ʿAbd Allāh: \O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," I see you frequently raising your hands — do you wish to fly?\"" ʿAbd Allāh replied: \""O Abū Ḥanīfah"," I saw you raise your hands when you opened the prayer — did you wish to fly?\"" Abū Ḥanīfah fell silent. Wakīʿ said: \""I have never seen a more prompt reply than the reply of ʿAbd Allāh to Abū Ḥanīfah.\"" [Very weak]"""
"2539","(2539) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rumayḥ informed us; Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Marwazī in Marw informed us; Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd al-Ṭabarī informed us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Shādhakūnī said: I heard Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah say: \Al-Awzāʿī and al-Thawrī met in Minā. Al-Awzāʿī said to al-Thawrī: 'Why do you not raise your hands when going into rukūʿ and when raising from it?' Al-Thawrī said: 'Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād narrated to us.' Al-Awzāʿī said: 'Shall I narrate to you from al-Zuhrī"," from Sālim"," from his father"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," and you oppose me with Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād — when Yazīd is a weak narrator whose hadith contradicts the Sunnah?'\"" He said: \""The face of Sufyān al-Thawrī turned red.\"" Al-Awzāʿī said: \""It seems you disliked what I said?\"" Al-Thawrī said: \""Yes.\"" Al-Awzāʿī said: \""Come"," let us go to the place of standing and invoke curses upon one another — [to see] which of us is upon the truth.\"" He said: \""Al-Thawrī smiled when he saw that al-Awzāʿī had become heated.\"" [Mawḍūʿ]"""
"2540","(2540) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Barzaʿī in Bukhārā informed us; Abū Manṣūr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ḥamdawayh al-Ishtaykhinī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd al-Ṭabarī informed us, and he mentioned the hadith with the same meaning as the narration of al-Marwazī. [Mawḍūʿ]"
"2541","(2541) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us; Abū Muʿāwiyah informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ibrāhīm, from al-Aswad and ʿAlqamah, who said: \We came to ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — in his house.\"" He said: \""Did these people pray behind you?\"" We said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Stand and pray.\"" He did not command us to give the adhān or the iqāmah. We went to stand behind him"," and he took our hands and placed one of us on his right and the other on his left. When we went into rukūʿ"," we placed our hands on our knees. He struck our hands and clasped his palms together"," then placed them between his thighs. When we finished the prayer"," he said: 'There will be over you rulers who will delay the prayer from its prescribed times and squeeze it to the last moment — meaning the end of the time. When you see them doing that"," pray the prayer at its proper time"," and make your prayer with them a supererogatory prayer. If you are three"," pray together"," and if you are more than that"," let one of you lead. When one of you goes into rukūʿ"," let him spread his forearms on his thighs.' Then he clasped his palms together and showed us. He said: 'It is as though I am looking at the fingers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spread apart.'\"" Abū Muʿāwiyah said: \""This practice has been abandoned.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 722]"""
"2542","(2542) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rumayḥ informed us; Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Marwazī in Marw informed us; Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd al-Ṭabarī informed us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Shādhakūnī said: I heard Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah say: \Al-Awzāʿī and al-Thawrī met in Minā…\"" and he mentioned the hadith with the same meaning as the narration of al-Marwazī. [Mawḍūʿ]"""
"2543","(2543) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Ibn al-Muṣaffā al-Ḥimṣī informed us; Baqiyyah informed us; al-Zubaydī informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer"," he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders"," then he pronounced the takbīr while they were in that position and went into rukūʿ. Then when he intended to raise his back"," he raised them until they were level with his shoulders"," then he said: 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah.' He did not raise his hands in sujūd"," and he raised them with every takbīr he pronounced before rukūʿ until his prayer was completed.\"" Al-Zubaydī — his name is Muḥammad ibn al-Walīd ibn ʿĀmir. [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 722]"""
"2544","(2544) Abū Saʿd ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī ʿUthmān al-Zāhid informed us; Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us; Abū ʿAwanah informed us, from Abū Yaʿfūr, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, who said: \I prayed beside Saʿd. I clasped my hands and placed them between my knees. He struck my hands.\"" He said: \""Then I prayed another time beside him. I clasped my hands and placed them between my knees.\"" He said: \""He struck my hands and said: 'O my son"," we used to do this"," but we were commanded to place the palms on the knees.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others"," and he added: \""We were prohibited from this and were commanded to place the palms on the knees.\"" He also narrated it from the hadith of al-Zubayr ibn ʿAdī from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd. [Ṣaḥīḥ; as previously mentioned]"""
"2545","(2545) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī informed us; Abū Usāmah informed us, from Ismāʿīl — meaning Ibn Abī Khālid — from al-Zubayr ibn ʿAdī, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, who said: \I was praying beside my father. When I went into rukūʿ"," I did such\"" — and he clasped his hands between his legs. \""When he finished"," he said: 'We used to do this"," then we were commanded to raise them to the knees.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; as previously mentioned]"""
"2546","(2546) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Miʿsar informed us, from Abī Ḥuṣayn, from Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, who said: \ʿUmar came forward and said: 'O people"," the knees have been prescribed for you as the Sunnah"," so hold fast to the knees.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated by al-Ṭayālisī]"""
"2547","(2547) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalīyy narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Khālid narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated from Abī Ḥaṣīn, from Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, who said: When we used to bow (in rukūʿ), we would place our hands between our thighs. Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Indeed, from the Sunnah is to grasp the knees. [Ḥasan]"
"2548","(2548) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Khaythamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Sabrah al-Juʿfī, who said: I came to al-Madīnah and I would clasp my hands between my thighs as the companions of ʿAbd Allāh used to do when bowing. A man said: \O ʿAbd Allāh"," what compels you to do this?\"" I said: \""ʿAbd Allāh used to do it","\"" and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do it. He said: \""ʿAbd Allāh spoke the truth"," but the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) may have done something for a time"," then Allah revealed to him the other command. So look at what the Muslims have agreed upon and do that.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""When he (ʿAbd Allāh) came again"," he would not clasp (his hands).\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: That upon which the matter has settled is found in the ḥadīth of Abī Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī and others regarding the description of the Prophet's (ﷺ) rukūʿ. In this is evidence that the people of al-Madīnah are more knowledgeable regarding the abrogating (nāsikh) and the abrogated (mansūkh) than the people of al-Kūfah. And through Allah is success. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2549","(2549) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from Ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who said: He was sitting with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: We mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī said: \I am the most knowledgeable among you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I saw him: when he said the takbīr"," he placed his hands level with his shoulders; and when he bowed in rukūʿ"," he placed his hands firmly upon his knees"," then he bent his back.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 828]"""
"2550","(2550) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-ʿĀmirī, who said: I was in a gathering of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and they discussed his prayer. Abū Ḥumayd said — and he mentioned part of this ḥadīth and said: \When he bowed in rukūʿ"," he placed his palms upon his knees and spread his fingers apart"," then he bent his back without raising his head excessively or letting his cheek hang down.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 626]"""
"2551","(2551) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAmr informed me: Fulayḥ narrated to me: ʿAbbās ibn Sahl narrated, saying: Abū Ḥumayd, Abū Usayd, Sahl ibn Saʿd, and Muḥammad ibn Muslimah gathered and mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Abū Ḥumayd said: \I am the most knowledgeable among you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth and said: \""Then he bowed in rukūʿ and placed his hands upon his knees as though he were grasping them"," and he stretched his arms out"," keeping them away from his sides.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 730]"""
"2552","(2552) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abī al-Jawzāʾ, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would commence the prayer with the takbīr. She mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it: \When he bowed in rukūʿ"," he would not raise his head nor lower it"," but rather he would keep it between the two.\"" And she mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 498]"""
"2553","(2553) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Abī Sufyān al-Saʿdī, from Abī Naḍrah, from Abī Saʿīd — I think he attributed it (to the Prophet, ﷺ); Abū Muʿāwiyah was uncertain — who said: \The key of prayer is purification; its prohibition (iḥrām) is the takbīr; and its release (taḥlīl) is the taslīm. There is a salām after every two rakʿahs. There is no prayer in which the Opening of the Book (Sūrat al-Fātiḥah) is not recited along with another passage"," whether obligatory or supererogatory. When one of you bows in rukūʿ"," let him not lower himself like the lowering of a donkey; rather"," let him keep his back straight. And when he prostrates"," let him extend his back"," for the human being prostrates upon seven bones: his forehead"," his two hands"," his two knees"," and the tops of his two feet. And when he sits"," let him erect his right leg and let him lay down his left leg.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2554","(2554) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Jarīr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Saʿd ibn ʿUbaydah, from al-Mustawrid ibn al-Aḥnaf, from Ṣilah, from Ḥudhayfah, who said: I prayed one night with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He opened with Sūrat al-Baqarah and I thought: \Perhaps he will recite one hundred verses and then bow.\"" But he continued. I thought: \""Perhaps he will complete it and then bow.\"" But he continued until he recited Sūrat al-Nisāʾ and Āl ʿImrān. Then he bowed in rukūʿ for approximately as long as his standing"," saying: \""Subḥāna Rabbiya al-ʿAẓīm"," Subḥāna Rabbiya al-ʿAẓīm\"" (Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent"," Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent). Then he raised his head and said: \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah"," Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd\"" (Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah"," to You is all praise). He prolonged the standing. Then he prostrated and prolonged the prostration"," saying in his prostration: \""Subḥāna Rabbiya al-Aʿlā\"" (Glory be to my Lord the Most High). He would not pass by a verse containing a warning or glorification except that he would make mention of Him.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 772]"""
"2555","(2555) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Ayyūb al-Ghāfiqī narrated from his paternal uncle, Iyās ibn ʿĀmir al-Ghāfiqī, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When {So glorify the name of your Lord the Magnificent} (al-Wāqiʿah: 74) was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to us: \Make it part of your rukūʿ.\"" And when {Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High} (al-Aʿlā: 1) was revealed"," he said to us: \""Make it part of your sujūd.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 869]"""
"2556","(2556) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us: al-Layth, meaning Ibn Saʿd, narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā — or Mūsā ibn Ayyūb — from a man of his people, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, with the same meaning. He added and said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he bowed in rukūʿ, would say: \Subḥāna Rabbiya al-ʿAẓīm wa bi-ḥamdih\"" (Glory be to my Lord the Magnificent and by His praise) three times; and when he prostrated"," he would say: \""Subḥāna Rabbiya al-Aʿlā wa bi-ḥamdih\"" (Glory be to my Lord the Most High and by His praise) three times. Abū Dāwūd said: \""This addition — we fear it may not be preserved.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ"," without the words \""wa bi-ḥamdih\"" three times]"""
"2557","(2557) Abū ʿAlī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Musaddad informed us that Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Saʿīd al-Jurayrī informed us from al-Saʿdī, from his father or his uncle, who said: \I observed the Prophet ﷺ during his prayer"," and he would remain in his rukūʿ and sujūd for as long as it would take to say 'Subḥān Allāhi wa bi-ḥamdihi' three times.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 885]"""
"2558","(2558) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb informed us from Isḥāq ibn Yazīd, from ʿAwn, who attributed it to ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you performs rukūʿ and says 'Subḥāna Rabbiya al-ʿAẓīm' three times"," his rukūʿ is complete"," and that is its minimum. And when he performs sajdah and says 'Subḥāna Rabbiya al-Aʿlā'—meaning three times—his sujūd is complete"," and that is its minimum.\"" This is a mursal narration. ʿAwn ibn ʿAbd Allāh did not meet ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 869]"""
"2559","(2559) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us by dictation that Abū al-Qāsim Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Mūsawī in Makkah—may Allah the Most High protect it—informed us that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us that ʿUbayy ibn Marḥum al-ʿAṭṭār informed us that Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl informed us that Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad informed us from his father, who said: \The woodcutters came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we are always travelling; how should we perform the prayer?' He ﷺ said: 'Say three tasbīḥs in rukūʿ and three tasbīḥs in sujūd.'\"" This is also a mursal narration. [Weak. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Musnad 1/47]"""
"2560","(2560) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Shabīb ibn al-Fāmī and Abū Naṣr Manṣūr ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Muqriʾ, among others, said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī informed us from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Abī al-Ḍuḥā, from Masrūq, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would frequently say in his rukūʿ: 'Subḥānaka wa bi-ḥamdika"," Allāhumma ighfir lī' (Glory be to You"," and praise be to You; O Allah"," forgive me).' He was acting upon the Qurʾān.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 817]"""
"2561","(2561) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me that Ibn Khallād informed us that Yaḥyā informed us that Sufyān informed us that Manṣūr informed us, and he mentioned it and said: \'Subḥānaka Rabbanā wa bi-ḥamdika"," Allāhumma ighfir lī' (Glory be to You"," our Lord"," and praise be to You; O Allah"," forgive me).' He was acting upon the Qurʾān.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to in the preceding narration]"""
"2562","(2562) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Dallawayh al-Daqqāq informed us that Abū al-Azhar al-Sulayṭī informed us that Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir informed us that Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah informed us from Qatādah, from Muṭarrif ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from ʿĀʾishah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say in his rukūʿ and sujūd: \Subbūḥun Quddūsun Rabb al-malāʾikati wa al-rūḥ (Glorious"," Most Holy"," Lord of the angels and the Spirit).\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī ʿArūbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 487]"""
"2563","(2563) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that ʤmar ibn Ḥafṣ informed us that ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī informed us that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah informed us that al-Mājishūn ibn Abī Salamah informed us from al-Aʿraj, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When he commenced the prayer\""—and he mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it he said: \""When he performed rukūʿ"," he would say: 'Allāhumma laka rakaʿtu"," wa bika āmantu"," wa laka aslamtu"," khashaʿa laka samʿī wa baṣarī wa ʿiẓāmī'\""—I think he said—\""wa mukhkhī wa ʿaṣabī (O Allah"," to You I bowed"," in You I believed"," and to You I submitted; my hearing"," my sight"," my bones"," my marrow"," and my nerves are humbled before You).'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from two routes from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 487]"""
"2564","(2564) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Anmāṭī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Dawraqī informed us that Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad informed us from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Faḍl, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from Ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he commenced the obligatory prayer—and he mentioned the ḥadīth, and in it he said: \When he performed rukūʿ"," he would say: 'Allāhumma laka rakaʿtu"," wa bika āmantu"," wa laka aslamtu"," anta Rabbī"," khashaʿa laka samʿī wa baṣarī wa mukhkhī wa ʿaẓmī"," wa mā istaqalla bihi qadamī lillāhi Rabb al-ʿālamīn (O Allah"," to You I bowed"," in You I believed"," and to You I submitted; You are my Lord; my hearing"," my sight"," my marrow"," my bones"," and whatever my foot carries are humbled before You"," the Lord of the worlds).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah 607]"""
"2565","(2565) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, and it was read to Ibn Wahb: Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥunayn informed me that his father informed him that he heard ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from reciting [the Qurʾān] while in rukūʿ or sujūd.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim 480]"""
"2566","(2566) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us that Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī and Hārūn ibn Mūsā said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us. I read to Mālik from Nāfiʿ, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥunayn, from his father, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing silk garments and garments dyed with saffron"," wearing gold rings"," and reciting [the Qurʾān] during rukūʿ.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\nLikewise"," it was narrated by Zayd ibn Aslam"," al-Walīd ibn Kathīr"," Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb"," Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAlqamah"," and Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār"," from Ibrāhīm"," from his father"," from ʿAlī. And it was narrated by al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān and Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān.\n\nIn one of the two narrations from Dāwūd ibn Qays"," it is from Ibrāhīm"," from his father"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from ʿAlī. And it was narrated by Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥunayn"," from ʿAlī. And it was narrated by Abū Bakr ibn Ḥafṣ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥunayn"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ 212]"""
"2567","(2567) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Suḥaym, the mawlā of the family of ʿAbbās, said: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿbad ibn ʿAbbās informed me, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) drew back the curtain while the people were standing in rows behind Abū Bakr, and he said: \There remains nothing of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream"," which a Muslim sees or which is shown to him. Verily"," I have been forbidden to recite while in rukūʿ or sujūd. As for the rukūʿ"," magnify the Lord therein"," and as for the sujūd"," strive in supplication therein"," for it is worthy that your supplications be answered.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr and others"," from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 479.]"""
"2568","(2568) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from al-Ḥasan, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \We used to perform tasbīḥ in rukūʿ and sujūd"," and to make supplication while standing and sitting.\""\n\nHe said: And Muʿādh narrated to us"," from al-Ashʿath"," from al-Ḥasan"," who said: Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh was asked about recitation in rukūʿ"," and he said: \""We used to make the rukūʿ [a time of] tasbīḥ.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"2569","(2569) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us: ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd and ʿUbayd Allāh al-Jushamī both said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated to me, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the mosque and mentioned the hadith concerning the man who did not perform the prayer well, until the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught him. Among what he taught him was: \Then go into rukūʿ until you are at rest in rukūʿ.\""\n\nExtracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥs. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was previously cited under number 2258.]"""
"2570","(2570) Abū Zakariyyā — Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā — informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Salām narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: al-Aʿmash narrated to us, from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr, from Abī Maʿmar, from Abī Masʿūd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A prayer is not valid in which a man does not straighten his back in rukūʿ and sujūd.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 265.]"""
"2571","(2571) Abū al-Qāsim — Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-ʿAlawī — and Abū al-Qāsim — ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Najjār al-Muqriʾ — in al-Kūfah, both from the original of their audition, said: Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Qāḍī — narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Qabīṣah narrated to us, from Sufyān, from al-Aʿmash, from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr, from Abī Maʿmar, from Abī Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The prayer of a man is not valid if he does not straighten his back therein in rukūʿ and sujūd.\""\n\nThis is a ṣaḥīḥ isnād. And likewise it was narrated by the generality of the companions of al-Aʿmash from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was previously cited in the one before it.]"""
"2572","(2572) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī informed us: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Sufyān, from Jābir, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \A prayer is not valid in which a man does not straighten his back therein in rukūʿ and sujūd.\""\n\nYaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr was alone in narrating it. [Munkar — the isnād.]"""
"2573","(2573) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs al-Ṭarāʾifī — informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: Ṣafwān ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Dimashqī narrated to us: al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us: Shaybah ibn al-Aḥnaf al-Awzāʿī narrated to us: Abū Salām — al-Aswad — narrated to us: Abū Ṣāliḥ al-Ashʿarī narrated to us, from Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-Ashʿarī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed with his Companions, then sat among a group of them. A man entered and stood to pray, but he would not perform rukūʿ properly and would peck in his sujūd, while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was looking at him. He said: \Do you see this one? If he were to die in this state"," he would die upon other than the religion of Muḥammad. He pecks in his prayer as the crow pecks at blood. The likeness of one who prays without performing rukūʿ properly and who pecks in his sujūd is like the hungry person who eats only one or two dates — what will they avail him? So perform your wuḍūʾ well. Woe to the heels from the Fire. And complete the rukūʿ and sujūd.\""\n\nAbū Ṣāliḥ said: I said to Abī ʿAbd Allāh al-Ashʿarī"," \""Who narrated this hadith to you?\"" He said: \""The commanders of the armies — Khālid ibn al-Walīd"," ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," Sharḥabīl ibn Ḥasanah"," and Yazīd ibn Abī Sufyān — all of them heard it from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Mājah"," 455.]"""
"2574","(2574) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb al-ʿAllāf narrated to us: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Jaʿfar — Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ — narrated to us: al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us: Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd narrated to me: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Sulaymān narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Abī ʿAttāb and Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When you come and we are in sujūd"," then prostrate"," and do not count it as anything [separate]. And whoever catches the rakʿah has caught the prayer.\""\n\nYaḥyā ibn Abī Sulaymān al-Madanī was alone in narrating it. And it has been narrated through another isnād"," weaker than that"," from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 893.]"""
"2575","(2575) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Ramlī, al-Qāsim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mahdī, and al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās said: ʿAmr ibn Sawwād narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥumayd informed me, from Qurrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever catches a rakʿah of the prayer has caught it before the imām straightens his back.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: This addition — \""before the imām straightens his back\"" — is stated by Yaḥyā ibn Ḥumayd"," and he is an Egyptian.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: I heard Ibn Ḥammād say that al-Bukhārī said: Yaḥyā ibn Ḥumayd"," from Qurrah"," from Ibn Shihāb — Ibn Wahb heard from him; he is an Egyptian who is not followed in his hadith.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: And al-Junaydī narrated to us: al-Bukhārī said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Sulaymān al-Madanī"," from al-Maqburī and Ibn Abī ʿAttāb"," is munkar al-ḥadīth.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And it has been narrated through a mursal isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ"," except for his statement \""before the imām straightens his back.\"" Al-Arwāʾ"," 496.]"""
"2576","(2576) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed me: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Rufayʿ, from a man, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \When you come and the imām is in rukūʿ"," then go into rukūʿ"," and if he is in sujūd"," then prostrate. And do not count the sujūd [as a rakʿah] if the rukūʿ was not performed with it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2577","(2577) Abu 'Abd Allah informed us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Farra' narrated to us; Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Mu'adh narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us; 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Makki narrated from a man from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever does not catch the rak'ah has not caught the prayer.\"" And it has been narrated on this topic from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. [Sahih. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2578","(2578) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī informed us; Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Faqīh informed us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; 'Ali ibn 'Asim narrated to us; Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated to us; from 'Ali ibn al-Aqmar; from Abū al-Ahwaz; from 'Abd Allah, i.e., Ibn Mas'ud, who said: \Whoever does not catch the imam in rukū' has not caught that rak'ah.\"" [Sahih. It has a witness in the one after it.]"""
"2579","(2579) And Abū 'Ali ibn Shādhān informed us in Baghdad; Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbās narrated to us; al-'Abbās ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Isrā'īl narrated to us; from Abū Isḥāq; from Abū al-Ahwaz and Hubayrah; from 'Abd Allah, who said: \Whoever does not catch the rak'ah should not count the prostration (as part of it).\"" [Sahih. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it as 2617.]"""
"2580","(2580) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Abū 'Āmir Mūsā ibn 'Āmir narrated to us; al-Walīd, i.e., ibn Muslim, narrated to us; Mālik and Ibn Jurayj informed me; from Nāfi'; from Ibn 'Umar, that he used to say: \Whoever catches the imam in rukū' and performs rukū' before the imam raises his head has indeed caught that rak'ah.\"" [Sahih. Like the narration of Mālik from Nāfi' from Ibn 'Umar.]"""
"2581","(2581) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Nāfi' that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar used to say: \If the rak'ah escapes you"," then the sajdah has escaped you.\"" [Sahih. Like the narration of Mālik from Nāfi' from Ibn 'Umar.]"""
"2582","(2582) He said: And Mālik narrated to us that it reached him that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar and Zayd ibn Thābit used to say: \Whoever catches the rak'ah before the imam raises his head has indeed caught the sajdah.\"" [Sahih. It is a narration from the balāghāt of Mālik.]"""
"2583","(2583) He said: And Mālik narrated to us that it reached him that Abū Hurayrah used to say: \Whoever catches the rak'ah has indeed caught the sajdah"," and whoever misses the recitation of Umm al-Qur'ān has indeed missed abundant good.\"" [Da'īf. It is from the balāghāt of Mālik.]"""
"2584","(2584) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us; Abū 'Umar narrated to us; Hammām narrated to us; Ziyād al-A'lam narrated to us; from al-Ḥasan; from Abū Bakrah: that he entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was in rukū', so he performed rukū' before reaching the row. The Prophet ﷺ then said: \May Allah increase your eagerness"," but do not repeat it.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismā'īl from Hammām. Al-Shāfi'ī said: His statement \""do not repeat it\"" resembles His statement \""do not come to prayer running.\"" That is—and Allah knows best—it is not upon you to perform rukū' until you reach your place in the row"," due to the hardship involved"," just as it is not upon you to run when you hear the iqāmah. [Sahih. Imam al-Bukhārī narrated it from Mūsā ibn Ismā'īl from Hammām. Mālik narrated it in al-Muwaṭṭā' as 285.]"""
"2585","(2585) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū 'Āmir narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us; Ibn Thawbān informed me; from his father; from Makḥūl; from Abū Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām: that Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq and Zayd ibn Thābit entered the mosque while the imam was in rukū', so they both performed rukū' and then crept forward while in rukū' until they joined the row. [Ḥasan.]"
"2586","(2586) Abū Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; it was read to Ibn Wahb: Yūnus ibn Yazīd and Ibn Abī Dhi'b informed you; from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf informed me: that he saw Zayd ibn Thābit enter the mosque while the imam was in rukū'. He walked until, when he was able to reach the row while in rukū', he said the takbīr, performed rukū', and then crept forward while in rukū' until he reached the row. [Sahih. Mālik narrated it in al-Muwaṭṭā' as 393.]"
"2587","(2587) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ informed us; Manṣūr narrated from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said:\n\nI went out with ʿAbdullāh—meaning Ibn Masʿūd—from his house toward the mosque. When we reached the middle of the mosque, the imām was in rukūʿ. ʿAbdullāh said the takbīr and went into rukūʿ, and I went into rukūʿ with him. Then we walked while in rukūʿ until we reached the row just as the people raised their heads. When the imām completed the prayer, I stood up, thinking that I had not caught the rakʿah. But ʿAbdullāh took my hand and made me sit, then said: \You have indeed caught it.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated in this regard from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr"," may Allah be pleased with them both. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2622]"""
"2588","(2588) ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said:\n\nIbn ʿUmar and Zayd ibn Thābit, when they came to the imām and he was in rukūʿ, would say one takbīr and enter rukūʿ with it. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"2589","(2589) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī informed us; Bishr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed us; from his father, from al-Zuhrī, who said:\n\nZayd ibn Thābit, when he entered the mosque and the people were in rukūʿ, would face the qiblah and say the takbīr, then go into rukūʿ, then walk on his toes while in rukūʿ until he reached the row.\n\nMuḥammad said: Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf al-Anṣārī informed me that from Zayd ibn Thābit.\n\nShuʿayb said: And Hishām ibn ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said: ʿUrwah used to do that.\n\nThe Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: And we have narrated in this chapter before it from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd. [Ṣaḥīh. It was previously cited under no. 2586]"
"2590","(2590) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū ʿĀmir informed us; al-Walīd—meaning ibn Muslim—said:\n\nI said to Mālik ibn Anas: \Someone informed me from Ḥammād"," from Abū Wāʾil"," from Ibn Masʿūd"," who said: 'If you find them in rukūʿ"," or sujūd"," or sitting"," say two takbīrs.'\"" Mālik said: \""As for in rukūʿ and sujūd"," that is the matter we know. But as for two takbīrs for sitting"," I do not know this.\"" I said: \""Does he say one takbīr with which he opens the prayer and sits with it?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: If this is authentic from Ibn Masʿūd"," it may be that he meant regarding sujūd—that he said the takbīr for the opening of the prayer"," and when he finished the opening"," the imām raised his head with a takbīr and sat"," so he would conform with him in his remembrances and actions. And similarly regarding sujūd"," he may have meant that the imām's takbīr for sujūd came after his opening of the prayer and his following him in it. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2591","(2591) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibrāhīm informed us; Abū ʿĀmir informed us; al-Walīd said: And Ismāʿīl informed me from ʿAmr ibn Muhājir, from ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, who said:\n\nIf you find them in rukūʿ, say two takbīrs: one takbīr for the opening of the prayer and one takbīr for the rukūʿ. And you have caught the rakʿah. [Ḥasan]"
"2592","(2592) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us; ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated from al-Mukhtār ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer one day. When he had completed the prayer, he turned his face toward us and said: \O people"," I am your imām"," so do not precede me in rukūʿ"," nor in sujūd"," nor in standing"," nor in the salām. For I see you in front of me and behind me.\"" Then he said: \""By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad"," if you had seen what I have seen"," you would have laughed little and wept much.\"" They said: \""What have you seen"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""I have seen Paradise and the Fire.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Muslim"," 426]"""
"2593","(2593) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl both said: Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us: \Do not hasten ahead of the imām in rukūʿ. When he says the takbīr"," say the takbīr. And when he says {ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā ḍ-ḍāllīn}"," say 'Āmīn.' For when his speech coincides with that of the angels"," forgiveness is granted to those in the mosque. And when he goes into rukūʿ"," go into rukūʿ. And when he says 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' say 'Rabbanā laka l-ḥamd.' And when he prostrates"," prostrate.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus from al-Aʿmash"," and the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd is more complete. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2596]"""
"2594","(2594) Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir ibn al-Bayyāḍ informed us in Baghdād; Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us; it was recited to al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad while I was listening; ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us in the year two hundred; Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The imām is only appointed to be followed. So when he says the takbīr"," say the takbīr. When he goes into rukūʿ"," go into rukūʿ. When he raises his head"," raise your heads. When he says 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' say altogether: 'Allāhumma Rabbanā laka l-ḥamd.' When he prostrates"," prostrate"," and do not prostrate before he prostrates. When he raises his head"," raise your heads"," and do not raise your heads before he raises his.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Dārawardī from Suhayl"," and the ḥadīth of ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim is more complete. [Ṣaḥīh. It was cited in the one before it]"""
"2595","(2595) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Khazzāz informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahm al-Anṭākī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham ibn Ḥammād informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahm al-Anṭākī Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us; Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī informed us that Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī informed him from Muḥārib ibn Dithār, who said:\n\nI heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd say from the minbar: \Al-Barāʾ ibn ʀāzib narrated to us: They used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he went into rukūʿ"," they went into rukūʿ. When he raised his head from rukūʿ and said 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' we remained standing until we saw him place his face on the ground"," then we would follow him.\"" In the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān: \""his forehead on the ground"," then we would prostrate.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sahm. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 690]"""
"2596","(2596) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Khaythamah narrated from Abū Isḥāq, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd informed me, who said: Al-Barāʾ—and he was no liar—informed me:\n\nThey used to pray behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he raised his head from rukūʿ, I did not see anyone bend his back until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his forehead on the ground. Then those behind him would fall down in prostration.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. And al-Bukhārī narrated it through other routes from Abū Isḥāq al-Sabīʿī. [Ṣaḥīh. It was cited in the one before it]"
"2597","(2597) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Sadūsī informed us; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī informed us; Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, from Ibn Muḥayrizz, that he heard Muʿāwiyah upon the minbar saying: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not precede me in rukūʿ (bowing) and sujūd (prostration)"," for I have grown old (advanced in age). So whatever I precede you in when I bow"," you will catch up with me when I raise (my head)"," and whatever I precede you in when I prostrate"," you will catch up with me when I raise (my head).\""\n\nAnd Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān likewise narrated it from Ibn ʿAjlān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (1549)]"""
"2598","(2598) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū al-Azhar al-Sulayṭī informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd informed us; my father narrated to me from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm narrated to me from Abū al-Zinād, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \O people"," I have grown old"," so do not precede me in rukūʿ and sujūd. Rather"," it is for me to precede you so that you may make up what you have missed.\""\n\nWe did not accurately preserve from our shaykhs whether it is badantu (with light dāl) or badantu (with shadda on the dāl). Abū ʿUbayd preferred badantu with shadda and with the dāl in the accusative"," meaning \""I have grown old.\"" And whoever said baduntu with the dāl in the nominative"," he intended thereby abundance of flesh. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Ḥibbān (2231)]"""
"2599","(2599) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah; al-Haytham ibn Sahl al-Tustarī informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ziyād narrated to us from Abū Hurayrah, who said: Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Does he not fear — the one who raises his head before the imām — that Allah may transform his head into the head of a donkey?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (691)]"""
"2600","(2600) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Ibrāhīm al-Jaddī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah, Ḥammād ibn Zayd, Shuʿbah, and Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah say: I heard Abū al-Qāsim (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \Does he not fear Allah — the one who raises his head while the imām is in prostration — that Allah may make his head the head of a donkey?\""\n\nShuʿbah said in his hadith: \""Or his form the form of a donkey.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Shuʿbah"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of the two Ḥammāds. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced in the preceding hadith]"""
"2601","(2601) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us by dictation; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl informed us from his book and from his memory; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to me from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad — meaning Ibn Sīrīn — from Abū Hurayrah, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Does one of you not fear"," when he raises his head from prostration before the imām"," that Allah may transform his head into the head of a donkey?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced in the preceding hadith]"""
"2602","(2602) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū ʿĀmir informed us; al-Walīd informed me; Ibn Lahīʿah narrated to me from Bukayr ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Ashajj, from al-Ḥārith ibn Makhlad, from his father, that he heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb say: When one of you raises his head and thinks that the imām has raised (his head), let him return his head (to prostration). Then when the imām raises his head, let him remain (in prostration) for the duration of what he had left out.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Shaʿbī and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that he should return and prostrate. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"2603","(2603) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us; al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām informed me that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when he stood for prayer, would say the takbīr when he stood, then he would say the takbīr when he bowed, then he would say: \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaḥ\"" (Allah hears the one who praises Him) when he raised his back from the rukūʿ. Then he would say while standing: \""Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd\"" (Our Lord"," to You is all praise). And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (789)]"""
"2604","(2604) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh and Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnazī informed us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated, having it read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbdillāh, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when he commenced the prayer, would raise his hands level with his shoulders, and when he raised (his head) from rukūʿ, he would raise them likewise and say: \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaḥ"," Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd\"" (Allah hears the one who praises Him; our Lord"," to You is all praise). And he would not do that in prostration.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (735)]"""
"2605","(2605) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydillāh al-ʿAlawī narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥakam al-Ḥibarī narrated to us; Abū Ghassān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us; al-Mājishūn narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when he raised his head, would say: \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaḥ. Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd milʾa al-samāwāti wa al-arḍi wa milʾa mā baynahumā wa milʾa mā shiʾta min shayʾin baʿd\"" (Allah hears the one who praises Him. Our Lord"," to You is all praise"," filling the heavens and the earth"," and filling what is between them"," and filling whatever else You will).\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Salamah. [Narrated by Muslim (771)]"""
"2606","(2606) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿUbayd ibn al-Ḥasan, from Ibn Abī Awfā, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when he raised his head from rukūʿ, would say: \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaḥ. Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd milʾa al-samāʾi wa milʾa al-arḍi wa milʾa mā shiʾta min shayʾin baʿd\"" (Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is all praise"," filling the heavens and the earth"," and filling whatever else You will).\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Abū Muʿāwiyah and Wakīʿ"," from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim (476)]"""
"2607","(2607) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq in Baghdād narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Khiraqī narrated to us, Abū Qilābah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us from Qays ibn Saʿd, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH (Allah hears the one who praises Him)","\"" would say"," \""Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd milʾa al-samāwāti wa milʾa al-arḍi wa milʾa mā shiʾta min shayʾin baʿd (Our Lord"," to You is praise filling the heavens and filling the earth"," and filling whatever You will beyond that).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 478.]"""
"2608","(2608) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us from Qays ibn Saʿd, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Prophet ﷺ, when he raised his head from rukūʿ, would say, \Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd milʾa al-samāwāti wa milʾa al-arḍi wa mā baynahumā wa milʾa mā shiʾta min shayʾin baʿd"," Ahl al-thanāʾi wa al-l-majd"," lā māniʿa li-mā aʿṭayta wa lā muʿṭiya li-mā manʿta wa lā yanfaʿu dhā al-jaddu minka al-jadd (O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise filling the heavens and the earth and what is between them"," and filling whatever You will beyond that. O Possessor of praise and glory! None can withhold what You give"," and none can give what You withhold"," and the might of any mighty one avails nothing before You).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced in the preceding hadith.]"""
"2609","(2609) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād narrated to us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Miṣrī narrated to us, Miqdām ibn Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us from ʿAṭiyyah ibn Qays, from Qazaʿah ibn Yaḥyā, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ, when he said, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH","\"" would say"," \""Allāhumma Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd milʾa al-samāwāti wa milʾa al-arḍi wa milʾa mā shiʾta min shayʾin baʿd"," Ahl al-thanāʾi wa al-l-majd"," aḥaqqu mā qāla al-ʿabd"," wa kullunā laka ʿabd"," lā māniʿa li-mā aʿṭayta wa lā yanfaʿu dhā al-jaddu minka al-jadd (O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise filling the heavens and the earth"," and filling whatever You will beyond that. O Possessor of praise and glory! The truest words a servant has spoken are these"," and we are all Your servants. None can withhold what You give"," and the might of any mighty one avails nothing before You).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dārimī from Marwān ibn Muḥammad al-Dimashqī from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," except that he said: \""When he raised his head from rukūʿ"," he would say"," 'Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd","'\"" and he added: \""wa lā muʿṭiya li-mā manʿta (and none can give what You withhold).\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me"," Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh narrated to us"," ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us"," ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dārimī narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 477.]"""
"2610","(2610) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah and Ibn Bukayr narrated to us from Mālik.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from Mālik, from Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Mujmir, from ʿAlī ibn Yaḥyā al-Zuraqī, from his father, from Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ al-Zuraqī, who said: One day we were praying behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from rukūʿ and said, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH","\"" a man behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd ḥamdan kathīran ṭayyiban mubārakan fīh (Our Lord"," to You is praise—abundant"," pure"," blessed praise).\"" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ completed the prayer"," he said"," \""Who was the one who spoke just now?\"" The man said"," \""It was me"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""I saw more than thirty angels racing to be the first to record it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī.\n\nMuʿādh ibn Rifāʿah narrated it from his father"," mentioning it after a sneeze that Rifāʿah sneezed"," without specifying its place"," and he added therein: \""kamā yuḥibbu Rabbanā wa yarḍā (as our Lord loves and is pleased with).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 799.]"""
"2611","(2611) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Baṣrī from his book narrated to me, Rifāʿah ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ al-Zuraqī, Abū Zayd, the imām of the mosque, narrated to me, saying: I heard Muʿādh ibn Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ al-Anṣārī narrating from his father Rifāʿah, that he prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Rifāʿah sneezed and said, \Al-ḥamdu lillāhi ḥamdan kathīran ṭayyiban mubārakan fīh"," mubārakan ʿalayhi kamā yuḥibbu Rabbanā wa yarḍā (All praise is for Allah—abundant"," pure"," blessed praise"," blessed upon it as our Lord loves and is pleased with).\"" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer"," he said"," \""Where is the one who spoke during the prayer?\"" Rifāʿah said: \""I wished I had lost a portion of my wealth and had not witnessed that prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," 'Where is the one who spoke during the prayer?'\"" So I said"," \""It was me"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said"," \""How did you say it?\"" He said: I said"," \""Al-ḥamdu lillāhi ḥamdan kathīran ṭayyiban mubārakan fīh kamā yuḥibbu Rabbanā wa yarḍā (All praise is for Allah—abundant"," pure"," blessed praise as our Lord loves and is pleased with).\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," more than thirty angels raced to be the first to ascend with it.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah"," who said: A young man from the Anṣār sneezed while in prayer and said such-and-such"," mentioning part of its meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced in the preceding hadith.]"""
"2612","(2612) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qarqūb al-Tammār in Hamadhān narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us, Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated to us from Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he said, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH","\"" would say"," \""Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd (O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise).\"" And when he bowed into rukūʿ"," he would say the takbīr"," and when he raised his head"," he would say the takbīr"," and when he stood up from the two prostrations"," he would say"," \""Allāhu akbar (Allah is the Greatest).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Iyās.\n\nHis statement \""kāna (he used to)\"" is an expression denoting the continuity of his action. Ibn ʿUmar"," Ibn ʿAbbās"," and others also mentioned this.\n\nAs for his statement \""and when he raised his head"," he would say the takbīr","\"" he intended thereby—and Allah knows best—that after raising his head"," when he was about to go into sujūd"," and this is clear in the hadith of Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nWe have narrated from Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and described his prayer"," saying: Then he raised his head and said"," \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH"," Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd (Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced recently"," and narrated more than once; it is agreed upon (muttafaq ʿalayh).]"""
"2613","(2613) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān in Hamadhān in the year forty-one narrated to us, Hilāl ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd narrated to us from Shuʿbah, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn al-Musayyib, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, from Ṭalḥah ibn Yazīd, from Ḥudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the month of Ramaḍān. When he raised his head from rukūʿ, he said, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH"," Allāhumma Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd (Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise).\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2614","(2614) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aṣbahānī al-Tājir in al-Rayy narrated to us, Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from al-Thawrī, from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, that when he said, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH","\"" he would say"," \""Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd"," Allāhumma bi-ḥawlika wa quwwatika aqūmu wa aqʿud (O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise. O Allah"," by Your strength and Your power I stand and I sit).\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2548.]"""
"2615","(2615) Abū al-Qāsim al-Tājir in al-Rayy narrated to us, Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Isḥāq narrated to us from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd, that he heard Abū Hurayrah, while he was leading the people in prayer, saying, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH"," Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd"," Allāhu akbar (Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise. Allah is the Greatest).\"" He raised his voice with that"," and we followed him together. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 2915.]"""
"2616","(2616) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyāsh narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us from Ibn ʿAwn, who said:\n\nMuḥammad, meaning Ibn Sīrīn, said: When the imām says, \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH","\"" the one behind him says"," \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH"," Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd (Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is praise).\""\n\nIt is narrated from Abū Burdah ibn Abī Mūsā that he would say behind the imām"," \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidaH (Allah hears the one who praises Him).\""\n\nAnd ʿAṭāʾ said: Combining both of them with the imām is more beloved to me. Two weak hadīths have been narrated concerning this"," which I have cited in al-Khilāf. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2600.]"""
"2617","(2617) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, he said: I read to Mālik. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh, meaning al-Qaʿnabī, narrated from Mālik, from Sumayy, from Abī Ṣāliḥ al-Sammān, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When the imām says"," 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him)"," then say"," 'Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd' (O Allah"," to You is all praise)"," for whoever's utterance coincides with that of the angels"," his past sins will be forgiven.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and it was narrated by Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ from his father from Abū Hurayrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned and is agreed upon.]"""
"2618","(2618) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us that Maʿmar narrated from Qatādah, from Yūnus ibn Jubayr, from Ḥiṭṭān ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Raqāshī, that Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, may Allah be pleased with him, led the people in prayer and mentioned the hadith, and in it Abū Mūsā said: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," delivered a sermon to us and taught us our prayer and explained to us our Sunnah"," saying: 'When you pray"," straighten your rows. When the imām says the takbīr"," say the takbīr. When he says"," \""Ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā ḍāllīn\"" (Not of those who have earned Your wrath"," nor of those who are astray)"," say \""Āmīn","\"" and Allah will answer you. When he says the takbīr and bows"," say the takbīr and bow"," for the imār says the takbīr before you and raises his head before you.'\"" The Prophet of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""That is for that [i.e."," the follower follows the imām in each action]. And when he says"," 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him)"," say"," 'Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd' (To You"," our Lord"," is all praise)"," and Allah will answer you.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and others from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\nIt was also narrated by ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid from his father from Maṭar"," from Zuhdram al-Jarmī"," who said: \""I prayed behind Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī"," and he said to us: 'When the imām says \""Allāhu Akbar","\"" say \""Allāhu Akbar\""—that is for that. And when he raises his head and says"," \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","\"" say the same—that is for that.'\"" The authentic narration is the first narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 2647.]"""
"2619","(2619) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, he said: It was read to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas, al-Layth ibn Saʿd, and Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you that Ibn Shihāb informed them, he said: Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, rode a horse and was thrown from it, and his right side was scratched. He then led us in one of the prayers while sitting, and we prayed with him sitting. When he finished, he said: \The imām is only appointed to be followed"," so do not differ from him. If he prays standing"," pray standing. When he says the takbīr"," say the takbīr. When he says"," 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' say"," 'Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd' (To You"," our Lord"," is all praise). When he prostrates"," prostrate. And if he prays sitting"," pray sitting"," all of you together.\""\n\nIt is recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the hadith of Mālik and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb.\n\nSimilarly"," it was narrated from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 789.]"""
"2620","(2620) And similarly it was narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Tājir in al-Rayy informed us that Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from al-Thawrī, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \When the imām says"," 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","' let the one behind him say"," 'Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd' (To You"," our Lord"," is all praise).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 2915.]"""
"2621","(2621) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us that Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us that ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd and ʿUbayd Allāh al-Jushamī both said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, entered the mosque. Then he mentioned the hadith regarding the story of the one who entered, and in it: \Then raise your head until you stand upright.\"" Recorded in the two Ṣaḥīḥs. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 724.]"""
"2622","(2622) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Abī Qilābah, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith, who said: He said one day—and that was not at the time of prayer—\Shall I not show you how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," was?\"" He stood and made the standing prolonged"," then he bowed and made the bowing prolonged"," then he raised his head and stood upright for a while. Abī Qilābah said: \""He prayed with us the prayer of our shaykh here"," Abī Burayd.\"" And Abū Burayd"," when he raised his head from the prostration of the first rakʿah"," would sit upright and then rise.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. Abū Burayd"," with the bāʾ and the rāʾ"," is ʿAmr ibn Salamah al-Jarmī. Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj gave him this kunyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 469.]"""
"2623","(2623) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to me that al-Layth narrated from Ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, that he was sitting with a group of the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and he mentioned the hadith from Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī regarding the description of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. He said: \When he raised his head"," he stood upright until every vertebra returned to its place.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ"," and he said in the hadith: \""Until every one of his bones returned to its place in proper alignment.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 828.]"""
"2624","(2624) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to me that Abū al-Walīd narrated to us that Shuʿbah informed us that Thābit informed us, he said: Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to describe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him for us. He would pray, and when he raised his head from the bowing, he would stand until we would say, \He has forgotten.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 800.]"""
"2625","(2625) Abū Saʿd ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī ʿUthmān al-Zāhid informed us that Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Abū al-Faḍl Aḥmad ibn Salamah al-Bazzāz narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbadah al-Ḍabbī informed us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us that Thābit al-Bunānī narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Mālik said to us: \I will not fall short in praying with you as I saw the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," praying with us.\"" Ḥammād said: Thābit said: \""Anas used to do something with us that I do not see you doing. When he raised his head from the bowing"," he would stand upright until the one who observed would say"," 'He has forgotten.' And when he raised his head from the prostration"," he would sit upright until the one who observed would say"," 'He has forgotten.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Khalaf ibn Hishām"," both from Ḥammād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 821.]"""
"2626","(2626) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, he said:\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr ibn Jaʿfar al-ʿAdl narrated to me that Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Bakhtarī narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh, my father narrated to me that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam, who said: A man whom he named gained authority over Kūfah in the time of Ibn al-Ashʿath, and he ordered Abū ʿUbaydah, meaning Ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, to lead the people in prayer. He would pray, and when he raised his head from the bowing, he would stand for as long as it would take me to say: \Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd"," milʾ al-samāwāt wa milʾ al-arḍ"," wa milʾ mā shiʾta min shayʾin baʿdu"," ahl al-thanāʾ wa al-majdu"," lā māniʿa li-mā aʿṭayta"," wa lā muʿṭiya li-mā manaʿta"," wa lā yanfāʿu dhā al-jaddi minka al-jadd\"" (O Allah"," our Lord"," to You is all praise"," filling the heavens and filling the earth"," and filling whatever You will thereafter. O You who are worthy of praise and glory! None can withhold what You give"," and none can give what You withhold"," and the greatness of the great avails nothing before You). Al-Ḥakam said: \""I mentioned this to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā"," and he said: 'I heard al-Barāʾ say: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," his bowing"," his rising from the bowing"," his prostration"," and what was between the two prostrations were nearly equal in duration.'\""\n\nShuʿbah said: \""I mentioned this to ʿAmr ibn Murrah"," and he said: 'I have seen Ibn Abī Laylā"," and his prayer was not like that.'\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh said: \""This is the wording of the hadith of Abī ʿAmr.\"" It was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 820.]"""
"2627","(2627) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Milḥān narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām narrated to me that he heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)…\"" Then he mentioned the hadith and said in it: \""Then he would say the takbīr when going down into prostration.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of al-Layth.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 803.]"""
"2628","(2628) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qāḍī in Marw informed us, al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Sharīk narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb from his father from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr, who said: \When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would prostrate"," his knees would touch the ground before his hands"," and when he would rise"," he would raise his hands before his knees.\""\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 268.]"""
"2629","(2629) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us, Hammām narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah narrated from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \When he would begin the prayer"," he would raise his hands and say the takbīr. Then he would wrap himself in his garment and place his right hand over his left hand. When he wished to bow"," he would do thus with his garment and bring out his hands"," then raise them and say the takbīr. When he wished to prostrate"," his knees would fall to the ground before his palms. When he prostrated"," he placed his forehead between his palms and kept his armpits open.\""\n\nHammām said: \""And Shaqīq narrated to us"," ʿĀṣim narrated from his father from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," who said something similar.\""\n\nHe said: \""And in the hadith of one of them"," Hammām said — and the most correct in my knowledge is that it is in the hadith of Muḥammad ibn Juḥādah: 'When he rose"," he rose upon his knees and leaned upon his thighs.'\""\n\nAnd Abū Dāwūd narrated something similar in the Sunan from Muḥammad ibn Maʿmar from Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 18362.]"""
"2630","(2630) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us from the original of his book, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us, Hammām narrated to us, Shaqīq Abū al-Layth said: \ʿĀṣim ibn Kulayb narrated to me from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," when he would prostrate"," his knees would fall to the ground before his palms.\""\n\nʿAffān said: \""And this hadith is gharīb.\"" (T) And Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated it from Sharīk.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""This hadith is counted among the unique narrations (afrād) of Sharīk al-Qāḍī. However"," Hammām followed him in this chain as a mursal narration. Thus did al-Bukhārī and other early ḥuffāẓ mention it"," may Allah the Most High have mercy upon them.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf jiddan.]"""
"2631","(2631) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥujr narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn Wāʾil from his mother from Wāʾil ibn Ḥajar, who said: \I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," then he prostrated"," and the first thing of his to reach the ground was his knees.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2632","(2632) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Ismāʿīl al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us, Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal from Anas, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say the takbīr and bring his thumbs level with his ears. Then he bowed until every joint of his settled in its place. Then he raised his head until every joint of his settled in his place. Then he went down with the takbīr until his knees preceded his hands.\""\n\nAl-ʿAlāʾ ibn Ismāʿīl is alone in narrating this"," and Allah the Most High knows best.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd regarding placing the knees before the hands"," from their own practice.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī in his Sunan"," 7.]"""
"2633","(2633) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Khalaf ibn ʿAmr al-ʿUkbariyy narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you prostrates"," let him not kneel as the camel kneels; rather let him place his hands and then his knees.\""\n\nIn the narration of Abū Dāwūd"," he said: \""Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to me","\"" and he said in the hadith: \""Rather let him place his hands before his knees.\"" And others narrated the same meaning from Saʿīd from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 8732.]"""
"2634","(2634) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you prostrates"," let him not kneel as the camel kneels; rather let him place his hands upon his knees.\"" He said: \""Upon his knees.\"" (Q) If this is preserved"," then it is evidence that he places his hands upon his knees when going down into prostration.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. And it has been mentioned previously.]"""
"2635","(2635) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ibn Fuḍayl narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd from his grandfather from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \When one of you prostrates"," let him begin with his knees before his hands"," and let him not kneel as the camel kneels.\""\n\nAnd Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated something similar from Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl.\n\n(C) However"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd al-Maqburī is weak"," and the one who contradicts him is Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan"," from whom al-Dārawardī narrated. And ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated it in an abridged form.\n\n[Bāṭil.]"""
"2636","(2636) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Qutaybah narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥasan from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \One of you leans in his prayer and kneels as the camel kneels.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated that this was the case initially and then it was abrogated"," and the ruling became what we have narrated from Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr"," although its chain is weak.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. And it was mentioned recently under numbers 2632 and 2634.]"""
"2637","(2637) Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī al-Faqīh — informed us. Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān — narrated to us. Ibn al-Ẓahrānī — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā — informed us. Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah — informed us. My grandfather — narrated to us. Both said: Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Yaḥyā ibn Salamah ibn Kuḥayl — narrated to us. My father — narrated to me, from his father, from Salamah ibn Kuḥayl, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from Saʿd, who said: \We used to place the hands before the knees"," and then we were commanded to place the knees before the hands.\""\n\nThus he said. And the well-known narration from Muṣʿab is from his father"," the hadith of the abrogation of al-tatbīq (clasping the hands). And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Dārawardī has another chain of narration for it"," and I do not consider it except a mistake. [Very weak]\n\n---"""
"2638","(2638) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us. Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Baṭṭah al-Aṣbahānī — narrated to us. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Zakariyyā — narrated to us. Muḥriz ibn Salamah al-ʿAdanī — narrated to us. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad — narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to place his hands before his knees. He said: \And the Prophet ﷺ used to do that.\""\n\nAnd similarly Ibn Wahb and Aṣbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated it from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz. And the well-known narration from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar regarding this is what Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us. Al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us. Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us. Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb — narrated to us. Ḥammād ibn Zayd — narrated to us"," from Ayyūb"," from Nāfiʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," who said: \""When one of you prostrates"," let him place his hands"," and when he raises"," let him raise them both"," for the hands prostrate just as the face prostrates.\"" [Hasan ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it (627)]\n\n---"""
"2639","(2639) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us. Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-ʿAdl — narrated to us. Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib — narrated to us. Al-Muʾammal ibn Hishām — narrated to us. Ismāʿīl, meaning Ibn ʿUlayyah — narrated to us. Ayyūb — narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who attributed it (to the Prophet ﷺ) and said: \The hands prostrate just as the face prostrates. So when one of you places his face"," let him place his hands"," and when he raises it"," let him raise them both.\""\n\nAnd similarly Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated it from Ismāʿīl. And the intended meaning from it is the placement of the hands in prostration"," not the precedence of one over the other. And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it (4478)]\n\n---"""
"2640","(2640) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us. Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us. Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us. Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb and ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl — both narrated to us. Ḥammād ibn Zayd — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me. Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Imām — narrated to us. Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā — informed us. Ḥammād ibn Zayd — narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh — said, and Abū al-Naḍr — narrated to me. Abū Bakr ibn Rajāʾ and Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr — both narrated to us. Abū al-Rabīʿ — narrated to us. Ḥammād — narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven bones"," and he was forbidden from tucking up his hair and his garments — the two hands"," the two knees"," the two feet"," and the forehead.\"" The wording is from the hadith of Abū al-Rabīʿ. And in the hadith of al-ʿAbbās: \""The Prophet ﷺ was commanded to prostrate on seven"," and he was forbidden from tucking up hair or garments"," or he said: his garments.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Nuʿmān ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī. And al-Bukhārī narrated it from Qabīṣah"," from Sufyān al-Thawrī"," from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār"," with the same meaning as the narration of Abū al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (809)]\n\n---"""
"2641","(2641) Abū Saʿd al-Zāhid — narrated to us by dictation, and Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī — narrated to us by recitation. Both said: Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī — informed us. Aḥmad ibn Salamah — narrated to us. Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī — narrated to us. Bakr ibn Muḍar — narrated to us, from Ibn al-Hād, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \When the servant prostrates"," seven limbs prostrate with him: his face"," his two palms"," his two knees"," and his two feet.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (491)]\n\n---"""
"2642","(2642) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdad — informed us. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh — informed us. ʿAlī ibn Isḥkāb — narrated to us. Abū Badr Shuʿjāʿ ibn al-Walīd — narrated to me. Abū Khaythamah — narrated to me. Al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr — narrated to me. ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mālik — narrated to me, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ. Mālik — informed me, from ʿAyyāsh or ʿAbbās ibn Sahl al-Sāʿidī, that he was in a gathering in which his father was present, and he was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and in the gathering were Abū Hurayrah, Abū Usayd, and Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī from the Anṣār. They discussed the prayer, and Abū Ḥumayd said: \I am the most knowledgeable among you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" They said: \""How so?\"" He said: \""I learned that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nThey said: \""Then show us.\"" So he stood to pray while they watched him. He began and said the takbīr"," raising his hands towards the level of his shoulders. Then he said the takbīr for rukūʿ"," and he raised his hands again"," then he placed his hands upon his knees without lowering his head excessively or raising it. Then he raised his head and said: \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah. Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd.\"" Then he raised his hands. Then he said: \""Allāhu Akbar.\"" And he prostrated"," placing firmly his two palms"," his two knees"," and the tops of his feet while he was in prostration. Then he said the takbīr and sat"," folding one of his feet beneath him and placing his other foot upright. Then he said the takbīr and prostrated. Then he said the takbīr"," meaning he stood"," without folding his foot beneath him. Then he repeated the second rakʿah in the same manner. Then he sat after the two rakʿahs until"," when he intended to rise for standing"," he stood with a takbīr. Then he performed the last two rakʿahs. Then he said the salām to his right: \""Al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmat Allāh","\"" and he said the salām to his left as well: \""Al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmat Allāh.\"" And ʿĪsā narrated to me that among what he also narrated to him regarding the sitting in the tashahhud was: that he placed his left hand on his left thigh"," and he placed his right hand on his right thigh"," then he pointed in supplication with a single finger.\n\nThus did more than one narrate it from Abū Badr. And some of them narrated it from Abū Badr and said: from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ"," who said: Mālik narrated to me"," from ʿAbbās ibn Sahl al-Sāʿidī. And ʿUtbah ibn Abī Ḥakīm narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĪsā"," from al-ʿAbbās ibn Sahl"," from Abū Ḥumayd"," and he did not mention Muḥammad in his chain. And the correct view is that Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ witnessed it from Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it (166)]\n\n---"""
"2643","(2643) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad — informed us. Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī — narrated to us. Miqdām ibn Dāwūd — narrated to us. Wahb ibn al-Mubārak — narrated to us. Ibn Lahīʿah — narrated to us. Miqdām said, and Abū al-Aswad — narrated to us. Al-Layth ibn Saʿd and Ibn Lahīʿah — narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \I was in a gathering of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and they discussed his prayer. Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī said: 'I am the most knowledgeable among you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","' and it was among my concerns. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: when he stood for the prayer"," he said the takbīr"," then he recited. When he bowed"," he said the takbīr"," and he placed his two palms upon his two knees"," and spread his fingers"," then he bent his back without lowering his head excessively or tilting his cheek. When he raised himself upright"," he stood until every limb returned to its place. When he prostrated"," he placed firmly on the ground his two palms"," his two knees"," and the tops of his two feet"," then he settled in prostration. When he raised his head"," he settled in a sitting position. When he sat after the two rakʿahs"," he sat on the underside of his left foot and placed his right foot upright. When it was the fourth rakʿah"," he extended his left hip towards the ground and brought out his feet to one side.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: And in the narration of ʿAbbās ibn Sahl from Abū Ḥumayd in this hadith is: \""He placed firmly his two palms"," his two knees"," and the tops of his two feet in prostration.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it (3046)]\n\n---"""
"2644","(2644) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us. Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh — informed us. ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — narrated to us. Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm — narrated to us. Wuhayb — narrated to us. Ayyūb — narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When one of you prostrates"," let him place his hands"," and when he raises"," let him raise them both"," for the hands prostrate just as the face prostrates.\"" Thus he said. And Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated it from Ayyūb and said: \""he raised it (marfūʿ).\"" And Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Ayyūb as a mawqūf narration from Ibn ʿUmar. And Ibn Abī Laylā narrated it from Nāfiʿ as a marfūʿ narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was previously mentioned (2639)]\n\n---"""
"2645","(2645) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us. ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl — narrated to us. ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — narrated to us. Al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Minhāl — narrated to us. Hammām — narrated to us. Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah — narrated to us. ʿAlī ibn Yaḥyā ibn Khallād — narrated to me, from his father, from his uncle Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ, that he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came and entered the mosque and prayed. When he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Wa ʿalayka al-salām. Go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" And he mentioned the hadith regarding the Prophet's ﷺ teaching him. He said in it: \""Then he says the takbīr and prostrates"," and he places his forehead firmly on the ground until his joints settle and become steady.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it (19206)]\n\n---"""
"2646","(2646) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us. Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq — informed us by dictation in the year thirty-three and three hundred. Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbbād — narrated to us. Muʿallā ibn Asad — narrated to us. Wuhayb — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us. Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us. Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us. Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj — narrated to us. Wuhayb ibn Khālid — narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: \I was commanded to prostrate on seven bones — on the forehead\"" — and he pointed with his hand to his nose — \""the two hands"," the two knees"," and the extremities of the two feet.\"" \""And we should not tuck up the garments or the hair.\"" And in the hadith of Muʿallā: \""And I should not tuck up the garment or the hair.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿallā ibn Asad"," except that he said: \""wa-lā nakfita.\"" And Muslim narrated it from another route from Wuhayb"," likewise."""
"2647","(2647) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: it was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibn Jurayj informed you, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I have been commanded to prostrate upon seven bones"," and not to tuck up the hair or the garments.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""And they are: the forehead"," the nose"," the two hands"," the two knees"," and the two feet.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir"," from Ibn Wahb"," except that he said: \""lā akfita\"" instead of \""lā akuffa.\"""""
"2648","(2648) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Ṭāwūs, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was commanded to prostrate upon seven (bones) from himself: his two hands"," his two knees"," the tips of his toes"," and his forehead. And he was forbidden from tucking up the hair and the garments.\"" Sufyān said: \""And Ibn Ṭāwūs added: 'He placed his hand upon his forehead"," then passed it over his nose until he reached the tip of his nose.' He said: 'And my father used to count this as one (bone).'\"""""
"2649","(2649) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿAlī, meaning Ibn al-Madīnī, narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Ibn Ṭāwūs narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās. And ʿAmr narrated, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \Your Prophet (ﷺ) was commanded to prostrate upon seven (bones)"," and he was forbidden\"" — Ibn Ṭāwūs said: \""from tucking up the hair and the garments\"" — and ʿAmr said: \""from tucking up his hair and his garments.\"" Sufyān said: \""And in the ḥadīth of ʿAmr: 'to prostrate upon seven (bones): his forehead"," his two hands"," his two knees"," and the tips of his toes.'\"" Sufyān said: \""Except that Ibn Ṭāwūs narrated to us that Ṭāwūs used to gesture with his hand upon his forehead and his nose"," and Ibn Ṭāwūs passed his hand over his nose and his forehead.\"" Ibn Ṭāwūs said: \""My father used to say: 'It (the nose and forehead) is one"," along with the two hands"," the two knees"," and the two feet.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""In the narration of Sufyān there is evidence that the mention of the nose in the ḥadīth is from the explanation (tafsīr) of Ṭāwūs. And Muslim has narrated the ḥadīth of Sufyān from Ibn Ṭāwūs in his Ṣaḥīḥ in an abridged form"," without the explanation.\"""""
"2650","(2650) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Bishshār narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah narrated to us, saying: \I heard Ṭāwūs narrating from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: 'The Prophet (ﷺ) was commanded to prostrate upon seven (bones) from himself.'\"" He (Ibrāhīm ibn Mayṣarah) said: \""I said: 'O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," what do you think about the nose?' He said: 'It is among the best of them (i.e."," it is certainly included).'\"""""
"2651","(2651) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated, from what he read to Mālik, from Yazīd ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Hād, from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Saʿīd, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform iʿtikāf.\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," who said: \""I saw this night"," then I was made to forget it. But I saw myself prostrating the following morning in water and mud.\"" Abū Saʿīd said: \""So I saw with my own eyes the traces of water and mud upon the forehead and nose of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the morning of the twenty-first.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from two other routes from Ibn al-Hād."""
"2652","(2652) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī informed me; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Mukram narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn ʿUbaydullāh al-Ghaylānī narrated to us; Abū Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Shuʿbah and al-Thawrī narrated, from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw a man performing prayer, and when he prostrated, his nose did not touch the ground. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is no prayer for the one whose nose does not touch the ground to the same extent as the forehead.\"""""
"2653","(2653) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath narrated to us; al-Jarrāḥ ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Abū Qutaybah narrated, and he mentioned the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah and al-Thawrī, each one of them individually, with the same meaning. Then Abū Bakr said: \ʿAbdullāh ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ashʿath: no one besides Abū Qutaybah narrated it with a chain from Sufyān and Shuʿbah. And the correct version is from ʿĀṣim"," from ʿIkrimah"," as a mursal narration.\"""""
"2654","(2654) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us, from Sufyān, who said: \ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated to me"," from ʿIkrimah"," who said: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a man or a woman who did not place his/her nose (on the ground) when he/she prostrated"," and he said: \""A prayer is not accepted in which the nose does not touch the ground to the same extent as the forehead.\""'\""\n\nAnd similarly Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah and ʿAbdah ibn Sulaymān narrated it from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal"," from ʿIkrimah"," as a mursal narration. And part of its meaning was narrated from Simāk"," from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," as his own statement."""
"2655","(2655) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād and Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us, from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: \When you prostrate"," place your nose upon the ground along with your forehead.\"" And in the ḥadīth of al-Ṣaffār: \""then your forehead.\"""""
"2656","(2656) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Barṭī al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym informed us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us, from Simāk, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \When any one of you prostrates"," let him place his nose upon the ground"," for you have been commanded to do so.\""\n\nAnd similarly Sharīk narrated it from Simāk. And Ḥarb ibn Maymūn narrated it"," from Khālid"," from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""Place your nose (on the ground) so that it prostrates with you.\""\n\nAbū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: \""The ḥadīth of ʿIkrimah from the Prophet (ﷺ) is more accurately mursal.\"""""
"2657","(2657) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr — he is Ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh — informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā informed us: ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated from Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah, from Abū Isḥāq, from Saʿīd ibn Wahb, from Khabbāb ibn al-Aratt, who said: \We complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the intense heat of Ramḍān on our foreheads and palms"," but he did not acknowledge our complaint.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it through another chain.]"""
"2658","(2658) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Isfarāʾinī informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us: ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbbād informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Ḥārith al-Anṣārī, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \I used to pray Ẓuhr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and I would take a handful of pebbles in my palm until they cooled down"," and then I would place them on my forehead area when I prostrated"," due to the intensity of the heat.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""If prostration upon a garment attached to one were permissible"," that would be easier than cooling pebbles in the hand and placing them for prostration upon them. And success is through Allah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it"," 14098.]"""
"2659","(2659) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr said: it was read to Ibn Wahb: \Ibn Lahīʿah and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed you from Bakr ibn Sawādah al-Judhāmī"," from Ṣāliḥ ibn Khaywān al-Sabāʾī"," who narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man prostrating on his side"," having covered his forehead. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ uncovered his forehead.\""\n\nAnd in what Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from ʿIyāḍ ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Qurashī"," who said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man prostrating on the fold of his turban"," so he gestured with his hand: 'Raise your turban","' and he gestured toward his forehead.\""\n\nThis mursal narration is a witness to the mursal of Ṣāliḥ. [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Wahb narrated it"," 391.]"""
"2660","(2660) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad informed us: Hannād informed us: Wakīʿ narrated from Isrāʾīl, from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from ʿAlī, who said: \When any one of you prays"," let him uncover the turban from his forehead.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it"," 2759.]"""
"2661","(2661) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū Bakr informed us: ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Hannād informed us: ʿAbdah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar, when he prostrated while wearing a turban, would raise it until he placed his forehead on the ground. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was cited previously.]"
"2662","(2662) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Abū Bakr informed us: ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Hannād informed us: Wakīʿ narrated from Sakan ibn Abī Karīmah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿUbādah, from Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ, from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, that when he stood for prayer, he would remove the turban from his forehead. [Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it.]"
"2663","(2663) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Asfaṭī informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal informed us: Ghālib al-Qaṭṭān narrated from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī, from Anas, who said: \When we prayed with the Prophet ﷺ"," and one of us was unable to place his forehead on the ground due to the intensity of the heat"," he would spread his garment and prostrate upon it.\"""""
"2664","(2664) Abū ʿAmr al-Bisṭāmī informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū Khalīfah informed us: Abū al-Walīd informed us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to me: Ghālib al-Qaṭṭān narrated from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \When we prayed with the Prophet ﷺ"," one of us would place the edge of his garment at the place of prostration due to the intensity of the heat.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ with wording close to this from Abū al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," 385.]"""
"2665","(2665) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal — (ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunayn informed us: Abū Ghassān informed me: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to me: Ghālib al-Qaṭṭān narrated from Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \We used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ during intense heat"," and when one of us was unable to place his forehead on the ground"," he would spread his garment and prostrate upon it.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā with this wording. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was cited previously.]"""
"2666","(2666) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: Abū Yaʿlā informed us: Surayj ibn Yūnus informed us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated, mentioning his chain of narration, except that he said in its text: \We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during intense heat"," and one of us would take pebbles in his hand; when they cooled"," he would place them and prostrate upon them.\""\n\nThe Shaykh Abū Bakr said: \""These are two hadiths that Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated — one concerning the garment and the other concerning pebbles.\""\n\nKhālid ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bukayr al-Sulamī narrated from Bakr"," with wording close to the first narration"," concerning garments.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""As for what has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ regarding prostration upon the fold of the turban"," nothing from that is established. The most authentic narration in this regard is the statement of al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī"," reported as a narration from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was previously cited under no. 2658.]"""
"2667","(2667) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us; Za'idah narrated from Hisham from al-Hasan, who said: \The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to perform prostration with their hands inside their garments"," and a man among them would prostrate upon his turban.\""\n\nThe first hadith may carry the meaning that the garment referred to is a separate cloth"," and this narration may indicate that a man among them would prostrate upon his turban and his forehead. However"," exercising caution in the matter of prostration is more prudent"," and success is through Allah.\n\n[Sound. As for al-Hasan"," it was narrated by Abu Shaybah (2739)]\n\n---"""
"2668","(2668) And Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Muqri', Ibn al-Hammami, in Baghdad, informed us; Isma'il ibn 'Ali ibn Isma'il al-Khattabi narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us; Wuhaib narrated from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi informed me; from 'Amir ibn Sa'd; from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded the placing of the two palms and the raising of the two feet during the prayer.\""\n\n[Weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (277)]\n\n---"""
"2669","(2669) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me; Abu Ishaq 'Amr ibn 'Abd Allah al-Suba'i said: I heard al-Bara' ibn 'Azib say: \The Prophet (ﷺ) used to prostrate upon the backs of his two hands (i.e."," the inner surfaces of the palms).\""\n\n[Sound. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah (639)]\n\n---"""
"2670","(2670) And Abu 'Abd Allah informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us; 'Affan ibn Muslim, Muslim ibn Ibrahim, Abu 'Umar al-Hawdhi, and 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; they said: Shu'bah narrated to us; he said: Abu Ishaq informed me; from al-Bara', who said: \When one of you prostrates"," let him prostrate upon the back of his palm.\"" The wording is that of al-Hawdhi.\n\n[Sound. It has been previously mentioned in the one before it]\n\n---"""
"2671","(2671) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran informed us; Abu Ja'far al-Razzaz narrated to us; Hanbal ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us; Wuhaib ibn Khalid narrated from Muhammad ibn Juhaadah; from Sulayman ibn Abu Hind; from Khabbab ibn al-Aratt, who said: \We complained to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the intense heat affecting our foreheads and our palms"," but he did not respond to our complaint.\""\n\n[Sound. Previously mentioned under number (2657)]\n\n---"""
"2672","(2672) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-'Adl informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakka narrated to us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Nafi': that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, when he prostrated, would place his two palms upon the place where he placed his face. Nafi' said: \And I saw him on an intensely cold day"," and he would bring his two palms out from beneath his hood until he placed them upon the pebbles.\""\n\n[Sound. As in al-Dhahabi from Malik…]\n\n---"""
"2673","(2673) And with his chain of narration, he said: Malik narrated from Nafi' that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar used to say: \Whoever places his forehead upon the ground"," let him place his two palms upon the place where he places his forehead. Then"," when he raises (his head)"," let him raise them both"," for the two hands prostrate just as the face prostrates.\""\n\n[Sound. Previously mentioned (2639)]\n\n---"""
"2674","(2674) And Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us; Abu al-Hasan al-Karzi narrated to us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us; Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated from Layth; from al-Hakam: that Sa'd led the people in prayer while his hands were inside his sleeves.\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: \Al-Mustaqah is a garment with long sleeves.\"" This is a mursal narration.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i that he said: \""They used to pray in their long-sleeved garments"," their cloaks"," and their wraps"," without taking their hands out.\"" A musnad hadith has been narrated concerning this"," but its chain contains some weakness.\n\n[Weak]\n\n---"""
"2675","(2675) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Abu Uways narrated to me; Ibrahim ibn Isma'il narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Samit; from his father; from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood to pray in the Mosque of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, and he had a cloak wrapped around him, and he placed his hands upon it to protect himself from the cold of the pebbles.\n\nIt has also been narrated through another weak chain.\n\n[Weak. Narrated by Ibn Majah (1032)]\n\n---"
"2676","(2676) It was narrated to us by 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdān; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us; al-Harith ibn Abu Usamah narrated to us; al-Waqidi narrated to us; Kharijah ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Sulayman ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated from Dawud ibn al-Husayn; from 'Ikrimah; from Ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) praying in a white cloak on a cold morning"," using the cloak to shield his hands and feet from the cold of the ground.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"2677","(2677) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq — via dictation — informed us that 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us that Muslim ibn Ibrahim informed us that Shu'bah narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was commanded to prostrate upon seven bones and not to tuck up his garment or his hair. Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, and Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj reported it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Sahih. Previously cited under no. 2640]"
"2678","(2678) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawiyy informed us that Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Hafiz informed us that Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami informed us that Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabiyy informed us that Sufyan narrated from 'Amr ibn Dinar, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: \upon seven","\"" and \""that he should not tuck up his garment or his hair.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it from Qabisah from Sufyan. [Sahih. Previously cited in the hadith before it]"""
"2679","(2679) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us that 'Ubayd ibn 'Abd al-Wahid narrated that Ibn Abi Maryam narrated that Ibn Wahb narrated. (H) And Abu 'Ali al-Rawdbariyy informed us — and the wording is his — that Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated that Abu Dawud narrated that Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated that Ibn Wahb narrated from 'Amr ibn al-Harith that Bukayr narrated to him that Krayb, the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, narrated to him that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas saw 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith praying with his head tied back from behind. He stood behind him and began to undo it. When he finished his prayer, he turned to Ibn 'Abbas and said: \What concern do you have with my head?\"" He replied: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'The likeness of this is the likeness of one who prays while his hands are tied (behind his back).'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Amr ibn Sawwad from Ibn Wahb. [Sahih. Muslim reported it"," no. 492]"""
"2680","(2680) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukariyy in Baghdad informed us that Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us that Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadiyy informed us that 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us that Ibn Jurayj informed us. (H) And Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said that Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated that Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghaniyy informed us that Hajjaj narrated — he said: Ibn Jurayj told me — that 'Imran ibn Musa informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburiyy informed us from his father that he saw Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Prophet (ﷺ), pass by Hasan ibn 'Ali while Hasan was standing in prayer having tucked his braids behind his neck. So Abu Rafi' undone them. Hasan turned to him angrily, and Abu Rafi' said: \Attend to your prayer and do not be angry"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'That is the seat of Satan'\"" — meaning the place where his braids are tucked. The wording is from the hadith of Hajjaj ibn Muhammad. In the hadith of 'Abd al-Razzaq from Sa'id"," he said: \""It is the seat of Satan","\"" meaning the place where his braids are tucked. We have also narrated reports regarding the dislike of this practice from 'Umar"," 'Ali"," Hudhayfah"," and 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them). [Da'if. Reported by 'Abd al-Razzaq"," no. 2991]"""
"2681","(2681) Abu 'Ali al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us that Yusuf ibn Ya'qub informed us that Nasr ibn 'Ali informed us that Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated from al-'Ala' ibn al-Musayyab from 'Amr ibn Murrah from Talhah ibn Yazid from Hudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say in his ruku': \Subhana Rabbiya al-'Azim\"" (Glory be to my Lord"," the Magnificent)"," repeating it. When he raised his head from ruku'"," he would say: \""Sami' Allahu liman hamidah"," Rabbana wa lak al-hamd\"" (Allah hears the one who praises Him; our Lord"," to You is all praise). When he prostrated"," he would say: \""Subhana Rabbiya al-A'la\"" (Glory be to my Lord"," the Most High)"," repeating it. And when he raised his head from prostration"," he would say: \""Rabb ighfir li\"" (O Lord"," forgive me). [Sahih. Previously cited under no. 2554]"""
"2682","(2682) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-'Anbariyy informed us that my grandfather Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi informed us that Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us that Qutaybah ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafiyy informed us that Jarir narrated. He said: And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated that Jarir narrated from Mansur from Abu al-Duha from Masruq from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to frequently say in his ruku' and sujud: \Subhanaka Allahumma Rabbana wa bihamdika"," Allahumma ighfir li\"" (Glory be to You"," O Allah"," our Lord"," and praise be to You; O Allah"," forgive me). He was acting upon the Qur'an. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from 'Uthman from Jarir. [Sahih. Previously cited under no. 2562]"""
"2683","(2683) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us that Abu 'Ali Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us that al-Hasan ibn Mukram informed us that Sa'id ibn 'Amir informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated from Qatadah from Mutarrif from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say in his sujud: \Subbuhun Quddusun"," Rabb al-mala'ikati wa al-Ruh\"" (Glorious"," Most Holy"," Lord of the angels and the Spirit). Muslim reported it in his Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Abi 'Arubah. [Sahih. Previously cited in the hadith before it]"""
"2684","(2684) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us that Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi informed us that Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddamiyy informed us that Yusuf al-Majishun said: My father informed me from 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi' from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood for prayer — and he mentioned the hadith, in which is: \When he prostrated"," he said: 'Allahumma laka sajadtu"," wa bika amantu"," wa laka aslamtu"," wa 'alayka tawakkaltu; sajada wajhi lladhi khalaqahu wa sawwarahu wa shaqqa sam'ahu wa basarahu; fa tabaraka Allahu ahsan al-khaliqin'\"" (O Allah"," to You I have prostrated"," in You I have believed"," to You I have submitted"," and upon You I have placed my trust. My face has prostrated to the One who created it"," fashioned it"," and opened its hearing and sight. So blessed is Allah"," the Best of Creators). Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddamiyy. [Sahih. Previously cited under no. 2546]"""
"2685","(2685) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Muqri' al-Mihrajaniyy in it informed us that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us that Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi informed us that Abu al-Rabi' informed us that Isma'il ibn Ja'far informed us that Sulayman ibn Suhaym, the freedman of al-'Abbas, narrated from Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah ibn Ma'bad ibn 'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib from his father from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) drew aside the curtain while he was bandaged during the illness in which he died, and said: \Allahumma hal ballaghtu?\"" (O Allah"," have I conveyed?) — three times. \""Indeed"," nothing remains of the glad tidings of prophethood except the righteous dream that a servant sees or that is shown to him. Beware"," I have indeed been forbidden from reciting the Qur'an during ruku' and sujud. So when you perform ruku'"," magnify Allah"," and when you prostrate"," exert yourselves in supplication"," for it is worthy that your supplications be answered.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Isma'il ibn Ja'far. [Sahih. Previously cited under no. 2567]"""
"2686","(2686) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us that Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — via dictation — informed us that 'Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Nasawiyy informed us that 'Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhiyy informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that 'Amr ibn al-Harith informed me from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr, that he heard Abu Salih Dhakwan narrating from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The closest a servant is to his Lord is while he is in prostration"," so increase in supplication.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Amr ibn Sawwad and others. [Sahih. Muslim reported it"," no. 482]"""
"2687","(2687) Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasa informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Ahmad ibn Salih narrated, and Ibn al-Sarh informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me from 'Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah from Sumayy, the freedman of Abu Bakr, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say in his prostration: \O Allah"," forgive me all my sins"," the small and the great"," the first and the last.\"" Ibn al-Sarh added: \""the open and the secret.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 483]"""
"2688","(2688) Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Faqih informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Ahmad ibn Salih and Ibn Rafi' both said: 'Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to me; my father narrated to me from Wahb ibn Manus, who said: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: \I have not prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) whose prayer more closely resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) than this young man\"" — meaning 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz. He said: \""We estimated his rukū' to contain ten tasbīḥs and his sujūd to contain ten tasbīḥs.\""\n\nAbu Dawud said: Ahmad ibn Salih said: \""I asked him: 'Mānus or Mābus?' He said: 'Abd al-Razzāq says Mābus"," but according to my memory it is Mānus.'\"" And this is the wording of Ibn Rafi'"," who said: Ahmad narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Anas ibn Malik. [Da'if]"""
"2689","(2689) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both said: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm informed us; Bahr ibn Nasr informed us; it was recited to Ibn Wahb: \Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed you from Ishaq ibn Yazid al-Hudhali from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When one of you bows (rukū') and says \""Subḥāna Rabbiya al-'Aẓīm\"" (Glory be to my Lord"," the Magnificent) three times"," his rukū' is complete"," and that is its minimum. And when he prostrates (sujūd) and says \""Subḥāna Rabbiya al-A'lā\"" (Glory be to my Lord"," the Most High) three times"," his sujūd is complete"," and that is its minimum.'\"" [Da'if. It was previously mentioned under number 2558]"""
"2690","(2690) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun informed us; 'Ali ibn al-Madini informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi informed us; Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated from a man from Banu Tamim — who was praised highly — from his father, who said: \I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" He said: \""I asked him about the extent of his rukū' and his sujūd"," and he said: 'The extent of what a person says \""Subḥān Allāhi wa bi ḥamdihi\"" (Glory be to Allah and praise Him) three times.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"2691","(2691) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamid al-Tirmidhi informed us; Muhammad ibn Jabal informed us; Salih ibn 'Abdullah al-Tirmidhi informed us; 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad informed us; 'Asim ibn Kulaib narrated from his father from Wā'il ibn Hujr al-Hadrami, who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'I shall certainly observe how you pray.' He said: He stood and faced the qiblah"," said the takbīr"," and raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. When he bowed (rukū')"," he placed his hands on his knees. When he raised his head from rukū'"," he raised his hands until they were level with his shoulders. When he prostrated (sujūd)"," he placed his face between his hands in that place.\"" And he mentioned the hadith. 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad thus said from 'Asim: \""level with his shoulders.\""\n\nAnd Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah agreed with him regarding the raising of the hands. But Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal and others said from 'Asim: \""level with his ears","\"" and said: \""When he prostrated"," he placed his head between his hands.\"" [Da'if in this wording"," but its meaning is established and sahih according to Muslim.]"""
"2692","(2692) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Asid ibn 'Asim informed us; al-Husayn ibn Hafs informed us from Sufyan from 'Asim ibn Kulaib from his father from Wā'il ibn Hujr, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prostrated"," his hands were level with his ears.\"" A group narrated this from al-Thawri. [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah"," 2667]"""
"2693","(2693) Waqi' said from al-Thawri with this chain of narration: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he prostrated"," and his hands were close to his ears.\""\n\nAbu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us; Hajib ibn Ahmad informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Hashim informed us; Waqi' informed us; Sufyan narrated it. And this is more appropriate for its agreement with the narration of Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi and his companions. [Sahih. It was previously mentioned in the hadith before it"," and it is the wording of Ibn Abi Shaybah]"""
"2694","(2694) Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasa informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Ahmad ibn Hanbal informed us; 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr informed me; Fulayh informed me; 'Abbas ibn Sahl said: \Abu Humayd"," Abu Usayd"," Sahl ibn Sa'd"," and Muhammad ibn Muslimah gathered and discussed the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" Abu Humayd said: \""I am the most knowledgeable among you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" Then he mentioned the hadith and said: \""Then he prostrated and placed his nose and forehead firmly on the ground"," moved his hands away from his sides"," and placed his palms level with his shoulders.\"" [Sahih. Previously mentioned under number 2518]"""
"2695","(2695) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan ibn 'Amir informed us; al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah ibn Isma'il ibn 'Uqbah al-Khazin informed us; Hushaym informed us from 'Asim ibn Kulaib from 'Alqamah ibn Wā'il ibn Hujr from his father, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) used to spread his fingers when he bowed (rukū') and close his fingers together when he prostrated (sujūd).\"" [Hasan. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 594]"""
"2696","(2696) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr informed us; 'Ayyash ibn Tamim al-Sukkari informed us; Makhlad ibn Malik ibn Jabir informed us; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated from al-Fazari from Abi Ishaq from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prostrated and placed his hands on the ground"," he directed his palms and his fingers toward the qiblah.\"" [Sahih]"""
"2697","(2697) Abu Hatim al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Suda'i narrated to me; my father, Ali ibn Yazid, narrated to me, from Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara', who said: When the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ruku', he would straighten his back, and when he prostrated, he would direct his fingers toward the qiblah and spread them apart. [Da'if]"
"2698","(2698) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani' al-Hafiz narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur Sajjada narrated to us; Abu Ma'mar narrated to us; Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umayr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: It is disliked for one not to direct his palms toward the qiblah when he prostrates. [Hasan]"
"2699","(2699) Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan informed us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab and Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit informed us, from Iyad, from al-Bara', who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \When you prostrate"," place your palms and raise your forearms.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya."""
"2700","(2700) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Be moderate in prostration"," and let none of you spread his forearms as a dog spreads its.\"" It is recorded in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj. [Sahih. Muslim narrated it"," 494]"""
"2701","(2701) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-Anbari informed us; my grandfather, Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi, narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us; al-Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abi al-Jawza', from A'ishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would commence the prayer with the takbir and the recitation with {Al-hamdu lillahi Rabb al-'alamin}. When he performed ruku', he would neither raise his head excessively nor lower it. When he raised his head from ruku', he would stand upright. When he prostrated and raised his head from the prostration, he would not prostrate again until he had sat upright. He would forbid the sitting of the devil (al-'aqib al-shaytan). He would spread his left leg and erect his right leg. He would dislike that one spread his forearms as a dog spreads its. He would conclude the prayer with the salam. He would say the tahiyyah after every two rak'ahs. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. [Sahih. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it, 636]"
"2702","(2702) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan informed us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; al-Husayn al-Mu'allim narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Maysarah, from Abi al-Jawza', from A'ishah, describing the prayer of the Prophet (peace be upon him), she said: He would forbid us from spreading our forearms as a beast of prey spreads its. We have also narrated on this subject from Jabir ibn Abdullah, Abu Hurayrah, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Shibl, from the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Sahih. It has been mentioned in the one before it]"
"2703","(2703) Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated to us; Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us; my father, Ishaq ibn Bakr, Abu Salih al-Juhani, and al-Nadr ibn al-Jabbar narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, from al-A'raj, from Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Buhaynah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prayed, he would spread his arms apart so that his underarms became visible. Abu Salih al-Juhani said in his hadith: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prostrated, he would keep his upper arms away from his sides so that the whiteness of his underarms could be seen. [Sahih. al-Bukhari narrated it, 3564, 807, 390]"
"2704","(2704) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir informed us; my grandfather, Yahya ibn Mansur, narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi narrated to us; Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, mentioning it with a similar chain of narration: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prayed, he would spread his arms apart so that the whiteness of his underarms could be seen. al-Bukhari and Muslim both narrated it from Qutaybah. [Sahih. It has been mentioned in the one before it]"
"2705","(2705) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Imam narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm, from his uncle Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prostrated, had a young sheep wished to pass between his arms, it would have done so. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya. [Sahih. Muslim narrated it, 497]"
"2706","(2706) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih narrated to us; Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Nasr and Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Ismail al-Anbari narrated to us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us; Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Asamm narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prostrated, he would spread his arms apart—meaning he would extend them—so that the whiteness of his underarms could be seen from behind him. And when he sat, he would rest upon his left thigh. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. It was also narrated by Ja'far ibn Burqan from Yazid ibn al-Asamm. [Sahih. It has been mentioned in the one before it]"
"2707","(2707) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us: Dāwūd ibn Qays narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Aqram al-Khuzāʿī, from his father, that he was with his father at the plain of Namirah. A caravan passed by them and dismounted at a side of the road. His father said to me: \Stay with your flock so that I may approach these people and ask about them.\"" He said: \""So he drew near"," and I drew near with him"," until the prayer was established"," and there was the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) among them. I would look at the whiteness of the two armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) whenever he prostrated.\""\n\nYaʿqūb said: \""He said 'min Namirah","' but the correct form is 'Thamirah.' He erred in it"," just as Ibn al-Mubārak also erred in it.\""\n\n[Hasan. Al-Shāfiʿī narrated it in al-Umm"," 1/13.]"""
"2708","(2708) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal informed us: al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī narrated to us: al-Nufaylī narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abū Isḥāq narrated from al-Tamīmī, the one who narrated tafsīr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) from behind him"," and I saw the whiteness of his armpits while he was in the posture of jakh"," having spread apart his arms.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd narrated it"," 899.]"""
"2709","(2709) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Naḍr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Naṣr al-Sūriyānī narrated to us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prayed"," he would perform jakh.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," saying: \""I heard Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī say: 'A man performs jakh in his prayer when he spreads out his upper arms and keeps them away from his sides during rukūʿ and sujūd.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"2710","(2710) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us: Maʿmar narrated from Manṣūr, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) prostrated"," he would keep his arms away from his sides until the whiteness of his armpits could be seen.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it"," 2922.]"""
"2711","(2711) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: ʿAbbād ibn Rāshid narrated from al-Ḥasan: Aḥmar, a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), narrated to us, saying: \We used to shelter the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from what he would keep his hands away from his sides when he prostrated.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Saʿd narrated it in al-Ṭabaqāt"," 7/47"," and Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2641.]"""
"2712","(2712) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān informed us: Baqiyyah narrated to me: ʿUtbah, meaning Ibn Abī Ḥakīm, narrated to me: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĪsā narrated from al-ʿAbbās ibn Sahl al-Sāʿidī, from Abī Ḥumayd, regarding the description of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: \When he prostrated"," he would spread apart his thighs without letting his rest his belly upon anything of his thighs.\""\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh also narrated it from ʿUtbah"," except that he said in his chain: ʿUtbah ibn ʿAbdillāh"," and this is the correct version.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"2713","(2713) Abū ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū Ṣāliḥ narrated to me: al-Layth narrated from Durrāj, from Ibn Ḥujayrah, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \When one of you prostrates"," let him not spread out his arms like the spreading of a dog"," and let him draw together his thighs.\""\n\nIbn Wahb also narrated it from al-Layth ibn Saʿd.\n\nAnd perhaps the spreading (al-tafrīj) is more consistent with the form of sujūd"," and Allah"," the Most High"," knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"2714","(2714) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us: Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ, that he described the sujūd: he spread out his hands, raised his posterior, and hollowed (his back), and said: \Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to prostrate.\""\n\nAnd al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ"," Abū Tawbah"," said"," from Sharīk"," from Abī Isḥāq: \""Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib described it to us: he placed his hands"," leaned upon his knees"," raised his posterior"," and said: 'Thus the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to prostrate.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"2715","(2715) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ narrated it.\n\nAbū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān narrated to me, from his uncle Wāsiʿ ibn Ḥabbān, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he mentioned the hadith regarding sitting for the need (relieving oneself), and in it: \Then he said: 'Perhaps you are among those who pray upon their haunches.'\"" He said: \""I said: 'I do not know"," by Allah.'\"" He said: \""He meant the one who prostrates without rising from the ground"," i.e."," he prostrates while clinging to the ground.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it in al-Muwaṭṭaʾ.]"""
"2716","(2716) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal informed us: Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Baṣrī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from Shaqīq, who said: ʿAbdullāh, meaning Ibn Masʿūd, said: \Let none of you prostrate while resting upon his haunches or lying on his side"," for when one perfects the sujūd"," all of his bones prostrate.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it"," 2942.]"""
"2717","(2717) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that al-Layth narrated to me from Ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ that he was sitting with a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and we mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I am the one among you who best remembers the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He then mentioned the hadith"," and in it is: \""And when he prostrated"," he placed his hands without spreading them out and without clasping them"," and he directed the tips of his toes toward the qiblah.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 828.]"""
"2718","(2718) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānʾ informed us that Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Akhram informed us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and Abū Kurayb said that Abū Usāmah informed us that ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar informed me that Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ said: \I heard Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī saying: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer…'\"" — the hadith. And in it he said: \""Then he inclined toward the ground in prostration"," then he kept his upper arms away from his sides and spread the toes of his feet.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2719","(2719) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī in Marw informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʪsā al-Ṭarsūsī informed us that Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb informed me that ʿUmārah ibn Ghaziyyah said: \I heard Abū al-Naḍr saying that ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr said: ʿĀʾishah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," said: 'I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was with me on my bed"," and I found him prostrating"," his heels pressed together and the tips of his toes directed toward the qiblah"," and I heard him saying: \""I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your displeasure"," and in Your forgiveness from Your punishment"," and in You from You. I praise You but cannot encompass all that is in You.\""' When he finished"," he said: 'O ʿĀʾishah"," your devil has taken hold of you.' I said: 'Do you have a devil?' He said: 'There is no human being who does not have a devil.' I said: 'And you"," O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'And I too"," but I supplicated Allah against it and it submitted.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by more than one from ʿĀʾishah.]"""
"2720","(2720) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that Shuʿayb ibn al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed us that my father informed me.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Qutaybah informed us that al-Layth narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from Sumayy, the freedman of Abū Bakr, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complained to the Prophet ﷺ of the difficulty of prostration upon them when they spread their arms. He said: 'Seek support with the knees.'\"" Shuʿayb added in his narration that Ibn ʿAjlān said: \""That is"," one places one's elbows upon one's knees when one prolongs the prostration and becomes weary.\"" [Munkar. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 286.]"""
"2721","(2721) And Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Sufyān, meaning Ibn ʿUyaynah, narrated from Sumayy from al-Nuʿmān ibn Abī ʿAyyāsh, who said: \We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about leaning and supporting oneself in prayer"," and he granted them permission that a man may support himself with his elbows upon his knees or his thighs.\""\n\nAnd similarly Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Sumayy from al-Nuʿmān"," who said: \""The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ complained…\"" and he mentioned it as a mursal narration. Al-Bukhārī said: \""And this is more correct"," that it is mursal.\"" [Ḍaʿīf because it is mursal.]"""
"2722","(2722) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me that Abū Yaʿlā informed us that ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd and ʿUbayd Allāh al-Jushamī said that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us that ʿUbayd Allāh informed me that Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd narrated from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, in the story of the man who entered and performed the prayer badly until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him. In it he said: \Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration.\"" [Extracted in the two Ṣaḥīḥs. Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 757.]"""
"2723","(2723) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad ibn Fāris informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Hishām narrated from Qatādah from Anas that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Perfect the bowing and the prostration. For by the One in whose Hand is my soul"," I surely see you from behind my back when you bow and when you prostrate.\"" Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah from Qatādah.\n\nAnd there has already passed the ḥadīth of Abū Masʿūd that the Prophet ﷺ said: \""A prayer is not valid in which a man does not straighten his back in the bowing and the prostration.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 742.]"""
"2724","(2724) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us by dictation that Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿImrān al-Qāḍī in Harāt informed us that Abū Ḥātim ʿAbd al-Jalīl ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us that al-Aʿmash informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash, who said: \I heard ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr narrating from Abū Maʿmar al-Azdī from Abū Masʿūd al-Badrī from the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: 'A prayer is not valid for a man in which he does not straighten his back — or he said his spine — in the bowing and the prostration.'\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Shuʿbah.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of ʿUbayd Allāh: \""his back","\"" without doubt.\n\nAnd he said from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr from Abū Maʿmar from Abū Masʿūd"," who said: \""He said…\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 646.]"""
"2725","(2725) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr informed us that Isrāʾīl narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū Sufyān from Jābir that the Prophet ﷺ said: \A prayer is not valid in which a man does not straighten his back in the bowing and the prostration.\"" [Munkar.]"""
"2726","(2726) Abū al-Fatḥ Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ḥāfiẓ in Baghdad informed us that Abū ʿAlī ibn al-Ṣawwāf informed us that Abū ʿAlī Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us that Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Isḥāq informed us that Mahdī ibn Maymūn narrated from Wāṣil al-Aḥdab from Abū Wāʾil from Ḥudhayfah that he passed by a man praying who did not perfect his bowing or his prostration. He said to him: \How long have you been praying this prayer?\"" He said: \""For forty years","\"" or he said"," \""For such and such a time.\"" He said: \""You have not prayed a single prayer for Allah for such and such a time.\"" Mahdī said: \""And I think he said to him: 'If you were to die"," you would die upon other than the Sunnah of Muḥammad ﷺ.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ṣalt ibn Muḥammad from Mahdī ibn Maymūn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 389"," 791"," 808.]"""
"2727","(2727) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Abū ʀāṣim narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated from his father, from Tamīm ibn Maḥmūd, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shibl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade three things: pecking like a crow, spreading out like a predatory beast, and that a man should not make a fixed place for himself in which to pray as the camel makes its resting place. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Without his statement \and he should not make a fixed place…\"" — Aḥmad reported it"," 15617.]"""
"2728","(2728) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Ibn Milḥān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to me: al-Layth narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Jaʿfar ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥakam, from Tamīm ibn Maḥmūd, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shibl, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade in the prayer: spreading out like a predatory beast, pecking like a crow, and that a man should make a fixed place for standing as the camel makes its resting place. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Without his statement \and he should not make a fixed place…\"" — and it has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2729","(2729) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ibn Milḥān narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who narrated to me: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to me that he heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)… Then he mentioned the hadith until he said: Then he would say the takbīr when going down into prostration, then he would say the takbīr when raising his head, then he would say the takbīr when prostrating, then he would say the takbīr when raising his head. And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr, and Muslim reported it from another route from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī reported it, 789.]"
"2730","(2730) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us: Abū ʀāṣim narrated from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar, who narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʀṭāʾ, who said: I heard Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī among ten of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), among whom was Abū Qatādah. Then he mentioned the hadith describing the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said in it: Then he would go down to the ground, drawing his arms away from his sides, then he would raise his head, bending his left leg and sitting upon it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has preceded under no. 2642, 2643.]"
"2731","(2731) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbbād al-Farghānī narrated to us: Abū Badr narrated to us: Abū Khaythamah narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr narrated to us: ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mālik narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʀṭāʾ, one of the Banī Mālik, from ʿAbbās ibn Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, that he was in a gathering in which his father was present, and he was among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), and in the gathering were Abū Hurayrah, Abū Usayd, and Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī from among the Anṣār. They discussed the prayer, and Abū Ḥumayd said: \I am the most knowledgeable among you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" Then he mentioned the hadith. He said in it: Then he said"," \""Allāhu Akbar","\"" and prostrated"," supporting himself on his hands"," his knees"," and the tops of his feet while in prostration. Then he said the takbīr and sat"," drawing up one of his legs and placing his other foot upright. Then he said the takbīr and prostrated. And he mentioned the hadith.\n\nIt has also been said in its isnād that ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd Allāh heard it from ʿAbbās ibn Sahl"," that he was present with Abū Ḥumayd"," Abū Usayd"," and other men among them during the prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has preceded in the one before it"," and its original is in al-Bukhārī.]"""
"2732","(2732) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us: My grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Ṭāwūs saying: We asked Ibn ʿAbbās about sitting on the two heels (al-iqʿāʾ), and he said: \It is a Sunnah.\"" We said: \""We consider it harshness when a man does it.\"" He said: \""Rather"," it is the Sunnah of your Prophet Muḥammad (ﷺ).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim reported it"," 536.]"""
"2733","(2733) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Asīd ibn ʀāṣim narrated to us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated from Sufyān, from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \It is from the Sunnah of the prayer that your buttocks touch your heels.\""\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd al-ʿAdanī added in it from Sufyān: \""Between the two prostrations.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has a witness in the one before it.]"""
"2734","(2734) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us: Abū al-Azhar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: My father narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Najīḥ al-Makkī narrated to me about the standing of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on his heels and the tops of his feet between the two prostrations when he prayed, from Mujāhid ibn Jabr Abī al-Ḥajjāj, who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās mentioning it. I said to him: \O Abū al-ʿAbbās"," by Allah"," we used to count this as harshness on the part of the one who did it.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," it is a Sunnah.\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"2735","(2735) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from Khālid ibn Yazīd, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, that Abū al-Zubayr informed him that he saw ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, when he raised his head from the first prostration, sitting on the tips of his fingers, and he would say: \It is from the Sunnah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Ṭabarānī reported it in al-Awsaṭ"," 8752.]"""
"2736","(2736) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Muslim narrated to us: Hishām narrated to us: Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Mujāhid that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās used to sit on their heels (yaqiʿān). Abū al-Zubayr said: And Ṭāwūs used to sit on his heels. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah, 2942.]"
"2737","(2737) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Zuhayr — Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥudayj said: I saw Ṭāwūs sitting on his heels (yuqʿī), so I said: \I see you sitting on your heels (tuqʿī).\"" He said: \""You did not see me sitting on his heels (uqʿī); rather"," this is the Ṣalāh. I saw the three ʿAbādilah doing that: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās"," ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar"," and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr — they used to do it.\"" Abū Zuhayr said: \""And I indeed saw him sitting on his heels (yuqʿī).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. It has been cited as a witness for the one before it.]"""
"2738","(2738) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Shaybān al-Baghdādī al-Harawī informed us there: Muʿādh ibn Najdah narrated to us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ṣafwān al-Kūfī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahman narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim,\n\nfrom Ṭāwūs, who said: \I saw Ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿAbbās sitting on their heels (yuqʿīyān) between the two prostrations on the tips of their toes.\""\n\nIbrāhīm said: \""So I asked ʿAṭāʾ about that"," and he said: 'Whichever of the two you do will suffice you — if you wish"," on the tips of your toes"," and if you wish"," on your haunches (ʿajuz).'\""\n\nThis is the type of iqʿāʾ that is permitted or established as Sunnah"," according to what we have narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar: that one places the tips of the toes of his feet on the ground"," places his buttocks upon his heels"," and places his knees on the ground.\n\n[Ṣaḥīh]"""
"2739","(2739) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿUrubah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade iqʿāʾ in the Ṣalāh.\""\n\nḤammād ibn Salamah contradicted him.\n\n[Ḥasan for other than that (i.e."," strengthened by other chains).]"""
"2740","(2740) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Shaghānī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us: al-Sālaḥīnī narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Anas, that the Prophet ﷺ forbade iqʿāʾ and tawarruk in the Ṣalāh.\n\nYaḥyā ibn Isḥāq al-Saylaḥīnī is the only one who narrated it from Ḥammād ibn Salamah.\n\nIt has also been narrated from him from Ḥammād and Baḥr ibn Kathīr, from Qatādah, from Anas, but the first narration is more authentic.\n\n[Ḥasan]"
"2741","(2741) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Naysābūrī informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghayāth narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujāhid, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me with three things and forbade me from three things. He commanded me to fast three days of every month"," to sleep only after performing Witr"," and to pray the two rakʿahs of Ḍuḥā. And he forbade me from looking around in my prayer like a fox looks around"," from sitting (uqʿī) like a monkey sits"," and from pecking like a rooster pecks.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Witnesses for it have been cited previously under no. 2727.]"""
"2742","(2742) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Jaʿfar al-Muqriʾ informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Warrāq narrated to us: Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \O ʿAlī!\"" — and he mentioned the hadith"," in which he said: \""And do not sit on your heels (tuqʿ) between the two prostrations.\""\n\nAl-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar is not used as a proof"," and likewise Layth ibn Abī Sulaym. And the hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar is authentic.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2743","(2743) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, from Abī ʿUbayd, who narrated from Abī ʿUbaydah, who said: \Iqʿāʾ is that one presses his buttocks to the ground"," raises his shins"," and places his hands on the ground.\""\n\nAnd he said in another place: \""Iqʿāʾ is a person sitting on his buttocks with his thighs raised"," like the sitting of a dog or a predatory animal.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""This type of iqʿāʾ is different from what we have narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar. This type is forbidden"," whereas what we have narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar is established as Sunnah. As for the hadith of Abū al-Jazāʾ from ʿĀʿishah from the Prophet ﷺ — that he used to forbid 'the sitting of the devil' (ʿaqib al-shayṭān) and that he used to spread his left leg and erect his right leg — it is possible that this refers to the sitting for the final Tashahhud"," in which case it would not contradict what we have narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar regarding the sitting between the two prostrations. And Allah knows best.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh]"""
"2744","(2744) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī narrated to us: Mūsā ibn Hārūn narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ, Khalaf ibn Hishām, and Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us: Abū Muslim informed us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to them: Ḥammād narrated to us, from Thābit, who said: Anas said: \I would not fall short of praying among you as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying among us.\"" Thābit said: \""Anas used to do something that I do not see you doing. When he raised his head from Rukūʿ"," he would stand until one would say"," 'He has forgotten.' And when he raised his head between the two prostrations"," he would sit until one would say"," 'He has forgotten.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Muslim narrated it from Khalaf ibn Hishām.\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. Al-Bukhārī recorded it"," no. 821.]"""
"2745","(2745) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us, saying: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated to us, from Budayl ibn Mayṣarah, from Abū al-Jazāʾ, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ…\"" — and she mentioned the hadith describing his prayer. She said: \""When he raised his head from Rukūʿ"," he would not prostrate until he stood fully upright. And when he raised his head from Sujūd"," he would not prostrate again until he sat fully upright.\""\n\nMuslim recorded it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim.\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. Al-Bukhārī recorded it"," no. 823.]"""
"2746","(2746) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿĀrim narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us: Ayyūb narrated to us, from Abū Qilābah, that Mālik ibn al-Ḥuwayrith said to his companions: \Shall I not show you how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was?\"" — and that was at a time other than the time of prayer. So he stood"," then performed Rukūʿ and said the Takbīr"," then raised his head and stood for a while"," then prostrated"," then raised his head"," then waited for a while"," then prostrated.\n\nAbū Qilābah said: \""He prayed the prayer of our shaykh\"" — meaning ʿAmr ibn Salamah.\n\nAyyūb said: \""And ʿAmr used to do something that I do not see the people doing. When he raised his head from the second prostration in the first and third rakʿahs"," he would sit fully upright"," then stand.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿĀrim.\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. Al-Bukhārī recorded it"," no. 819.]"""
"2747","(2747) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAmr informed me; Fuḥayl narrated to me; ʿAbbās ibn Sahl narrated to me, saying: Abū Ḥumayd, Abū Usayd, Sahl ibn Saʿd, and Muslim ibn Maslamah gathered together and mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). Abū Ḥumayd said: \I know best among you the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"" He then described it"," and when he mentioned the prostration"," he said: \""Then he raised his head until every bone returned to its place.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2748","(2748) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Razzāz informed us from his original book; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Nuṣayr narrated to us; al-Ḥārith ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated to us; ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated to us; from Sālim, Abū ʿAbd Allāh, who said: ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr said: \Shall I not pray as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) praying?\"" We said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""So he stood to pray"," and when he bowed (rukūʿ)"," he placed his palms upon his knees"," positioned his fingers behind his knees"," and spread his armpits until every part of him settled. Then he raised his head and stood until every part of him settled. Then he prostrated and spread his armpits until every part of him settled. Then he sat until every part of him settled. He performed four rakʿahs in this manner"," then said: 'Thus did I see the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) pray"," and thus did he pray with us.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2749","(2749) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed me; ʿAmr ibn Murrah informed me; he heard Abū Ḥamzah narrating from a man from ʿAbs — Shuʿbah thought he was Ṣilah ibn Zufar — from Ḥudhayfah, who said: He prayed with the Prophet (peace be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith, saying: \And he used to say between the two prostrations: 'Rabbigh-fir lī"," Rabbigh-fir lī (O my Lord"," forgive me; O my Lord"," forgive me).' And he sat for a duration equal to his prostration.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2750","(2750) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Khālid ibn Yazīd al-Ṭabīb narrated to us; Kāmil ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us; from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit; from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr; from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \I spent the night with my aunt Maymūnah. The Prophet (peace be upon him) rose from his sleep","\"" and he mentioned the hadith regarding the prayer of the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," in which is: \""When he raised his head from prostration"," he said: 'Rabbigh-fir lī war-ḥamnī"," waj-burnī war-faʿnī war-zuqnī wahdinī (O my Lord"," forgive me"," have mercy upon me"," strengthen me"," raise me in rank"," provide for me"," and guide me).' Then he prostrated.\""\n\nZayd ibn al-Ḥubāb followed him in narrating from Kāmil"," and it was also narrated from Zayd with ʿāfinī (grant me well-being) instead of waj-burnī war-faʿnī. [Ḥasan. Abū Dāwūd narrated it as 850.]"""
"2751","(2751) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Sulaymān al-Taymī informed me, saying: \It reached me that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say between the two prostrations: 'Rabbigh-fir lī war-ḥamnī"," war-faʿnī waj-burnī (O my Lord"," forgive me"," have mercy upon me"," raise me in rank"," and strengthen me).'\""\n\nAl-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar narrated it from ʿAlī"," except that he said wahdinī (guide me) instead of war-faʿnī (raise me). [Ṣaḥīḥ. It is among the balāghāt of Sulaymān ibn Ṭarhān.]"""
"2752","(2752) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh; Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated to me; from his father; from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) entered the mosque. A man entered, prayed, then came and greeted the Prophet (peace be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) returned his greeting and said: \Go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" This happened three times. The man said: \""By the One Who sent you with the truth"," I cannot do better than this"," so teach me.\"" He said: \""When you stand for prayer"," say the takbīr"," then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qurʾān"," then bow until you are at ease in rukūʿ"," then raise your head until you stand upright"," then prostrate until you are at ease in sujūd"," then raise your head until you are at ease sitting"," then prostrate again until you are at ease in sujūd"," then do this throughout all your prayer.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muttafaq ʿalayh"," and it has been previously mentioned.]"""
"2753","(2753) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed me; al-Ḥakam informed me that when Maṭar ibn Nājiyah gained authority over Kūfah, he ordered Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd Allāh to lead the people in prayer. He led them in prayer, and when he raised his head from rukūʿ, he prolonged the standing (qiyām). I mentioned this to Ibn Abī Laylā, and he narrated from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) — when he prayed and bowed"," and when he raised his head from rukūʿ"," and when he prostrated"," and when he raised his head from sujūd between the two prostrations — was nearly equal in length.\""\n\nBoth narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it as 792.]"""
"2754","(2754) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Miqrīʾ al-Mihrajānī informed us with it; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Naṣr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; Miṣʿar narrated from al-Ḥakam; from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā; from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \The prostration of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," his rukūʿ"," and his sitting between the two prostrations were nearly equal in length.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm from Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2755","(2755) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us; Abū Kāmil and Musaddad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Musaddad narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAānah narrated to us; from Hilāl ibn Abī Ḥumayd; from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā; from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I observed Muḥammad (peace be upon him) in prayer and found his standing (qiyām)"," his bowing (rukūʿ)"," his rising upright after rukūʿ"," his prostration (sujūd)"," his sitting between the two prostrations"," his prostration"," and his sitting between the taslīm and departure to be nearly equal in length.\""\n\nThe wording is that of the hadith of Musaddad. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kāmil and Ḥāmid ibn ʿUmar"," except that he said in its text: \""His rukūʿ"," his rising upright after rukūʿ"," his sujūd"," his sitting between the two prostrations"," his sujūd"," and his sitting"," and his sitting between the taslīm and departure were nearly equal in length.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2756","(2756) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Aḥmad al-Julūdī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us; Ḥāmid ibn ʿUmar al-Bakrāwī and Abū Kāmil Fuḍayl ibn Ḥusayn al-Jaḥdarī both narrated to us from Abū ʿAānah. Ḥāmid said: \Abū ʀAānah narrated to us","\"" and it is as though the mention of one of the two sittings was missing from our narration; only Ḥāmid mentioned both of them. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2757","(2757) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us — my grandfather, Abu 'Amr, meaning Ibn Nujayd, informed us; and Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us — they both said: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi informed us: Abu al-Rabi' informed us: Hushaym informed us: Khalid al-Hadha' informed us, from Abu Qilabah, who informed us: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith al-Laythi, may Allah be pleased with him, said: He saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) praying, and when he was in an odd-numbered rakah of his prayer, he would not rise until he had settled sitting upright."
"2758","(2758) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn Sinan informed us: Abu 'Asim informed us, from 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, who said: Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ata' informed me, saying: I heard Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi, in a gathering of ten Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him), among whom was Abu Qatadah, narrate the hadith describing the prayer of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and in it he said: \Then he would return to prostration"," then he would rise and say: 'Allahu Akbar.' Then he would fold his leg and sit upon it"," upright"," until every bone returned to its place.\"""""
"2759","(2759) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Ahmad Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdan informed us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi informed us; and Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj informed us: Wuhaib informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith used to come to us in our mosque to pray with us, and he would say: \I am indeed praying with you"," though I do not intend the prayer; rather I wish to show you how I saw the Prophet (peace be upon him) praying.\"" Ayyub said: I said to Abu Qilabah: \""How was his prayer — i.e."," his prayer?\"" He said: \""Like the prayer of this shaykh of ours\"" — meaning 'Amr ibn Salamah. Ayyub said: \""And that shaykh used to complete the takbir"," and when he raised his head from the second prostration"," he would sit"," then lean upon the ground.\"""""
"2760","(2760) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed us: al-Hasani, meaning Ibrahim ibn Yusuf, and 'Imran, meaning Ibn Musa, both said: 'Uthman ibn Abay Shaybah informed us: 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi informed us: Khalid al-Hadha' informed us, from Abu Qilabah, that he narrated from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith: \He entered our mosque and said: 'I shall pray with you"," though I do not intend the prayer; rather I wish to teach you as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) praying.'\"" He said: \""He mentioned that when he raised his head from the prostration — meaning in the first rakah — he sat upright"," then he rose"," leaning upon the ground.\"""""
"2761","(2761) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us, from Khalid al-Hadha', from Abu Qilabah, with something similar, except that he said: \And when Malik raised his head from the final prostration in the first rakah"," he sat upright"," then rose"," leaning upon the ground.\"""""
"2762","(2762) Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajani informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzakki informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Malik informed us, from Sadaqah ibn Yasar, from al-Mughirah ibn Hakim, who said: He saw 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar rise from two prostrations of the prayer upon the tops of his feet. When he completed the prayer, I mentioned that to him, and he said: \It is not a sunnah of the prayer; I only do it because I suffer from fatigue.\"""""
"2763","(2763) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Saffar informed us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Sawti informed us: 'Affan ibn Muslim informed us: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad informed us: Sulayman al-A'mash said: I saw 'Umayr ibn 'Umayr praying near the gates of Kindah. I saw him bow, then prostrate, and when he rose from the final prostration, he stood as he was. When I mentioned that to him after he completed the prayer, he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid informed me that he saw 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud standing upon the tops of his feet in the prayer.\ Al-A'mash said: I narrated this hadith to Ibrahim al-Nakha'i"," and he said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid informed me that he saw 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud doing that. I narrated it to Khaythamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman"," and he said: I saw 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar standing upon the tops of his feet. I narrated it to Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd Allah al-Thaqafi"," and he said: I saw 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla standing upon the tops of his feet. I narrated it to 'Ata' al-'Awfi"," and he said: I saw Ibn 'Umar"," Ibn 'Abbas"," Ibn al-Zubayr"," and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri"," may Allah be pleased with them"," standing upon the tops of their feet in the prayer."""
"2764","(2764) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Abu Yahya Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Asad informed us: Sufyan informed us, from 'Ubaydah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: I observed Ibn Mas'ud and saw him rise upon the tops of his feet, and he would not sit when praying in the first rakah after completing the prostration. The shaykh, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: \It is authentically reported from Ibn Mas'ud"," but following the sunnah is more appropriate. And 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar clarified in the narration of al-Mughirah ibn Hakim from him that it is not from the sunnah of the prayer; he only did it because he suffered from fatigue.\"" And the narration of 'Ata' al-'Awfi is not to be used as evidence."""
"2765","(2765) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Nasr al-Khaffaf informed us: Ahmad ibn Salamah informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us. He said: I said to Abu Usamah: \Did 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar narrate to you from Sa'id al-Maqburi"," from Abu Hurayrah"," who said: 'A man entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was sitting in a corner of the mosque. He prayed"," then came and gave him salam"," and he said: \""Wa 'alayka"," go back and pray"," for you have not prayed.\"" He went back and prayed"," then came and gave him salam"," and he said the same to him. The third time"," he said: \""Teach me"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""When you stand for prayer"," perform wudu' thoroughly"," face the qiblah"," and say takbir. Then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur'an. Then bow until you are at rest in ruku'. Then raise your head until you are standing upright. Then prostrate until you are in prostration. Then raise your head until you are sitting at rest. Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration. Then sit until you are at rest. Then do that in every rakah and prostration.\""'\"" Abu Usamah confirmed it and said: \""Yes.\"" Thus said Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanazali from Abu Usamah"," and his narration is also from another chain from Abu Usamah"," and from another chain from Ibn Numayr."""
"2766","(2766) And the sahih narration is from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'id, Abu Qudamah, and Yusuf ibn Musa, from Abu Usamah: \Then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration"," then raise your head until you are settled sitting"," then prostrate until you are at rest in prostration"," then raise your head until you are standing upright. Then do that in all of your prayer.\"" Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' informed us: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us: 'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'id informed us: Abu Usamah informed us."""
"2767","(2767) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, he said: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Thaqafī informed us: Yūsuf ibn Mūsā informed us: Abū Usāmah — Ḥammād ibn Usāmah — informed us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated it in similar wording, and he said at its end: \Then raise (your head) until you stand upright.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr"," from Abū Usāmah"," using the wording of the ḥadīth of Yūsuf ibn Mūsā. And Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Abū Usāmah and Ibn Numayr"," except that he referred it to the narration of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān and did not cite the full text. And in the narration of Yaḥyā"," the second prostration is not mentioned"," nor what follows it of sitting or standing.\n\nAnd standing (qiyām) is more consistent with the purpose for which the report was cited — namely"," the enumeration of the pillars (arkān) rather than the recommended acts (sunan). And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2768","(2768) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk informed us: Yaḥyā informed us: al-Layth, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām informed me that he heard Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, say: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the prayer"," he would say the takbīr when he stood"," then he would say the takbīr when he bowed"," then he would say: 'Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah' (Allah hears the one who praises Him) when he raised his back from the rukūʿ"," then he would say while standing: 'Rabbanā wa laka al-ḥamd' (Our Lord"," to You is all praise). Then he would say the takbīr when he went down into prostration"," then he would say the takbīr when he raised his head"," then he would say the takbīr when he prostrated"," then he would say the takbīr when he raised his head. He would do that throughout the entire prayer until he completed it"," and he would say the takbīr when he stood up from the two (rakʿahs) after the sitting.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim reported it from the ḥadīth of Ibn Jurayj and ʿUqayl"," from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī reported it (789).]"""
"2769","(2769) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb informed us: Jarīr, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Sālim al-Barrād, who said: \We came to ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr al-Anṣārī — Abū Masʿūd — and we said to him: 'Tell us about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He stood before us in the mosque and said the takbīr. When he bowed"," he placed his hands upon his knees and positioned his fingers below that"," and he kept his elbows apart until every part of him was settled. Then he said: 'Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah.' He stood until every part of him was settled. Then he said the takbīr and prostrated"," placing his palms upon the ground"," then he kept his elbows away from his sides until every part of him was settled. Then he raised his head and sat until every part of him was settled. He did the same again. Then he prayed four rakʿahs like this rakʿah — he prayed his prayer — then he said: 'This is how we saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad (16633).]"""
"2770","(2770) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk al-Bazzār informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us: al-Layth, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \He was sitting with a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.\"" He said: \""We mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī said: 'I am the most knowledgeable among you regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I saw him: when he said the takbīr"," he placed his hands level with his shoulders; when he bowed"," he firmly placed his hands upon his knees"," then he bent his back; when he raised his head"," he straightened up until every vertebra returned to its place; when he prostrated"," he placed his hands without spreading them out or gripping them"," and he directed the tips of his toes (toward the qiblah); when he sat in the two rakʿahs"," he spread his legs"," then sat upon his left leg; and when he sat in the last rakʿah"," he brought out his left foot and sat upon his seat.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd reported it (730"," 963).]"""
"2771","(2771) As Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī informed us: Ḥammād ibn Shākir and Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl — al-Bukhārī — informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr informed us: al-Layth, from Khālid, from Saʿīd, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ. He said: \And al-Layth narrated to us"," from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb and Yazīd ibn Muḥammad"," from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah"," from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ"," that he was sitting with a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.\"" He said: \""Then he mentioned the ḥadīth.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Except that al-Bukhārī says in his narration: 'And he directed the tips of his toes toward the qiblah. When he sat in the two rakʿahs"," he sat upon his left foot and erected the right; and when he sat in the last rakʿah"," he brought out his left foot"," erected the other"," and sat upon his seat.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2772","(2772) And Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated it from al-Layth, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, and he said in its text: \When he sat in the first two (rakʿahs)"," he sat upon his left foot and erected his right foot; and when he sat in the last (rakʿah)"," he sat upon his buttocks"," and he placed the inner side of his left foot near the inner part of his right thigh"," and he erected his right foot.\""\n\nAbū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad informed us: Shabābah informed us: Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it"," except that he omitted Ibn Ḥalḥalah from its chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2773","(2773) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Ibn Lahīʿah informed you"," from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb and ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn al-Ḥārith"," from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah al-Duʾalī"," from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ"," from Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī"," who said: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: when he sat in the two rakʿahs"," he sat upon the sole of his left foot and erected the right; and when it was the fourth (rakʿah)"," he lowered his left hip to the ground and brought out his feet from one side.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd (731).]"""
"2774","(2774) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAmr informed me: Fulayḥ informed me: ʿAbbās ibn Sahl said: \Abū Ḥumayd"," Abū Usayd"," Sahl ibn Saʿd"," and Muḥammad ibn Salamah gathered and they mentioned the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abū Ḥumayd said: 'I am the most knowledgeable among you regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth and said in it: \""Then he sat and spread his left foot"," and directed the front of his right foot toward the qiblah. He placed his right palm upon his right knee and his left palm upon his left knee"," and he pointed with his finger.\"" This was regarding the first tashahhud"," and in his ḥadīth there is no mention of the last tashahhud. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd reported it (734).]"""
"2775","(2775) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz informed us: Abū ʿĀṣim, from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar, who said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr informed me, he said: \I heard Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī among ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ"," among them Abū Qatādah. Abū Ḥumayd said: 'I am the most knowledgeable among you regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it: \""Until"," when he was in the prostration in which is the taslīm"," he moved his left foot aside and sat mutawakkilan (in the tawarruk position) upon his left side.\"" They all said: \""You have spoken the truth; thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray.\""\n\nThis is explicit regarding the last tashahhud. In this narration"," the manner of sitting in the first tashahhud is not mentioned. Ibn Ḥalḥalah preserved both of them together from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr"," as has preceded. And in Allah is the success.\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of Abū al-Jazāʾ from ʿĀʾishah regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \""He would recite the tashahhud in the two rakʿahs of the taḥiyyah"," and he would spread his left foot and erect his right foot"," and he would forbid sitting in the manner of the devil (ʿaqib al-shayṭān).\""\n\nAnd the ḥadīth of Wāʾil ibn Ḥujr regarding the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ: \""Then he sat and spread his left foot.\""\n\nOne of them pertains to the last tashahhud and the other pertains to the first tashahhud"," by inference from the ḥadīth of Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī and his companions. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it (730).]"""
"2776","(2776) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī said: Muḥammad — meaning Ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī — informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, who informed him: \He used to see ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar sit cross-legged (yatarrakuʿ) in the prayer when he sat. I did that while I was at that time young in age"," so ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar forbade me and said: 'The Sunnah of the prayer is that you erect your right foot and fold the left.' I said: 'But you do that!' He said: 'My legs cannot bear me.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī"," from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik reported it in al-Muwaṭṭāʾ (202)"," and through his chain al-Bukhārī (827).]"""
"2777","(2777) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us, Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us from his father, who said: \It is from the Sunnah in prayer that you lay down your left foot and erect the right one.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 658]"""
"2778","(2778) Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-'Adl informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzaki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, when he sat in the tashahhud, would erect his right foot, fold his left foot, and sit upon his left hip, and he would not sit upon his feet. Then he said: \I saw 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar doing this"," and he narrated to me that his father used to do so.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Malik in al-Muwatta'"," 203]"""
"2779","(2779) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzaki and Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Siraj narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us, al-Shafi'i informed us, Malik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me, Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed me, Abu Musa — meaning Harun ibn Muhammad — narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: I read before Malik ibn Anas, from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam, from 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Mu'awi, who said: \Ibn 'Umar saw me playing with pebbles during prayer. When he finished"," he forbade me and said: 'Do as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do.' I said: 'How did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do?' He said: 'When he sat in prayer"," he placed his right hand upon his right thigh"," gathered all his fingers together"," pointed with the finger next to the thumb"," and placed his left hand upon his left thigh.'\"" This is the wording of al-Shafi'i's hadith. Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya with this wording. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik in al-Muwatta'"," 199; Abu Dawud"," 987]"""
"2780","(2780) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi informed us, Abu Hamid ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr and Abu al-Azhar narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he sat in prayer, placed his hands upon his knees, raised his right finger — the one next to the thumb — and supplicated with it, while his left hand was upon his left knee, spread upon it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi' and 'Abd ibn Humayd from 'Abd al-Razzaq. [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq, 3238; Muslim, 1337]"
"2781","(2781) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me, Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih narrated to us, Salih ibn Muhammad al-Razi narrated to us, 'Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us. And Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, 'Ali ibn 'Uthman al-Laḥiqi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he sat to recite the tashahhud"," placed his right hand upon his right thigh"," his left hand upon his left thigh"," and clasped thirty-three and fifty"," supplicating.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd ibn Humayd from Yunus ibn Muhammad from Hammad"," except that he said: \""He clasped thirty-three and fifty and pointed with the index finger.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad"," 6153; Muslim"," 1240]"""
"2782","(2782) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Musa — meaning Isma'il — narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid — meaning Ibn Ziyad — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me, Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Rib'i narrated to us, Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, 'Amir ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he sat in prayer"," placed his left foot between his thigh and his shin"," spread his right foot"," placed his left hand upon his left knee"," placed his right hand upon his right thigh"," and pointed with his finger.\""\n\nThis is the wording of Abu 'Abdullah's hadith. In the hadith of Ibn 'Abdan it says: \""He placed his right hand upon his right knee and pointed with a single finger.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Rib'i. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 1245; Ibn Khuzaymah"," 696]"""
"2783","(2783) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-'Anbari informed us, my grandfather Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Quraysh and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn 'Ali narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Amir ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he sat to supplicate"," placed his right hand upon his right thigh"," his left hand upon his left thigh"," pointed with his index finger"," placed his thumb upon his middle finger"," and rested his left palm upon his knee.\"" This is the wording of Abu Khalid al-Ahmar's hadith. In the narration of Ibn Sa'd: \""When he sat in prayer"," he placed his hand upon his knee and pointed with his finger.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah and from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated in the book of supplications from Abu Salih that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw Sa'd pointing with two fingers in prayer"," and he said: \""Point with one"," point with one.\""\n\nAnd this has been narrated through another connected chain in the chapter of supplication. [Sahih. Referred to in the preceding hadith]"""
"2784","(2784) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, 'Ali ibn Hamshadh narrated to us, and Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Ya'qub al-Thaqafi informed me, saying: Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Musaddad informed us, Khalid ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, that the Prophet (ﷺ) stood for prayer and pronounced the takbir, raised his hands until they were level with his ears, and took his left hand with his right hand. When he intended to bow, he raised his hands; when he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands; when he prostrated, he placed his hands and prostrated between them. Then he sat and placed his left hand upon his left thigh and his right elbow upon his right thigh. Then he clasped the little finger and the ring finger, formed a ring with the middle finger and the thumb, and pointed with the index finger. A group narrated its meaning from 'Asim ibn Kulayb.\n\nWe summarize it and prefer what we have narrated in the hadith of Ibn 'Umar, then what we have narrated in the hadith of Ibn al-Zubayr, due to the established nature of their reports, the strength of their chains, the excellence of their narrators, and their superiority in merit over 'Asim ibn Kulayb. And with Allah is success. [Hasan. Narrated by Abu Dawud through another chain, 726]"
"2785","(2785) Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Musa ibn al-Fadl informed us, Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Saffar al-Isbahani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Birti al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, 'Isam ibn Qudamah al-Bajali narrated to us, Malik ibn Numayr al-Khuza'i, one of the people of Basrah, informed us, that his father narrated to him: \He saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) seated in prayer"," placing his right forearm upon his right thigh"," raising his index finger"," having bent it slightly"," while supplicating.\"" [Da'if. Narrated by Abu Dawud through another chain"," 991]"""
"2786","(2786) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj said: Ziyad informed me, from Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Amir ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'Abdullah, who mentioned that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to point with his finger when he supplicated, without moving it.\n\nIbn Jurayj said: And I saw 'Amr ibn Dinar say: 'Amir informed me from his father that he saw the Prophet (ﷺ) supplicating in this manner, the Prophet (ﷺ) leaning with his left hand upon his left leg upon his thigh.\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Bashir ibn Mukassir from Ibn 'Ajlan.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Wa'il ibn Hujr. [Sahih. Narrated by Abu Dawud, 841, 989]"
"2787","(2787) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, he said: My father informed me that Wa'il ibn Hujr informed him, he said: I said, \I shall certainly observe the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)\"" — and he mentioned the hadith"," and said therein: Then he sat and spread out his left foot"," placed his left palm upon his left thigh and left knee"," and positioned the edge of his right elbow upon his right thigh. Then he folded three of his fingers and formed a ring"," then he raised his finger and I saw him moving it"," supplicating with it.\n\nIt is possible that the intended meaning of \""moving it\"" is gesturing with it"," rather than repeatedly moving it"," in which case it would be consistent with the narration of Ibn al-Zubayr. And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. [Hasan. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 714]"""
"2788","(2788) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i in Baghdad — narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, al-Waqidi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Moving the finger in prayer is a cause of agitation for Satan.\"" This was narrated uniquely by Muhammad ibn 'Umar al-Waqidi"," and he is not strong (in hadith).\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Mujahid that he said: A man moving his finger while seated in prayer is a means of subjugating Satan. [Very weak]"""
"2789","(2789) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn 'Umar, that he saw a man moving pebbles with his hand while he was in prayer. When he had finished, 'Abd Allah said to him: \Do not move the pebbles while you are in prayer"," for that is from Satan. But do as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do.\"" He said: \""And how was that?\"" He said: \""He placed his right hand upon his right thigh"," and pointed with his finger next to the thumb — the index finger — toward the qibla"," and he would direct his gaze toward it or near it.\"" Then he said: \""Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) do.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Nasa'i"," 1160]"""
"2790","(2790) Abu al-Hasan — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Muqri' — narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from 'Amir ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, that when the Prophet (ﷺ) sat in prayer, he placed his left palm upon his left thigh and his right palm upon his right thigh, and pointed with his index finger — his gaze would not exceed his pointing. [Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad, 16145]"
"2791","(2791) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, Nu'aym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to us, 'Amir ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from his father, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat after two (rak'ahs) or after four, he placed his hands upon his knees, then pointed with his finger. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Nasa'i, 1161]"
"2792","(2792) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Faqih — narrated to us, Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abu al-Asbagh — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Yahya — narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from 'Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Miqsam Abu al-Qasim, who said: A man from the people of Madinah narrated to me, he said: I prayed beside Khufaf ibn Ima' ibn Rahdah. He saw me pointing with my finger in prayer, so he said: \O son of my brother"," why do you do this?\"" I said: \""I have seen the best of people and their jurists doing it.\"" He said: \""You have spoken the truth. I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pointing with his finger when he sat to recite the tashahhud in his prayer. And the polytheists used to say: 'He is merely bewitching us.' But the Prophet (ﷺ) intended thereby Tawhid (the declaration of Allah's Oneness).\"" [Weak]"""
"2793","(2793) Abu Tahir al-Faqih narrated to us, he said: Abu Ja'far — Hamid ibn Bilal — narrated to us, Abu al-Azhar narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, 'Imran ibn Abi Anas — one of the Banu 'Amir ibn Lu'ayy, and he was trustworthy — narrated to me, from Abu al-Qasim — Miqsam, the freed slave of 'Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal — who said: A man from the people of Madinah narrated to me, he said: I prayed in the mosque of Banu Ghifar. And he mentioned his sitting, and said: I placed my left hand upon my left thigh, and I placed my right hand upon my right thigh, and I raised my index finger. Khufaf ibn Ima' ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari — who had been a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — saw me doing that. When I had finished my prayer, he said to me: \Why did you raise your finger like that?\"" I said to him: \""I saw the people doing it.\"" He said: \""Then you have spoken the truth. Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he prayed"," would do that. And the polytheists used to say: 'Muhammad only does this with his finger to bewitch us.' But they lied. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) only did that to declare the Tawhid of his Lord"," the Blessed and Most High.\"" [Weak. And it has been mentioned in the one before it]"""
"2794","(2794) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abi Ishaq, from al-'Ayzar, who said: Ibn 'Abbas was asked about a man who supplicates, pointing with his finger. Ibn 'Abbas said: \It is sincerity (ikhlas).\"" [Weak]"""
"2795","(2795) And al-Thawri narrated it in al-Jami' from Abi Ishaq, from al-Tamimi — who is Arbadah — from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \It is sincerity (ikhlas).\"" And from Aban ibn Abi 'Ayyash"," from Anas ibn Malik"," who said: \""That is humility (tadarru').\"" And from 'Uthman"," from Mujahid"," who said: \""It is a means of subjugating Satan.\""\n\nAbu Bakr ibn Ibrahim narrated to us"," Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us"," Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us"," 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us"," 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us"," from Sufyan"," and he mentioned them. [Weak]"""
"2796","(2796) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from 'Abbas ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ma'bad ibn 'Abbas, from his brother Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Ma'bad, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \This is sincerity (ikhlas)\"" — and he pointed with his finger next to the thumb — \""and this is supplication (du'a')\"" — and he raised his hands level with his shoulders — \""and this is earnest imploring (ibtihal)\"" — and he raised his hands fully extended. [Munkar. Narrated by al-Hakim"," 8017]"""
"2797","(2797) Abu Ahmad — Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-'Adl — informed us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah — informed us: Yazid ibn Harun — informed us: Husayn al-Mu'allim — from Budayl ibn Maysarah — from Abu al-Jawza' — from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to… — and she mentioned the hadith regarding the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ, saying: He would recite the tahiyyat (greeting) between every two rak'ahs."
"2798","(2798) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari — informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah — informed us: Abu Dawud — informed us: Mu'mal ibn Hisham — informed us: Isma'il — from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Ali ibn Yahya ibn Khallad ibn Rafi' — informed me — from his father — from his uncle, Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' — from the Prophet ﷺ, who mentioned the hadith of the prayer and said regarding it: When you stand in your prayer, say Allahu Akbar (Allah is the Most Great), then recite whatever is easy for you from the Qur'an. And he said therein: When you sit in the middle of the prayer, be at rest, spread out your left thigh, then recite the tashahhud (testification), and when you stand, do likewise until you complete your prayer."
"2799","(2799) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya — Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Muzakki — both of them said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: Bahr ibn Nasser — who said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf — informed you — from his father — from Abu 'Ubaydah — from his father, 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was in the first two rak'ahs, was as though he were upon hot stones. He (the narrator) said: Until he stood up? He said: Until he stood up."
"2800","(2800) Abu Zakariyya and Abu Bakr — both of them said: Abu al-'Abbas — informed us: al-Rabi' — informed us: al-Shafi'i — informed us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ibn Ibrahim — and he mentioned it with the same meaning. And Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj narrated it similarly from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim."
"2801","(2801) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz — informed us: Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani — informed us: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa — informed us: Abu al-Yaman — informed us: Shu'ayb — from al-Zuhri — who informed me: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmaz, the mawla of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, informed him that 'Abd Allah ibn Uhaynah ibn Azd Shanu'ah — who was an ally of Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn 'Abd Manaf and was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ led them in the Zuhr (noon) prayer. He stood in the first two rak'ahs and did not sit, and the people stood with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he completed the prayer. The people waited for him to give the salam (greeting of peace), but he said Allahu Akbar while sitting, then prostrated twice before giving the salam, and then gave the salam."
"2802","(2802) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-'Alawi — informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Simsar — informed us: Hamid ibn Abi Hamid al-Mu'addi — informed us: Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi — informed us: Sufyan ibn Sa'id — from Yahya ibn Sa'id — from al-A'raj — from 'Abd Allah ibn Uhaynah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood in the two rak'ahs and did not sit, then he prostrated the two prostrations of sahw (forgetfulness)."
"2803","(2803) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan — informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar — informed us: Ibn Milhan — informed us: Yahya — informed us: Ibn Bukayr — informed us: al-Layth — from 'Uqayl — from Ibn Shihab, who said: Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham — informed me — that he heard Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stood for the prayer… — and he mentioned the hadith, saying: He would say Allahu Akbar when he stood up from the two rak'ahs after sitting."
"2804","(2804) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari — informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah — informed us: Abu Dawud al-Sijistani — informed us: Sulayman ibn Harb — informed us: Hammad — (h) and Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz — informed me: Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih — informed us: Muhammad ibn Nasser — informed us: Yahya ibn Yahya — informed us: Hammad ibn Zayd — from Ghaylan ibn Jarir — from Mutarrif, who said: I and 'Imran ibn Husayn prayed behind 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him. When he prostrated, he said Allahu Akbar; when he raised his head, he said Allahu Akbar; and when he rose from the two rak'ahs, he said Allahu Akbar. When he completed the prayer, 'Imran took my hand and said: This has reminded me of the prayer of Muhammad ﷺ — or he said: He has prayed with us like the prayer of Muhammad ﷺ. (These are the words of the hadith of Yahya ibn Yahya. In the hadith of Sulayman, it reads: When we finished, 'Imran took my hand.)"
"2805","(2805) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz — informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq — informed us: Musa ibn Ishaq — informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Shaybah — informed us: 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi — from Khalid — from Abu Qilabah, who said: Malik ibn al-Huwayrith used to come to us and say: Shall I not narrate to you about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He would pray at a time other than the prescribed prayer time. When he raised his head from the second prostration of the first rak'ah, he would sit upright and lean upon the ground."
"2806","(2806) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah — informed us: Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Shayban al-Baghdadi, in Harat — informed us: Mu'adh ibn Najdah — informed us: Kamil ibn Talhah — informed us: Hammad, that is Ibn Salamah — from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I saw Ibn 'Umar, when he rose from the two rak'ahs, lean upon the ground with his hands. I said to his son and to his companions: Perhaps he does this due to old age? They said: No, but this is what he would do. And it has been narrated to us from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar that he would lean upon his hands when he rose. And al-Hasan and more than one of the Tabi'un (Successors) used to do likewise."
"2807","(2807) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammādābādī dictated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar reported on the authority of Ismāʿīl ibn Umayya, from Nāʿif, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to lean upon his hand during Ṣalāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by ʿAbd al-Razzāq.]"
"2808","(2808) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Shabbawayh, Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ, and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Ghazzāl said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us from Maʿmar. He mentioned it with its chain of narration, similar to it.\n\nAnd in the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Shabbawayh it is: \He forbade a man to lean upon his hand during Ṣalāh.\""\n\nAnd Ibn Rāfiʿ said: \""He forbade a man to pray while leaning upon his hand.\""\n\nAnd Ibn ʿAbd al-Malik said: \""He forbade a man to lean upon his hands when he rises during Ṣalāh.\""\n\nThis is a ḥadīth in which there is a difference in its text (matn) as reported from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\nAnd Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal reported it from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," as Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us"," Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us"," Abū Dāwūd narrated to us"," and Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned.]"""
"2809","(2809) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated, and he mentioned it with its chain of narration, and said in the text of the ḥadīth: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade"," when a man sits in Ṣalāh"," that he lean upon his left hand.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad. And in the narration of Abū Dāwūd: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to sit in Ṣalāh while leaning upon his hand.\""\n\nThis is the clearest of the narrations"," and the narration of other than Ibn ʿAbd al-Malik does not contradict it"," even though it is clearer than it. And the narration of Ibn ʿAbd al-Malik is a confusion (wahm). And that which indicates that the narration of Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal is the one intended by the ḥadīth is that Hishām ibn Yūsuf reported it from Maʿmar likewise. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned.]"""
"2810","(2810) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Hishām reported from Maʿmar, from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayya, from Nāʿif, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Prophet ﷺ forbade a man who was sitting, leaning upon his left hand during Ṣalāh, and he said: \Indeed"," it is the prayer of the Jews.\"" And that which indicates this also is what… [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned.]"""
"2811","(2811) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥurfī informed us in Baghdad, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn reported from Hishām ibn Saʿd, who said: I heard Nāʿif saying: ʿAbd Allāh saw a man praying, fallen upon his knees, leaning upon his left hand, and he said: \Do not pray like this. Indeed"," those who are punished sit like this.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2812","(2812) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Abū Muʿāwiya reported from Abī Shayba, from Ziyād ibn Zayd, from Abī Juḥayfa, from ʿAlī, who said: \Indeed"," it is from the Sunnah in the obligatory prayer that when a man rises in the first two rakaʿāt"," he should not lean upon his hands upon the ground"," unless he is an elderly man who is unable (to do otherwise).\""\n\nThis Abū Shayba is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq al-Wāsiṭī al-Qurashī. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," and others narrated it"," reporting it sometimes thus"," and sometimes from al-Nuʿmān ibn Saʿd"," from ʿAlī. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2813","(2813) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shayba narrated to us, Ibn Fuḍayl reported from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq, from al-Nuʿmān ibn Saʿd, from ʿAlī, who said: \It is from the Sunnah that you do not lean upon your hands when you wish to stand after sitting in the two rakaʿāt.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2814","(2814) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Yūsuf ibn Khālid narrated to us, Ḥusayn ibn Muʿādh narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥīrī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Bishr ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā reported from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāʿif, that Ibn ʿUmar, when he entered into Ṣalāh, he pronounced the takbīr and raised his hands; and when he bowed (rukūʿ), he raised his hands; and when he said \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","\"" he raised his hands; and when he stood up from the two rakaʿāt"," he raised his hands. And Ibn ʿUmar attributed that to the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī reported it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAyāsh"," from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā. And ʿAbd al-Aʿlā is alone in raising it to the Prophet ﷺ"," and he is trustworthy (thiqah).\n\nAnd that has also been narrated in the ḥadīth of Abī Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by al-Bukhārī"," 739.]"""
"2815","(2815) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us, Abū Usāma narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ said: I heard Abū Ḥumayd saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stood for Ṣalāh, he faced the qiblah, then raised his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders, then he said: \Allāhu Akbar.\"" And when he bowed"," he pronounced the takbīr when he bowed"," and raised his hands"," then straightened his back"," neither lowering it nor raising it excessively. Then he raised his head and said: \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah.\"" Then he raised his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders. Then he stood upright until every limb returned to its place"," balanced. Then he did likewise in the other rakaʿah"," until when he stood from the two rakaʿāt"," he pronounced the takbīr and raised his hands as he had done at the beginning of the Ṣalāh"," until when it was the Ṣajdah which was the dissolution of the Ṣalāh"," he raised his head therein and sat mutawarrikan (with the left foot under and the right foot upright). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Abū Dāwūd"," 730.]"""
"2816","(2816) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz informed us, Abū ʿĀṣim reported from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar, who said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to me, saying: I heard Abū Ḥumayd al-Sāʿidī among ten of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among them Abū Qatāda al-Ḥārith ibn Ribʿī, and Abū Ḥumayd said: \I am the most knowledgeable among you of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" Then he mentioned the ḥadīth and mentioned in it: \""He raised his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders when he stood for Ṣalāh"," at the time of bowing (rukūʿ)"," and at the time of raising the head from it.\"" He said: \""Then when he stood from the two rakaʿāt"," he pronounced the takbīr and raised his hands until he brought them level with his shoulders"," as he did when he pronounced the takbīr at the opening of the Ṣalāh. Then he did likewise in the remainder of his prayer.\""\n\nAnd that has been narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālih"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2817","(2817) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us; Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Hāshimī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād narrated from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Faḍl al-Hāshimī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālli"
"2818","(2818) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd, Khalīl ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Bustī al-Qāḍī — who came to us to Naysābūr as a pilgrim — informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn al-Muẓaffar al-Bakrī informed us; Ibn Abī Khaythamah narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from Shaqīq, who said:\n\nʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"
"2819","(2819) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us by dictation; Abū ʿUbayd Allāh al-Makhzūmī Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Aʿmash and Manṣūr, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Masʿūd, who said:\n\nWe used to say before the tashahhud was made obligatory: \Peace be upon Allah; peace be upon Jibrīl and Mīkāʾīl.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do not say it thus"," for indeed Allah — He is al-Salām. Rather"," say: 'All compliments"," prayers"," and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and His Messenger.'\""\n\nʿAlī said: This is a ṣaḥīḥ isnād.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]\n\n---"""
"2820","(2820) Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓufar ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAlawī narrated to us by dictation; and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ in Naysābūr, and Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah — both reciting to them — said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah informed us; al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us; Sayf ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. He said: I heard Mujāhid say: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sakhrat Abū Maʿmar narrated to me. He said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd say:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me the tashahhud with my hands between his hands, just as he would teach me a sūrah from the Qurʾān: \All compliments"," prayers"," and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and His Messenger.\"" This was during his lifetime among us. When he passed away"," we said: \""Peace be upon the Prophet.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Abī Nuʿaym. It has also been narrated from Mujāhid"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the tashahhud.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It has a strong shāhid (witness) in ʿAbd al-Razzāq. Fatḥ al-Bārī"," 831.]\n\n---"""
"2821","(2821) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqrīʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us. Both said: Naṣr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Abī Bishr. He said: I heard Mujāhid narrate from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, regarding the tashahhud: \All compliments"," prayers"," and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah.\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: I added therein: \""and His blessings.\"" \""Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah.\"" Ibn ʿUmar said: I added therein: \""alone"," without partner.\"" \""And I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and His Messenger.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Dāwūd.\n\nIbn Abī ʿAdī narrated it from Shuʿbah and made it mawqūf"," except that he attributed it to the lifetime of the Prophet ﷺ"," saying: We used to say it during his lifetime"," and when he died we said: \""Peace be upon the Prophet and the mercy of Allah.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī considered the narration of Sayf from Mujāhid from Abī Maʿmar from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd to be the preserved one"," over the narration of Abī Bishr. And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best.\n\nIt has also been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bābī"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," except that he delayed his saying \""to Allah","\"" and added in the original: \""and His blessings.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated from Zayd al-ʿAmmī from Abī al-Ṣiddīq al-Nājī from Ibn ʿUmar from Abī Bakr"," in an abridged form.\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: As for what…\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dāraquṭnī said: This is a ṣaḥīḥ isnād.]\n\n---"""
"2822","(2822) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib and Mūsā ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād, from Bakr ibn Sawādah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"
"2823","(2823) Likewise, Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Tamtām narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād ibn Anʿam narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ and Bakr ibn Sawādah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When a man raises his head from prostration at the end of his prayer and then breaks his wuḍūʾ before he says the salām"," his prayer is valid.\""\n\nLikewise"," al-ʿAdanī narrated it from al-Thawrī from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād from both of them: \""When the imām sits and then breaks his wuḍūʾ before he says the salām"," his prayer is complete.\""\n\nMuʿādh ibn al-Ḥakam narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād and added therein: \""and he had completed his tashahhud therein.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād is al-Afrīqī. Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān"," ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī"," Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," and others of the imāms of ḥadīth declared him weak. There has been disagreement regarding him. It is mentioned with its defects in the book of al-Khilāf.\n\n[Weak.]\n\n---"""
"2824","(2824) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī both said: Shuʿbah narrated to us. He said: I heard Muslim Abū al-Naḍr say: I heard Ḥamlah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān say: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"
"2825","(2825) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us. He said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Muḥammad ibn Naṣr — said: ʿAlī ibn Saʿīd narrated to me. He said: I asked Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal about one who omits the tashahhud. He said: \He should repeat it.\"" I said: \""And the ḥadīth of ʿAlī — 'whoever sits for the duration of the tashahhud'?\"" He said: \""It is not authentic.\""\n\n[Ḥasan.]\n\n---"""
"2826","(2826) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Nasāʾī informed us in Egypt.\n\nAnd Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us by dictation; Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn Firās al-Mālikī informed us; Mūsā ibn Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh Abū ʿImrān al-Bazzāz narrated to us. Both said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Abī al-Zubayr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he used to teach us the Qurʾān. He would say: \All compliments"," blessed words"," prayers"," and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muḥammad is the Messenger of Allah.\""\n\nThe wording of both their ḥadīths is the same.\n\nMuslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others. He said in the wording of the ḥadīth of Qutaybah: \""Just as he would teach us a sūrah from the Qurʾān.\"" And he narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥumayd from Abī al-Zubayr from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās in an abridged form.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 2665.]"""
"2827","(2827) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr, who is al-Ramādī, narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Qatādah, from Yūnus ibn Jubayr, from Ḥiṭṭān ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that Abū Mūsā led the people in prayer. When he sat (for the tashahhud), a man said: \Al-ṣalātu uqirrāt bil-birri wa al-zakāh\"" (Prayer has been established with righteousness and purity). When Abū Mūsā completed the prayer (turned the salām)"," he said: \""Which one of you said such-and-such a word?\"" The people remained silent. Then he said again: \""Which one of you said such-and-such a word?\"" The people remained silent. Abū Mūsā then said: \""O Ḥiṭṭān"," perhaps you are the one who said it?\"" He (Ḥiṭṭān) said: \""By Allah"," I did not say it"," and I was afraid that you would reproach me for it.\"" Then a man stood up and said: \""I am the one who said it"," and I intended nothing but good by it.\"" Abū Mūsā then said: \""Do you not know how you should pray? Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us and taught us our prayer and explained to us our Sunnah"," saying: 'When you pray"," straighten your rows. When the imām says the takbīr"," say the takbīr. When he says {Ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā ḍ-ḍāllīn}"," say Āmīn"," and Allah will respond to you. When he says the takbīr and bows"," say the takbīr and bow"," for the imām says the takbīr before you and rises before you.'\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""That is in exchange for that (i.e."," the time he bows before you is compensated by the time he rises before you). And when he says Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah"," say Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd. And when it is time for sitting"," let the first thing any of you say be: Al-taḥiyyātu al-ṭayyibātu al-zākiyātu lillāh. Al-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh (All compliments"," pure words"," and devotions are for Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger).'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh and others"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad (19017"," 19098"," 19130)"," Abū Dāwūd (972)"," and Muslim (404).]"""
"2828","(2828) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Hishām narrated from Qatādah, from Yūnus ibn Jubayr, from Ḥiṭṭān ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Raqāshī, that al-Ashʿarī led his companions in a prayer. When he sat during his prayer, a man behind him said: \Uqirrati al-ṣālātu bil-birri wa al-zakāh\"" (Prayer has been established with righteousness and purity). When al-Ashʿarī completed his prayer"," he said: \""Which one of you said such-and-such a word?\"" The people fell silent. He then said to me: \""O Ḥiṭṭān"," perhaps you said it?\"" I said: \""I did not say it"," and I was afraid that you would reproach me for it.\"" Al-Ashʿarī then said: \""Do you not know what you say during your prayer? Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us and taught us our Sunnah"," and explained to us our prayer"," saying: 'Straighten your rows"," then let one of you lead you. When the imām says the takbīr"," say the takbīr. When he recites {Ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā ḍ-ḍāllīn}"," say Āmīn"," and Allah will respond to you. When he bows"," bow"," for the imām bows before you and rises before you.' The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'That is in exchange for that. And when he says Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah"," say Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd"," and Allah will hear you"," for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said through the tongue of His Prophet: Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah. When he says the takbīr and prostrates"," say the takbīr and prostrate"," for the imām prostrates before you and rises before you.' The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'That is in exchange for that. And when it is time for the sitting"," let the first words of any of you be: Al-taḥiyyātu al-ṭayyibātu al-ṣalawātu lillāh. Al-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāh. Al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh wa anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh (All compliments"," pure words"," and prayers are for Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger).'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"," Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," and Abī ʿAwanah"," from Qatādah"," with this wording"," except that they did not mention his statement: \""For Allah said through the tongue of His Prophet: Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah\"" — except in the narration of Abī ʿAwanah"," and it is also mentioned in the narration of ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," though it is not in what we have narrated from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. As mentioned in the preceding narration.]"""
"2829","(2829) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Ayman ibn Nābil narrated from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to teach us the tashahhud: \Bismillāhi wa billāh. Al-taḥiyyātu lillāh wa al-ṣalawātu wa al-ṭayyibāt. Al-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh. Asʾalu Allāha al-jannata"," wa aʿūdhu bihi min al-nār (In the name of Allah and through the grace of Allah. All compliments"," prayers"," and pure words are for Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. I ask Allah for Paradise"," and I seek refuge in Him from the Fire).\""\n[Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Mājah (902).]"""
"2830","(2830) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Muslim informed us: Abū ʿĀṣim informed us: Ayman ibn Nābil narrated to us: Abī al-Zubayr narrated it with the same meaning, and added: \Just as he would teach us a sūrah from the Qurʾān","\"" and he said: \""Al-taḥiyyātu lillāh"," al-ṣalawātu al-ṭayyibātu lillāh (All compliments are for Allah; the prayers and pure words are for Allah).\"" And at the end he said: \""Nasʾalu Allāha al-jannata"," wa naʿūdhu bihi min al-nār (We ask Allah for Paradise"," and we seek refuge in Him from the Fire).\""\n\nAyman ibn Nābil is alone in narrating this from Abī al-Zubayr"," from Jābir.\n\nAbū ʿĪsā said: I asked al-Bukhārī about this ḥadīth"," and he said: \""It is an error. The correct narration is what al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated from Abī al-Zubayr"," from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and Ṭāwūs"," from Ibn ʿAbbās.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥumayd al-Ruʾāsī likewise narrated it from Abī al-Zubayr"," similar to what al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated. It has also been narrated"," in one of the two narrations"," from ʿUmar"," Ibn ʿUmar"," and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them).\n[Munkar. As mentioned in the preceding narration.]"""
"2831","(2831) As for the narration from ʿUmar: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Khuzāʿī informed us in Makkah from the original of his book: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to teach the people the tashahhud in prayer while he was addressing the people from the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He would say: \When any of you sits for the tashahhud"," let him say: Bismillāhi khayri al-asmāʾ. Al-taḥiyyātu al-zākiyātu al-ṣalawātu al-ṭayyibātu lillāh. Al-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," wa anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh (In the name of Allah"," the best of names. All pure compliments"," prayers"," and devotions are for Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone"," with no partner"," and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger).\""\n\nʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Begin with yourselves (by sending salām) after the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and then send salām upon the righteous servants of Allah.\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrated it from al-Zuhrī and Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from ʿUrwah"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī"," from ʿUmar"," and he mentioned the tasmiyah (saying Bismāllāh) in it and added: \""He placed some things before and others after","\"" and that will be addressed"," if Allah the Most High wills.\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2832","(2832) As for the narration from Ibn ʿUmar: Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Nāʿif, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to recite the tashahhud, saying: \Bismillāh. Al-taḥiyyātu lillāh wa al-ṣalawātu al-zākiyātu lillāh. Al-salāmu ʿalā al-Nabiyyi wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn. Shahidtu an lā ilāha illā Allāh. Shahidtu anna Muḥammadan rasūlullāh (In the name of Allah. All compliments are for Allah"," and the pure prayers are for Allah. Peace be upon the Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah).\"" He would say this in the first two rakʿahs"," and he would supplicate after completing his tashahhud with whatever he wished. When he sat in the last rakʿah of his prayer"," he would likewise recite the tashahhud"," except that he would place the tashahhud first"," then supplicate with whatever he wished. When he completed his tashahhud and wished to say the salām"," he would say: \""Al-salāmu ʿalā al-Nabiyyi wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn. Al-salāmu ʿalaykum","\"" turning to his right. Then he would return the salām to the imām. If someone on his left said salām to him"," he would respond to him.\n[Ṣaḥīf. Mawqūf (stopped at the Companion).]"""
"2833","(2833) As for the narration from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us: Abū al-Azhar narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: My father narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to me, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, who said: He (the Prophet ﷺ) used to say one and the same thing in the tashahhud during the prayer, whether in the middle or at the end: \Bismillāh. Al-taḥiyyātu lillāh"," al-ṣalawātu lillāh"," al-zākiyātu lillāh. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh. Al-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn (In the name of Allah. All compliments are for Allah"," the prayers are for Allah"," the pure devotions are for Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah).\"" And he would count it for us on his fingers"," according to the count of the Arabs.\n\nIt has also been narrated from al-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar"," from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him).\n[Munkar.]"""
"2834","(2834) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhabārī al-Faqīh in Naysābūr and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us, both saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Isrāʾīl, from Abī Isḥāq, from al-Ḥārith, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), that when he sat for the tashahhud, he would say: \Bismillāh (In the name of Allah).\""\n\nIt has also been narrated from Wakīʿ"," from al-Aʿmash"," from Abī Isḥāq"," from al-Ḥārith"," that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say when he sat for the tashahhud: \""Bismillāhi wa billāh (In the name of Allah and through the grace of Allah).\"" (c) However"," al-Ḥārith is not a valid authority for such a narration.\n\nThe well-known connected narration from al-Zuhrī"," from ʿUrwah"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Qārī"," from ʿUmar"," does not contain any mention of the tasmiyah (saying Bismillāh).\n\nLikewise"," the authentic narration from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," from al-Qāsim"," from ʿĀʾishah"," does not contain any mention of the tasmiyah"," except what Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār is alone in narrating.\n\nAs for the narration from Ibn ʿUmar"," even though it is authentic"," it is possible that the tasmiyah was an addition on the part of Ibn ʿUmar"," for we have narrated from him"," from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," the ḥadīth of the tashahhud in which there is no mention of the tasmiyah. And Allah knows best.\n\nThābit ibn Zuhayr narrated from Nāʿif"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," and from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," from ʿĀʾishah — both of them from the Prophet (ﷺ) — regarding the tasmiyah before the taḥiyyāh. (c) However"," Thābit ibn Zuhayr is munkar al-ḥadīth (his narrations are rejected) and ḍaʿīf (weak). The authentic narration from Ibn ʿUmar is mawqūf (stopped at the Companion)"," as we have narrated. We have also narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that he heard a man saying \""Bismillāh"," al-taḥiyyātu lillāh","\"" and he rebuked him.\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2835","(2835) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim al-Zāhid narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Ibn Juʿshum narrated to us: Sufyān, who is al-Thawrī, narrated from Dāwūd, from Abī al-ʿĀliyah, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard a man, when he sat in prayer, saying \Al-ḥamdu lillāh\"" before the tashahhud. He rebuked him and said: \""Begin with the tashahhud.\""\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (3058).]"""
"2836","(2836) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, both saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated from Miʿsar, from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, who said: I said to Ibrāhīm: \Should I say Bismillāh in the tashahhud?\"" He said: \""Say: Al-taḥiyyātu lillāh (All compliments are for Allah).\"" He said: I said: \""Should I say Al-ḥamdu lillāh?\"" He said: \""Say: Al-taḥiyyātu lillāh.\"" He said: Saʿīd ibn Jubayr used to say"," when reciting the tashahhud: \""Bismillāh.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Rūdhabārī.\n[Ṣaḥīf.]"""
"2837","(2837) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original source: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us: Abū al-Azhar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: my father informed us, from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī and Hishām ibn ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr — both of them informed me — from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, who had been appointed by ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb as overseer of the Bayt al-Māl, who said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) teaching the people the Tashahhud in prayer while he was upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), saying: \O people"," when any one of you sits to make the salām at the end of his prayer or recites the Tashahhud in its middle"," let him say: 'Bismillāhi Khayri al-Asmā' — All praise"," all prayers"," all pure words"," and all blessed devotions belong to Allah — four [phrases]. O people"," I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah"," and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. The Tashahhud"," O people"," comes before the Salām. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah.' And let none of you say: 'Peace be upon Jibrīl"," peace be upon Mīkā'īl"," peace be upon the angels of Allah.' For when one says: 'Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah","' he has thereby sent peace upon every righteous servant of Allah in the heavens or on the earth. Then let him make the salām.\""\n\nThe hadith of Ibn Shihāb and the hadith of Hishām ibn ʿUrwah differed only in that Ibn Shihāb said: \""al-Zākiyāt\"" (the pure ones)"," while Hishām said: \""al-Mubārakāt\"" (the blessed ones). Ibn Isḥāq said: \""And I do not see except that Hishām was the more retentive of the two in what he adhered to.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Thus did Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār narrate it. And it was narrated by Mālik"," Maʿmar"," Yūnus ibn Yazīd"," and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith"," from Ibn Shihāb — they did not mention the Tasmiyyah (the phrase \""Bismillāh\"") in it"," and they placed the two words of the Salām before the two words of the Shahādah. And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. [Munkar]"""
"2838","(2838) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Zakariyyā, and Abū Bakr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, saying: it was read to Ibn Wahb: Mālik ibn Anas, Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed you that Ibn Shihāb informed them, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, that he heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) teaching the people the Tashahhud from the minbar, saying: \Say: 'Al-Taḥiyyātu lillāh"," al-Zākiyātu lillāh"," al-Ṭayyibātu lillāh"," al-Ṣalawātu lillāh. Al-Salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-Salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibādillāhi al-Ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh.'\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Wahb. And in the hadith of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him)"," it states: he heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb saying from the minbar while he was teaching the people the Tashahhud"," and he said: \""Al-Ṭayyibātu al-Ṣalawātu lillāh.\"" And the remainder is the same. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2839","(2839) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, who said: I witnessed ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb upon the minbar teaching the people the Tashahhud, and he said: \Al-Taḥiyyātu lillāh"," al-Zākiyātu lillāh"," al-Ṣalawātu al-Ṭayyibātu lillāh. Al-Salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-Salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibādillāhi al-Ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh.\"" Maʿmar said: al-Zuhrī used to adhere to it and say: \""He taught it to the people from the minbar"," and the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) were present in large numbers and did not reject it.\"" Maʿmar said: \""And I adhere to it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And in one of the two narrations from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," the two words of the Shahādah are placed first. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2840","(2840) Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānjānī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that when she recited the Tashahhud she would say: \Al-Taḥiyyātu al-Ṭayyibātu"," al-Ṣalawātu al-Zākiyātu lillāh. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh waḥdahu lā sharīka lah"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh. Al-Salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-Salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibādillāhi al-Ṣāliḥīn. Al-Salāmu ʿalaykum.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2841","(2841) And Abū Aḥmad informed us: Abū Bakr informed us: Muḥammad informed us: Ibn Bukayr informed us: Mālik informed us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), with the same meaning, except that he did not mention his words: \waḥdahu lā sharīka lah\"" (He alone"," He has no partner).\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she placed the two words of the Salām first. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2842","(2842) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Shādhān in Baghdād informed us: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī informed us: Ḥajjāj said: Ibn Jurayj informed me: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed me, saying: I heard al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad saying: ʿĀ'ishah used to teach us the Tashahhud, gesturing with her hand, saying: \Al-Taḥiyyātu al-Ṭayyibātu al-Ṣalawātu al-Zākiyyātu lillāh. Al-Salāmu ʿalā al-Nabiyyi wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-Salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibādillāhi al-Ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh.\"" Then the person may supplicate for himself thereafter.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Dīnār"," from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"," as a marfūʿ narration"," but the correct one is mawqūf. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2843","(2843) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān al-Nasawī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Khallād informed me: Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Tammār informed me, from his father, from al-Qāsim, who said: ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) taught me. She said: \This is the Tashahhud of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): 'Al-Taḥiyyātu lillāh wa al-Ṣalawātu wa al-Ṭayyibāt. Al-Salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. Al-Salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibādillāhi al-Ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh.'\"" Muḥammad said: I said: \""Bismillāh?\"" So al-Qāsim said: \""Bismillāh is at every moment.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2844","(2844) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us.\n\nMālik informed us, and he mentioned the hadith of ʿUmar regarding the Tashahhud as has preceded. (Sh) Then he said: \And this is what those of our fuqahā' who preceded us in knowledge taught us when we were young. Then we heard it with its chain of narration"," and we heard what contradicted it. And what we hold as our position is that ʿUmar would not teach the people from the minbar in the midst of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) except what the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had taught them. When a hadith from our companions reached us that we could establish as being from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," we inclined toward it"," and it was more deserving of our adherence.\"" Then he mentioned the hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās. He said: \""That is what some of those who spoke to al-Shāfiʿī about it meant. For we see that the narrations have differed regarding it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Ibn Masʿud narrated something contrary to this"," and Abū Mūsā and Jābir narrated as well"," and some of them differ from others in some of the wording. Then ʿUmar taught something contrary to all of this in some of its wording. And likewise the Tashahhud of ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and Ibn ʿUmar — some of them add something over others.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""I said: The matter in this is clear. Every word by which the magnification of Allah (Mighty and Majestic) is intended — the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) taught it to them"," so one of them preserved it in one wording and another preserved it in a wording that differs from it"," though they do not differ in meaning. Perhaps the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted each one of them to recite as he had preserved it"," since there is in it no meaning that would alter anything from its ruling.\"" And he drew an analogy for that with the hadith of the modes (aḥruf) of the Qur'an. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain has preceded in 2838]"""
"2845","(2845) Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Mālik informed us, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd al-Qārī, who said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \I heard Hishām ibn Ḥakīm ibn Ḥizām reciting Sūrat al-Furqān differently from how I had recited it"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had taught it to me. I was about to hasten to interrupt him"," but I gave him respite until he finished. Then I grabbed him by his cloak and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I heard this one reciting Sūrat al-Furqān differently from how you taught it to me.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: 'Recite.' So he recited the recitation that I had heard him recite. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Thus it was revealed.' Then he said to me: 'Recite.' So I recited"," and he said: 'Thus it was revealed. Indeed"," this Qur'an was revealed upon seven modes (aḥruf)"," so recite thereof what is easy for you.'\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Since Allah"," by His gentleness toward His creation"," revealed His Book upon seven modes — as a sign from Him that preservation may falter"," thereby permitting them its recitation even if their wording differs in it — then matters other than the Book of Allah are more deserving of permitting differences in wording"," so long as the meaning is not altered.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And it is not for anyone to deliberately omit the recitation of a mode of the Qur'an except out of forgetfulness. And this"," regarding the Tashahhud and all forms of dhikr"," is even more flexible.\""\n\nAnd the one who spoke to al-Shāfiʿī said: \""How did you come to choose the hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the Tashahhud over others?\"" Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""When I saw it to be comprehensive"," and I heard it from Ibn ʿAbbās as authentic"," it appeared to me to be more encompassing and more abundant in wording than others"," so I adopted it without being harsh toward anyone who adopted something else that is established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And what is established from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in that regard are the hadiths of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās"," and Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (2419)]"""
"2846","(2846) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Dimashqī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Khālid al-Wahbī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \It is from the Sunnah that the Tashahhud be recited softly (in a subdued voice).\""\n\nAnd similarly it was narrated from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (986)]"""
"2847","(2847) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Faqīh in Bukhārā informed us that Sahl ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Bukhārī narrated to us that al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Aswad from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh — that is, Ibn Masʿūd — who said: \From the Sunnah of the prayer is that the tashahhud be recited quietly.\"""""
"2848","(2848) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us from the original of his book that Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ informed us that Mālik narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām al-Warrāq informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, saying: I read to Mālik from Nuʿaym ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Mujmir that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd al-Anṣārī — and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd is the one who was shown the call to prayer in a dream — informed him from Abū Masʿūd, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us while we were in the gathering of Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah"," and Bashīr ibn Saʿd said to him: 'Allah has commanded us to send blessings upon you"," O Messenger of Allah"," so how should we send blessings upon you?' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent until we wished he had not asked him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Say: O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad"," as You sent blessings upon Ibrāhīm"," and bless Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrāhīm among the worlds. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious. And [send] peace as you have been taught.'\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," except that he said: \""as You blessed the family of Ibrāhīm.\"""""
"2849","(2849) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original that Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzāz informed us that Abū al-Azhar Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us that the Imam Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Abū al-Azhar Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar informed us, and I wrote it from his original. Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us; my father narrated to me from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: \And Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to me regarding sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when a Muslim sends blessings upon him in his prayer — from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn ʿAbd Rabbih"," from Abū Masʿūd ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr"," who said: 'A man came and sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while we were with him"," and he said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," as for the salām upon you"," we know it"," but how should we send blessings upon you when we send blessings upon you in our prayer — may Allah send blessings upon you?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent until we wished the man had not asked him. Then he said: \""When you send blessings upon me"," say: O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad"," the Unlettered Prophet"," and upon the family of Muhammad"," as You sent blessings upon Ibrāhīm and upon the family of Ibrāhīm"," and bless Muhammad"," the Unlettered Prophet"," and upon the family of Muhammad"," as You blessed Ibrāhīm and upon the family of Ibrāhīm. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious.\""'\""\n\nTheir wording is the same. Abū ʿAbd Allāh said: \""This is a sound ḥadīth regarding sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in the prayers.\"""""
"2850","(2850) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr — that is, ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī — informed us that Abū al-Azhar Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar informed us, and he mentioned it similarly. Then ʿAlī said: \This is a good"," connected chain of narration.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""It has also been narrated from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm similarly.\"""""
"2851","(2851) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad al-Asadī informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us that Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us that Shuʿbah informed us that al-Ḥakam informed us, saying: \I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā say: 'Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah met me and said: \""Shall I not give you a gift? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came out to us and we said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we know how to send salām upon you"," but how should we send blessings upon you?' He said: 'Say: O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad"," as You sent blessings upon Ibrāhīm. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious. O Allah"," bless Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad"," as You blessed Ibrāhīm. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and he said: \""as You blessed Ibrāhīm.\"" And Muslim narrated it from another route from Shuʿbah likewise.\n\nHis statement in the ḥadīth: \""We know how to send salām\"" is a reference to the salām upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in the tashahhud. His statement: \""How should we send blessings upon you?\"" also refers to [sending blessings] in the sitting for the tashahhud."""
"2852","(2852) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad informed me that Saʿd ibn Isḥāq narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he used to say in the prayer: \O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad"," as You sent blessings upon Ibrāhīm and the family of Ibrāhīm"," and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad"," as You blessed Ibrāhīm and the family of Ibrāhīm. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious.\"""""
"2853","(2853) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Ibn Milḥān informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that al-Layth narrated from Ibn al-Hād, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khabbāb, from Abū Saʿīd, who said: \We said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," this is the salām"," but how should we send blessings upon you?' He said: 'Say: O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad"," Your servant and Your Messenger"," as You sent blessings upon Ibrāhīm"," and bless Muhammad"," as You blessed Ibrāhīm.'\""\n\nIn this [ḥadīth] there is also a reference to what the ḥadīth of Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah alluded to. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from al-Layth."""
"2854","(2854) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw informed us that ʿAbd al-Ṣamd ibn al-Faḍl informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Muqriʾ informed us that Ḥaywah narrated from Abū Hānīʾ, from Abū ʿAlī ʿAmr ibn Mālik, from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd al-Anṣārī, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a man who prayed without praising Allah, glorifying Him, or sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and then he departed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \This one has been hasty.\"" So he called him and said to him and to others: \""When one of you prays"," let him begin with praising his Lord"," the Mighty and Majestic"," and extolling Him"," and let him send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," then let him supplicate for whatever he wishes.\"""""
"2855","(2855) Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓufur ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAlawī and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ both said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī in Kūfah narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghurazah al-Ghifārī narrated to us that ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū al-Aḥwaṣ, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \When we used to sit between the two rakʿahs in the prayer"," we did not know what to say except to glorify [Allah]"," declare His greatness"," and remember Allah. And indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) knew the comprehensive words of goodness and their openings. He turned his face toward us and said: 'When you sit between the two rakʿahs"," say: All compliments"," prayers"," and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah"," and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.'\""\n\nʿAbd Allāh said: \""And when one says 'Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah","' it reaches every righteous servant or sent prophet. Then one begins with extolling Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," and praising Him as He deserves"," and with sending blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," then one asks [one's needs] thereafter.\"""""
"2856","(2856) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — more than once — that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh in Baghdad informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb informed us that Abū Salamah Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us that Abū Farwah narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā informed him that he heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā say: \Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah met me and said: 'Shall I not give you a gift that I heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)?' I said: 'Yes"," by all means"," give it to me.' He said: 'We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," how should we send blessings upon you"," the People of the House?\"" He said: \""Say: O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad"," as You sent blessings upon Ibrāhīm and upon the family of Ibrāhīm. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious. O Allah"," bless Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad"," as You blessed Ibrāhīm and upon the family of Ibrāhīm. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious.\""'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl and others."""
"2857","(2857) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Fadl Hasan ibn Ya'qub al-'Adl informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Farra' informed us; Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us; Abu Hayyan Yahya ibn Sa'id ibn Hayyan narrated from his paternal uncle Yazid ibn Hayyan, who said: I set out to Zayd ibn Arqam, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood among us at a body of water called Khum, situated between Makkah and Madinah. He praised Allah, extolled Him, admonished, and reminded. Then he said: \To proceed: O people"," I am but a mortal"," and the messenger of my Lord [i.e."," the angel of death] is about to come to me"," and I shall respond [to his call]. I am leaving among you the two weighty things (al-thaqalayn). The first of them is the Book of Allah"," in which there is guidance and light. So hold fast to the Book of Allah and adhere to it.\"" He exhorted and encouraged regarding it. Then he said: \""And my Ahl al-Bayt. I remind you of Allah concerning my Ahl al-Bayt.\"" Husayn said: \""O Zayd"," who are his Ahl al-Bayt? Are not his wives among his Ahl al-Bayt?\"" He said: \""Indeed"," his wives are among his Ahl al-Bayt"," but his Ahl al-Bayt whom he mentioned are those upon whom charity (sadaqah) was forbidden after him.\"" He said: \""And who are they?\"" He said: \""The family of 'Ali"," the family of 'Aqil"," the family of Ja'far"," and the family of al-'Abbas.\"" He said: \""Were all of these forbidden from charity?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah"," Muhammad ibn Fudayl"," and Jarir"," from Abu Hayyan.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad"," 19479.]"""
"2858","(2858) Abu 'Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Tahir al-Daqqaq in Baghdad informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Uthman al-Adami informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah informed us; my father informed us; Muhammad ibn Bishr al-'Abdi informed us; Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah informed us; Mus'ab ibn Shaybah narrated from Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) went out one morning wearing a striped garment of black hair. Al-Hasan came, and he included him under it. Then al-Husayn came, and he included him under it. Then Fatimah came, and he included her under it. Then 'Ali came, and he included him under it. Then he said: \{Indeed"," Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity [of sin]"," O Ahl al-Bayt"," and to purify you with [extensive] purification.}\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and others"," from Muhammad ibn Bishr."""
"2859","(2859) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us; al-'Abbas al-Dawri informed us; Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us; my father narrated from Salih ibn Kaysan; from Ibn Shihab; from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib, who informed him that Ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith informed him that he heard Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith and al-'Abbas ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib say: \Had we sent these two young men of mine and al-Fadl's to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he appointed them over this charity"," they would have delivered what the people deliver"," and they would have obtained the benefit that the people obtain.\"" Then he mentioned the narration concerning their going to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," until he said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Beware"," charity is not permissible for Muhammad nor for the family of Muhammad. It is but the refuse of the people.\"" And he mentioned the narration concerning their marriage and the payment of their dower from the khums.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of Malik and Yunus ibn Yazid"," from Ibn Shihab"," from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Harith. Al-Bukhari said: 'Abdullah is more correct"," and Ibn Rabi'ah is 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Rabi'ah ibn al-Harith ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim."""
"2860","(2860) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; 'Ubayd ibn Sharik informed us; Yahya ibn Bukayr informed us; al-Layth narrated from Yunus; from Ibn Shihab; from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab that Jubayr ibn Mut'im informed him: He and 'Uthman ibn 'Affan came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to speak to him when he was distributing the war booty of Khaybar between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib. They said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you have distributed among our brothers"," Banu al-Muttalib ibn 'Abd Manaf"," and you have given us nothing"," yet our kinship is the same as theirs.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to them: \""Banu Hashim and al-Muttalib are but one thing.\"" Jubayr ibn Mut'im said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not distribute anything from that khums to Banu 'Abd Shams or to Banu Nawfal"," as he distributed to Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ibn Bukayr with its meaning. Its supporting evidences will be mentioned in the book of the distribution of war booty"," by the will of Allah the Most High."""
"2861","(2861) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us on more than one occasion, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami from his original, and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram informed us; 'Uthman ibn 'Umar informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated from Sharik ibn Abi Namir; from 'Ata' ibn Yasar; from Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \In my house the verse was revealed: '{Indeed"," Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity [of sin]"," O Ahl al-Bayt"," and to purify you with [extensive] purification.}'\"" She said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent for Fatimah"," 'Ali"," al-Hasan"," and al-Husayn"," and said: 'These are my Ahl al-Bayt.'\""\n\nIn the hadith of al-Qadi and al-Sulami: \""These are my family (ahli).\"" She said: \""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," am I not among the Ahl al-Bayt?' He said: 'Yes"," indeed"," if Allah the Most High wills.'\""\n\nAbu 'Abdullah said: This is a sound hadith; its chain is reliable"," and its narrators are trustworthy.\n\nThe Sheikh said: Supporting narrations and counter-narrations have been reported regarding it"," but none of them are established. In the Book of Allah is the clarification of what we intended. Then"," the Prophet's (ﷺ) general mention of al (the family)"," and his intended meaning thereby — whether his wives are included in it or not — [is a matter of discussion].\n\n[Weak]"""
"2862","(2862) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us; Ibn 'Affan, i.e., al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan, informed us; Abu Usamah narrated from al-A'mash; from 'Umarah ibn al-Qa'qa'; from Abu Zur'ah; from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Allah"," make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient nourishment (qut).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj"," from Abu Usamah. Al-Bukhari narrated it from another chain from 'Umarah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \""The family of Muhammad eat only from this wealth. It is not for them to have more than food.\"" He intended thereby those under his care (nafaqah).\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \""The family of Muhammad (ﷺ) never ate their fill of food for three days until he was taken [in death].\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: \""The family of Muhammad (ﷺ) never ate their fill of wheat food for three consecutive nights since arriving in Madinah until he was taken [in death].\""\n\nAnd from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: \""We"," the family of Muhammad (ﷺ)"," would remain for a month without kindling a fire. It was only dates and water.\""\n\nAbu 'Abdullah al-Hulaymi indicated that the term Ahl al-Bayt is established for the wives as a matter of fact"," and the term al (family) for them is by way of resemblance to lineage"," especially the wives of the Prophet"," because their connection to him is not severed"," and they are forbidden to others during his lifetime and after his death. Thus"," the bond they have with him stands in the place of lineage.\n\nThe Sheikh said: The explicit statement of the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the command to send blessings upon his wives suffices over anything else.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 6460.]"""
"2863","(2863) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated from Malik; from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn Hazm; from his father; from 'Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zurqi, who said: Abu Humayd al-Sa'idi informed me that they said: \O Messenger of Allah"," how should we send blessings upon you?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Say: 'O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad"," his wives"," and his progeny"," as You sent blessings upon the family of Ibrahim. And bless Muhammad"," his wives"," and his progeny"," as You blessed the family of Ibrahim. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious.'\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 3369.]"""
"2864","(2864) Abu al-Rudhabari informed us; 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar ibn Shawdhab al-Muqri' in Wasit informed us; Ahmad ibn Sinan informed us; Ruh ibn 'Ubadah informed us; Malik narrated it with a similar chain.\n\n[Sahih. It has been preceded in the one before it.]"
"2865","(2865) Abu Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' and Muhammad ibn Idris — i.e., al-Shafi'i — both said: Malik narrated it with a similar meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi, and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Rahawayh and others, from Ruh ibn 'Ubadah, from Ibn Numayr, from 'Abdullah ibn Nafi'.\n\n[Sahih. It has been preceded with a similar meaning in the one before it.]"
"2866","(2866) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhabari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Musa ibn Isma'il informed us; Hibban ibn Yasar al-Kalabi informed me; Abu Mutarrif 'Ubaydullah ibn Talhah ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Kariz informed me; Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Hashimi narrated from al-Mujmir; from Abu Hurayrah; from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Whoever would like to be given the fullest measure when blessings are sent upon us"," the Ahl al-Bayt"," let him say: 'O Allah"," send blessings upon Muhammad the Prophet"," his wives — the Mothers of the Believers — his progeny"," and his Ahl al-Bayt"," as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim. Indeed"," You are Praiseworthy"," Glorious.'\""\n\nIt is as though he (ﷺ) singled out his wives and progeny by mention by way of emphasis"," then returned to the general term so as to include others besides the wives and progeny among his Ahl al-Bayt (ﷺ)"," and upon all of them collectively.\n\n[Weak]"""
"2867","(2867) Al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī in Ṭūs informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī in al-Baṣrah narrated to us: Jaʿfar al-Qalānisī narrated to us: Ādam narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us: Qatādah and Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The freed slave of a people is considered as one of them.\"""""
"2868","(2868) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from al-Ḥakam, from Ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from Abī Rāfiʿ, that the Prophet ﷺ sent a man from Banū Makhzūm to collect the ṣadaqah and he said to my father (Abī Rāfiʿ): \Accompany me"," for you shall receive a share of it.\"" He said: \""Not until I come to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him.\"" So he went to him and asked him"," and he ﷺ said: \""The freed slave of a people is considered as one of them"," and ṣadaqah is not permissible for us.\"""""
"2869","(2869) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkārī in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq said: I heard a man say to al-Thawrī: \Who are the Āl of Muḥammad?\"" He said: \""The people have differed. Among them are those who say 'Ahl al-Bayt' (the People of the House)"," and among them are those who say 'Whoever obeys him and acts upon his Sunnah.'\"""""
"2870","(2870) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed me: My father narrated to us: I heard al-Awzāʿī say: Abū ʿAmmār narrated to us: Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ al-Laythī narrated to us, saying: \I came seeking ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) but did not find him. Fāṭimah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: 'He has gone to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," who has called for him"," so sit (and wait).' He said: 'Then he came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and they entered"," and I entered with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn"," and seated each one of them upon his lap"," and drew Fāṭimah close to his bosom along with her husband"," then wrapped his garment over them while I was sitting apart"," and he said: {Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity [of sin]"," O Ahl al-Bayt"," and to purify you with [extensive] purification} (O Allah"," these are my family; O Allah"," these are my family — the people of the household have the greatest right).' Wāthilah said: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah"," am I also of your family?' He said: 'You are of my family.' Wāthilah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'This was the most hoped-for thing I could have wished for.'\"""""
"2871","(2871) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān and Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān said: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us, from al-Awzāʿī, who said: Abū ʿAmmār narrated to me: Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ narrated to me: \I came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) but did not find him…\"" and he narrated the hadith with a similar wording."""
"2872","(2872) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿUqaylī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn al-Furāt narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \The Āl of Muḥammad ﷺ are his Ummah.\"""""
"2873","(2873) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Mahrūyah ibn ʿAbbās al-Rāzī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ziyād narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Nāfiʿ Abū Hurmazah said: I heard Anas ibn Mālik being asked: \Who are the Āl of Muḥammad?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Every pious person (muttaqī).\"" And it is not permissible to use such a narration as evidence."""
"2874","(2874) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Abū Muslim narrated to us: Abū al-Walīd and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb — and the wording is that of Abī al-Walīd — said: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Awfī — and he was among the Companions of the Tree (aṣḥāb al-shajarah) — say: \When a people would come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with their ṣadaqāt"," he would say: (O Allah"," send ṣalawāt upon them). Then my father came with his ṣadaqah and he said: (O Allah"," send ṣalawāt upon the family of Abī Awfī).\"""""
"2875","(2875) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsá narrated to us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Qays, from Nubayḥ al-ʿAnazī, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that a woman said to the Prophet ﷺ: \Send ṣalawāt upon me and upon my husband.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: (May Allah send ṣalawāt upon you and upon your husband)."""
"2876","(2876) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, and Abū ʿUthmān Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdān said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿAṭāridī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated to us, from ʿUthmān ibn Ḥakīm, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \It is not befitting for anyone to send ṣalawāt upon anyone except upon the Prophet ﷺ.\"""""
"2877","(2877) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Saʿdān narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Shaqīq who said: ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When we sat with the Prophet ﷺ in the prayer"," we used to say: 'Peace be upon Allah before His servants; peace be upon Jibrīl; peace be upon Mīkāʾīl; peace be upon so-and-so; peace be upon so-and-so.'\"" He said: \""Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard us and said: 'Indeed"," Allah is al-Salām (the Source of Peace). When one of you sits in the prayer"," let him say: \""All compliments"," prayers"," and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you"," O Prophet"," and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah.\"" For when he says this"," it reaches every righteous servant in the heavens and the earth. \""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"," and I bear witness that Muḥammad is His servant and His Messenger.\"" Then thereafter"," let him choose whatever supplication he wishes.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Abī Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 6230.]"""
"2878","(2878) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from al-Aʿmash; Shaqīq narrated from ʿAbdullāh, and he mentioned it with part of its meaning. And at the end of it: \Then let one of you choose the supplication that is most pleasing to him and supplicate therewith.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān. Likewise"," Manṣūr narrated it from Shaqīq"," and he said at the end of it: \""Then thereafter"," let him choose whatever request he wishes.\""\n\nAnd the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated in his prayer for certain peoples and against certain peoples by their names. That will come"," if Allah the Most High wills"," and we have narrated it from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Bukhārī"," 6230] (a) [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 6230.]"""
"2879","(2879) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dārim al-Ḥāfiẓ in al-Kūfah informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Kindī narrated to us; ʿAwn ibn Salām narrated to us; Salām ibn Sulaym, Abū al-Aḥwaṣ, narrated from Abī Isḥāq from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ and Abī ʿUbaydah, who both said: ʿAbdullāh said: \A man recites the tashahhud"," then sends blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ"," then supplicates for himself.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 3026.]"""
"2880","(2880) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Abū Shuʿayb al-Ḥarrānī narrated to me; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Abū Isḥāq narrated that he heard Abā ʿUbaydah narrate from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ went out, and Abū Bakr and ʿUmar were with him. Abū Bakr had invited them, and they set out from his house to the mosque — the Mosque of al-Madīnah. ʿAbdullāh was standing, reciting in prayer. Then he sat and recited the tashahhud, then he praised Allah as He deserves, in the most excellent manner in which a man can praise Him. Then he sent blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then he earnestly beseeched in supplication, while the Prophet ﷺ stood listening. He ﷺ began to say: \Ask"," and it will be given to you.\"" Abū Bakr said: \""Who is this"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He ﷺ said: \""This is ʿAbdullāh ibn Umm ʿAbd. Whoever would like to recite the Qurʾān fresh as it was revealed"," let him recite it as Ibn Umm ʿAbd recited it.\"" Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) hastened toward him"," and Abū Bakr outran him. ʿUmar asserted that Abū Bakr had outrun him. ʿUmar said: \""He was always the foremost in every good.\"" May Allah be pleased with them all. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2881","(2881) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Jakānī informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb informed us from al-Zuhrī; ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that the Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate in the prayer: \O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave"," and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Messiah al-Dajjāl"," and I seek refuge in You from sin and from debt.\"" She said: A person said to him: \""How frequently you seek refuge from debt"," O Messenger of Allah!\"" He said: \""When a man falls into debt"," he speaks and lies"," and he makes a promise and breaks it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn Isḥāq from Abī al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 833.]"""
"2882","(2882) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaydalānī and Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr, meaning al-Harwī, both said: Abū Kurayb narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated from al-Awzāʿī from Ḥassān ibn ʿAṭiyyah from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah from Abī Hurayrah.\n\nAnd from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abī Salamah from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you recites the tashahhud"," let him seek refuge in Allah from four things. He should say: 'O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Jahannam"," and from the punishment of the grave"," and from the trial of life and death"," and from the trial of the Messiah al-Dajjāl.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Kurayb and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 37451. Muslim"," 1262.]"""
"2883","(2883) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bishrān informed us; Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Hāʾīʾ al-Naysābūrī informed us; Abū al-Mughīrah and Muḥammad ibn Kathīr both narrated from al-Awzāʿī from Ḥassān, meaning Ibn ʿAṭiyyah, from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you finishes his prayer"," let him supplicate with four things"," then thereafter let him supplicate with whatever he wishes: 'O Allah"," I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Jahannam"," and from the punishment of the grave"," and from the trial of life and death"," and from the trial of the Messiah al-Dajjāl.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Refer to the one before it.]"""
"2884","(2884) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us; Yaḥyā, that is Ibn Bukayr, informed us; al-Layth informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān and al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṭayyib both said: Qutaybah narrated to us; al-Layth narrated from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from Abī al-Khayr from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Teach me a supplication that I may make in my prayer.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Say: 'O Allah"," I have wronged myself greatly"," and none forgives sins except You. So forgive me with a forgiveness from Your mercy"," and have mercy upon me. Indeed"," You are the All-Forgiving"," the Most Merciful.'\""\n\nThe wording of both is the same. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 834"," 6326.]"""
"2885","(2885) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Miskīn ibn Bukayr al-Ḥarrānī narrated from Thābit ibn ʿAjlān from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The believer is attentive to listening except in an obligatory prayer"," or a prescribed prayer"," or the day of Jumuʿah"," or the day of Fiṭr"," or the day of Aḍḥā\"" — meaning the verse: {And when the Qurʾān is recited"," listen to it and be silent} [al-Aʿrāf: 204].\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from another chain"," which is not strong"," from ʬAṭāʾ that he asked Ibn ʿAbbās about this verse: \""Is this for every reciter?\"" He said: \""No"," rather this pertains to the prayer.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Ḥātim in al-Tafsīr"," 9493.]"""
"2886","(2886) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reciting in the prayer when he heard the recitation of a young man from the Anṣār"," and the verse was revealed: {And when the Qurʾān is recited"," listen to it and be silent} [al-Aʿrāf: 204].\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from another chain from Mujāhid that he said it pertains to the sermon (khuṭbah) on the day of Jumuʿah"," and from another chain that it pertains to both the prayer and the sermon. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"2887","(2887) It has been narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān, who was informed by Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār, who was informed by Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq, who was informed by Shaybān ibn Farrūkh, who was informed by ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muslim, who was informed by Ibrāhīm al-Hajarī, from Abū ʿIyāḍ, from Abū Hurayrah, that he said regarding this verse: {And when the Qurʾān is recited, listen to it and be silent} [al-Aʿrāf: 204]: \The people used to speak during the Salāh"," so this verse was revealed.\""\n\nIn the narration of Ibn ʿAbdān"," he said: \""They used to speak during the Salāh until this verse was revealed.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And thus said Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah. [Very Weak]"""
"2888","(2888) It was narrated to him by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who was informed by Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, who was informed by Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who was informed by ʿAffān, who was informed by ʿAwn ibn Mūsā, who said: I heard Muʿāwiyah ibn Qurrah say: \Allāh revealed this verse: {And when the Qurʾān is recited"," listen to it and be silent} [al-Aʿrāf: 204].\"" He said: \""The people used to speak during the Salāh.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr from ʿAwn"," and he added in it: \""So the storytellers (al-quṣṣāṣ) narrated it in their stories.\"" [Authentic]"""
"2889","(2889) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Jarīr informed us, from Sulaymān al-Taymī, from Qatādah, from Abū Ghallāb, from Ḥiṭṭān ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Raqāshī, who said: \We performed Salāh with Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī"," and he mentioned the ḥadīth from the Prophet ﷺ"," and in it is: 'When the Imām says the takbīr"," then say the takbīr"," and when he recites"," then be silent.'\""\n\nAnd Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated in his Ṣaḥīḥ the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAwānah from Qatādah with the context of the matn without this specific wording. Then he followed it with the narration of Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah and Hishām al-Dastawāʾī.\n\nHe said: And Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us"," and he mentioned this narration"," then he said: \""And in the ḥadīth of Jarīr from Sulaymān from Qatādah there is the addition: 'When he recites"," then be silent.'\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us"," who said: Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī said: \""His statement 'then be silent' (faʾnṣitū) is not preserved"," or it is nothing.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," who said: I heard Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ say: \""Jarīr differed from all the companions of Qatādah in this ḥadīth. And the preserved narration from Qatādah is the narration of Hishām al-Dastawāʾī"," Hammām"," Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," Maʿmir ibn Rāshid"," Abū ʿAwānah"," al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj"," and those who followed them in their narration—meaning without this wording. And it was narrated by Sālim ibn Nūḥ from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah and ʿUmar ibn ʿĀmir from Qatādah"," and he erred therein.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of that"," who said: I heard Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ mention it. [Authentic. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 19017]"""
"2890","(2890) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Muḥammad ibn Hārūn al-Ḥaḍramī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Quṭaʿī informed us; Sālim ibn Nūḥ informed us; ʿUmar ibn ʿĀmir and Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah informed us, from Qatādah, from Yūnus ibn Jubayr—that is, Abū Ghallāb—from Ḥiṭṭān ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Raqāshī, who said: \Abū Mūsā led us in Salāh"," and Abū Mūsā said: 'Indeed"," the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ used to teach us when he led us in Salāh"," and he said: \""Indeed"," the Imām is appointed only to be followed. So when he says the takbīr"," then say the takbīr"," and when he recites"," then be silent.\""'\""\n\nʿAlī ibn ʿUmar said: \""Sālim ibn Nūḥ is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And it was narrated by Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from another route.\"" [Fair]"""
"2891","(2891) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥbūr al-Dahhān informed us; Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Bilāl al-Bazzār informed us; Abū al-Azhar informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abān informed us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from Zayd ibn Aslam and Muṣʿab ibn Sharḥīl, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Indeed"," the Imāh is appointed only to be followed"," so do not differ from him. When he says the takbīr"," then say the takbīr; and when he recites"," then be silent; and when he says {Not of those who have earned Your anger"," nor of those who have gone astray}"," then say 'Āmīn'; and when he bows"," then bow; and when he says 'Allāh hears the one who praises Him","' then say 'Our Lord"," to You is all praise'; and when he prostrates"," then prostrate; and when he prays sitting"," then pray sitting"," all of you together.'\""\n\nAnd thus narrated Abū Khālid al-Aḥmar from Ibn ʿAjlān"," and it is a confusion (wahm) from Ibn ʿAjlān.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us"," who said: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say regarding the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAjlān: \""When he recites"," then be silent\""—it is nothing (laysa bi-shayʾ).\n\nAbū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us; Ibn Abī Ḥātim informed us"," who said: I heard my father mention this ḥadīth"," and my father said: \""This word is not preserved; it is from the confusion (takhāluṭ) of Ibn ʿAjlān.\""\n\nHe said: And it was narrated by Khārijah ibn Muṣʿab also"," meaning from Zayd ibn Aslam. And Khārijah also is not strong.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allāh have mercy on him"," said: And it was narrated by Yaḥyā ibn al-ʿAlāʾ al-Rāzī as they narrated it. And Yaḥyā ibn al-ʿAlāʾ is abandoned (matrūk). And the reliance of al-Shāfiʿī in the older view"," after the verse"," is upon the ḥadīth which… [Authentic. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2596]"""
"2892","(2892) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us; al-Qaʿnabī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us—and the wording is his—Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; al-Qaʿnabī informed us, from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Ibn Ukaymah al-Laythī, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Prophet ﷺ concluded a prayer in which he recited aloud and then said: \Did anyone among you recite with me just now?\"" A man said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allāh.\"" He said: \""I was saying to myself"," why am I being contended with regarding the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""So the people stopped reciting with the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ in those prayers in which the Prophet ﷺ recited aloud"," after they heard that from the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: \""This ḥadīth of Ibn Ukaymah was narrated by Maʿmir"," Yūnus ibn Yazīd"," and Usāmah ibn Zayd"," with the same meaning as Mālik's narration.\"" [Authentic. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 3776]"""
"2893","(2893) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Musaddad, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Zuhrī, and Ibn al-Sarḥ informed us, who said: Sufyān informed us, from al-Zuhrī.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī informed us; Sufyān informed us; al-Zuhrī—I preserved it from his mouth—said: I heard Ibn Ukaymah narrate to Saʿīd al-Musayyib, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah say: \The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ led us in a prayer which we thought was the Fajr prayer. When he concluded it"," he said: 'Did anyone among you recite?'\"" A man said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allāh.\"" The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \""I was saying to myself"," why am I being contended with regarding the Qurʾān?\""\n\nʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī said: Sufyān said: \""Then al-Zuhrī said something which I did not preserve. My preservation ends at this point.\""\n\nAnd Maʿmir narrated from al-Zuhrī: \""So the people stopped reciting in those prayers in which the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ recited aloud.\""\n\nʿAlī said: Sufyān said to me one day: \""I looked into something I had"," and it was: 'The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ led us in the Fajr prayer"," without doubt.'\""\n\nAnd Musaddad said in his ḥadīth: Maʿmir said: \""So the people stopped reciting in those prayers in which the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ recited aloud.\""\n\nAnd Ibn al-Sarḥ said in his ḥadīth: Maʿmir narrated from al-Zuhrī"," who said: Abū Hurayrah said: \""So the people stopped.\""\n\nAnd ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Zuhrī said: Sufyān said: \""And al-Zuhrī spoke a word which I did not hear.\"" Maʿmir said: \""He said: 'So the people stopped.'\""\n\nAnd Abū Dāwūd said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," and his ḥadīth ends at his statement: \""Why am I being contended with regarding the Qurʾān?\"" And al-Awzāʿī narrated it from al-Zuhrī"," and in it al-Zuhrī said: \""So the Muslims took heed of that"," and they did not recite with him in those prayers in which he recited aloud.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: I heard Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Fāris say: \""His statement 'So the people stopped' is from the speech of al-Zuhrī.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And thus said Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī in al-Tārīkh. He said: \""This speech is from the words of al-Zuhrī.\""\n\nMuḥammad al-Fārisī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris informed us"," who said: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl mentioned it"," and he said regarding Ibn Ukaymah: \""He is ʿUmarah ibn Ukaymah al-Laythī"," and it is also said ʿAmmār.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: And what indicates that it is from the speech of al-Zuhrī is that… [Authentic. As in the one before it]"""
"2894","(2894) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us; my father informed me; al-Awzāʿī informed me; al-Zuhrī informed me, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: \Some people recited with the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ in a prayer in which recitation is done aloud. When the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ finished"," he turned to them and said: 'Did anyone among you recite with me?'\"" They said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allāh.\"" The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \""I say to myself"," why am I being contended with regarding the Qurʾān?\"" Al-Zuhrī said: \""So the Muslims took heed of that"," and they did not recite.\""\n\nAl-Awzāʿī preserved that this speech was from al-Zuhrī"," so he separated it from the ḥadīth"," except that he did not preserve its isnād.\n\nThe correct version is what Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī"," who said: \""I heard Ibn Ukaymah narrate to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib.\""\n\nAnd thus said Yūnus ibn Yazīd al-Aylī.\n\nAnd it was narrated by the brother of al-Zuhrī from his uncle"," from al-Aʿraj"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buḥaynah"," from the Prophet ﷺ. [Authentic. As in the one before it]"""
"2895","(2895) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿd informed us; my uncle informed me; the brother of al-Zuhrī informed me from his uncle, who said: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmuz informed me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Buḥaynah—who was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ—that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \Did anyone among you recite just now during the Salāh?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I was saying to myself"," why am I being contended with regarding the Qurʾān.\""\n\nSo the people stopped reciting when he said that.\n\nYaʿqūb ibn Sufyān said: \""This is an error without doubt or uncertainty.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated by Mālik"," Maʿmir"," Ibn ʿUyaynah"," al-Layth ibn Saʿd"," Yūnus ibn Yazīd"," and al-Zubaydī—all of them from al-Zuhrī"," from Ibn Ukaymah"," from Abū Hurayrah.\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""There is consideration regarding the authenticity of this ḥadīth from the Prophet ﷺ"," and that is because the narration of Ibn Ukaymah al-Laythī—and he is an unknown man (majhūl)—he did not narrate except this ḥadīth alone"," and no one narrated from him other than al-Zuhrī"," and al-Zuhrī's knowledge of him did not exceed that he saw him narrating to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib.\""\n\nAnd in what Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us—that Abū Baḥr al-Barbarhārī informed them—Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us"," who said: Al-Ḥumaydī said regarding the ḥadīth of Ibn Ukaymah: \""This is a ḥadīth narrated by an unknown man from whom no one else narrated.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""And in the authentic ḥadīth narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," from Abū al-Sāʾib"," from Abū Hurayrah"," from the Prophet ﷺ: 'Whoever performs a prayer in which he does not recite the Mother of the Qurʾān"," it is deficient.' I said: 'O Abū Hurayrah"," sometimes I am behind the Imām.' He said: 'He squeezed my arm and said: \""O Persian"," recite it to yourself.\""'\""\n\nAnd Abū Hurayrah being the narrator of both ḥadīths is evidence of the weakness of the narration of Ibn Ukaymah"," or he intended by what is in the ḥadīth of Ibn Ukaymah the prohibition of reciting aloud behind the Imām"," or the prohibition of reciting a sūrah in those prayers in which recitation is done aloud"," and it is like the ḥadīth of ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn that comes in this topic"," and it is mentioned in the chapter that follows it. [Authentic. Al-Bazzār"," 6/293"," 2313]"""
"2896","(2896) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī informed us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl al-Balkhī informed us; Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, from Abū Ḥanīfah, from Mūsā ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he performed Salāh and those behind him were reciting. A man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ began forbidding him from reciting during the Salāh. When he concluded, the man turned to him and said: \Are you forbidding me from reciting behind the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ?\"" They disputed until they mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Whoever prays behind the Imām"," then the recitation of the Imāh is recitation for him.\""\n\nThus narrated a group from Abū Ḥanīfah"," connected (mawṣūl).\n\nAnd ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated it from him"," disconnected (mursal)"," without the mention of Jābir"," and that is the preserved version. [Denounced. Abū Ḥākim in al-ʿIlal"," 282]"""
"2897","(2897) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Halim al-Sa'igh al-Thiqah in Marw, from his original copy — the Book of Prayer of 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak — informed us: Abu al-Muwajjih informed us: 'Abd ibn 'Uthman informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak informed us: Sufyan and Shu'bah, and Abu Hanifah, narrated from Musa ibn Abi 'A'ishah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever has an imam"," then the imam's recitation is his recitation.\""\n\nAnd similarly did 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrate it from Ibn al-Mubarak; and similarly did others narrate it from Sufyan ibn Sa'id al-Thawri and Shu'bah ibn al-Hajjaj; and similarly did Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir"," Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah"," Isra'il ibn Yunus"," Abu 'Awanah"," al-Ahwas"," and Jarir ibn 'Abd al-Hamid"," and other reliable and trustworthy narrators; and al-Hasan ibn 'Umarah narrated it from Musa in a connected (mawsul) chain. And al-Hasan ibn 'Umarah is abandoned (matruk). [Da'if]"""
"2898","(2898) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr and Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli both narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Hayy narrated to us, from Jabir and Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever has an imam"," then the imam's recitation is his recitation.\""\n\nJabir al-Ju'fi and Layth ibn Abi Sulaym — no proof is sought from them"," and everyone who followed them on that is weaker than them"," or weaker than either of them. And the preserved narration from Jabir in this regard is what… [Da'if. In it"," Jabir al-Ju'fi is a liar]"""
"2899","(2899) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far al-Muzanni informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-'Abdi informed us: Malik informed us: from Abu Nu'aym Wahb ibn Kisān, that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah saying: Whoever prays a rak'ah in which he does not recite Umm al-Qur'an, then he has not prayed except behind the imam.\n\nThis is the correct (sahih) narration from Jabir as his own statement, without being raised (mawquf). And Yahya ibn Salam and other weak narrators raised it (marfu') from Malik, and that is not permissible to narrate as proof. And it is possible that Jabir's position on this matter was the abandonment of recitation behind the imam in prayers where recitation is performed aloud (jahr), not in those where it is not. For Yazid al-Faqir narrated from Jabir, who said: We used to recite behind the imam in the Dhuhr and 'Asr prayers in the first two rak'ahs with the Opening of the Book and a surah, and in the last two rak'ahs with only the Opening of the Book. And similarly, it is possible that this was the position of Ibn Mas'ud. [Sahih]"
"2900","(2900) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Harun ibn Sulayman narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: from Sufyan and Shu'bah, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, that a man asked Ibn Mas'ud about recitation behind the imam. He said: \Be silent for the listening of the Qur'an"," for in the prayer there is occupation"," and the imam will suffice you in that.\""\n\nAnd the phrase \""Be silent for the listening of the Qur'an\"" is said only for what is heard"," not for what is not heard.\n\nAnd 'Alqamah said: I prayed beside 'Abd Allah"," and I did not know that he was reciting until he recited aloud with this verse: \""And say: My Lord"," increase me in knowledge\"" [Taha: 114].\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from 'Abd Allah ibn Ziyad al-Asadi that he said: I prayed beside 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud behind the imam"," and I heard him reciting in Dhuhr and 'Asr. [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah"," 3780]"""
"2901","(2901) As for 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn al-Khattar, may Allah be pleased with him — Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran in Baghdad informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us: al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated to us: from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that he used to say: Whoever prays behind the imam, the imam's recitation suffices him.\n\nThis is the correct (sahih) narration from Ibn 'Umar as his own statement, and with its meaning. Malik narrated it in al-Muwatta' from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, as a mawquf narration. And it has been narrated from Suwayd ibn Sa'id, from 'Ali ibn Mushir, from 'Ubayd Allah, as a marfu' narration, and it is an error. And Suwayd changed in his later years, and errors became frequent in his narrations. And it has been narrated from Kharijah ibn Mus'ab, from Ayyub, from Nafi', as a marfu' narration. And Kharijah is not used as proof.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, informed us, saying: I heard Abu Bakr ibn Abi Nasr al-Darabadiyy saying: I heard 'Abdān Muhammad, the hafiz — he al-Marwaziyy — saying: The hadith of Kharijah from Ayyub from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet ﷺ: \Whoever has an imam…\"" — it is a reprehensible error"," and it is only from Ibn 'Umar as his own statement"," although the opposite has also been narrated from Ibn 'Umar.\n\n'Abdān said: Ishaq ibn Abi 'Imran narrated to us: Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us: al-Jurayri narrated to us: Abu al-Azhar narrated: Ibn 'Umar was asked about recitation behind the imam"," and he said: \""I would feel shy before the Lord of this House to perform a prayer in which I do not recite Umm al-Qur'an.\"" Thus he said. [Hasan]"""
"2902","(2902) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: Ibn 'Uthman informed us: 'Abd Allah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: from Abu al-Azhar al-Du'ba'iyy, from Abu al-'Aliyah al-Bara', who mentioned a story in which 'Abd Allah ibn Safwan said to Ibn 'Umar: \O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman"," do you recite in every prayer?\"" He said: \""I would feel shy before the Lord of this House to perform two rak'ahs in which I do not recite Umm al-Qur'an — as an addition\"" — or he said \""and beyond that.\""\n\nYa'qub said: And 'Amr ibn 'Asim narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us: Abu al-Azhar narrated from Abu al-'Aliyah al-Bara' something similar to that.\n\nThus it was as though he considered recitation behind the imam to be valid only in prayers where the imam recites quietly (sirr). And upon this basis Malik ibn Anas placed it"," although the opposite has been narrated from him. [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq"," 2626]"""
"2903","(2903) Abu 'Abd Allah, the hafiz, and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: Asid ibn 'Asim informed us: al-Husayn ibn Hafs informed us: Sufyan informed us: Usamah informed us: from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, who said: Ibn 'Umar would not recite behind the imam, whether the recitation was aloud or not, while other men among the imams would recite behind the imam.\n\nThus did he narrate it, and the one who confirmed it (al-muthabbit) is more deserving than al-Nafi'. [Sahih. Narrated by Malik in al-Muwatta', 192]"
"2904","(2904) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah ibn Ya'qub informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us: Ja'far ibn 'Awn informed us: Usamah ibn Zayd said: I asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad about recitation behind the imam, and he said: \If you recite"," then a people among whom there was an example (uswah) have recited"," and following their command is taken; and if you leave it"," then a people among whom there was an example have left it.\""\n\nHe said: And Ibn 'Umar would not recite. [Hasan]"""
"2905","(2905) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us: Abu Ahmad 'Abd Allah ibn 'Adiyy, the hafiz, informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Saffar and Ibn Sa'id both informed us: Yusuf ibn Musa informed us: Salamah ibn al-Fadl informed us: al-Hajjaj ibn Arta'ah informed us: from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying with the people, and a man was reciting behind him. When he finished, he said: \Who is it that contended with me over my surah?\"" Then he forbade recitation behind the imam. Ibn Sa'id said: His statement \""Then he forbade recitation behind the imam\"" — al-Hajjaj was alone in narrating it.\n\nAnd Shu'bah"," Ibn Abi 'Arubah"," Ma'mar"," Isma'il ibn Muslim"," al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj"," Ayyub ibn Abi Miskin"," Hammam"," Aban"," and Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated it from Qatadah"," and none of them said what al-Hajjaj was alone in saying.\n\nShu'bah said: I asked Qatadah"," as though he disliked it? He said: Had he disliked it"," he would have forbidden it. [Sahih"," except for the addition \""Then he forbade recitation behind the imam\"" — it is munkar]"""
"2906","(2906) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Adan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us: al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl informed us: Abu al-Walid informed us: Shu'bah informed us: from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from 'Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet ﷺ prayed Dhuhr one day, and a man came and recited behind him \Glorify the name of your Lord"," the Most High\"" [al-A'la]. When he finished"," he said: \""Which one of you recited?\"" He said: \""I did.\"" He said: \""I had a feeling that one of you was contending with me over it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih with this meaning from the hadith of Shu'bah"," Abu 'Awanah"," and Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah"," from Qatadah. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Humaydi"," 835]"""
"2907","(2907) Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak — informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud, i.e., al-Tayalisi, narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated.\n\n(And) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dassah informed us: Abu Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Kathir al-'Abdi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated, and he mentioned the hadith with the meaning of the hadith of Abu al-Walid. And at the end of it, he said: Shu'bah said: \I said to Qatadah: 'It is as though he disliked it?' He said: 'Had he disliked it"," he would have prohibited it.'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from 'Imran ibn Husayn that he said: \""No prayer is valid except with the Opening of the Book (Surat al-Fatihah).\"" And the Prophet (ﷺ) — if he disliked something from the one reciting behind him — disliked the loudness of the recitation"," not the recitation itself. And it is similar to what has preceded.\n\n[Authenticated. It has been discussed previously in 2905"," 2906.]"""
"2908","(2908) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: Abu Ja'far — Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz — narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Rashid, that he heard him narrating from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah: that 'Abdullah ibn Hudhafah prayed and recited loudly. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: \O Ibn Hudhafah"," do not make me hear"," but make Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," hear.\""\n\n[Weak. Al-Shawkani said in al-Nayl 3/72.]"""
"2909","(2909) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Abu Salih narrated to me: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me: Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to me: Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami said: I heard Abu al-Darda' saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: \Is there recitation in every prayer?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" A man from the Ansar said: \""This has become obligatory.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me — and I was the closest of the people to him — \""I do not think that when the Imam leads the people"," he suffices them (with his recitation).\""\n\nThis is how Abu Salih"," the scribe of al-Layth"," narrated it"," and he erred in it.\n\nLikewise"," Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated it in one of the two narrations from him"," and he also erred in it. The correct version is that Abu al-Darda' said that to Kathir ibn Murrah.\n\n[Munkar. Al-Daraqutni and al-Nasa'i said: The correct view is that it is mawquf (a statement of Abu al-Darda').]"""
"2910","(2910) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi — 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad and 'Abd al-Malik ibn Ahmad al-Daqqaq — both said: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to me: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abu al-Zahiriyyah, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Darda', who said: A man stood and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," is there recitation in every prayer?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" A man from the people said: \""This has become obligatory.\"" Abu al-Darda' said: \""O Kathir"," I was beside him — I do not think that when the Imam leads the people"," he suffices them (with his recitation).\""\n\n'Ali said: The correct view is that it is from the statement of Abu al-Darda'"," as Ibn Wahb said"," and Zayd ibn al-Hubab erred in it.\n\nThe Sheikh said: And Zayd narrated it as Ibn Wahb narrated it"," and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi — and he is an Imam and a Hafiz — narrated it from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih"," and he made it from the statement of Abu al-Darda'.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abu al-Darda' that he held the view of recitation behind the Imam"," while Zayd ibn Thabit did not hold that view with the Imam.\n\n[Authenticated. The discussion on it has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2911","(2911) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abdullah — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya informed us: Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfah, from Ibn Qusayt, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, who informed him: that he asked Zayd ibn Thabit about recitation with the Imam. He said: \There is no recitation with the Imam in anything.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\nAnd it is interpreted as referring to loud recitation with the Imam. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Authenticated. Muslim narrated it"," 577.]"""
"2912","(2912) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Muhammad ibn Musa ibn al-Fadl both informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Asid ibn 'Asim narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Sufyan, from 'Umar ibn Muhammad, from Musa ibn Sa'd, from Ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, from his father Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: \Whoever recites behind the Imam"," there is no prayer for him.\""\n\nAnd if this is authentic with this wording — and there is room for consideration in it — then it is interpreted as referring to loud recitation. And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best.\n\n'Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-'Adani contradicted him in its narration"," for he narrated it from Sufyan"," from 'Umar ibn Muhammad"," from Musa ibn Sa'd"," from his father"," from Zayd ibn Thabit. And Dawud ibn Qays and 'Abdullah ibn Dawud narrated it from 'Umar ibn Muhammad"," from Musa ibn Sa'd"," from Zayd"," without mentioning his father in the chain.\n\nAl-Bukhari said: It is not known that any of them heard from one another with this chain"," and its like is not authentic.\n\n[Very weak.]"""
"2913","(2913) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu al-Nadr — Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Faqih — narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book (Surat al-Fatihah).\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Ali ibn al-Madini"," and Muslim narrated it from a group from Sufyan.\n\n[Authenticated. Al-Bukhari narrated it"," 756.]"""
"2914","(2914) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — and Abu al-Qasim — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Sarraj — narrated to us by dictation. They said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us. He said: It was recited to 'Abdullah ibn Wahb: Yunus ibn Yazid informed you, from Ibn Shihab, who said: Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' informed me, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Mother of the Qur'an (Umm al-Qur'an).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Harmalah"," from Ibn Wahb."""
"2915","(2915) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — both informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Abu Zur'ah al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Khalid narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Sa'id ibn 'Uthman al-Tanukhi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in the morning prayer, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he turned (after finishing), he said: \I see that you recite behind your Imam.\"" We said: \""Yes"," by Allah"," O Messenger of Allah"," we do indeed do this.\"" He said: \""Then do not do so"," except with the Mother of the Qur'an (Umm al-Qur'an)"," for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of al-Tanukhi.\n\nAnd likewise Isma'il ibn 'Ulayyah and Yazid ibn Harun and a group narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yasar.\n\nAnd Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq"," and he mentioned in it that Ibn Ishaq heard from Makhul.\n\n[Authenticated. Without the phrase \""there is no prayer except with the Mother of the Qur'an\"" (for that is from the statement of 'Ubadah). Ahmad narrated it"," 316.]"""
"2916","(2916) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Faqih — informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz narrated to us: Ibn Sa'id narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah ibn Sa'd narrated to us: My paternal uncle narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, who said: Makhul narrated to me with this, and he said in it: He said: \I see that you recite behind your Imam when he recites aloud.\"" We said: \""Yes"," by Allah"," O Messenger of Allah"," this (is what we do).\"" He said: \""Then do not do so"," except with the Mother of the Qur'an (Umm al-Qur'an)"," for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.\""\n\n'Ali ibn 'Umar said: This is a hasan chain.\n\n[Authenticated. The detailed discussion has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2917","(2917) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān al-Azdī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us; al-Haytham ibn Ḥumayd informed us; Zayd ibn Wāqid informed me from Makḥūl, from Nāfiʿ ibn Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Anṣārī.\n\nNāfiʿ said: ʿUbādah was delayed from the Fajr prayer, so Abū Nuʿaym, the mu'adhdhin, led the people in prayer. Abū Nuʿaym led the people in prayer, and ʿUbādah came, and I was with him, until we lined up behind Abū Nuʿaym. Abū Nuʿaym was reciting aloud, and ʿUbādah began reciting Umm al-Qur'ān (Sūrat al-Fātiḥah) [silently]. When he finished, I said to ʿUbādah: \I heard you reciting Umm al-Qur'ān while Abū Nuʿaym was reciting aloud.\"" He said: \""Yes. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in one of the prayers in which the recitation is performed aloud"," and the recitation became confused for him. When he finished"," he turned his face toward us and said: 'Do you recite when I recite aloud?' Some of us said: 'We do that.' He said: 'Do not. I say to myself"," why am I being contended with the Qur'ān? So do not recite anything from the Qur'ān when I recite aloud except Umm al-Qur'ān.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Without his statement \""for there is no prayer except with Umm al-Qur'ān","\"" and the detailed discussion on that has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"2918","(2918) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Sahl al-Ramlī narrated to us; al-Walīd narrated from Ibn Jābir, Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, from Makḥūl, from ʿUbādah — similar to the ḥadīth of al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān."
"2919","(2919) The Shaykh said: Others narrated it from al-Walīd ibn Muslim, from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz and others, from Makḥūl, from Maḥmūd, from Abū Nuʿaym, that he heard ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit narrate from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \Do you recite during the prayer with me?\"" We said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then do not do so except with Fātiḥat al-Kitāb.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū Zurʿah ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAmr al-Dimashqī narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn ʿUtbah narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to me: \""More than one of them — Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Tanūkhī — narrated it to me","\"" and he mentioned it.\n\nThis is an error. The mu'adhdhin and the imām was Abū Nuʿaym. The ḥadīth is from Makḥūl"," from Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ"," from ʿUbādah"," and from Makḥūl"," from Nāfiʿ ibn Maḥmūd"," from ʿUbādah — as though he heard it from both of them together.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me. Ibn Ṣāʿid said: \""His statement 'from Abū Nuʿaym' — I think he said it is an error. Abū Nuʿaym was only the mu'adhdhin"," and it is not as al-Walīd stated: from Abū Nuʿaym"," from ʿUbādah.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Ḥarām ibn Ḥakīm also narrated it from Nāfiʿ ibn Maḥmūd. [Munkar]"""
"2920","(2920) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ṣāʿid narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Zanjawayh and Abū Zurʿah al-Dimashqī narrated to us — the wording being his — they said: Muḥammad ibn al-Mubārak al-Ṣūrī narrated to us; Ṣadaqah ibn Khālid narrated to us; Zayd ibn Wāqid narrated to us from Ḥarām ibn Ḥakīm and Makḥūl, from Nāfiʿ ibn Maḥmūd ibn Rabīʿah — thus he said — that he heard ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit reciting Umm al-Qur'ān while Abū Nuʿaym was reciting aloud. I said: \I saw you doing something in your prayer.\"" He said: \""What is that?\"" I said: \""I heard you reciting Umm al-Qur'ān while Abū Nuʿaym was reciting aloud.\"" He said: \""Yes. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in one of the prayers in which the recitation is performed aloud. When he finished"," he said: 'Is there anyone among you who recites something from the Qur'ān when I recite aloud?' We said: 'Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I was saying to myself"," why am I being contended with the Qur'ān? Let none of you recite anything from the Qur'ān when I recite aloud except Umm al-Qur'ān.'\""\n\nAbū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""This is a good isnād"," and its narrators are trustworthy.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Hishām ibn ʿAmmār also narrated it in the same manner from Ṣadaqah. [Munkar. The detailed discussion on that has preceded.]"""
"2921","(2921) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Abū ʿImrān al-Jawnī narrated to us; Hishām, meaning Ibn ʿAmmār, narrated to us; Ṣadaqah narrated to us; Zayd ibn Wāqid narrated to us from Ḥarām ibn Ḥakīm and Makḥūl, from Nāfiʿ ibn Maḥmūd al-Anṣārī, from ʿUbādah: ʿUbādah was in Īliyāʾ, and he was delayed from the Fajr prayer. Abū Nuʿaym — who was the first to give the adhān in Bayt al-Maqdis — led the prayer. I came with ʿUbādah until he lined up with the people. Abū Nuʿaym was reciting the Qur'ān aloud, and ʿUbādah recited Umm al-Qur'ān until I understood it from him. When he finished, I said: \I heard you reciting Umm al-Qur'ān.\"" He said: \""Yes. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) led us in one of the prayers in which the recitation is performed aloud"," and he said: 'Let none of you recite when I recite aloud except Umm al-Qur'ān.'\""\n\nThe ḥadīth is authentic from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and it has corroborating narrations. [Munkar. The discussion on it has preceded.]"""
"2922","(2922) Among them is what Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to me verbally; Yazīd ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth narrated to us; al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ, from Abū Qilābah, from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah, from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Perhaps you recite while the imām is reciting?\"" They said: \""Indeed"," we do that.\"" He said: \""Then do not do so unless one of you recites Fātiḥat al-Kitāb.\"" This is a good isnād.\n\nIt has also been said: from Abū Qilābah"," from Anas ibn Mālik — but it is not preserved. [Munkar. Ibn al-Qayyim said in Tahdhīb Sunan Abī Dāwūd"," 826.]"""
"2923","(2923) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ, Ibn al-Ḥammāmī, in Baghdād, informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Aḥwaṣ Muḥammad ibn al-Haytham — reading over him — narrated to us; Abū Tābah al-Rabīʿ ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr, from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from Anas ibn Mālik: When the Prophet (ﷺ) finished his prayer, he turned his face toward them and said: \Do you recite in your prayers while the imām is reciting?\"" They fell silent. He said it three times. Then a speaker or speakers said: \""Indeed"," we do that.\"" He said: \""Then do not do so. Let one of you recite Fātiḥat al-Kitāb to himself.\"" [Munkar. al-Fawāʾid al-Muʿallahah"," 102.]"""
"2924","(2924) Abū al-Ḥasan informed us; Aḥmad informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū Salamah narrated to us; Ḥammād, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from the Prophet (ﷺ) — similar to it.\n\nʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr al-Raqqī alone narrated it from Anas, and he is trustworthy, except that this is only known from Abū Qilābah from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah. [Abū Qilābah's narration is weak.]"
"2925","(2925) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Muʾammal narrated to us; Ismāʿīl, meaning Ibn ʿUlayyah, narrated from Ayyūb, from Abū Qilābah, from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding recitation.\n\nIsmāʿīl said, from Khālid: \I said to Abū Qilābah: 'Who narrated this to you?' He said: 'Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿĀʾishah"," a freedman of Banī Umayyah.'\"" [Weak. Due to the disconnection between Mūsā ibn Umayyah and the Prophet (ﷺ).]"""
"2926","(2926) Among them is what ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us; Mālik ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated to us. He said: \I was narrated to from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah"," from his father"," that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Do you recite behind me?' They said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Then do not do so except with Fātiḥat al-Kitāb.'\""\n\nMuḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī also narrated it from Yazīd ibn Hārūn"," and it is mursal.\n\nIt has also been narrated from another route from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr"," from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Qatādah"," from his father"," regarding what we have mentioned from him. [Weak. Due to the disconnection between al-Taymī and Ibn Abī Qatādah.]"""
"2927","(2927) Abū Saʿīd — Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl — informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī — informed us: Abū Usāmah — from al-Walīd, who is Ibn Kathīr — informed me: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the client of al-Ḥurqah — from Abū al-Sāʾib — from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmār al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād — informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh — informed us: it was recited to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad while I was listening — informed us: Bishr ibn ʿUmar — informed us: Mālik ibn Anas — from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, who said: I heard Abū al-Sāʾib, the client of Hishām ibn Zuhrah, saying: I heard Abū Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever performs a prayer in which he does not recite the Opening of the Book (Umm al-Qurʾān)"," it is deficient"," not complete.\"" He (Abū al-Sāʾib) said: I said: O Abū Hurayrah"," sometimes I am behind the imam"," so shall I recite behind him? He said: He took hold of my arm and said: Recite it"," O Persian"," to yourself (in your heart)"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: 'I have divided the prayer between Myself and My servant into two halves; half of it is for Me"," and half of it is for My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The servant says: {All praise is due to Allah"," Lord of the worlds} — Allah says: My servant has praised Me. The servant says: {The Most Merciful"," the Especially Merciful} — Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," says: My servant has extolled Me. The servant says: {Master of the Day of Judgment} — Allah says: My servant has glorified Me. The servant says: {You alone we worship"," and You alone we ask for help} — Allah says: This is between Me and My servant"," and My servant shall have what he asks.'\"" In the ḥadīth of al-Walīd ibn Kathīr: \""And when he says {Master of the Day of Judgment}"," He says: My servant has glorified Me — this is for Me"," and what remains is for him. He says: {You alone we worship"," and You alone we ask for help}.\"" Then he recited until he reached {not of those who have gone astray}.\n\nMuslim narrated it from Qutaybah"," from Mālik. And al-Ḥumaydī narrated it in the book of al-Radd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 395.]"""
"2928","(2928) From Sufyān — from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — from his father — from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Every prayer in which the Opening of the Book is not recited is deficient.\"" He said: I said: O Abū Hurayrah"," I hear the recitation of the imam. He said: O Persian — or O son of the Persian — recite it to yourself.\n\nAbū Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾinī informed us of it: Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: al-Ḥumaydī informed us"," and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd we have received reports of recitation behind the imam from a group of the Companions"," may Allah be pleased with them"," among them being the Commander of the Faithful ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥumaydī"," 973"," 974.]"""
"2929","(2929) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār — informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, and said: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: Abū Kurayb informed us: Ḥafṣ — from Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī — from Jawwāb al-Taymī and Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Muntashir — from al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd — from Yazīd ibn Sharīk, that he asked ʿUmar about recitation behind the imam, and he said: Recite the Opening of the Book. I said: Even if you are the imam? He said: Even if I am. I said: Even if you recite aloud? He said: Even if I recite aloud.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dāraquṭnī said: Its narrators are all trustworthy (thiqāt).]"
"2930","(2930) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Saʿīd al-Iṣṭakhrī — al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad — from his book, informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nawfal informed us: My father informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth informed us, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nʿAlī said: Its narrators are all trustworthy.\n\nAl-Shaykh said: What is indicated by the rest of the narrations is that Jawwāb took it from Yazīd ibn Sharīk, and Ibrāhīm took it from al-Ḥārith ibn Suwayd from Yazīd ibn Sharīk. And Ibrāhīm has another chain of narration for it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. As in the one before it.]"
"2931","(2931) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī informed us: Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd informed us: al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: from Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad, meaning Ibn al-Muntashir, who said: I heard my father saying: I heard ʿAbāyah, a man from Banī Tamīm, saying: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: There is no prayer except with the Opening of the Book and something along with it. He said: I said: What is your view when I am behind the imam? He said: Recite it to yourself.\n\nAnd among them is the Commander of the Faithful ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf. The condition of the man from Banī Tamīm is unknown (jahālah).]"
"2932","(2932) Abū al-Ḥusayn — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād — informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Darastūyah informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān al-Fārisī informed us: Ādam informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn informed us: I heard al-Zuḥrī narrating from Ibn Abī Rāfiʿ — from his father —\n\n(Ḥ) And Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Muʿallā informed us: from Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ — from Maʿmar — from al-Zuḥrī — from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ — from ʿAlī, that he used to command or encourage that recitation be done behind the imam in the first two rakʿahs of Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr with the Opening of the Book and a sūrah, and in the last two rakʿahs with the Opening of the Book.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Shāmī narrated it similarly from Maʿmar, and it is more authentic than the narration of Shuʿbah, where he said: from his father, from ʿAlī. And others narrated it from Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn in a manner similar to the narration of Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 3726.]"
"2933","(2933) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Sufyān ibn Ḥusayn informed us: from al-Zuḥrī — from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ — from ʿAlī, and from a client of theirs — from Jābir, both saying: The imam and those behind him recite in the first two rakʿahs the Opening of the Book and a sūrah, and in the last two rakʿahs the Opening of the Book.\n\nAnd the hearing of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, is established, for he was his scribe.\n\nAnd we have received from al-Ḥakam and Ḥammād that ʿAlī used to command recitation behind the imam, and it is a mursal narration serving as testimony for what preceded of the connected narrations, and in all of that there is evidence for the weakness of what has been narrated from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, to the contrary, through chains that are not worth mentioning due to their weakness.\n\nAnd among them is ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. From ʿAlī, and it is not authentic from Jābir.]"
"2934","(2934) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū Salamah informed us: Ḥammād informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwn informed us: from Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah — from Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ, who said: I heard ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, may Allah be pleased with him, reciting behind the imam, so I said to him: Do you recite behind the imam? ʿUbādah said: There is no prayer except with recitation.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain is authentic (isnāduhū ṣaḥīḥ). And it is also established as marfūʿ with these words.]"
"2935","(2935) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ informed me: al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Bayhaqī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us: Shuʿbah informed us: from Muslim, Abū al-Naḍr, who said: I heard Ḥamlah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrating from ʿUbādah ibn al-Ṣāmit, that he saw a man who did not complete his rukūʿ or his sujūd. So he came to him, took him by the hand, and said: Do not resemble this one or his likes, for there is no prayer except with the Mother of the Book (Umm al-Kitāb). If you are behind an imam, recite to yourself, and if you are alone, let your ears hear it, and do not harm those on your right or those on your left.\n\nHe is Muslim ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAkkī al-Shāmī, and the position of ʿUbādah in this matter is well known.\n\nAnd among them is Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"2936","(2936) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Makhlad informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAtīq informed us: Isḥāq al-Rāzī informed us: from Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī — from Abū Sinān — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī al-Hudhayl, who said: I asked Ubayy ibn Kaʿb: Shall I recite behind the imam? He said: Yes.\n\nAnd among them is ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"2937","(2937) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Abū ʿAmr Aḥmad ibn al-Mubārak al-Mustamlī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; Sharīk narrated from Ashʿath ibn Sulaym from ʿAbdullāh ibn Ziyād al-Asadī, who said: I prayed beside ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him) behind the imam, and I heard him reciting in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr.\n\nAnd among them is Muʿādh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him). [Weak]"
"2938","(2938) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūd narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Abū al-Fayḍ, who said: I heard Abū Shaybah al-Mahrī say: A man asked Muʿādh ibn Jabal about recitation behind the imam. He said: When the imam recites aloud, recite Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and {Qul Huwa Allāhu Aḥad}. And if you do not hear [him], then recite within yourself, and do not disturb those on your right or those on your left.\n\nAnd among them is ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him). [Authentic]"
"2939","(2939) Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated from al-ʿAyzār ibn Ḥurayth from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Recite Sūrat al-Fātiḥah behind the imam. [Authentic. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 3773]"
"2940","(2940) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Ibn ʿArafah narrated to us; Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Layth from ʬāʾiʿ from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: Do not abandon reciting Sūrat al-Fātiḥah behind the imam in every rakʿah, whether he recites aloud or does not recite aloud.\n\nAnd among them are ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with them both). The narration of Abū al-Azhar al-Ḍubaʿī from Abū al-ʿĀliyah from Ibn ʿUmar has already been cited.\n\nAnd ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr from Mujāhid, who said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar and Ibn ʿUtbah reciting behind the imam — thus he said.\n\nAnd it is narrated from Layth ibn Abī Sulaym from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿUmar with the same meaning.\n\nAnd in my view, he intended ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ. [Weak. Narrated by Ibn ʿAbd al-Razzāq, 2773]"
"2941","(2941) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrawayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; Ḥuṣayn narrated, who said: I prayed beside ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah and heard him reciting behind the imam. Then I met Mujāhid and mentioned that to him.\n\nMujāhid said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ reciting behind the imam in the Ẓuhr prayer from Sūrah Maryam. [Authentic. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 3750]"
"2942","(2942) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us; al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us; Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥuṣayn, who said: I heard Mujāhid say: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr reciting in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr behind the imam. This is an authentic chain of narration, as is the one before it.\n\nAnd among them is Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him). The narration of al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from his father and from Abū al-Sāʾib from Abū Hurayrah has already been cited.\n\nAnd among them is Abū al-Dardāʾ (may Allah be pleased with him). [Authentic. Ibn Abī Shaybah, 3749]"
"2943","(2943) Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥawārī, ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān, Maḥmūd ibn Khālid, Kathīr ibn ʿUbayd, and ʿAlī ibn Sahl — they all said: al-Walīd, who is ibn Muslim, narrated to us from al-Awzāʿī from Ḥassān ibn ʬāʾiyyah that Abū al-Dardāʾ said: Do not abandon the recitation of Sūrat al-Fātiḥah behind the imam, whether he recites aloud or does not recite aloud.\n\nThese are the words of Kathīr.\n\nAnd ʿAlī and Ibn Abī al-Ḥawārī added: \Even if you recite and then go into rukūʿ.\""\n\nAnd ʿAmr added alone: \""And if he is in rukūʿ"," then recite it when you know that you will complete it.\""\n\nAnd among them is Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Weak]"""
"2944","(2944) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Misʿar from Yazīd al-Faqīr from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: We used to recite behind the imam in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr — in the first two rakʿahs, Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and a sūrah, and in the last two rakʿahs, Sūrat al-Fātiḥah alone.\n\nAnd among them is Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him). [Authentic. Narrated by Ibn Mājah, 827]"
"2945","(2945) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Sahl narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥamzah narrated from Abū Naḍrah, who said: I asked Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him) about recitation behind the imam. He said: [Recite] Sūrat al-Fātiḥah.\n\nAnd among them is Hishām ibn ʿĀmir (may Allah be pleased with him). [Weak. Ibn Abī Shaybah, 3791]"
"2946","(2946) Abū Saʿīd al-Ḥākim al-Isfarāʾinī informed us; Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Hilāl that Hishām ibn ʿĀmir recited, and it was said to him: Do you recite behind the imam? He said: Indeed, we do so.\n\nAnd among them is Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him). [Weak. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr, 443]"
"2947","(2947) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in al-Tārīkh, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Jawharī narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Wajīh, meaning al-Naysābūrī, narrated to us, al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥawshab informed us from Thābit from Anas, who said: \He used to command us to recite behind the imam.\"" He (Thābit) said: \""I used to stand beside Anas and he would recite Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and a sūrah from al-Mufaṣṣal"," and he would make us hear his recitation so that we might learn from him.\""\n\nThus he said"," and Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in the book *al-Qirāʾah khalfa al-Imām* from Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī from al-Naḍr from al-ʿAwwām"," and he is ibn Ḥamzah. [Munkar]"""
"2948","(2948) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, al-ʿAwwām — and he is ibn Ḥamzah — informed us, and he mentioned it similarly. And this is more authentic. And among them is ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal al-Muzanī, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"2949","(2949) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Yūnus narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, Ḥammād ibn Salamah, and Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, from ʿUmar ibn Abī Suḥaym, who said: \ʿAbdullāh ibn Mughaffal al-Muzanī"," the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," used to teach us to recite behind the imam in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr in the first two rakʿahs — Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and a sūrah — and in the last two rakʿahs"," Sūrat al-Fātiḥah alone.\""\n\nSaʿīd ibn ʿĀmir followed him (in narration) from Shuʿbah.\n\nAnd among them is ʿĀʾishah al-Ṣiddīqah"," daughter of al-Ṣiddīq"," may Allah be pleased with her and with her father. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2950","(2950) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Yaḥyā al-Samarqandī narrated to me verbally that Muḥammad ibn Naṣr narrated to them, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from ʢāṣim from Dhakwān from ʿĀʾishah, and from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with both of them: that they both used to command recitation behind the imam when he did not recite aloud. [Ḥasan]"
"2951","(2951) And Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Rustah narrated to us, Shaybān ibn Farrūkh narrated to us, ʿIkrimah ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, ʢāṣim ibn Bahdalah narrated from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah and ʿĀʾishah: that they both used to command recitation behind the imam in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr in the first two rakʿahs — Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and something from the Qurʾān — and ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, used to recite in the last two rakʿahs Sūrat al-Fātiḥah alone.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʢImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn, and it has been narrated to us from a group of the Tābiʿīn. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"2952","(2952) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Sahl al-Ramlī narrated to us, al-Walīd — meaning ibn Muslim — narrated from Ibn Jābir, Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-ʿAlāʾ, who said: \Makhūl used to say: 'Recite in Maghrib"," ʿIshāʾ"," and Ṣubḥ — Sūrat al-Fātiḥah — in every rakʿah"," silently.'\""\n\nMakhūl said: \""Recite it in that in which the imam recites aloud"," when he recites Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and then falls silent — silently. And if he does not fall silent"," then recite it before him"," with him"," or after him; do not leave it under any circumstance.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān that he said: \""The imam has two pauses; so seize them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2953","(2953) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us, Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Suwayd narrated to me from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, Maʿmar and Ibn Jurayj informed us from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khuthaym from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said: \But those who have passed away — when they pronounced the takbīr"," the imam would remain silent for a period during which they would recite Umm al-Kitāb.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Ibn Jurayj said in his ḥadīth from Ibn Khuthaym from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr: \""When they pronounced the takbīr"," they would not begin recitation until they knew that those behind them had recited Sūrat al-Fātiḥah.\"" [Ḥasan. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 2789]"""
"2954","(2954) He said: And Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Suwayd narrated from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father, that he said: \O my sons"," recite during the imam's pause"," for no prayer is complete except with Sūrat al-Fātiḥah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2955","(2955) He said: And Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Yūnus and Manṣūr narrated from al-Ḥasan that he used to say: \Recite behind the imam in every prayer — Sūrat al-Fātiḥah — to yourself.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2956","(2956) He said: And Muḥammad narrated to us, Muḥammad narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq al-Shaybānī narrated from al-Shaʿbī that he used to say: \Recite behind the imam in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr — in the first two rakʿahs"," Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and a sūrah"," and in the last two rakʿahs"," Sūrat al-Fātiḥah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2957","(2957) Abū Saʿīd al-Isfarāʾinī informed us, Abū Baḥr al-Barbahārī informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Wakīʿ narrated to us, Mālik ibn Mughwal said: I heard al-Shaʿbī reciting the Qurʾān aloud behind the imām.\n[Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 3772]"
"2958","(2958) He said, and Wakīʿ narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abī Khālid reported from al-Shaʿbī, he said: \Recite in all five\"" — meaning all the prayers.\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2959","(2959) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us, they said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original copy, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Saʿdī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā — who is ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim — narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Budayl reported from Abū al-Jawzāʾ, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to commence the prayer with the takbīr and the recitation with {al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi l-ʿālamīn}. When he bowed (rukūʿ), he neither raised his head excessively nor lowered it completely, but kept it between the two. When he raised his head from rukūʿ, he did not prostrate until he stood upright. When he raised his head from prostration, he did not prostrate again until he sat upright. He used to spread his left leg and erect his right leg. He used to recite the tashahhud between every two rakʿahs. He forbade us from sitting in the manner of the devil (ʿaqib al-shayṭān). He forbade one of us from spreading his arms like a predatory animal. And he concluded the prayer with the salām. The wording of both narrations is the same, except that in the narration of Yazīd it states: \And he used to forbid the ʿaqib al-shayṭān.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Aʿlā said: ʿAqib al-shayṭān means sitting on the backs of both feet entirely.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus and others from Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim.\n[Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Muslim"," 498]"""
"2960","(2960) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us from the original of his book, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us in Kūfah, Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn and Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd reported from Misʿar, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Qibṭiyyah, from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: When we used to pray behind the Prophet ﷺ, we would say — meaning by gesturing with his index finger — \al-salāmu ʿalaykum"," al-salāmu ʿalaykum.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said to us: \""What is the matter with people that they gesture with their hands during prayer as though they are the tails of refractory horses? Is it not sufficient for one of you — or he said: for one of them — to place his hand upon his thigh"," then greet his brother to his right and to his left?\""\n[Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Muslim"," 431]"""
"2961","(2961) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā and Wakīʿ reported from Misʿar, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Qibṭiyyah, from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: When we used to pray behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one of us would gesture with his hand to his right and to his left. When he finished the prayer, he said: \What is the matter with one of you that he gestures with his hand as though it were the tails of refractory horses? It is sufficient — or he said: Is it not sufficient — for one of you to say thus.\"" And he gestured with his index finger: \""And greet his brother to his right and to his left.\""\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Wakīʿ"," and from Abī Kurayb from Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah with the meaning of this ḥadīth"," except that he said: \""Amā yakfī\"" — he did not express doubt in it — and he attributed the wording to Ibn Abī Zāʾidah.\n[Ṣaḥīh. See the preceding ḥadīth]"""
"2962","(2962) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Ṭabarānī informed us, Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us, al-Thawrī reported from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, from Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who attributed it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The key of prayer is purification (ṭahārah)"," its consecration (iḥrām) is the takbīr"," and its dissolution (iḥlāl) is the salām.\""\n\nAnd we have narrated that in the ḥadīth of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and others from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAnd in that there is an indication of the weakness of that.\n[Ṣaḥīh for other reasons. Previously narrated as no. 2261]"""
"2963","(2963) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us from the original of his book, Abū ʿAmr ibn Najayd informed us, Abū Muslim informed us, Abū ʀāṣim informed us, Abū ʿAwānah reported from al-Ḥakam, from ʀāṣim ibn Ḍamrah, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When one sits for the duration of the tashahhud and then breaks his wuḍūʾ, his prayer has been completed.\n\nʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī).\n\nThe Commander of the Believers ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, does not contradict what he narrated from the Prophet ﷺ. Even if that is authentically reported from him, he is rebutted by what he himself and others narrated from our master al-Muṣṭafā ﷺ, before whose authority no statement of anyone in his Ummah constitutes proof.\n[Ḍaʿīf. Ibn Abī Shaybah, 8469]"
"2964","(2964) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Saʿid ibn ʀāmir reported from Shuʿbah, from Abī Isḥāq, from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ, who said: ʿAbd Allāh said: \The key of prayer is the takbīr"," and its conclusion is the salām. When the imām gives salām"," then stand if you wish.\""\n\nThis authentic athar from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd indicates the correctness of what we maintain.\n[Ṣaḥīh]"""
"2965","(2965) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Khāliq al-Muʾadhdhin informed us, Abū Muḥammad ʿAlī ibn Ḥamawayh informed us in Bukhārā, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū Khaythamah reported from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr, from al-Qāsim ibn Mukhaymirah, who said: ʿAlqamah took hold of my hand and narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd took hold of his hand, and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of ʿAbd Allāh's hand, and taught him the tashahhud in prayer, and said: \Say: al-taḥiyyātu lillāhi wa-l-ṣalawātu wa-l-ṭayyibāt. al-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibād Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn.\""\n\nAbū Khaythamah said: And some of our companions added to me in this ḥadīth from al-Ḥasan: \""Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh.\""\n\nAbū Khaythamah said: What reached my memory from al-Ḥasan regarding the remainder of this ḥadīth is: \""When you have done this"," or fulfilled this"," you have completed your prayer. If you wish to stand"," stand"," and if you wish to sit"," sit.\""\n\nThis is a ḥadīth which a group narrated from Abū Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah"," and they appended the end of the ḥadīth to its beginning. Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā indicated that part of the ḥadīth had been lost from Zuhayr's memory from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr.\n\nAnd Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated it from Zuhayr"," and he claimed that part of the ḥadīth had been erased from his book or had become illegible.\n\nAnd Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated it from Zuhayr"," and he separated the end of the ḥadīth from its beginning"," and made it the statement of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," as though he had taken it from him before it was lost from his memory or from his book.\n[Ṣaḥīh]"""
"2966","(2966) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed it to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, Shabābah ibn Sawwār narrated to us, Abū Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr narrated to us, and he mentioned the ḥadīth with the meaning of the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā up to his words \al-ṣāliḥīn","\"" then he said: \""Ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa rasūluh.\""\n\nʿAbd Allāh said: \""When you have said that"," you have fulfilled what was obligatory upon you of prayer. If you wish to stand"," stand"," and if you wish to sit"," sit.\""\n\nʿAlī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Shabābah is trustworthy (thiqah)"," and he separated the end of the ḥadīth"," making it the statement of Ibn Masʿūd"," and it is more authentic than the narration of the one who appended its end to the words of the Prophet ﷺ"," and Allah knows best.\n\nGhassān ibn al-Rabīʿ and others followed him"," and they narrated it from Ibn Thawbān from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr likewise — the end of the ḥadīth being the words of Ibn Masʿūd"," not raised to the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nAbū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us"," Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," he said: Zuhayr erred in his narration from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr"," and he appended to the words of the Prophet ﷺ what was not from his words"," namely his statement: \""When you have done this"," you have completed your prayer.\""\n\nAnd this is only from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. Likewise ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thābit ibn Thawbān narrated it from al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥurr.\n[Ṣaḥīh. See the preceding ḥadīth]"""
"2967","(2967) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aziz narrated to us; Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' al-Mawsili narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn al-Hur, who mentioned the hadith similar to the narration of Shababat and Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\nAnd he said at its end: 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: \When you have finished this"," you have completed your prayer. Then if you wish"," sit"," and if you wish"," stand.\"""""
"2968","(2968) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz informed me; 'Arubah al-Harrani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us; Ibn Thawban narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn al-Hur from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah from 'Alqamah ibn Qays from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: \The Prophet ﷺ taught me the Tashahhud","\"" and he mentioned it up to \""'Abdihi wa Rasulihi\"" (His servant and His Messenger).\n\n'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud said: \""When you have finished your prayer"," if you wish"," remain seated"," and if you wish"," depart.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: This phrase — \""When you have finished your prayer\"" — if it is preserved (in the narration)"," it is more consistent with what has been narrated to us from Ibn Mas'ud regarding the completion of the prayer with the Salam"," and with what we shall narrate from him from the Prophet ﷺ concerning the Salam. It is as though he (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to oppose the one who claimed that it is not permissible for the follower to depart after finishing the prayer before the Imam departs. If the first wording is established from the Prophet ﷺ"," then it is known that the Prophet's ﷺ teaching of 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud the Tashahhud of the prayer was at the beginning of when the Tashahhud was legislated. After that"," the prayer upon the Prophet ﷺ was legislated"," as indicated by their statement: \""We have known the Salam upon you"," so how is the prayer upon you?\"" Then the Salam at the end of the prayer was legislated along with it or after it"," and the matter was left to him. And Allah knows best. What confirms this is… [Sound. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2969","(2969) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us from his original; Abu Muhammad Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Shaibani al-Baghdadi in Harah informed us; Mu'adh ibn Najdah narrated to us; Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Dharr narrated to us.\n\n'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah informed us: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ completed the Tashahhud in the prayer, he would turn his face toward the people before the Salam was revealed.\n\nYunus ibn Bukayr likewise narrated it from 'Umar ibn Dharr from 'Ata', who said: \And that was before the Salam was revealed.\"" And even though this is a Mursal narration"," it agrees with the connected"," Musnad narrations regarding the Salam. [Weak"," Mursal.]"""
"2970","(4) As for the hadith which Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn An'um narrated to us from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi' and Bakr ibn Sawadah from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When the Imam completes the prayer and is seated"," and he nullifies his wudu before speaking"," his prayer is complete"," and the prayer of those behind him who completed the prayer is also complete\"" — then it is not sound.\n\n'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad is alone in narrating it"," and there is disagreement regarding his wording. 'Abd al-Rahman is not used as a proof; Yahya al-Qattan and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi would not narrate from him due to his weakness. Ahmad ibn Hanbal"," Yahya ibn Ma'in"," and other huffaz criticized him. The response to it is the same as the response to what has been narrated to us from Ibn Mas'ud. And with Allah is success. [Weak. Abu Hatim said: This is a Munkar hadith.]"""
"2971","(2971) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam and Mansur from Mujahid from Abu Ma'mar, who said: \I prayed behind a man in Makkah"," and he gave two Salams. I mentioned that to 'Abdullah"," and he said: 'How did he come to know it?'\"" And al-Hakam said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Zuhayr ibn Harb from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan"," except that he said: \""'Anna 'aliqaha\"" (how did he grasp it?) instead of \""'Anna 'aqalaha\"" (how did he understand it?). [Sound. Ahmad narrated it (4239).]"""
"2972","(2972) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam from Mujahid from Abu Ma'mar: that an Imam of the people of Makkah gave two Salams. I mentioned that to 'Abdullah, and 'Abdullah said: \How did he grasp it?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Shu'bah"," and he added in it: Shu'bah said: \""He raised it (to the Prophet) once.\"" [Sound. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2973","(2973) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, and he mentioned it and said: \An amir or a man…\""\n\nThis hadith has corroborating narrations from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud from the Prophet ﷺ. [Sound. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2974","(2974) Among them is what Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Qasim ibn al-Qasim al-Sayyari in Marw narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Hatim narrated to us; 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us; al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us; Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us; 'Alqamah ibn Qays, al-Aswad ibn Yazid, and Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the Salam on his right: \As-salamu 'alaykum wa rahmatullah\"" until the whiteness of his right cheek could be seen"," and on his left: \""As-salamu 'alaykum wa rahmatullah\"" until the whiteness of his left cheek could be seen.\n\nThis is a hadith narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri"," Zaidah ibn Qudamah"," Abu al-Ahwas"," 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd al-Tanafisi"," Isra'il ibn Yunus"," and Sharik ibn 'Abdullah al-Nakha'i from Abu Ishaq from Abu Ishaq from Abu al-Ahwas and al-Aswad. In a third narration from him: from Abu Ishaq from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad from his father and 'Alqamah from 'Abdullah.\n\nLikewise"," Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated it from Abu Ishaq. [Sound. Al-Tirmidhi said: This is a Hasan Sahih hadith.]"""
"2975","(2975) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us.\n\n(And) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi informed us. Both said: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us; Abu Badr Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Abu Ishaq narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us from his father and 'Alqamah from 'Abdullah, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the Takbir at every rising"," lowering"," standing"," and sitting"," and he would give the Salam on his right and on his left until I could see the whiteness of both his cheeks. And I saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar doing that.\"" [Sound. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2976","(2976) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Mukram narrated to us; Abu al-Nadr narrated to us; Abu Khaythamah narrated to us; Abu Ishaq narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us; Abu Ja'far ibn Duha narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us; Isra'il and Zuhayr narrated to us from Abu Ishaq with its like, and he added: \As-salamu 'alaykum wa rahmatullah"," as-salamu 'alaykum wa rahmatullah.\"" And I saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar doing it.\n\nLikewise"," Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated it from Abu Khaythamah — Zuhayr.\n\nAbu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni"," may Allah have mercy on him"," used to regard this narration favorably and say: \""It has the best isnad.\"" Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us of that from him.\n\nIt has also been narrated from another chain from 'Abdullah. [Sound. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"2977","(2977) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim narrated to us; Abū Saʿīd al-Mu'addib narrated from Zakariyyā, from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq, from ʿAbdullāh, who said: \I have not forgotten any matter"," for indeed I have not forgotten the salām of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) in the prayer — from his right and from his left: 'Alaykum wa raḥmatullāh. As-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh.' Then he said: 'It is as though I am looking at the whiteness of his cheek.'\""\n\nAnd others narrated it from Manṣūr. And Ḥurayth ibn Abī Maṭar narrated it from al-Shaʿbī from al-Barā'. [Ḥasan]"""
"2978","(2978) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh, who is Ibn Mūsā, informed us; Ḥurayth narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from al-Barā' ibn ʿĀzib, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to make salām from his right and from his left until his cheek would become visible: 'As-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh.'\""\n\nAnd it is established from Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ and Jābir ibn Samurah from the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"2979","(2979) As for the ḥadīth of Saʿd, Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us from the original of his book; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated — Ibn Salamah said: and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated — both saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿd, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from his father, who said: \I used to see the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) make salām from his right and from his left until I could see the whiteness of his cheek.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Dāraquṭnī said: Its chain is ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"2980","(2980) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; ʿUbayd ibn Sharik narrated to us; Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us; Bishr ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad al-Kātib narrated to us; Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us; Muṣʿab ibn Thābit ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd, from his father Saʿd, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) make salām in the prayer with two salāmas — a salām from his right: 'As-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh","' and a salām from his left: 'As-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh' — until the whiteness of his cheeks could be seen from this side and that side.\""\n\nHe said: \""Then I mentioned this ḥadīth to al-Zuhrī and he said: 'This is a ḥadīth I have not heard from the ḥadīths of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).'\"" Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad said to him: \""Have you heard all the ḥadīths of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?\"" Al-Zuhrī said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then two-thirds of them?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then half of them?\"" Al-Zuhrī stopped at the half or at the third. Ismāʿīl said to him: \""Then place this ḥadīth among what you have not heard.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"2981","(2981) As for the ḥadīth of Jābir ibn Samurah: Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duhaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us in Kūfah; Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghazrah al-Ghifārī narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd, and Abū Nuʿaym narrated from Misʿar, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Qibṭiyyah, from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: \When we prayed behind the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," we would say — meaning by the gesture of his index finger — 'As-salāmu ʿalaykum"," as-salāmu ʿalaykum.' The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to us: 'What is the matter with people that they gesture with their hands in the prayer as though they are the tails of restive horses? Is it not sufficient for one of them — or one of you — to place his hand upon his thigh and then make salām to his right and to his left?'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Misʿar ibn Kidām"," except that he said: \""Then he should make salām upon his brother on his right and his left.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Mundhirī cited it (896).]"""
"2982","(2982) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us; Ḥajjāj said: Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā informed me, from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān, from his uncle Wāsiʿ ibn Ḥabbān, that he asked ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He said: \Allāhu Akbar. Whenever he lowered"," [he said] Allāhu Akbar. Whenever he raised"," [he said Allāhu Akbar]. Then he would say: 'As-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh' — from his right: 'As-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh' — from his left.\""\n\nḤajjāj ibn Muḥammad and a group established its chain"," and some of them shortened it from Ibn Jurayj.\n\nʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī differed regarding it from ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā"," and those who established it are authoritative; the disagreement of those who opposed them does not harm them. And Allāh knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad cited it (2/71/5402).]"""
"2983","(2983) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed me; Salamah ibn Kuhayl said: \I heard Ḥujr"," Abū al-ʿAnbas"," say: 'I heard ʿAlqamah ibn Wā'il narrate from Wā'il — and I heard it from Wā'il — that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).'\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth"," and in it: \""And he made salām from his right and from his left.\""\n\nSimilarly"," ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Yuḥṣubī narrated it from Wā'il ibn Ḥujr from the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been previously cited in a similar manner.]"""
"2984","(2984) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Khaḍir al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Razīn, from ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him), that he made salām from his right and from his left, then stood up.\n\nAnd al-Mughīrah narrated it from Abī Razīn, and added in it: \Salāmun ʿalaykum"," salāmun ʿalaykum.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2985","(2985) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Tinnīsī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Abī Salamah narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad al-Makkī narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to make salām in the prayer with a single salām, facing his face, inclining slightly to the right side — a little or somewhat.\n\nZuhayr ibn Muḥammad was alone in narrating it.\n\nAnd it was narrated from another route from ʿĀ'ishah as a mawqūf [statement]. [Munkar. Ibn Mājah cited it (919).]"
"2986","(2986) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī narrated to us; Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from al-Qāsim, from ʿĀ'ishah (may Allāh be pleased with her), that she used to make salām in the prayer with a single salām, facing her face: \As-salāmu ʿalaykum.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdullāh said: Wahb and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd followed him from ʿUbaydullāh from al-Qāsim.\n\nAnd al-Dārawardī said from ʿUbaydullāh from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim from his father.\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""The majority are more deserving of preservation than the lone narrator.\""\n\nAnd it was narrated from Anas ibn Mālik"," Samurah ibn Jundub"," and Salamah al-Akwāʿī from the Prophet (peace be upon him). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"2987","As for the hadith of Anas: Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Abu al-Muthanna informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated from Humayd, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to give one single salutation (taslim). [Munkar. Ibn Rajab said in al-Fath 6/92]"
"2988","As for the hadith of Samurah ibn Jundub: Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed it to us; Abu 'Amr ibn Matar informed us; Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Katib informed us; Nu'aym ibn Hammad informed us; Ruh ibn 'Ati' ibn Abi Maymunah narrated from his father, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to give one salutation in prayer facing forward, and when he gave the salutation to his right, he would then give it to his left."
"2989","As for the hadith of Salamah al-Akwa': Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Qurashi, the mu'adhdhin of the mosque of Egypt, informed us; Yahya ibn Rashid al-Basri narrated from Yazid, the mawla of Salamah ibn al-Akwa', from Salamah ibn al-Akwa' (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) perform ablution and wipe his head once, and he prayed and gave the salutation once. And it has been narrated from a group of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) that they used to give a single salutation. And this is among the permissible matters of difference, and restricting oneself to what is permissible is sufficient. And with Allah lies success. [Da'if. Narrated by Ibn Majah 437]"
"2990","Abu al-Husayn ibn Bushran informed us in Baghdad; Abu 'Ali Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; Ahmad ibn Mulab informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Uqbah al-Shaybani informed us; Ibn al-Mubarak narrated from al-Awza'i, from Qurrah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Shortening the salutation (hafdh al-salam) is a Sunnah.\"" Thus narrated al-Firyabi and Mubashir ibn Isma'il al-Halabi from al-Awza'i"," as a marfu' narration. And 'Abdhan narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak from al-Awza'i"," but he stopped it (as a mawquf narration)"," and it appears to be a deficiency on the part of some of the narrators. [Munkar. Narrated by Ahmad 2/532/10898"," Abu Dawud 1004]"""
"2991","Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed it to us; Abu al-'Abbas al-Qasim ibn al-Qasim al-Sayyari informed us; Abu al-Muwajjih informed us; 'Abdhan informed us; 'Abd Allah narrated from al-Awza'i, mentioning it with his chain of narration as a mawquf narration traced back to Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him). [Da'if. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi 997]"
"2992","Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, saying: I asked Abu Zakariyya al-'Anbari, and he narrated it to us from Abu 'Abd Allah al-Bushanj regarding shortening the salutation, and he said: That one should not prolong the salutation, nor should one abbreviate it excessively. [Sahih]"
"2993","Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qattan informed us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf informed us; 'Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad informed us; Mis'ar narrated from 'Ubayd Allah ibn al-Qibtiyyah, who said: Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me, saying: When we used to pray behind the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), we would say with our hands, \Al-salamu 'alaykum"," al-salamu 'alaykum.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""What is the matter with these people who gesture with their hands as though they were the tails of headstrong horses? Is it not sufficient for one of you to place his hand upon his thigh and then greet his brother to his right and to his left?\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of Mis'ar ibn Kidam. [Sahih. And it has been previously cited by number]"""
"2994","Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-Tanukhi narrated to me. (H) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Nadr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Faqih informed us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi informed us; Abu al-Jawahir Muhammad ibn 'Uthman al-Tanukhi informed us; Sa'id ibn Bashir narrated from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to respond to the Imam, to show mutual love, and for some of us to greet one another. [Da'if. Narrated by Abu Dawud 1001]"
"2995","Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Dawud informed us; 'Amr ibn 'Ali, 'Umar ibn Shabbah, and Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati said: 'Abd al-A'la ibn al-Qasim Abu Bishr informed us; Hammam narrated from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to greet our Imams and for some of us to greet one another. [Da'if. And it has been previously cited in the one before it]"
"2996","Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud informed us; Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sufyan informed us; Yahya ibn Hassan informed us; Sulayman ibn Musa Abu Dawud informed us; Ja'far ibn Sa'd ibn Samurah ibn Jundub informed us; Khubayb ibn Sulayman narrated from his father Sulayman ibn Samurah, from Samurah ibn Jundub: To proceed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us, when in the middle of the prayer or at its conclusion: \Begin before the salutation and say: 'At-tahiyyat at-tayyibat"," as-salawat"," al-mulku lillah' (All compliments"," pure words"," prayers"," and sovereignty belong to Allah). Then give the salutation to the right"," then give the salutation to your reciter (i.e."," your Imam) and to yourselves.\"" In this there is evidence that the intended meaning of responding to the Imam is that one intends"," in one's salutation concluding the prayer"," to respond to him"," not that one gives a separate salutation for him. And it has been narrated to us from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to say: \""Al-salamu 'alaykum\"" to his right"," then he would respond to the Imam"," and if someone greeted him from his left"," he would respond to him. And it has been narrated to us from al-Zuhri that he said: Responding to the Imam with his salutation is a Sunnah. And Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari used to say: When you give the salutation to your right"," it suffices you for responding to him (the Imam). [Da'if]"""
"2997","(2997) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Shādhān narrated to me: Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsá narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū al-Walīd informed me: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsá narrated from Isrāʾīl, from Furāt al-Qazzāz, from ʿUbaydullāh — meaning Ibn al-Qibṭiyyah — from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when we gave the salām, we would say with our hands, \Al-salāmu ʿalaykum"," al-salāmu ʿalaykum.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at us and said: \""What is the matter with you that you gesture with your hands as though they were the tails of headstrong horses? When one of you gives the salām"," let him turn to his companion and not gesture with his hand.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qāsim ibn Zakariyyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was previously cited under no. 2981"," 2993.]"""
"2998","(2998) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥibbān ibn Mūsá informed us: ʿAbdullāh narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī — he narrated to him — Maḥmūd ibn al-Rabīʿ informed me: I heard ʿItbān ibn Mālik al-Anṣārī, and he mentioned the hadith regarding the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with them, saying: Then he gave the salām, and we gave the salām when he gave the salām.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥibbān, and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Maʿmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 840.]"
"2999","(2999) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyá narrated from Sufyān, who narrated to me: Yaʿlá ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated from Jābir ibn Yazīd ibn al-Aswad, from his father, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he finished (the prayer), he would turn (from the direction of the qiblah). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad, 160/17613.]"
"3000","(3000) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Marwazī informed us: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us. Both said: Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us: Misʿar narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed me: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from Misʿar, from Thābit ibn ʿUbayd, from Ibn al-Barrāʾ, from al-Barrāʾ, who said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we liked to be on his right side so that he might turn his face toward us. He said: I heard him say: \Rabbi qinī ʿadhābaka yawma tabʿathu ʿibādaka\"" (My Lord"," protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 4/290/18753.]"""
"3001","(3001) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Baghdādī narrated to us: Yaḥyá ibn Ayyūb al-Miṣrī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Farrūkh informed us: Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAṭāʾ, from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer, yet complete. He said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and at the moment he gave the salām, he would stand up. Then I prayed with Abū Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and when he gave the salām, he would spring up from his place, as though he were rising from a heated stone.\n\nThis was narrated uniquely by ʿAbdullāh ibn Farrūkh al-Miṣrī, and he has other unique narrations, and Allah knows best.\n\nAnd the well-known narration is from Abū al-Ḍuḥá, from Masrūq, who said: Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, when he gave the salām, would stand as though he were sitting on a heated stone. And it has been narrated from ʿAlī that he gave the salām and then stood up. [Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah, 1717.]"
"3002","(3002) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aʿṣam informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm al-Samarī narrated to us: Ḥajjāj narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who informed me: Ziyād narrated from Abū al-Zinād, who said: I heard Khārijah ibn Zayd criticizing the imāms for sitting in their prayer after giving the salām, and he said: The Sunnah regarding that is that the imām should stand at the moment he gives the salām.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Shaʿbī and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī that both of them disliked it. And it is mentioned from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, and Allah, the Most High, knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. (Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī and al-Shaʿbī disliked it.)]"
"3003","(3003) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Hind bint al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Abī Rabīʿah informed me from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave the salām from his prayer, the women would stand as soon as he completed his salām, and the Prophet ﷺ would remain in his place for a short while.\n\nIbn Shihāb, may Allah have mercy on him, said: And we think — and Allah, the Most High, knows best — that his remaining was so that the women might depart before those of the men who had turned away could catch up with them.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd and others, from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd, and he said: Hind bint al-Ḥārith. And some of them said: from al-Zuhrī: al-Firāsiyyah. And some of them said: al-Qurashiyyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm, 1/14.]"
"3004","(3004) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq ibn Hammām informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Hind bint al-Ḥārith, from Umm Salamah, who said: The Prophet ﷺ, when he gave the salām, would remain briefly. They (the Companions) used to think that this was so that the women might depart before the men. [Munkar.]"
"3005","(3005) Abā Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyá al-Bazzāz informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: ʿĀṣim narrated from Abū al-Walīd — who is ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith — from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not sit after the prayer except for the duration in which he would say: \Allāhumma anta al-salāmu wa minka al-salāmu"," tabārayka yā dhā al-jalāli wa al-ikrām\"" (O Allah"," You are al-Salām and from You is salām"," blessed are You"," O Possessor of majesty and honour).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal and Khālid al-Ḥadhāʾ from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ḥārith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 24979"," 25448.]"""
"3006","(3006) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Ṣayrafī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd informed me: My father narrated to us: al-Awzāʿī narrated to us: Shaddād Abū ʿAmmār narrated to us: Abū Asmāʾ al-Raḥabī narrated to us: Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me, saying: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to turn from his prayer, he would seek forgiveness three times, then say: \Allāhumma anta al-salāmu wa minka al-salāmu"," tabārayka yā dhā al-jalāli wa al-ikrām\"" (O Allah"," You are al-Salām and from You is salām"," blessed are You"," O Possessor of majesty and honour). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 5/275/22723. Abū Dāwūd"," 1513.]"""
"3007","(3007) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd Allah informed me — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us — al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us — al-Awza'i narrated from Abu 'Ammar — from Abu Asma' — from Thawban, who mentioned the hadith similarly, except that he added: **\Wa ilayka al-salam"," tabarakta ya dhal-jalali wa al-ikram\""** (And upon You be peace"," blessed are You"," O Possessor of Majesty and Honour).\n\nAl-Walid said: I asked al-Awza'i"," \""How was the istighfar (seeking of forgiveness) done?\"" He would say: **\""Astaghfirullah"," astaghfirullah\""** (I seek forgiveness from Allah"," I seek forgiveness from Allah).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Dawud ibn Rushayd"," except he did not mention his saying: *\""Wa ilayka al-salam.\""* And he said: **\""Tabarakta ya dhal-jalali wa al-ikram\""** (Blessed are You"," O Possessor of Majesty and Honour). Then he mentioned the statement of al-Awza'i"," may Allah have mercy upon him.\n\n[Sahih. Without the phrase \""wa ilayka al-salam\""]"""
"3008","(3008) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us — Ibn Fudayl narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah — from his father — from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, regarding His statement, **\And do not be loud in your prayer nor be silent therein\""** [Al-Isra': 110]: She said: **It refers to supplication (du'a).**\n\n[Sahith. The athar was narrated by al-Bukhari"," 6327]"""
"3009","(3009) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Hayri narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us — 'Ubayd al-Habari narrated to us — Abu Usamah narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah — from his father — from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her. She said: This verse — **\And do not be loud in your prayer nor be silent therein\""** [Al-Isra': 110] — was revealed **concerning supplication (du'a).**\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah"," from Abu Usamah.\n\nLikewise"," Mujahid stated that it was revealed **concerning supplication and asking (al-mas'alah).**\n\n[Sahih. And it has preceded in the one before it]"""
"3010","(3010) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us — Ibn Fudayl narrated from Ash'ath — from 'Ikrimah — from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding His statement, **\And do not be loud in your prayer nor be silent therein\""** [Al-Isra': 110]: He said: **A man would raise his voice when he supplicated during the prayer.**\n\nThus is it in this narration"," and it is **not strong (la bi-qawiyyah).**\n\n[Da'if]"""
"3011","(3011) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us — Musaddad narrated to us — Hushaym narrated from Abu Bishr — from Sa'id ibn Jubayr — from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding **\And do not be loud in your prayer nor be silent therein\""** [Al-Isra': 110]: He said: **It was revealed while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in concealment in Makkah. When he raised his voice"," the polytheists would hear it and would revile the One who revealed the Qur'an"," and the one who brought it. Allah"," the Most High"," said: \""And do not be loud in your prayer\""** [Al-Isra': 110] — lest the polytheists hear — **\""nor be silent therein\""** [Al-Isra': 110] — from your companions"," so that they do not hear — **\""And seek a way between that\""** [Al-Isra': 110] — i.e."," let them hear — **\""and do not be loud\""** [Al-Isra': 110] — until they take the Qur'an from you.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musaddad and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabah and others"," from Hushaym.\n\n**And it is possible that all of these are intended by the verse"," and Allah knows best.**\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 4722]"""
"3012","(3012) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdu narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us — 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us — 'Asim al-Ahwal narrated from Abu 'Uthman — from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: **When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for the Battle of Hunayn** — or he said, **when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ headed towards Hunayn** — the people overlooked a valley and raised their voices with the takbir: **\Allahu Akbar"," la ilaha illa Allah.\""** The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\""O people"," be gentle upon yourselves (arba'u 'ala anfusikum). You do not call upon one who is deaf or absent; rather"," you call upon One who is All-Hearing"," All-Nigh"," and He is with you.\""** He said: **I was behind the banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he heard me saying: \""La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah\"" (There is no power nor strength except with Allah). He said: \""O 'Abd Allah ibn Qays!\"" I said: \""Here I am"," O Messenger of Allah (labbayka ya Rasul Allah)!\"" He said: \""Shall I not direct you to a word from the treasures of Paradise?\"" I said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah"," may my father and mother be your ransom!\"" He said: \""La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah\"" (There is no power nor strength except with Allah).**\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Musa ibn Isma'il"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from 'Asim.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 4205]"""
"3013","(3013) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakka and others said — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from 'Amr — from Abu Ma'bad — from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: **I used to recognise the conclusion of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by the takbir.**\n\n'Amr ibn Dinar said: Then I mentioned it to Abu Ma'bad afterwards, and he said: **\I did not narrate that to you.\""**\n\n'Amr said: **And he had narrated it to me"," and he was the most truthful of the mawali of Ibn 'Abbas.**\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: **It is as though he (Abu Ma'bad) forgot after he had narrated it to him.**\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 842]"""
"3014","(3014) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us — 'Ali narrated to us — Sufyan narrated — 'Amr ibn Dinar informed me — Abu Ma'bad informed me — from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: **I used to recognise the conclusion of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by the takbir.**\n\n'Amr said: **Then Abu Ma'bad denied it.**\n\n'Amr said: **And he had informed me of it.**\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ali ibn 'Abd Allah, and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abi 'Umar and others, from Sufyan. And Ibn Jurayj narrated it from 'Amr.\n\n[Sahih. And it has preceded in the one before it]"
"3015","(3015) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari narrated to us — 'Abdah narrated —\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — 'Ali ibn 'Isa ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Ahmad ibn al-Nadr ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us — 'Abdah narrated — from Hisham ibn 'Urwah — from Abu al-Zubayr — that **'Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr used to make tahlil at the end of every prayer, saying: \La ilaha illa Allah"," wahdahu la sharika lah"," lahul-mulk"," wa lahul-hamd"," wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir. La hawla wa la quwwata illa billah. La na'budu illa iyyah. lahul-ni'mah"," wa lahul-fadl"," wa lahul-thana' al-hasan. La ilaha illa Allah"," mukhlisina lahu al-din wa law kariha al-kafirun\""** (There is no deity but Allah"," alone"," without partner. To Him belongs sovereignty"," and to Him belongs praise"," and He is over all things competent. There is no power nor strength except with Allah. We worship none but Him. To Him belongs grace"," and to Him belongs bounty"," and to Him belongs beautiful praise. There is no deity but Allah"," being sincere in religion to Him"," even if the disbelievers detest it).\n\nThen Ibn al-Zubayr would say: **The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to make tahlil with these at the end of every prayer.**\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. And likewise"," Musa ibn 'Uqbah and Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated it from Abu al-Zubayr"," that he heard Ibn al-Zubayr mentioning it.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad"," 4/4/16204]"""
"3016","(3016) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir informed us — my grandfather Yahya ibn Mansur narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali narrated. Qutaybah said: \He narrated to us","\"" and Ishaq said: \""He informed us\"" — Jarir narrated from Mansur — from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi' — from Warrad"," the mawla of al-Mughirah"," who said: **Al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah wrote to Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say at the end of his prayer when he gave salam: \""La ilaha illa Allah"," wahdahu la sharika lah"," lahul-mulk"," wa lahul-hamd"," wa huwa 'ala kulli shay'in qadir. Allahumma la ma'ni'a lima a'tayt"," wa la mu'tiya lima manamt"," wa la yanfa'u dhal-jaddi minkal-jadd\""** (There is no deity but Allah"," alone"," without partner. To Him belongs sovereignty"," and to Him belongs praise"," and He is over all things competent. O Allah"," none can withhold what You have given"," and none can give what You have withheld"," and the wealth of the wealthy will not avail them before You).\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah"," and Muslim narrated it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 6330]"""
"3017","(3017) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us from his original source: Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Mālik ibn Suʿayr Abū Muḥammad narrated to us: al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr and al-Musayyib ibn Rāfiʿ from Warrād, who said: al-Mughīrah ibn Shuʿbah dictated a letter to Muʿāwiyah stating that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished his prayer, he would say — and he mentioned it with the identical wording.\n\nMuslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash from al-Musayyib ibn Rāfiʿ, and from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr and ʿAbdah ibn Abī Lubābah. Al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of al-Thawrī from ʿAbd al-Malik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"
"3018","(3018) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: al-Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Salamah narrated from his uncle, al-Mājishūn ibn Abī Salamah, from al-Aʿraj, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), regarding his prayer, that he said: \When he finished his prayer and gave the salām"," he said: 'O Allah"," forgive me what I have sent ahead and what I have left behind"," what I have concealed and what I have done openly"," and what I have exceeded in — and You know better than I. You are the One Who brings forward and the One Who puts back. There is no deity except You.'\""\n\nYūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated it from his father"," al-Mājishūn"," with his isnād"," and he mentioned this supplication between the tashahhud and the salām. Both of these are recorded in the book of Muslim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1509).]"""
"3019","(3019) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The angels send blessings upon any one of you so long as he remains in the place where he prayed"," provided he does not break his wudu or stand up"," saying: 'O Allah"," forgive him. O Allah"," have mercy on him.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (445).]"""
"3020","(3020) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī narrated to us by dictation: Abū al-Qāsim ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Bālawayh al-Muzakkī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Hammām ibn Munabbih, who said: \This is what Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us.\"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""The angels send blessings upon any one of you so long as he remains in the place where he prayed"," saying: 'O Allah"," forgive him. O Allah"," have mercy on him","' provided he does not break his wudu.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3021","(3021) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb al-Ṭāʾī said: Abū Jaddī ʿAlī ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd, who is al-Ḥafarī, narrated from Sufyān from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Jābir ibn Samurah, who said: \When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed the morning prayer (al-Ṣubḥ)"," he would sit in his place of prayer until the sun rose.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah from Wakīʿ from Sufyān"," and he added in it: \""until the sun rose fully (ḥasanan).\""\n\nAbū Khaythamah narrated it from Simāk and added in it: \""When it rose"," he would stand","\"" and he did not say \""ḥasanan.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah (26384).]"""
"3022","(3022) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī al-Razzāz recited to him: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Daqīqī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Warqāʾ narrated from Sumayy from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: They said: \O Messenger of Allah"," the people of great wealth have taken the high ranks and everlasting bliss.\"" He said: \""How is that?\"" He said: \""They pray as we pray"," and they strive as they strive"," and they spend from the surplus of their wealth"," and we have no wealth.\"" He said: \""Shall I not tell you of a matter by which you will overtake those who came before you and surpass those who come after you"," and no one will come with the like of what you have brought except one who brings the same? You say subḥān Allāh ten times after every prayer"," al-ḥamdulillāh ten times"," and Allāhu akbar ten times.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq from Yazīd ibn Hārūn.\n\nThe Shaykh said: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated it from Sumayy. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (843).]"""
"3023","(3023) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqrī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who is al-Isfarāʾinī, narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūd al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī narrated to us: Muʿtamir narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh from Sumayy from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The poor came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'The people of great wealth have taken the highest ranks and everlasting bliss. They pray as we pray"," and they fast as we fast"," and they have surplus wealth with which they perform Ḥajj"," ʿUmrah"," strive in jihād"," and give in charity.'\"" He said: \""Shall I not tell you of a matter which"," if you adhere to it"," you will overtake those who preceded you and none will overtake you after you"," and you will be the best of those among whom you live"," except one who does the same as you do? You say subḥān Allāh"," al-ḥamdulillāh"," and Allāhu akbar thirty-three times after every prayer.\"" He said: \""We differed among ourselves"," and some of us said: 'We will say subḥān Allāh thirty-three times"," al-ḥamdulillāh thirty-three times"," and Allāhu akbar thirty-four times.' So I went back to him and he said: 'Say subḥān Allāh"," al-ḥamdulillāh"," and Allāhu akbar until all of them together amount to thirty-three.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿĀṣim ibn al-Naḍr from al-Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3024","(3024) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam al-Miṣrī narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to me: Ibn ʿAjlān narrated from Sumayy, the freedman of Abī Bakr, from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the poor among the Muhājirūn came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \The people of great wealth and riches have taken the highest ranks and everlasting bliss.\"" He said: \""And what is that?\"" He said: \""They pray as we pray"," and they fast as we fast"," and they give in charity and we cannot give charity"," and they free slaves and we cannot free slaves.\"" He said: \""Shall I not teach you something by which you will overtake those who preceded you and surpass those who come after you"," and no one will be better than you except one who does the same as you do?\"" They said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""You glorify Allah (tasbiḥ)"," you praise Him (taḥmīd)"," and you declare His greatness (takbīr) thirty-three times after every prayer.\""\n\nSumayy said: \""I narrated this ḥadīth to some of my family and they said: 'You have made a mistake. He said: \""You say subḥān Allāh thirty-three times"," al-ḥamdulillāh thirty-three times"," and Allāhu akbar thirty-three times.\""'\"" So I went back to Abī Ṣāliḥ and said that to him. He took my hand and said: \""Say Allāhu akbar"," subḥān Allāh"," and al-ḥamdulillāh until all of them together reach thirty-three.\"" Abī Ṣāliḥ said: \""Then the poor among the Muhājirūn went back to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: 'Our brothers"," the people of wealth"," have heard what you said and have done the same.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'That is the bounty of Allah; He gives it to whom He wills.'\""\n\nIbn ʿAjlān said: \""I narrated this ḥadīth to Rajāʾ ibn Ḥaywah"," and he narrated to me the like of it from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth"," except for the statement of Sumayy. Then he said: \""Others besides Qutaybah added in this ḥadīth and mentioned it.\""\n\nSuhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ narrated it from his father from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) and incorporated the statement of Abī Ṣāliḥ regarding the return of the poor Muhājirūn into the ḥadīth. Suhayl added"," saying: \""Eleven"," eleven"," eleven — all of that together makes thirty-three.\"" Suhayl has another isnād for it with additional text and additional count. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3025","(3025) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Musaddad narrated to us: Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Suhayl narrated from Abī ʿUbayd from ʬAṭāʾ ibn Yazīd from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever says subḥān Allāh thirty-three times after every prayer"," Allāhu akbar thirty-three times"," and al-ḥamdulillāh thirty-three times — that makes ninety-nine — and then completes the hundred by saying: 'Lā ilāha illā Allāhu waḥdahu lā sharīka lahu"," lahu al-mulku wa lahu al-ḥamdu"," wa huwa ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr' — his sins will be forgiven"," even if they are like the foam of the sea.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Bayān from Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3026","(3026) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: Shuʿbah, Mālik ibn Mighwal, and Ḥamzah al-Zayyāt narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī narrated to us: Abū al-Muwajjih informed us: ʿAbdān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Mālik ibn Mighwal said: I heard al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah narrating from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā from Kaʿb ibn ʿUjrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There are certain phrases — the one who says them or acts upon them after every obligatory prayer will never be disappointed: thirty-three tasbīḥah"," thirty-three taḥmīdah"," and thirty-four takbīrah.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn al-Mubārak.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak"," and from another route from Ḥamzah al-Zayyāt. [Narrated by Muslim (596).]"""
"3027","(3027) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khusrujardī informed us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us that Abū Ḥafṣ ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥalabī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Qudāmah ibn Aʿyan narrated to us that ʿUthām narrated from al-Aʿmash from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from his father from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) counting his tasbīḥ on his right hand.\"""""
"3028","(3028) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us that Abū Rajāʾ narrated from Samurah ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: \When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had prayed the morning prayer (Ṣalāt al-Ṣubḥ)"," he would turn his face toward us and say: 'Has anyone of you seen a dream?'…\"" (the hadith continues). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 7046. It is part of a longer hadith.]"""
"3029","(3029) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Yaḥyā al-Adamī narrated to us that Abū Qilābah narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us that my father narrated, saying: \I heard Abū Rajāʾ narrating from Samurah ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: 'When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had prayed the morning prayer (al-Ṣubḥ)"," he would turn his face toward us and say: \""Whoever among you has seen a dream"," let me relate its interpretation for him…\""'\"" He mentioned the hadith as such.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Jarīr"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār from Wahb ibn Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3030","(3030) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated from Mālik from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) led us in the morning prayer (Ṣalāt al-Ṣubḥ) at al-Ḥudaybiyah following a night of rain. When he had finished (the prayer)"," he turned his face toward the people and said: 'Do you know what your Lord has said?' They said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'He said: Among My servants this morning there are those who believe in Me and those who disbelieve. As for the one who says"," \""We have been given rain by the bounty and mercy of Allah","\"" that one believes in Me and disbelieves in the star. And as for the one who says"," \""We have been given rain by such-and-such a nawʾ (star)","\"" that one disbelieves in Me and believes in the star.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 846.]"""
"3031","(3031) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us that al-Anṣārī narrated to me that Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated, saying: \It was asked of Anas: 'Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) take to wearing a ring?' He said: 'Yes. He delayed the last ʿIshāʾ prayer until close to half the night. When he had prayed"," he turned his face toward us and said: \""The people have already prayed and gone to sleep"," and you continue to be in prayer so long as you await it.\""'\"" Anas said: \""It is as though I am now looking at the gleam of his ring.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it from the hadith of Yazīd ibn Hārūn from Ḥumayd"," as has been mentioned above. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 572"," 661.]"""
"3032","(3032) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us that ʿAffān narrated to us that Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from al-Ḥasan who said: \They (the early Muslims) considered it desirable that a man"," when he had prayed the morning prayer (al-Ṣubḥ)"," should not eat any food until the sun had risen"," and that he should pray two rakʿahs for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Mālik ibn Anas that he said: \""I found the people and they would not speak until the sun had risen.\"" He meant speech that did not concern them. And success is by Allah.\n\nAs for after the rise of dawn (al-Fajr)… [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"3033","(3033) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Hārūn ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Waḍḍāḥ from ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Jazarī from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿUmar that he used to dislike speaking after dawn (al-Fajr) — or he said after the two rakʿahs of al-Fajr — and he considered it desirable to make tasbīḥ and takbīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr, 1805.]"
"3034","(3034) He said: And ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us from al-Masʿūdī from ʿAmr ibn Murrah from Abī ʿUbaydah who said: \It was grievous to ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — that he should not mention Allah and the Qurʾān until he had prayed al-Fajr.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr and Ibrāhīm ibn Yazīd al-Nakhaʿī that they both disliked speaking after the two rakʿahs of al-Fajr"," and it is as though they disliked speech that did not concern one. [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"3035","(3035) For it has been established from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would pray the two rakʿahs of al-Fajr. If I was awake"," he would speak to me; otherwise"," he would lie down until it was time to stand for the prayer.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; Abū al-Naḍr narrated from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," and he mentioned it. Both (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) narrated it from the hadith of Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 1161.]"""
"3036","(3036) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad narrated to me that my father narrated to us that Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abī Sufyān from Jābir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you has completed his prayer in his mosque"," let him set aside a portion of his prayer for his home"," for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," will place goodness in his home on account of his prayer.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Abī Muʿāwiyah. And likewise ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated it from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 4837; and Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 9450.]"""
"3037","(3037) It was narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Jabir from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\nIt was related to us by Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'quob narrated to us, Asid ibn 'Asim narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Sufyan; al-A'mash narrated to us, and he mentioned it with the same wording, except that he said: \in the mosque.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad 3/15/11128]"""
"3038","(3038) Similarly, it was narrated by Zaidah from al-A'mash. It was related to us by Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan, Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us, Salih ibn Muhammad al-Razi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us from al-A'mash, and he mentioned it with the same wording, with the addition of Abu Sa'id in its chain of narration.\n\n[Sahih. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"
"3039","(3039) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us, Abu Hamid ibn Bilal al-Bazzaz narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Perform some of your prayers in your homes"," and do not make them graves.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Musa and Zuhayr"," all of them from Yahya.\n\nAnd in the authentic hadith from Zayd ibn Thabit from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""The best prayer of a person is in his home"," except the obligatory prayer.\"" And that will be mentioned"," if Allah the Most High wills.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 432]"""
"3040","(3040) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qob al-Qadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq ibn Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (ﷺ) prayed Maghrib in the mosque of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal. When he finished, he saw the people performing supererogatory prayers, so he said: \O people"," these prayers are for the homes.\""\n\n[Da'if. Narrated by Abu Dawud 1300]"""
"3041","(3041) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah informed us, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: I prayed with the Prophet (ﷺ) two rak'ats before Zuhr and two rak'ats after it, and two rak'ats after Maghrib, and two rak'ats after 'Isha, and two rak'ats after Jumu'ah. As for Maghrib, 'Isha, and Jumu'ah, they were in his home.\n\nAnd Hafsah informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to pray two brief rak'ats when dawn broke, before he prayed Fajr, and it was a time during which I would not enter upon the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad, and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr and others from Yahya al-Qattan.\n\nAnd in it there is an indication that the two rak'ats before Zuhr and the two rak'ats after it were performed in the mosque.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari 937]"
"3042","(3042) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Jarjari informed us, Talq ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Ya'qob ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Abi al-Mughirah, from Sa'd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to lengthen the recitation in the two rak'ats after Maghrib until the people of the mosque dispersed.\n\nIt was narrated by Nasr al-Mujaddar from Ya'qob al-Qummi, and he transmitted it with a similar chain.\n\nAbu Dawud said: Sulayman ibn Dawud al-'Ataki and Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, they said: Ya'qob narrated to us, from Ja'far, from Sa'd ibn Jubayr, from the Prophet (ﷺ) with its meaning — it is mursal.\n\nThe Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It is as though he (ﷺ) did this for a period of time, and what Ibn 'Umar narrated about the two rak'ats of Maghrib being in his home was also for a period of time. And with Allah is the success.\n\n[Da'if]"
"3043","(3043) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Tawbah Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, 'Ata' al-Khurasani narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The imam should not pray supererogatory prayer in the place where he prayed the obligatory prayer until he moves to another position.\""\n\nAbu Dawud said: 'Ata' al-Khurasani did not meet al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah.\n\n[Da'if]"""
"3044","(3044) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qob narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn 'Ubayd, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you wishes to perform a supererogatory prayer after the obligatory prayer"," let him move forward or backward"," or to his right or to his left.\""\n\n[Da'if]"""
"3045","(3045) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qob narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, from al-Layth, from al-Hajjaj, from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Is any one of you unable"," when he has prayed and wishes to perform a supererogatory prayer"," to move forward or backward"," or to turn to his right or to his left?\""\n\nAnd it was narrated by Jarir from al-Layth"," from al-Hajjaj"," from Isma'il ibn Ibrahim or Ibrahim ibn Isma'il.\n\nAl-Bukhari (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim is more correct"," and al-Layth is inconsistent in it.\n\nThe Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And he is al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym"," who is alone in narrating it. And Allah the Most High knows best.\n\n[Da'if. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3046","(3046) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Nusayr al-Khuldi in Baghdad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us, 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: An imam of ours, known as Abu Rimthah, led us in prayer. He said: I prayed this prayer or the like of this prayer with the Prophet (ﷺ).\n\nHe said: Abu Bakr and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to stand in the front row to his right. And there was a man who had caught the first takbir of the prayer. When the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) finished, he gave salutation to his right and to his left until we saw the whiteness of his cheeks. Then he turned away, as Abu Rimthah himself turned away. Then the man who had caught the first takbir of the prayer stood up to perform a supererogatory prayer. 'Umar leapt toward him, seized him by his shoulders, and shook him. Then he said: Sit down, for the People of the Book were destroyed only because there was no interval between their prayers. The Prophet (ﷺ) raised his gaze and said: \May Allah guide you"," O son of al-Khattab!\""\n\nAnd Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us"," Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us"," Abu Dawud narrated to us"," 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us"," and he mentioned something similar to it.\n\nAbu Dawud said: And it has been said that instead of Abu Rimthah it was Abu Umayyah.\n\nThe Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: If this is established"," it applies to both the imam and the one who follows him. And likewise the hadith of Abu Hurayrah. And in this topic there is a hadith that is more authentic than all that we have mentioned.\n\n[Da'if. Narrated by Abu Dawud 1007]"""
"3047","(3047) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me that al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us that Ghundar narrated from Ibn Jurayj that ʿUmar ibn ʬAṭāʾ ibn Abī al-Khuwār informed him: that Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr had sent him to al-Sāʾib ibn Ukht Namir to ask him about something he had observed from Muʿāwiyah during the prayer. He said: \Yes"," I prayed the Jumuʿah prayer with him in the maqṣūrah. When the Imām pronounced the salām"," I stood in my place and prayed. When he entered"," he sent word to me and said: 'Do not repeat what you have done. When you have prayed the Jumuʿah"," do not attach another prayer to it until you speak or go out"," for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded us that we should not join one prayer to another until we speak or go out.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah with this wording.\n\nAnd ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it from Ibn Jurayj with the same meaning"," and he said at its end: \""For the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) commanded this and said: 'Let no prayer be joined to another prayer until you go out or speak.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 5534]"""
"3048","(3048) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us that my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr and Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ both said: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj informed us, and he mentioned it with a similar narration, except that he said: \When I pronounced the salām"," I stood","\"" and he did not mention the Imām.\n\nThis narration encompasses both the Jumuʿah and other prayers"," since he said: \""Let no prayer be joined to another prayer.\"" It encompasses both the Imām and the one who prays behind him. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) mentioned this narration in the transmission of al-Muzanī from ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz from Ibn Jurayj"," and I have transmitted it together with the athar of Ibn ʿAbbās and the statement of al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) in the dictation in the book of al-Jumuʿah from al-Mabṣūṭ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3049","(3049) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us that Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Sammāk narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Ghaffār narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr from ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: I heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \It is from the Sunnah that when the Imām pronounces the salām"," one should not stand from the place in which he prayed to perform a voluntary prayer until he turns aside"," or changes position"," or separates it with speech.\""\n\nAl-Thawrī narrated it from Maysarah ibn Ḥabīb from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr"," except that he said: \""It is not proper for the Imām","\"" and in another narration: \""It is not befitting for the Imām.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding this"," and he said: \""Let him move forward or speak to someone.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"3050","(3050) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that the Qāḍī Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūd ibn Khurrāzādh narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad, meaning al-Shāfiʿī, narrated to us that Dāwūd narrated from ʿAmr, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whoever has prayed the obligatory prayer and then wishes to pray after it"," let him move forward or speak to someone.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"3051","(3051) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Malik narrated from ʬAṭāʾ, who said: I saw Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) push a man from the place in which he had prayed the obligatory prayer, and he said: \I only pushed you so that you may move forward or backward.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from him with the same meaning regarding the Jumuʿah. [Ḍaʿīf. Al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr"," 2999]"""
"3052","(3052) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ informed us that Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth that Ibn ʿUmar, when he prayed, would move from the place in which he had prayed. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"3053","(3053) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated, he said: It was read to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed you from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar used to pray his voluntary prayer in the place in which he had prayed.\n\nAnd Shuʿbah narrated it similarly from Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar.\n\nAnd it is as though he would separate between the two with speech, or turning aside, or by doing something that is permissible to do. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"3054","(3054) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk narrated to us that Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn Thābit narrated to us that Furāt ibn Aḥnaf narrated from his father from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishr al-Hilālī from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him): He used to see no harm in a man performing a voluntary prayer in his place, or he saw someone do it. ʿAlī expressed doubt.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar that he differentiated in this matter between the Imām and the one who prays behind him, disliking it for the Imām but not for the one who prays behind him, though its chain of narration is not strong. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr, 104]"
"3055","(3055) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated in Ziyādāt al-Fawāʾid that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us that ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar ibn Fāris narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated from al-Zuhrī from Hind bint al-Ḥārith al-Qurashiyyah from Umm Salamah, who said: \The women"," during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when they had pronounced the salām from the obligatory prayer"," would stand up"," while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and the men behind him would remain seated. Then when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood up"," the men would stand up.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned previously under numbers 3043 and 3044.]"""
"3056","(3056) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr al-Azdī narrated to us that Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us that Zāʾidah narrated from al-Mukhtār ibn Fulful from Anas that the Prophet (ﷺ) urged them regarding the prayer and forbade them from dispersing before he himself had dispersed from the prayer.\n\nThis is an abridged version of the established ḥadīth from ʿAlī ibn Mushir from al-Mukhtār ibn Fulful from Anas regarding the prohibition of the one praying behind the Imām preceding the Imām in rukūʿ, sujūd, standing, and dispersing.\n\nAnd it is possible that by \dispersal\"" he meant exiting the prayer by pronouncing the salām"," and it is also possible that he meant something else. And Allah knows best.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \""The key to prayer is the takbīr"," and its conclusion is the taslīm. When the Imām pronounces the salām"," then stand if you wish.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. The origin of this ḥadīth is with Muslim with different wording"," and it has been mentioned previously.]"""
"3057","(3057) Abū Naṣr — ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah, from his original book — informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl al-Khuzāʿī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim al-Baghawī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ informed us: Juwayriyyah ibn Asmāʾ, from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Ibn ʿUmar — when he began the recitation in the prayer, he would say {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}, and when he finished Sūrat al-Fātiḥah, he would say that again when he commenced the next sūrah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīgh for other than it. And it has a witness in the one after it.]"
"3058","(3058) Abū Naṣr informed us: Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khamīrūyah al-Harawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he would recite aloud when he read {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm}, and when he read the sūrah, he would also recite it aloud.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. And it has a witness in the one before it.]"
"3059","(3059) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Naḍr informed us: Shuʿbah, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I prayed behind Ibn al-Zubayr — may Allah be pleased with them both — and he would recite {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} aloud, and when he said {Wa lā al-ḍāllīn}, he would also say {Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm} aloud.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Abū Hurayrah and more than one of the Companions — may Allah be pleased with them.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain is sound.]"
"3060","(3060) There has already passed therein the ḥadīth of Abū Qatādah. Abū ʿAbd Allāh — al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Makhzūmī al-Ghaḍāʾirī in Baghdad — informed us: ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Sammāk informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Salām al-Sawwāq informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: al-Aʿmash —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī informed us: Musaddad informed us: ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us: Sulaymān al-Aʿmash, from ʿUmārah ibn ʿUmayr, from Abū Maʿmar, who said: We said to Khabbāb ibn al-Aratt: \Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" We said: \""How did you know that?\"" He said: \""By the movement of his beard.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbdān.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā"," from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād"," through other routes from al-Aʿmash.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (761).]"""
"3061","(3061) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ, dictating, informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar al-Jurjānī informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr informed us: Abū Usāmah, from Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd, who said: I heard ʿAṭāʾ narrate from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no prayer without recitation.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""Whatever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited aloud"," we have made it audible to you"," and whatever he concealed"," we have concealed it from you.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (772).]"""
"3062","(3062) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdad informed us: Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr al-Zubayrī informed us: Kathīr ibn Zayd, from al-Muṭṭalib ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥanṭab, who said: They disputed regarding the recitation in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr, so they came to Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit, and he said: \My father told me: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and led us in Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr"," moving his lips"," and I do not know that except to be from recitation"," so we do the same.'\""\n\n[Ḥasan for other than it. Aḥmad narrated it (182/21913).]"""
"3063","(3063) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq, dictating, informed us: Abū Muslim informed us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl informed us: Hammām ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah, from his father, that the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Ẓuhr prayer, in the first two rakʿahs, Sūrat al-Fātiḥah and a sūrah, and he would occasionally make us hear a verse. He said: And he would recite in the last two rakʿahs Sūrat al-Fātiḥah only, and he would lengthen the first rakʿah more than he would lengthen the second. He said: And likewise in the ʿAṣr prayer. He said: And likewise in the Fajr prayer.\n\nBoth (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hammām ibn Yaḥyā and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (776).]"
"3064","(3064) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī, dictating, informed us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah, informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from al-Zuhrī, from Muḥammad ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from his father, who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting al-Ṭūr in the Maghrib prayer.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," from Sufyān"," and Muslim narrated it through other routes from al-Zuhrī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (3050).]"""
"3065","(3065) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Fāriyābī informed us: ʿAbbās al-ʿAnbarī informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Muḥammad ibn Jubayr, from his father — who had come among the captives of Badr — who said: \I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reciting al-Ṭūr in the Maghrib prayer"," and that was the first time faith settled in my heart"," while I was at that time a polytheist.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr"," from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned in the one before it"," and the wording is that of al-Bukhārī (4023).]"""
"3066","(3066) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh al-Jallāb informed us: Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us: Khallād ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Miʿsar informed me: ʿAdī ibn Thābit, that he heard al-Barāʾ say: \I heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting al-Tīn wa al-Zaytūn in the ʿIshāʾ prayer"," and I have not heard anyone with a more beautiful voice and recitation than him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Khallād ibn Yaḥyā"," and Muslim narrated it through another route from Miʿsar and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (767).]"""
"3067","(3067) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Miʿsar informed us, from al-Walīd ibn Sarīʿ, from ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth, who said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) reciting in the Fajr prayer: {"
"3068","(3068) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abū ʿAwānah informed us, from Abū Bishr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) neither recited to the jinn nor saw them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out with a group of his Companions heading towards the market of ʿUkāẓ. The devils had been barred from receiving news of the heavens, and shooting stars had been hurled at them. The devils returned to their people, and they said: \What is the matter with you?\"" They said: \""We have been barred from receiving news of the heavens"," and shooting stars have been hurled at us.\"" They said: \""Nothing has barred you from receiving news of the heavens except that something has occurred. Travel to the east and west of the earth and see what it is that has barred you from receiving news of the heavens.\"" Those who had set out towards Tihāmah came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was at Nakhlah"," heading towards the market of ʿUkāẓ"," and he was praying the Fajr prayer with his Companions. When they heard the Qurʾān"," they listened to it and said: \""By Allah"," this is what has barred you from receiving news of the heavens.\"" Thereupon"," when they returned to their people"," they said: \""O our people! Indeed"," we have heard a wondrous Qurʾān"," which guides to righteousness"," so we have believed in it"," and we will never associate anyone with our Lord.\"" Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed to His Prophet (ﷺ): {"""
"3069","(3069) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar informed us, from ʿAlī ibn Zayd ibn Judʿān, from Abū Naḍrah, who said: We were with ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him) and we were discussing knowledge. A man said: \Do not speak except about what is in the Qurʾān.\"" ʿImrān said to him: \""You are indeed foolish! Have you found in the Qurʾān: pray Dhuhr as four rakʿahs"," and ʿAṣr as four"," without raising the recitation in any of them; and Maghrib as three"," raising the recitation in two of its rakʿahs and not raising it in one; and ʿIshāʾ as four rakʿahs"," raising the recitation in two of them and not raising it in two; and Fajr as two rakʿahs"," raising the recitation in both of them?\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 20474.]"""
"3070","(3070) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muslim narrated to us; Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us; Hushaym informed us, from Abū Bishr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: This verse was revealed while the Prophet (ﷺ) was in concealment in Makkah. Whenever he prayed, he would raise his voice. When the polytheists heard that, they reviled the Qurʾān, the One who revealed it, and the one who brought it. So Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said to His Prophet (ﷺ): {"
"3071","(3071) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Bukhārī informed me; Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"
"3072","(3072) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik informed us, from his paternal uncle Abū Suhayl, from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) used to raise his voice in recitation during the prayer, and that his recitation could be heard at the house of Abū Jahl in al-Balāṭ.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh — that is, al-Būshanjī (may Allah have mercy on him) — said: Al-Balāṭ is a place in Madīnah near the market.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: At the time when ʿUmar raised his voice in this manner, there was no longer the fear of the polytheists causing harm that had existed at the time of the revelation of the verse. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik in al-Muwaṭṭāʾ, 180.]"
"3073","(3073) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd informed us, from ʿUmārah ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ, from Abū Zurʿah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said the takbīr to commence the prayer, he would remain silent for a brief moment before reciting. I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," may my father and mother be sacrificed for you"," tell me about your silence between the takbīr and the recitation — what do you say?\"" He said: \""I say: 'O Allah"," put a distance between me and my sins as You have put a distance between the East and the West. O Allah"," purify me of my sins as a white garment is purified of dirt. O Allah"," wash me of my sins with snow"," water"," and hail.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 744.]"""
"3074","(3074) Abū al-Ḥasan informed us; Aḥmad informed us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us; Abū Kāmil narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us; ʿUmārah ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ narrated to us, and he mentioned something similar to it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Kāmil and from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it; previous source.]"
"3075","(3075) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Thaqafī informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, from Ibn Abī Dhiʿb, from Saʿīd ibn Simʿān, who said: Abū Hurayrah came to us in the mosque of Banī Zuraīq and said: \There are three things that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do which the people have abandoned: he would raise his hands when he entered the prayer"," extending them fully; he would remain silent after the recitation for a brief moment"," asking Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," for His bounty; and he would say the takbīr when he bowed and when he lowered himself.\"" In this narration it says: \""after the recitation.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 2/434/9606.]"""
"3076","(3076) ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʿb, and he said in the hadith: \He would remain silent before the recitation for a brief moment.\""\n\nʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿAlī narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\nWith this meaning"," ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Ḥanafī and others narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhiʿb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3077","(3077) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Musaddad informed us — Yazīd informed us — Saʿīd informed us — Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan: that Samurah ibn Jundub and ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) were conversing. Samurah ibn Jundub related that he had preserved from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) two moments of silence (saktatān): one when he pronounced the takbīr, and one when he finished reciting {"
"3078","(3078) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Ismāʿīl, from Yūnus, from al-Ḥasan, who said: Samurah said: \I preserved two moments of silence in the prayer: a moment of silence when the imam pronounces the takbīr until he recites"," and a moment of silence when he finishes reciting the Opening of the Book and a sūrah"," at the time of rukūʿ.\""\n\nHe said: ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn disputed that"," so they wrote to Ubayy in Madīnah"," and he confirmed Samurah.\n\nIt was also narrated from Hushaym"," from Yūnus: \""And when he recited {"""
"3079","(3079) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Abū Yaʿqūb Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Kathīr informed us — Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub: that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had two moments of silence. ʿImrān ibn Ḥuṣayn said: \I did not preserve them from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"" So they wrote to Ubayy ibn Kaʿb regarding it"," and Ubayy wrote: \""Samurah has indeed preserved correctly.\""\n\nWe said to Qatādah: \""What are the two moments of silence?\"" He said: \""A moment of silence when he pronounces the takbīr"," and the other when he finishes the recitation at the time of rukūʿ.\"" Then he said — meaning the other time — \""A moment of silence when he pronounces the takbīr"," and a moment of silence when he says {"""
"3080","(3080) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Ibn al-Muthannā informed us — ʿAbd al-Aʿlā informed us — Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I preserved two moments of silence from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\""\n\nIn it"," Saʿīd said: \""We said to Qatādah: 'What are these two moments of silence?' He said: 'When he enters into his prayer"," and when he finishes the recitation.' Then he said afterwards: 'And when he says {"""
"3081","(3081) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī informed us — ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us — ʿUmārah ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ informed us — Abū Zurʿah ibn ʿAmr ibn Jarīr informed us — Abū Hurayrah said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would"," when he rose for the rakʿah"," begin with {"""
"3082","(3082) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — my father informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāh ibn Khuzaymah informed us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr ibn Muʿārik al-Miṣrī informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān informed us — ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated it with the same meaning.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"
"3083","(3083) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us — my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Salmah informed me — Muḥammad ibn Aslam informed us — Yūnus ibn Muḥammad informed us — ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād, from ʿUmārah ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ, from Abū Zurʿah, who said: \I heard Abū Hurayrah saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would"," when he rose from the second rakʿah"," begin the recitation and would not remain silent.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""I was informed about Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān"," Yūnus al-Mu'addib"," and others"," who said: 'ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us","' and he mentioned it.\""\n\nIn this hadith there is an indication that there is no moment of silence in the second rakʿah before the recitation"," and it is a ṣaḥīḥ hadith. And it is possible that what is meant is that he did not remain silent in the second rakʿah as he did in the first for the opening supplication. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"3084","(3084) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Faḍl ibn Muḥammad al-Shaʿrānī informed me — my grandfather informed me — Abū Thābit informed us — Ibrāhīm —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us — Abū Bakr Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Khālid informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd, from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)"," when he wished to supplicate against someone or for someone"," would perform the qunūt after the rukūʿ. Sometimes he would say"," when he said: 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah"," Rabbanā wa-laka al-ḥamd' — 'O Allah"," save Walīd ibn Walīd"," Salamah ibn Hishām"," and the weak among the believers. O Allah"," make Your punishment severe upon Muḍar"," and make it upon them like the years of Yūsuf.' He would say this aloud. And he would say in some of his prayers"," in the Fajr prayer: 'O Allah"," curse so-and-so and so-and-so' — living Arab tribes — until Allah"," the Most High"," revealed: {"""
"3085","(3085) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Yūnus ibn Yazīd informed you"," from Ibn Shihāb","\"" who said: \""Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me that they both heard Abū Hurayrah saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) would"," when he finished the recitation in the Fajr prayer"," pronounce the takbīr and raise his head"," saying: Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah"," Rabbanā wa-laka al-ḥamd. Then he would say"," while standing: O Allah"," save Walīd ibn Walīd"," Salamah ibn Hishām"," ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah"," and the weak among the believers. O Allah"," make Your punishment severe upon Muḍar"," and make it upon them like the years of Yūsuf. O Allah"," curse Layḥān"," Riʿl"," and Dhakwān"," and ʿUṣayyah"," who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.'\"" Then it reached us that he abandoned this when Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," revealed: {"""
"3086","(3086) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Sufyān, from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah: \The Prophet (peace be upon him)"," when he raised his head from the second rakʿah of the morning prayer"," said: 'O Allah"," save Walīd ibn Walīd"," Salamah ibn Hishām"," ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah"," and the weak in Makkah. O Allah"," make Your punishment severe upon Muḍar. O Allah"," make it upon them like the years of Yūsuf.'\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAmr al-Nāqid and others"," from Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Shāfiʿī narrated it (895). Previously mentioned.]"""
"3087","(3087) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah al-Shaybānī in Kūfah informed us; al-Haytham ibn Khālid narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was once praying al-ʿIshāʾ when he said: \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah\"" (Allah hears those who praise Him). Then"," before he prostrated"," he said: \""O Allah"," grant salvation to ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah. O Allah"," grant salvation to Salamah ibn Hishām. O Allah"," grant salvation to al-Walīd ibn al-Walīd. O Allah"," grant salvation to the oppressed among the believers. O Allah"," intensify Your punishment upon Muḍar. O Allah"," make it years like the years of Yūsuf (i.e."," years of severe famine).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it through another route from Shaybān.\n\nSimilarly"," al-Awzāʿī said it from Yaḥyā as \""ṣalāt al-ʿAtamah.\"" Similarly"," Hishām al-Dastawāʾī said it from Yaḥyā"," and in one of the two narrations from him it is \""al-ʿIshāʾ al-Ākhirah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3088","(3088) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr al-Sahmī narrated to us; Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah narrated to us; Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said \Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah\"" in the last rakʿah of the prayer of al-ʿIshāʾ al-Ākhirah"," he would perform qunūt and say: \""O Allah"," grant salvation to al-Walīd ibn al-Walīd. O Allah"," grant salvation to ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah. O Allah"," grant salvation to Salamah ibn Hishām. O Allah"," grant salvation to the oppressed among the believers. O Allah"," intensify Your punishment upon Muḍar. O Allah"," make it years like the years of Yūsuf.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3089","(3089) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Abū ʿUmar al-Ḥawḍī narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Yaḥyā, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \By Allah"," I shall pray to you a prayer most closely resembling the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" So Abū Hurayrah would perform qunūt in the last rakʿah of the Ẓuhr prayer"," al-ʿIshāʾ al-Ākhirah"," and the Fajr prayer"," after saying \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah","\"" supplicating for the believers and invoking curses upon the disbelievers.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (764).]"""
"3090","(3090) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Umayyah narrated to us; Muʿādh, meaning Ibn Hishām, the companion of al-Dastawāʾī, said: My father narrated to me, mentioning it with a similar meaning, except that he said: \By Allah"," I shall bring you close to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah from Hishām. And Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā from Muʿādh ibn Hishām. This narration establishes the qunūt in the three prayers. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]\n\n(3090) A similar narration is transmitted through another chain of narration"," except that in it are the words: \""By Allah"," I shall bring you close to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\n(b) This narration is likewise found in Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim and Ṣaḥīḥ al-Bukhārī.\n\n(c) From all these narrations"," the qunūt in three prayers is established."""
"3091","(3091) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed me; ʿAmr ibn Murrah informed us; he heard Ibn Abī Laylā narrating from al-Barāʾ that the Prophet (ﷺ) used to perform qunūt in al-Fajr and al-Maghrib.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ghundar from Shuʿbah, and he narrated it through another route from al-Thawrī from ʿAmr ibn Murrah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim narrated it (305).]"
"3092","(3092) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb informed us; Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Muḥammad, meaning, narrated from Muṭarrif, from Abū al-Jahm, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (ﷺ) would not pray any obligatory prayer except that he performed qunūt in it.\n\nThis Muḥammad is Ibn Anas, Abū Anas, the freed slave of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and Muṭarrif is Ibn Ṭarīf.\n\n[Ḥasan. Al-Dāraquṭnī narrated it (2/37).]"
"3093","(3093) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Ḥibbān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī; Sālim informed me from his father that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ), when he raised his head from rukūʿ in the last rakʿah of al-Fajr, say: \O Allah"," curse so-and-so and so-and-so.\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: \""Not for you is any matter of command\"" (Āl ʿImrān: 128).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥibbān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (3842).]"""
"3094","(3094) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me; ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād al-Narsī narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, that Riʿl, Dhakwān, ʿUṣayyah, and Banū Liḥyān sought the help of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) against an enemy, so he sent them seventy from the Anṣār, whom we used to call al-Qurrāʾ in their time. They would gather firewood by day and pray by night, until when they were at Biʾr Maʿūnah, they were killed and betrayed. This reached the Prophet (ﷺ), so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed qunūt for a month, supplicating in the Ṣubḥ prayer against certain Arab tribes—against Riʿl, Dhakwān, ʿUṣayyah, and Banū Liḥyān.\n\nAnas said: We recited Qurʾān concerning them, then that was lifted: \Convey to our people that we have met our Lord"," and He was pleased with us and we were pleased with Him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād al-Narsī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (3862).]"""
"3095","(3095) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us orally; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from ʿĀṣim, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \I never saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) grieve over anything as he grieved over the companions of Biʾr Maʿūnah and the companions of the expedition of al-Mundhir ibn ʿAmr. He remained for a month supplicating against those who had killed them in the qunūt of the prayer of al-Ghadāh"," invoking curses upon Riʿl"," Dhakwān"," ʿUṣayyah"," and Liḥyān.\""\n\nQatādah"," ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb"," Abū Mijlaz Lāḥiq ibn Ḥumayd"," Anas ibn Sīrīn"," Mūsā ibn Anas"," and ʿĀṣim ibn Sulaymān al-Aḥwal all narrated from Anas ibn Mālik"," and they said in the ḥadīth: \""a month.\""\n\nMālik ibn Anas narrated from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Anas"," likewise: \""thirty mornings.\""\n\nHammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated from Isḥāq"," and he said: \""forty mornings.\""\n\nThe correct narration is thirty. And that has also been narrated from Hammām.\n\nIt was narrated from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl from Anas in the story of the ʿUrayniyyīn that he said: \""He sent in their pursuit after having invoked curses upon them in his prayer for twenty-five days.\"" And that story is different from this one.\n\nThe preserved narration from Ḥumayd regarding the story of the Qurrāʾ is what [has been mentioned]. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it (3/194).]"""
"3096","(3096) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Yaʿqūb al-Iyādī al-Mālikī in Baghdad informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf ibn Khallād al-Naṣībī narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to me; Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated to me that he heard Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Young men from the Anṣār used to listen to the Qurʾān and then retire to a corner of Madīnah. Their families would think they were in the mosque"," and the people of the mosque would think they were with their families. They would pray at night until"," when the morning drew near"," some of them would gather firewood and some of them would draw fresh water. Then they would return and place their bundles and water-skins at the doors of the chambers of the Prophet (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) sent them to Biʾr Maʿūnah"," and they were all martyred. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then supplicated against those who had killed them for fifteen nights.\""\n\nSimilarly"," ʿAlqamah ibn Abī ʿAlqamah narrated from Anas ibn Mālik"," who said: \""He supplicated against those who had killed them for fifteen days.\""\n\nSimilarly"," Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated from his father"," in a mursal narration: \""fifteen days.\""\n\nThe narrations mentioning a month are more well-known"," more numerous"," and more correct"," and Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. The majority of narrations from Anas establish the qunūt in the Ṣubḥ prayer"," and it has also been established from him in the Maghrib prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Aḥmad narrated it (3/235).]"""
"3097","(3097) Abū ʿAmr al-Bisṭāmī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Wahb, who is Ibn Baqiyyah, informed us; Khālid, who is ʿAbdullāh, informed us from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from Abū Qilābah from Anas that he used to say: \The qunūt is performed in the Maghrib and the morning (al-ghadāh) prayers.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad and others from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah from Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ"," and he said: \""The qunūt was performed in the Maghrib and Fajr prayers.\""\n\nIt is also narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās in the account narrated by Anas that the qunūt was performed in all the prayers. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 2765.]"""
"3098","(3098) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Thābit ibn Yazīd narrated to us; Hilāl ibn Khabbāb narrated to us from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed qunūt consecutively for one month in the Ẓuhr"," Maghrib"," ʿIshāʾ"," and Ṣubḥ prayers"," in the last rakʿah of each prayer after saying: 'Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah.' He supplicated against certain tribes of Banī Sulaym — against Riʿl"," Dhakwān"," and ʿUṣayyah — and those behind him would say āmīn. He had sent them (the emissaries) to invite them to Islam"," but they killed them.\"" ʿIkrimah said: \""This is the origin of the qunūt.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 1/301.]"""
"3099","(3099) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ said: al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to me; ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas narrated to me from Ḥanẓalah ibn ʿAlī from Khufāf ibn Īmāʾ al-Ghifārī, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said in the morning prayer: \O Allah"," curse Banī Liḥyān"," Riʿl"," and Dhakwān"," and ʿUṣayyah"," for they disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. And forgive Ghifār"," and grant safety to Aslam.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 679.]"""
"3100","(3100) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbdillāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us; my father narrated to me; al-Awzāʿī narrated to me; Yaḥyā narrated to me; Abū Salamah narrated to me; Abū Hurayrah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed qunūt in the ʿAtamah (ʿIshāʾ) prayer in the last rakʿah after saying: \Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah","\"" for one month. In his qunūt he would say: \""O Allah"," save al-Walīd ibn al-Walīd. O Allah"," save Salamah ibn Hishām. O Allah"," save ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah. O Allah"," save the weak among the believers. O Allah"," intensify Your punishment upon Muḍar. O Allah"," make it upon them years like the years of Yūsuf.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; al-Walīd"," who is Ibn Muslim"," narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated to us"," mentioning it with its chain"," and said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed qunūt in the ʿAtamah prayer for one month"," saying in his qunūt…\"" and he mentioned something similar"," except that he did not mention ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah. At the end he added: Abū Hurayrah said: \""Then one day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not supplicate for them"," so I mentioned that to him"," and he said: 'Do you not see that they have arrived (been saved)?'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Mihrān al-Rāzī from al-Walīd ibn Muslim"," and he mentioned ʿAyyāsh. At the end he said: Abū Hurayrah said: \""Then I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cease the supplication thereafter"," so I said: 'I see that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has stopped supplicating for them.' It was said: 'Do you not see that they have arrived?'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Refer to ḥadīth 3084"," beginning of the chapter.]"""
"3101","(3101) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā and Abū ʿAbdillāh ibn Yazīd said: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Mihrān al-Rāzī narrated to us; al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, mentioning it, except that he did not mention ʿAtamah. He said: \In his prayer for one month"," when he said: 'Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah","' he would say in his qunūt…\""\n\nḤarb ibn Shaddād narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr with the meaning of the narration of al-Awzāʿī. At the end it states: \""He continued supplicating until Allah saved them"," then he ceased supplicating for them.\"" In another narration from Ḥarb in this ḥadīth"," it is said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," why do you not supplicate for the group?\"" He said: \""Do you not know that they have arrived?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Refer to the preceding ḥadīth.]"""
"3102","(3102) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; Hishām narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbdillāh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Qatādah from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed qunūt for one month, supplicating against certain Arab tribes, then he abandoned it. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim, 677.]"
"3103","(3103) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ṣaydalānī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us. He said: I heard Abū Qudāmah narrate from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī regarding the ḥadīth of Anas: \He performed qunūt for one month"," then abandoned it.\"" ʿAbd al-Raḥmān (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""He only abandoned the curse (laʿn).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"3104","(3104) Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Mihrān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated from al-Rabīʿ ibn Anas from Anas that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performed qunūt for one month, supplicating against them, then abandoned it. As for the morning (Ṣubḥ) prayer, he continued to perform qunūt until he departed from this world. [Munkar. Narrated by Aḥmad, 3/162.]"
"3105","(3105) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Bakr ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣayrafī in Marw narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Rāzī narrated from al-Rabīʿ ibn Anas, who said: \I was sitting with Anas when it was said to him: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) only performed qunūt for one month.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to perform qunūt in the morning (al-ghadāh) prayer until he departed from this world.'\""\n\nAbū ʿAbdillāh said: \""This chain is sound; its narrators are trustworthy. Al-Rabīʿ ibn Anas is a well-known Successor from the people of Baṣrah who heard from Anas ibn Mālik. Sulaymān al-Taymī"," ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak"," and others narrated from him.\""\n\nAbū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥātim said: \""I asked my father and Abū Zurʿah about al-Rabīʿ ibn Anas"," and they both said: 'Trustworthy and reliable (ṣadūq"," thiqah).'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim al-Makkī and ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd narrated it from al-Ḥasan from Anas"," but we do not use Ismāʿīl al-Makkī or ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd as evidence.\"" [Munkar. Refer to the preceding ḥadīth.]"""
"3106","(3106) It was informed to us by Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan al-Makhzūmī al-Ghaḍāʾirī in Baghdād; ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Simāk narrated to us; Abū Qilābah ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī narrated to us; Quraysh ibn Anas narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Makkī and ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd narrated from al-Ḥasan from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," Abū Bakr"," ʿUmar"," and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them) performed qunūt — and I think he said a fourth (referring to ʿAlī) — until I parted from them.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd narrated it from ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd and said: \""In the morning (al-ghadāh) prayer.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth of theirs has corroborating evidences from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and then from his Caliphs (may Allah be pleased with them). [Munkar. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 2/40.]"""
"3107","(3107) Among them is what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl and Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAnbarī both said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nufaylī narrated to us: Khulayd ibn Daʿlaj narrated from Qatādah from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he recited the qunūt, and behind ʿUmar and he recited the qunūt, and behind ʿUthmān and he recited the qunūt. [Munkar]"
"3108","(3108) And among them is what Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: al-Sājī narrated to us: Bundār narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥamzah said: I asked Abū ʿUthmān about the qunūt in the morning prayer, and he said: \After the rukūʿ.\"" I said: \""From whom?\"" He said: \""From Abū Bakr"," ʿUmar"," and ʿUthmān"," may Allah be pleased with them.\"" This is a ḥasan isnād. And Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd does not narrate except from those he considers trustworthy. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 2/60]"""
"3109","(3109) And Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Khaṭīb narrated to us: Abū Baḥr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Barbahārī narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us: al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to me: Mukhāriq narrated from Ṭāriq, who said: I prayed the Fajr prayer behind ʿUmar and he recited the qunūt. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 4959]"
"3110","(3110) And through his isnād, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, who said: I heard ʿUmar reciting the qunūt here in Makkah during the Fajr prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrihi. In the narration of ʿAbd al-Razzāq 4971, 4979]"
"3111","(3111) And through his isnād, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr from ʿUmar, similarly. These are authentic, connected narrations. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawīyah narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Bishr al-Marthadī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us: Shuʿbah said: And al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Dārimī narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, that is Ibn Khuzaymah, narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Ḥammād from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad, who said: I prayed behind ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, both while travelling and while resident, and he would not recite the qunūt except in the Fajr prayer. [Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrihi. In the narration of ʿAbd al-Razzāq 4979, Ṣaḥīḥ ghayrihi. And it has been discussed in the one before it]"
"3112","(3112) And Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated it from Shuʿbah through his isnād, and he said: \He would recite the qunūt in the second rakʿah of the Fajr prayer and would not recite the qunūt in any of his other prayers.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated it to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated it. And in this there is evidence of an abridgment that occurred in the hadith. [Ṣaḥīḥ. And the discussion on its isnād has preceded in the one before it]"""
"3113","(3113) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥīm ibn Munīb narrated to us: al-Fuḍayl narrated from Manṣūr from Ibrāhīm that al-Aswad and ʿAmr ibn Maymūn both said: \We prayed the Fajr prayer behind ʿUmar and he did not recite the qunūt.\"" Although Manṣūr is more precise and more reliable than Ḥammād ibn Abī Sulaymān"," the narration of Ḥammād in this matter agrees with the well-known position reported from ʿUmar regarding the qunūt. [Ṣaḥīḥ. In the narration of ʿAbd al-Razzāq 4948]"""
"3114","(3114) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us: Saʿid ibn ʿĀmir narrated to us: ʿAwf narrated from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, who said: \I prayed behind ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," for six years"," and he would recite the qunūt.\"" And Sulaymān al-Taymī narrated it from Abū ʿUthmān that ʿUmar recited the qunūt in the morning prayer. And Abū Rāfiʿ also narrated it from ʿUmar"," as we shall mention"," if Allah the Most High wills. And the ruling in such a case is the statement of the one who witnessed and retained"," not the statement of the one who neither witnessed nor retained. And through Allah is success. [Ṣaḥīḥ. This is a ṣaḥīḥ connected isnād]"""
"3115","(3115) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Khushaysh al-Tamīmī al-Muqriʾ narrated to us in Kūfah: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Azdī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Ghurzah narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Abū Ḥuṣayn from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maʿqil, who said: \ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," recited the qunūt in the Fajr prayer.\"" And this is a well-known authentic narration from ʿAlī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah 7509]"""
"3116","(3116) And Abū Naṣr ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah narrated to us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sarrāj narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ghannām narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥakīm narrated to us: Sharīk narrated from Fiṭr ibn Khalībah from Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Suwayd al-Kāhilī, who said: \It is as though I hear ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," in the Fajr prayer when he recited the qunūt"," saying: 'Allāhumma innā nastaʿīnuka wa nastaghfiruka (O Allah"," we seek Your help and we seek Your forgiveness).'\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 4978]"""
"3117","(3117) Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Shurayḥī informed us, Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd informed us, Sharīk reported from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Zurʿah from ʿArfajah, who said: I prayed Fajr prayer with Ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him), and he did not recite the qunūt. Then I prayed with ʿAlī, and he recited the qunūt. [Weak. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd, 2149]"
"3118","(3118) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Saʿīd—that is Ibn ʿĀmir—reported from ʿAwf from Abū Rajāʾ, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās prayed the morning prayer in this mosque and recited the qunūt, reciting this verse: {And stand before Allah in devout obedience} [al-Baqarah: 238]. [Sound. A sound chain of narration]"
"3119","(3119) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Baghawī in Baghdād informed us, ʿAlī—meaning Ibn al-Jaʿd—informed us, Shuʿbah reported from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Ibn Abī Laylā narrating from al-Barāʾ from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he used to recite the qunūt in the morning prayer.\n\nʿAmr said: I mentioned this to Ibrāhīm, and he said: He was not like the companions of ʿAbd Allāh; he was a follower of the governors.\n\nHe said: So I went back and abandoned the qunūt.\n\nThe people of the mosque said: By Allah, we have never seen anything like today in our mosque—a practice that had always been observed therein.\n\nHe said: So I returned to the qunūt, and this reached Ibrāhīm, who met me and said: This one is overcome in his prayer.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This statement of Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī (may Allah have mercy on him and on us) is not approved. It is not the case that every piece of knowledge found with the companions of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him) and not found with anyone else should not be acted upon. Rather, it is acted upon when it comes from one who is of higher standing than the companions of ʿAbd Allāh and the narrator is trustworthy. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā is a trustworthy narrator. ʿAmr ibn Murrah reported from the people of the mosque that this practice had always been observed in their mosque. We have also narrated from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib (may Allah be pleased with him) through another chain that he recited the qunūt in the Fajr prayer. [Sound. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd, 71]"
"3120","(3120) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us, Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah informed us, Sufyān reported from Muḥārib ibn Dithār from ʿUbayd ibn al-Barāʾ from al-Barāʾ, that he recited the qunūt in the Fajr prayer. [Sound. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah, 7010]"
"3121","(3121) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Shaybān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān reported from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: By Allah, I shall pray for you in the manner closest to the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite the qunūt in the last rakʿah of the morning prayer, after saying \Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah","\"" supplicating for the believers and cursing the disbelievers. [Sound. Previously cited under number 3089]"""
"3122","(3122) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh al-ʿAdl informed us, Abū Muslim informed us that Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed them, Hishām reported from Qatādah from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the qunūt for a month after the rūkūʿ, supplicating against certain Arab tribes. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 3861]"
"3123","(3123) Abū al-Khayr Jāmiʿ ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Wakīl informed us, Abū Ṭāhir al-Muḥammadābādhī informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Yūsuf al-Qāḍī informed us, Musaddad informed us. They both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd reported from Ayyūb from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), that he was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recite the qunūt in the morning prayer? He said: Yes. He was asked: Before the rūkūʿ or after it? He said: After the rūkūʿ, for a short while. He said: I do not know whether \for a short while\"" refers to the standing or to the qunūt. The wording is that of Sulaymān's ḥadīth. In the ḥadīth of Musaddad it is: Anas ibn Mālik was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recite the qunūt in the morning prayer before the rūkūʿ or after the rūkūʿ? He said: After the rūkūʿ"," for a short while. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 956]"""
"3124","(3124) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed me, Abū Yaʿlā informed us, Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb informed us, Ismāʿīl reported from Ayyūb from Muḥammad, who said: I asked Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recite the qunūt in the morning prayer? He said: Yes, after the rūkūʿ. Then he was asked again: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recite the qunūt in the morning prayer? He said: Yes, after the rūkūʿ, for a short while. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others. [Sound. Previously cited in the one before it]"
"3125","(3125) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, and Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us, Makhlad ibn Jaʿfar informed us. They both said: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Musaddad informed us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us, ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal informed us, who said: I asked Anas ibn Mālik about the qunūt, and he said: Indeed, the qunūt existed. I asked: Before the rūkūʿ or after it? He said: Before it. I said: So-and-so informed me from you that you said after the rūkūʿ. He said: He has lied. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) only recited the qunūt after the rūkūʿ for a month, because he had sent a group called al-Qurrāʾ—approximately seventy men—to a group of polytheists, and they were killed by a polytheist group other than those, while there was a covenant between them and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the qunūt for a month, supplicating against them. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. In this narration from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, the qunūt was after the rūkūʿ, and it was only for a month when he was supplicating against those who killed the Qurrāʾ. He was under the impression that the qunūt before and after that was only before the rūkūʿ. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb narrated from Anas regarding the story of the Qurrāʾ: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated against them for a month in the morning prayer, and that was the beginning of the qunūt, and we used not to recite the qunūt. Then ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated that a man asked Anas about the qunūt: Is it after the rūkūʿ or after completing the recitation? He said: Rather, after completing the recitation. We have narrated from Abū Hurayrah, outside the context of the story of the Qurrāʾ, that the qunūt of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) therein was after the rūkūʿ, and likewise from Ibn ʿUmar. [Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 957]"
"3126","(3126) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī in Ṭūs informed us, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh informed us, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us. They both said: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us, saying: We read to Abū al-Yamān that Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed him from al-Zuhrī, who informed me: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf both reported, saying:\n\nAbū Hurayrah said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his back from the rūkūʿ, he would say: \Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah"," Rabbaka wa laka al-ḥamd.\"" He would supplicate for certain men"," mentioning them by their names"," saying: \""O Allah"," grant salvation to al-Walīd ibn al-Walīd"," Salamah ibn Hishām"," ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah"," and the weak among the believers. O Allah"," intensify Your punishment upon Muḍar"," and make it upon them years like the years of Yūsuf.\"" The people of the east from Muḍar at that time were in opposition to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Sound. Previously cited under number 3084 and those after it]"""
"3127","(3127) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us; Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak informed us; Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who narrated from his father: that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) when he raised his head from rukūʿ in the last rakʿah of the Fajr prayer, say: \O Allah"," curse so-and-so"," and so-and-so"," and so-and-so","\"" after he had said: \""Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah"," Rabbaka laka al-ḥamd.\"" Then Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: \""Not for you is any matter of command\"" [Āl ʿImrān: 128].\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see no. 3093]"""
"3128","(3128) From Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Sulamī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak, with his chain of narration, and he added: and from Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān, who said: I heard Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to invoke curses upon Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah, Suhayl ibn ʿAmr, and al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, and so the verse was revealed: \Not for you is any matter of command\"" up to His words: \""Ẓālimūn\"" [Āl ʿImrān: 128].\n\n[Ḍaʿīf; narrated by Ibn al-Mubārak in al-Jihād"," no. 57]"""
"3129","(3129) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī informed me; Ḥammād ibn Shākir narrated to us; Muḥammad, i.e., al-Bukhārī, narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd this hadith has been narrated from ʿUmar ibn Ḥamzah, from Sālim, from his father, as a connected (mawṣūl) narration, except that he mentioned Abū Sufyān instead of Suhayl.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ; by reference, see the one before it]"
"3130","(3130) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ḥarmalah, from al-Ḥārith ibn Khufāf, that he said: Khufāf ibn Imāʾ said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed rukūʿ, then raised his head and said: \(The tribe of) Ghifār — Allah has forgiven them; (the tribe of) Aslam — Allah has granted them peace; (the tribe of) ʿUṣayyah — they disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. O Allah"," curse Banī Liḥyān"," and curse Riʿl and Dhakwān.\"" Then he went into prostration. Khālid said: The curse upon the disbelievers was made for that reason.\n\nNarrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb"," Qutaybah"," and ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr"," except that he said: Khufāf said: \""It was made.\"" And we have narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal"," from Anas"," that he gave a fatwā regarding the qunūt after rukūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ; previously narrated under no. 3099]"""
"3131","(3131) Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-ʿAṭṭār narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Aṣamm narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) only performed qunūt for one month. I said: How is the qunūt performed? He said: After rukūʿ.\n\nThus, he has informed that the customary, general qunūt is performed after rukūʿ.\n\nHis statement: \He only performed qunūt for one month\"" — he means by it the curse (laʿnah). And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best.\n\nThe narrations of qunūt after rukūʿ are more numerous and better preserved"," and thus it is more deserving. Upon this the Rightly Guided Caliphs (may Allah be pleased with them) acted"," according to the most well-known and most numerous narrations from them. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"3132","(3132) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ḥannāṭ narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Abī Isrāʾīl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us; al-ʿAwwām, a man from Banī Māzin, narrated to us, from Abū ʿUthmān: that Abū Bakr and ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) performed qunūt in the Ṣubḥ prayer after rukūʿ.\n\nAnd we have narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, from al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥamzah, with the addition of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ḍaʿīf; narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī, 2/33]"
"3133","(3133) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed it to us; Abū al-ʿAbbāṣ al-Umawī narrated to us; al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, Sulaymān al-Taymī, and ʿAlī ibn Zayd — each of them informed me that he heard Abū ʿUthmān narrating from ʿUmar: that he used to perform qunūt after rukūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ; narrated by Aḥmad, 3/166]"
"3134","(3134) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Mulāʿib narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Wahb narrated to us, from al-Ḥasan, from Abū Rāfiʿ: that ʿUmar performed qunūt in the Ṣubḥ prayer after rukūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih]"
"3135","(3135) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh informed me; Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us; Rūḥ narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: ʿUmar performed qunūt. I said: After rukūʿ? He said: Yes. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih]"
"3136","(3136) With his chain of narration, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ziyād, who said: I heard our elders narrating that ʿAlī used to perform qunūt in the Ṣubḥ prayer after rukūʿ.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And it has been narrated from ʿUmar and ʿAlī (may Allah, the Most High, be pleased with them both) that qunūt was performed before rukūʿ, but the authentic narration from ʿUmar is that it was after rukūʿ. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"3137","(3137) And Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿArūbah informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī Maʿshar al-Sulamī in Ḥarrān narrated to me — Aḥmad ibn Bakkār ibn Abī Maymūnah al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us — Makhlad ibn Yazīd narrated to us, from Khulayd ibn Daljaʿ, from Qatādah, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) — along with Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with them) — recited the qunūt after the rukūʿ. Then the dwellings grew distant, and the people came to ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) requesting that he place the qunūt in the prayer before the rukūʿ so that they might catch the prayer. So he recited the qunūt before the rukūʿ.\n\nKhulayd ibn Daljaʿ is not used as a ḥujjah (authoritative proof). What has preceded is sufficient. [Ḍaʿīf (Weak)]"
"3138","(3138) And Abū Manṣūr informed us: Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nūḥ, from the descendants of Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī, in al-Kūfah, informed us — Abū Jaʿfar: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāẓim ibn Abī Gharazah informed us — ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsá informed us — Isrāʾīl informed us, from Abī Isḥāq, from Burayd ibn Abī Maryam, from Abī al-Ḥawrāʾ, from al-Ḥasan, or al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) taught me words which I recite in the qunūt:\n\n\O Allah"," guide me among those whom You have guided"," and grant me well-being among those whom You have granted well-being"," and take me as a friend among those whom You have taken as a friend"," and bless me in what You have given me"," and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed"," You decree and none can decree against him"," and he whom You take as a friend is never humiliated"," and he whom You take as an enemy is never honored. Blessed are You"," our Lord"," and Exalted.\""\n\nThus it was in the original of his book: \""from al-Ḥasan"," or al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī","\"" as though the doubt did not occur regarding al-Ḥasan himself but rather occurred only in the attribution or the lineage. And in the original of his book there was the additional wording: \""and he whom You take as an enemy is never honored.\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak). Abū Dāwūd narrated it (no. 1425).]"""
"3139","(3139) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshād al-ʿAdl narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Bishr al-ʿAbdī narrated to us — al-Aʿlāʾ ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me — Burayd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to me — Abū al-Ḥawrāʾ said: I asked al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī, \What did you memorize from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?\"" He said: \""He taught me supplications which I recite: O Allah"," guide me among those whom You have guided"," and grant me well-being among those whom You have granted well-being"," and take me as a friend among those whom You have taken as a friend"," and bless me in what You have given me"," and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed"," You decree and none can decree against You.\""\n\nI think he also said: \""and he whom You take as a friend is never humiliated. Blessed are You"," our Lord"," and Exalted.\""\n\nHe said: \""So I mentioned that to Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah"," and he said: 'That is the supplication which my father used to recite in the prayer of Fajr in his qunūt.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Burayd says"," \""I mentioned that to Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah.\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak). It has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"3140","(3140) For Abū al-Ḥasan: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq al-Bazzār in Baghdad informed us, from his original copy in the handwriting of Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī — Abū Muḥammad: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī in Makkah narrated to us — Abū Yaḥyá: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Zakariyyā ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Masarrah informed me — my father informed me — ʿAbd al-Majīd, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Rāwād, informed me — from Ibn Jurayj — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmuz informed him that Burayd ibn Abī Maryam informed him, saying: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās and Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī, who is Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah, at al-Khayf, both saying: \The Prophet (ﷺ) used to recite the qunūt in the morning prayer and in the witr of the night with these words:\n\n'O Allah"," guide me among those whom You have guided"," and grant me well-being among those whom You have granted well-being"," and take me as a friend among those whom You have taken as a friend"," and bless me in what You have given me"," and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed"," You decree and none can decree against You. He whom You take as a friend is never humiliated. Blessed are You"," our Lord"," and Exalted.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf (Weak). Al-Fākihī narrated it (1/18/1-2).]"""
"3141","(3141) And al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated it, as Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Walīd: Ḥassān ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abū Bakr: Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — Hishām ibn Khālid al-Azraq narrated to us — al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Hurmuz, from Burayd ibn Abī Maryam, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to teach us a supplication which we would recite in the qunūt of the morning prayer:\n\n'O Allah"," guide us among those whom You have guided"," and grant us well-being among those whom You have granted well-being"," and take us as friends among those whom You have taken as friends"," and bless us in what You have given us"," and protect us from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed"," You decree and none can decree against You. He whom You take as a friend is never humiliated. Blessed are You"," our Lord"," and Exalted.'\""\n\nAnd Makhlad ibn Yazīd al-Ḥarrānī narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"," mentioning Burayd's narration as a mursal (disconnected) report regarding the Prophet (ﷺ) teaching one of the two sons of his daughter this supplication in his witr. Then Burayd said: \""I heard Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah and Ibn ʿAbbās both saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to recite it in the qunūt of the night.'\""\n\nAnd likewise Abū Ṣafwān al-Amawī narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"," except that he said \""from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hurmuz","\"" and in the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah he said \""in the qunūt of the morning prayer.\""\n\nThus all of this establishes that the teaching of this supplication pertains to the qunūt of the morning prayer and the qunūt of witr"," and that Burayd took the ḥadīth from the two routes we have mentioned. And with Allah is the granting of success. [Ḍaʿīf (Weak). It has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"3142","(3142) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlānī said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ informed you"," from ʿAbd al-Qāhir"," from Khālid ibn Abī ʿImrān"," who said: 'While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was supplicating against Muḍar"," Jibrīl came to him and gestured to him to be silent"," so he fell silent. He said: \""O Muhammad"," Allah has not sent you as one who curses or invokes evil. Rather"," He has sent you as a mercy"," and He has not sent you as a punishment. You have no authority over the matter — whether He turns to them in repentance or punishes them"," for they are wrongdoers.\"" Then he taught him this qunūt:\n\n\""O Allah"," we seek Your help and we seek Your forgiveness"," and we believe in You"," and we humble ourselves before You"," and we disavow and forsake whoever disbelieves in You. O Allah"," You alone do we worship"," and for You alone do we pray and prostrate"," and toward You alone we strive and hasten. We hope for Your mercy and we fear Your punishment — the severe one. Indeed"," Your punishment will overtake the disbelievers.\""'\n\nThis is a mursal (disconnected) report. And it has been narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) in a ṣaḥīḥ (sound)"," connected chain. [Ḍaʿīf (Weak). Abū Dāwūd narrated it in al-Marāsīl.]"""
"3143","(3143) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Asīd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us — from Sufyān — Ibn Jurayj narrated to me — from ʿAṭāʾ — from ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) recited the qunūt after the rukūʿ and said:\n\n\O Allah"," forgive us"," and the believing men and believing women"," and the Muslim men and Muslim women. Reconcile between their hearts"," set right their mutual affairs"," and grant them victory over Your enemy and their enemy. O Allah"," curse the disbelievers among the People of the Book who bar others from Your way"," and who deny Your messengers"," and who fight against Your friends. O Allah"," sow discord among them"," make their feet tremble"," and send upon them Your punishment which You do not turn away from the wrongdoing people. In the name of Allah"," the Most Merciful"," the Especially Merciful. O Allah"," we seek Your help and we seek Your forgiveness"," and we praise You and we do not disbelieve in You"," and we disavow and forsake whoever is ungrateful to You. In the name of Allah"," the Most Merciful"," the Especially Merciful. O Allah"," You alone do we worship"," and for You alone do we pray and prostrate"," and for You alone do we strive and hasten. We fear Your punishment — the severe one — and we hope for Your mercy. Indeed"," Your punishment will overtake the disbelievers.\""\n\nAnd Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzá narrated it from his father from ʿUmar"," differing from this in some of it. [Ṣaḥīḥ (Sound). ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it (no. 4968).]"""
"3144","(3144) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd informed me — my father narrated to me — al-Awzāʿī narrated to me — ʿAbadah ibn Abī Lubābah narrated to me — from Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abzá — from his father, who said: \I prayed behind ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) the morning prayer"," and I heard him saying after the recitation"," before the rukūʿ:\n\n'O Allah"," You alone do we worship"," and for You alone do we pray and prostrate"," and toward You alone do we strive and hasten. We hope for Your mercy and we fear Your punishment. Indeed"," Your punishment will overtake the disbelievers. O Allah"," we seek Your help and we seek Your forgiveness"," and we praise You with all goodness and we do not disbelieve in You"," and we believe in You and we humble ourselves before You"," and we disavow whoever disbelieves in You.'\""\n\nThus he said: \""before the rukūʿ.\""\n\nAnd even though its chain is sound"," those who narrated the qunūt of ʿUmar after the rukūʿ are more numerous. Abū Rāfiʿ"," ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr"," Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī"," and Zayd ibn Wahb all narrated it"," and the majority are more reliable in memorization than the single narrator. And in the excellence of ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr's presentation of the ḥadīth there is an indication of his precision and the precision of those who learned from him.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he recited the qunūt in Fajr and said: \""O Allah"," we seek Your help and we seek Your forgiveness.\"" And it has been narrated to us from Abū ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAlāʾ that he used to recite in the supplication of the qunūt: \""Indeed"," Your punishment will overtake the disbelievers\"" — meaning with a ḥāʾ in the genitive (majrūr). [Ṣaḥīḥ (Sound). It has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"3145","(3145) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah both informed us — Abū Muḥammad: Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us — Abū al-Qāsim: ʿAlī ibn Ṣaqr ibn Naṣr ibn Mūsá al-Sukkārī in Baghdad, from his book in Sūq Ghālib, narrated to us — ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us — from Thābit — from Anas ibn Mālik, in the story of the Qurʾāʾ and their being killed, he said: Anas said to me: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," whenever he prayed the morning prayer"," raise his hands and supplicate against them\"" — meaning against those who had killed them. [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than it (i.e."," ṣaḥīḥ lighayrihi). Aḥmad narrated it (3/137).]"""
"3146","(3146) Abū al-Ḥusayn: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik informed us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us — a shaykh in the gathering of ʿAmr ibn ʿUbayd, whom they claimed was Jaʿfar ibn Maymūn — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ṭaʿī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Ibn Abī Adī narrated to us — from Jaʿfar ibn Maymūn, the seller of al-Anmāṭ, from Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī, from Salmān al-Fārisī (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Indeed"," Allah is Shy and Generous. He is shy when His servant raises his hands to Him to return them empty and disappointed.\""\n\nJaʿfar ibn Maymūn raised it (marfūʿ) in this manner. And Sulaymān al-Taymī stopped it (mawqūf) from Abū ʿUthmān in one of the two narrations from him. And the ḥadīth regarding the supplication is established in general"," even though a number of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) raised their hands in the qunūt"," in addition to what we have narrated from Anas ibn Mālik from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ḥasan in other than it (i.e."," ḥasan lighayrihi). Abū Yaʿlā narrated it (no. 1868). Abū Dāwūd narrated it (no. 1488).]"""
"3147","(3147) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Jaʿfar Abū ʿAlī, the seller of carpets, who said: I heard Abū ʿUthmān say: I saw ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) raising his hands during the qunūt. [Ḥasan for other narrations. Al-Bukhārī cited it in Rafʿ al-Yadayn, 95, and its chain is weak.]"
"3148","(3148) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Maymūn, who said: Abū ʿUthmān al-Nahdī narrated to me, saying: We used to come while ʿUmar was leading the people in prayer, and he would perform the qunūt after rukūʿ, raising his hands until his palms became visible and he would spread out his upper arms. [Ḥasan for other narrations. Al-Bukhārī cited it in Rafʿ al-Yadayn, 94.]"
"3149","(3149) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from Abū ʿUthmān, who said: I prayed behind ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and he recited eighty verses from Sūrat al-Baqarah, then performed the qunūt after rukūʿ, raising his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, and he raised his voice in supplication until those behind the wall could hear him. [Ḥasan for other narrations.]"
"3150","(3150) Through this chain of narration, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan and Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh, both from Abū Rāfiʿ, who said: I prayed behind ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and he performed the qunūt after rukūʿ, raised his hands, and raised his voice in supplication. Qatādah said: Al-Ḥasan used to do the same. This narration from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) is authentic. It has also been narrated from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) through a chain containing weakness. It has also been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd and Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the qunūt of witr. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: As for wiping the hands over the face upon completion of the supplication, I do not preserve this from any of the early predecessors regarding the supplication of qunūt, although it is narrated from some of them regarding supplication outside of ṣalāh. A weak ḥadīth has been narrated regarding it from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and it is practiced by some outside of ṣalāh. As for within ṣalāh, it is an action not established by a sound ḥadīth, nor a reliable narration, nor analogy. Thus, it is more appropriate not to do it, and to limit oneself to what the early predecessors (may Allah be pleased with them) did—raising the hands without wiping them over the face during ṣalāh. And with Allah lies success. [Ḥasan for other narrations.]"
"3151","(3151) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad ibn Ayman narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq, from one who narrated to him from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb al-Quraẓī, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Ask Allah"," the Mighty and Sublime"," with the palms of your hands (facing upward)"," and do not ask Him with their backs (facing downward). When you have finished"," wipe your faces with them.\"" Abū Dāwūd said: This ḥadīth has been narrated from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb through various routes"," all of them weak"," and this route is the best among them"," though it is also weak. [Munkar. Abū Dāwūd cited it"," 1485.]"""
"3152","(3152) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Jarrāḥī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Shāsawayh narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Karīm al-Sukkari narrated to us; Wahb ibn Zamʿah informed me; ʿAlī al-Bāshānī said: I asked ʿAbd Allāh, meaning Ibn al-Mubārak, about the one who wipes his face when he supplicates. He said: I do not find any established basis for it. ʿAlī said: And I did not see him do that. He (Ibn al-Mubārak) used to perform the qunūt after rukūʿ in witr, and he used to raise his hands. [Weak.]"
"3153","(3153) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Jumaḥī narrated to us; Thābit ibn Yazīd narrated from Hilāl ibn Khabbāb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the qunūt consecutively for one month in ẓuhr, ʿaṣr, maghrib, ʿishāʾ, and fajr, in the last rakʿah of every prayer, after saying \Samiʿa Allāhu liman ḥamidah","\"" suppressing against certain tribes of Sulaym—against Riʿl"," Dhakwān"," and ʿUṣayyah—and those behind him would say āmīn. [Strong. Abū Dāwūd cited it"," 1443"," and its meaning in 3098.]"""
"3154","(3154) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Mūsā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jābir narrated from Ḥammād, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah and al-Aswad, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not perform the qunūt in any of his prayers. This is how Muḥammad ibn Jābir al-Suḥaymī narrated it, and he is abandoned (matrūk). [Munkar. Al-Ṭabarānī cited it in al-Awsaṭ, 7483.]"
"3155","(3155) Abū Ḥamzah al-Aʿwar narrated from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the qunūt for one month, supplicating against ʿUṣayyah and Dhakwān. When victory was granted over them, he abandoned the qunūt. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū Ghassān narrated to us; Sharīk narrated from Abū Ḥamzah, and he mentioned it. We have narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī (may Allah have mercy on him) that he said: He only abandoned the curse (laʿn). [Weak. Al-Ṭaḥāwī cited it, 1/245.]"
"3156","(3156) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū ʿAānah narrated from Abū Mālik al-Ashjaʿī, who said: I said to my father: O father, have you not prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), behind Abū Bakr, and behind ʿUmar? He said: Yes. I said: Did they perform the qunūt in fajr? He said: O my son, it is an innovation (muḥdathah). Ṭāq ibn Ashyam al-Ashjaʿī did not preserve it from the one behind whom he prayed, so he considered it an innovation, while others have preserved it. Thus, the ruling belongs to them over him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Mājah cited it, p. 1241.]"
"3157","(3157) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnazī informed me that ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Hammām narrated from Qatādah from Abī Mijlaz, who said: I prayed the morning prayer (ṣalāt al-ṣubḥ) with Ibn ʿUmar, and he did not perform the qunūt. So I said to Ibn ʿUmar: \I do not see you performing the qunūt.\"" He said: \""I do not preserve it from any of our Companions.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The forgetting of some of the Companions or their negligence regarding some of the Sunnahs does not impugn the narration of the one who preserved it and established it.\n\n[Sound. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 4954.]"""
"3158","(3158) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us that Bishr ibn Ḥarb narrated to us — he said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar saying: \Have you seen their standing after the reciter finishes the sūrah? This qunūt is indeed an innovation (bidʿah). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) only performed it for one month"," then he abandoned it.\""\n\nBishr ibn Ḥarb al-Nadabī is weak.\n\nIf his narration from Ibn ʿUmar is authentic"," then it indicates that he only rejected the qunūt before the rukūʿ.\n\n[Weak narrator — Bishr ibn Ḥarb al-Nadabī is weak.]"""
"3159","(3159) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed me that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar informed us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Ṭūsī narrated to us that Shabābah narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maysarah, Abū Laylā, narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ḥurrah from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he said: \The qunūt in the morning prayer (ṣalāt al-ṣubḥ) is an innovation (bidʿah).\""\n\nThis is not authentic. Abū Laylā al-Kūfī is abandoned (matrūk).\n\nAnd we have narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that he performed the qunūt in the morning prayer. [Weak]"""
"3160","(3160) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh, Abū Muslim, narrated to us that al-Ramādī, meaning Ibrāhīm ibn Bashshār, narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Yaʿlā narrated to us that ʿAnbasah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ from his father from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade the qunūt in the morning prayer (ṣalāt al-ṣubḥ).\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī said: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿlā, ʿAnbasah, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ are all weak, and there is no authentic record of Nāfiʿ having heard from Umm Salamah.\n\nHe also said: Hiyāj narrated from ʿAnbasah from Ibn Nāfiʿ from his father from Ṣafiyyah ibn Abī ʿUbayd from the Prophet (ﷺ). And Ṣafiyyah ibn Abī ʿUbayd did not meet the Prophet (ﷺ). [False. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr, 643.]"
"3161","(3161) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that Abū Badr narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zubayd al-Iyāmī narrated from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd from Saʿd ibn Abī Wāqqāṣ, who said, regarding the verse: {Those who are heedless of their prayers} (Q. al-Māʿūn: 5) — and in the recitation of ʿAbd Allāh: \lāhūn\"" — he said: \""Being heedless of it means abandoning its appointed time.\""\n\n[Sound in other than this chain. Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā"," 705.]"""
"3162","(3162) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdad that Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Abān ibn Yazīd narrated from ʿĀṣim, meaning Ibn Abī al-Najūd, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, who said: I said to my father: \What do you think about the statement of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic: {Those who are heedless of their prayers} (Q. al-Māʿūn: 5)? Is it the one who converses with himself during the prayer?\"" He said: \""No — and which one of us does not converse with himself during the prayer? Rather"," being heedless means delaying the prayer from its appointed time.\""\n\nThis was also narrated with a chain by ʿIkrimah ibn Ibrāhīm al-Azdī. [Sound in other than this chain.]"""
"3163","(3163) Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mahrānī informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us that Shaybān ibn Farrūkh narrated to us that ʿIkrimah ibn Ibrāhīm al-Azdī narrated from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd from Saʿd, who said: I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about His statement: {Those who are heedless of their prayers} (Q. al-Māʿūn: 5). He said: \They are those who delay the prayer from its appointed time.\""\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by al-Ṭabarī in his Tafsīr"," 12/706.]"""
"3164","(3164) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to me that Ḥarmī ibn Ḥafṣ al-Qasmalī narrated to us that ʿIkrimah ibn Ibrāhīm narrated — he mentioned it with its chain: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about {Those who are heedless of their prayers} (Q. al-Māʿūn: 5). He said: \It means wasting the time.\""\n\nThis hadith is only authentic as a mawqūf narration.\n\nAnd ʿIkrimah ibn Ibrāhīm was declared weak by Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and other imams of hadith. [Munkar. It was previously mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3165","(3165) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-Ḥasanī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us by dictation that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Dallawayh al-Daqqāq narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī narrated to us that Abū al-Walīd Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated — al-Walīd ibn al-ʿAyzār informed me, saying: I heard Abū ʿAmr al-Shaybānī say: The owner of this house informed me — and he pointed with his hand toward the house of ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿud (may Allah be pleased with him) — he said: I asked the Prophet (ﷺ): \Which deed is most beloved to Allah?\"" He said: \""Prayer at its appointed time.\"" I said: \""Then which?\"" He said: \""Kindness to parents.\"" I said: \""Then which?\"" He said: \""Jihād in the cause of Allah.\"" He said: \""He narrated these three things to me"," and had I asked him for more"," he would have added for me.\""\n\nThus did al-Bukhārī narrate it in the Ṣaḥīḥ"," and Muslim narrated it through another route from Shuʿbah.\n\n[Sound. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 504.]"""
"3166","(3166) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham al-Baladī narrated to us that Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us that Abū Ghassān, meaning Muḥammad ibn Muṭarrif, narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — and the wording is his — that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us that Muḥammad, meaning Ibn Muṭarrif, narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣunābihī, who said: Abū Muḥammad claimed that the witr prayer is obligatory.\n\nʿUbaydah said: \Abū Muḥammad is mistaken. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'There are five prayers that Allah has made obligatory. Whoever performs their wuḍūʾ well"," prays them at their appointed times"," and completes their rukūʿ and their khushūʿ"," then he has with Allah a promise that He will forgive him. And whoever does not do so has no promise from Allah — if He wills"," He will forgive him"," and if He wills"," He will punish him.'\""\n\nIn the hadith of Ādam"," there is no mention of the witr"," and he narrated it from Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣunābihī.\n\n[Sound. Previously mentioned under no. 1692.]"""
"3167","(3167) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Abī Khalaf al-Ṣūfī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yazdād ibn Masʿūd al-Jawsqānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr al-Ashʿathī narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, a companion of Misʿar ibn Kidām, from Yazīd al-Faqīr, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," the most fearful thing I fear for my Ummah is their delaying the Ṣalāh from its time and their performing the Ṣalāh before its time.\"""""
"3168","(3168) Abū Bakr ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed him; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī narrated to us; Aḥmad said: al-Ashʿathī narrated this ḥadīth, then al-Bukhārī said: \I do not know what this ḥadīth is.\"" The Shaykh said: This is because he does not know the condition of this ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. And Allah knows best. The narrations regarding the times (of prayer) have already passed"," and they are sufficient. Others besides al-Ashʿathī narrated it from Ḥafṣ and gave it a complete chain."""
"3169","(3169) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn ʿIṣām narrated to us; Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād from Yazīd al-Raqāshī from Anas ibn Mālik (may may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), something similar to it."
"3170","(3170) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us; Jaʿfar al-Qalānisī narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from al-Ḥakam from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad, who said: I asked ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): \What did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to do among his family?\"" She said: \""He used to be in the service of his family\"" — meaning"," he used to serve his family — \""and when the time for Ṣalāh came"," he would go out for the Ṣalāh.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam."""
"3171","(3171) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf both informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us; Thābit al-Bunānī narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rabāḥ narrated from his father, Abū Qatādah, who said: We travelled with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during a journey one night and we said: \O Messenger of Allah"," if only you would allow us to camp (and rest).\"" He mentioned the ḥadīth about their sleeping through the Ṣalāh. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," Allah took your souls when He willed and returned them to you when He willed.\"" Then He commanded them"," so they went out to relieve themselves and performed wuḍūʾ. The sun had risen"," and he led them in prayer. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Salām from Hushaym."""
"3172","(3172) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf both informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us; Thābit al-Bunānī narrated to me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rabāḥ narrated from Abū Qatādah, who mentioned the ḥadīth about their journey. He said: The Prophet (ﷺ) turned off the road and laid down his head, then said: \Guard our prayer for us.\"" The first of them to awaken was the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and the sun was upon his back. We arose in a state of alarm"," and he said: \""Mount up.\"" We travelled until the sun rose high. Then he called for a water vessel that I had with me"," which contained some water"," and we performed wuḍūʾ from it. He mentioned the ḥadīth"," then said: Then Bilāl called the adhān"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed two rakʿahs"," then he prayed the Ṣalāh of al-Ghadāh (Fajr)"," doing as he used to do every day. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) mounted and we mounted"," and some of us began whispering to one another: \""What is the expiation for what we did by neglecting our prayer?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""What is this that you are whispering among yourselves?\"" We said: \""O Prophet of Allah"," our neglect of our prayer.\"" He said: \""Is there not in me a good example for you?\"" Then he said: \""There is no neglect in sleep; neglect is only upon one who does not pray the Ṣalāh until the time of the next prayer comes. When that happens"," let him pray it when he awakens"," and if it is the following day"," let him pray it at its time.\"" He mentioned the remainder of the ḥadīth. Then ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rabāḥ said: \""Indeed"," I narrate this ḥadīth in the congregational mosque"," and ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn said to me: 'Look"," young man"," how you narrate"," for I was among the riders that night.' I said: 'O Abū Najīd"," you narrate"," for you know the ḥadīth better.' He said: 'From whom are you?' I said: 'From the Anṣār.' He said: 'Then you know the ḥadīth better.' So I narrated it to the people"," and ʿImrān said: 'I was indeed present that night"," and I did not think anyone had preserved it as you have preserved it.'\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Shaybān ibn Farrūkh from Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah"," and he said: \""Whoever does that"," let him pray it when he becomes aware of it"," and if it is the following day"," let him pray it at its time.\"" And he intended thereby — and Allah knows best — to clarify that its time did not shift to after sunrise; rather"," the following day he should pray it at its time"," meaning the prayer of the next day. Some of them narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rabāḥ erroneously."""
"3173","(3173) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed him; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us; Abū Khalīfah narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; al-Aswad ibn Shaybān narrated from Khālid ibn Shumayr, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rabāḥ al-Anṣārī came to us, and the Anṣār used to consider him a faqīh. He narrated to us and said: Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), narrated to us. He mentioned the story of their sleeping through the Ṣalāh, until he said: \We did not awaken except with the sun rising upon us. We stood up"," alarmed about our prayer"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Gently"," gently","' until the sun rose high. Then he said: 'Whoever prays these two rakʿahs before the Ṣalāh of al-Ghadāh"," let him pray them.' So those who used to pray them prayed them"," and those who did not pray them also prayed them. Then he commanded"," and the call to prayer was made. He came forward and led us in prayer. When he completed the prayer"," he said: 'Indeed"," by the praise of Allah"," we were not occupied by any worldly affair that distracted us from our prayer. Rather"," our souls were in the Hand of Allah; He sent them forth when He willed. Whoever catches this prayer the next day in a sound state"," let him pray along with it the like of it.'\"" Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: He is not supported in his statement: \""Whoever forgets a prayer"," let him pray it when he remembers it"," along with its time the following day.\"" Abū Bakr al-Fārisī informed him; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated to us; Muḥammad mentioned it. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: What indicates the weakness of this word"," and that the correct narration is what has passed from the narration of Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah"," is that ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn was among the riders"," as ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rabāḥ narrated from him"," and he explicitly stated in the narration of this ḥadīth that nothing is obligatory alongside the qaḍāʾ."""
"3174","(3174) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us; Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām narrated from al-Ḥasan from ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We travelled with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during a raid — or he said, a sariyyah — and when it was the last part of the night, we camped. We did not awaken until the heat of the sun roused us. Some of us began to awaken in alarm, bewildered. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke, he commanded us, and we set out. We travelled until the sun rose high. Then we dismounted, and the people took care of their needs. Then he commanded Bilāl, and he gave the adhān. We prayed two rakʿahs, then he commanded him, and he gave the iqāmah. Then he prayed al-Ghadāh (Fajr). We said: \O Prophet of Allah"," should we not make it up the following day at its time?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to them: \""Allah forbids you from ribā and accepts it from you.\"" And Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated it similarly from Hishām."""
"3175","(3175) Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated from Hishām from al-Ḥasan that ʿImrān ibn al-Ḥuṣayn narrated it to him, and he mentioned its meaning. ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed him; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Bayān al-Muqriʾ narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Muhallab narrated to us; Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah narrated it."
"3176","(3176) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — and the wording is his — Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) returned from the expedition of Khaybar, he travelled by night until drowsiness overcame him, and he camped. He said to Bilāl: \Keep watch for us during the night.\"" Bilāl prayed as much was decreed for him"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and his Companions slept. When Fajr drew near"," Bilāl leaned against his mount"," facing the direction of Fajr. Sleep overcame Bilāl's eyes while he was leaning against his mount. Neither the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) nor Bilāl nor any of his Companions awoke until the sun struck them. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was the first of them to awaken. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was alarmed and said: \""O Bilāl!\"" Bilāl said: \""May my father and mother be your ransom"," O Messenger of Allah! The One who overcame you with sleep has overcome me with sleep.\"" He said: \""Move on.\"" They moved their mounts a short distance. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed wuḍūʾ and commanded Bilāl"," and he gave the iqāmah for the Ṣalāh. He led them in the morning prayer. When he completed the prayer"," he said: \""Whoever forgets a prayer"," let him pray it when he remembers it"," for indeed Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: {Establish the prayer for My remembrance} [Ṭā Hā: 14].\"" Yūnus said: Ibn Shihāb used to recite it as \""li-dhikrī.\"" And in the ḥadīth of Aḥmad it is \""li-dhikrā.\"" Yūnus said: Ibn Shihāb used to recite it likewise. Aḥmad said: ʿAnbasah narrated — meaning from Yūnus — in this ḥadīth: \""li-dhikrī.\"" Aḥmad said: \""Al-karī\"" means drowsiness and sleep. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah."""
"3177","(3177) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us — Abān informed us — Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, from Abū Hurayrah, regarding this ḥadīth, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Move from the place in which heedlessness overcame you.\"" He said: He then commanded Bilāl"," and he gave the adhān and the iqāmah"," and he prayed.\n\nAnd this ḥadīth was narrated by Mālik ibn Anas and a group"," from al-Zuhrī"," from Ibn al-Musayyib"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," as a mursal ḥadīth.\n\nAnd Mālik narrated it from Zayd ibn Aslam"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," as a munqaṭiʿ ḥadīth"," and the one who connected it is a thiqah (trustworthy narrator). And it has been established from another route from Abū Hurayrah in an abridged form. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (436)]"""
"3178","(3178) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us — Yaḥyā, from Yazīd ibn Kayyān, who said: Abū Ḥāzim narrated to me, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: We encamped with the Prophet ﷺ at night, and we did not wake until the sun had risen. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let each one of you take hold of the head of his mount"," for indeed this is a place in which Shayṭān has come upon us.\"" So we did that. Then he called for water and performed wuḍūʾ"," then he prostrated two prostrations. Then the iqāmah was called"," and he prayed the morning prayer.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim and others"," from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. The preceding ḥadīth has already been mentioned.]"""
"3179","(3179) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us — Abū Nuʿaym, Abū al-Walīd, and Muslim said: — Hammām ibn Yaḥyā informed us, from Qatādah, from Anas, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Whoever forgets a prayer"," let him pray it when he remembers it"," and there is no expiation for it other than that.\"" Then Qatādah recited: {And establish prayer for My remembrance} [Ṭā Hā: 14].\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim (680)]"""
"3180","(3180) And Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Hudbah informed us — Hammām informed us — Qatādah, and he mentioned it with a similar wording.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Haddāb ibn Khālid, who is Hudbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (572)]"
"3181","(3181) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us — Abū ʿAwānah, from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever forgets a prayer or sleeps through it"," its expiation is that he pray it when he remembers it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and others.\n\nAnd similarly"," Ibn Abī ʿArūbah and al-Muthannā ibn Saʿīd and others narrated it from Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It has been mentioned in the preceding ḥadīth]"""
"3182","(3182) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us — Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī informed us — Shuʿbah and al-Masʿūdī, from Jāmiʿ ibn Shaddād, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī ʿAlqamah al-Qārī, from the Banī Qārah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd — and the ḥadīth of al-Masʿūdī is more complete — who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his return from al-Ḥudaybiyyah, and he encamped. He said: \Who will guard us for our prayer?\"" And Shuʿbah said: \""Who will protect us?\"" Bilāl said: \""I will.\"" Al-Masʿūdī said in his ḥadīth: \""Indeed you will sleep.\"" Then he said: \""Who will guard us for our prayer?\"" ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said: \""I will"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed you will sleep.\"" So I guarded them until"," when it was near dawn"," what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said befell me"," and I slept. We did not wake except with the sun. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and did what he used to do"," then he said: \""If Allah had willed that you not sleep from it"," you would not have slept. But He willed that it be for those after you"," so whoever among you sleeps or forgets"," let him do thus.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Aḥmad (1/391)]"""
"3183","(3183) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Sulaymān al-Burulūsī informed us — Abū Thābit informed us — Ḥafṣ ibn Abī al-ʿAṭṭāf, from Abū al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Whoever forgets a prayer"," its time is when he remembers it.\""\n\nThus did Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar ibn Abī al-ʿAṭṭāf narrate it. And it has been said that he narrated it from Abū al-Zinād"," from al-Qaʿqāʿ ibn Ḥakīm"," or from al-Aʿraj"," from Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him. (c) And it is munkar (objectionable).\n\nAl-Bukhārī and others said"," and the ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth from Abū Hurayrah and others from the Prophet ﷺ is what we have mentioned"," in which there is no mention of \""its time is when he remembers it.\""\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Abū Qatādah"," Abū Hurayrah"," and others"," there is evidence that the time for making up a missed prayer is not restricted. And if it were restricted"," it would be more appropriate not to delay it from the state of alertness due to the place of Shayṭān. For the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed while choking Shayṭān.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And choking Shayṭān in prayer is greater than a valley in which there is a Shayṭān.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (449)"," Muslim (541)]"""
"3184","(3184) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Qaṭīʿī informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me — my father informed me — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us — Shuʿbah, from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \An ʿifrīt from the jinn confronted me last night to interrupt my prayer. Allah enabled me to overpower him"," and I seized him. I wanted to tie him to one of the pillars of the mosque until morning"," so that all of you could look at him.\"" He said: \""Then I remembered the supplication of my brother Sulaymān: {My Lord"," grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me} [Ṣād: 35]. So I drove him away"," humiliated.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār"," from Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (449)]"""
"3185","(3185) Abū Muḥammad Junāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Junāḥ al-Muḥāribī in al-Kūfah informed us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym informed us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim informed us — ʿUbaydullāh, who is Ibn Mūsā, informed us — Isrāʾīl, from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh, who is Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Shayṭān passed by me"," and I seized him and took hold of him. I choked him until I felt the coldness of his tongue upon my hand. He said: 'You have pained me"," you had pained me!' Were it not for the supplication of Sulaymān"," peace be upon him"," he would have been tied to one of the pillars of the mosque"," and the children of the people of al-Madīnah would have looked at him.\""\n\nJābir ibn Samurah followed him in narrating it from the Prophet ﷺ with its meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi. Narrated by Aḥmad (1/413)]"""
"3186","(3186) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us — Ḥājib ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭūsī informed us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim informed us — Wakīʿ informed us — ʿAlī ibn al-Mubārak, from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Abū Salamah, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of the Trench, and he began to insult the disbelievers of Quraysh and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I did not pray the ʿAṣr prayer until the sun was about to set.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""By Allah"," I have not prayed it yet.\"" He said: He then descended to Buṭḥān and performed wuḍūʾ"," and prayed the ʿAṣr after the sun had set"," then prayed the Maghrib after that. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī (573)]"""
"3187","(3187) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated it with a similar chain.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā, from Wakīʿ, and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\n[Reference as mentioned above. Authentic. Preceded in the one before it.]"
"3188","(3188) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿUthmān Abū ʿUthmān al-Tanūkhī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated to me; Abū al-Zubayr narrated to me from Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, from Abī ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) facing the enemy in battle formation, and they kept the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be occupied from the Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, and ʿIshāʾ prayers until half of the night had passed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood and began with the Ẓuhr prayer and prayed it, then the ʿAṣr, then the Maghrib, then the ʿIshāʾ, following one upon the other.\n\nAl-Walīd ibn Muslim added on the authority of Abū ʿAmr al-Awzāʿī: \Following one upon the other"," each with a separate iqāmah\"" — and its mention has already preceded.\n\nAnd we have received it from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in the matter of the adhān. [Authentic through other chains. Al-Tirmidhī narrated it (179).]"""
"3189","(3189) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī narrated to us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Farāʾ narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to me from al-Aʿmash, from Abū al-Ḍuḥā, from Shutayr ibn Shakal, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was kept occupied on the Day of al-Aḥzāb from the ʿAṣr prayer until he prayed it between the Maghrib and the ʿIshāʾ. He said: \They kept us from the middle prayer — the ʿAṣr prayer. May Allah fill their graves and their houses with fire.\""\n\n[Authentic. Preceded under no. 2160.]"""
"3190","(3190) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from al-Aʿmash, from Muslim ibn Ṣubayḥ, from Shutayr ibn Shakal, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said on the Day of al-Aḥzāb: \They kept us from the middle prayer — the ʿAṣr prayer. May Allah fill their houses and their graves with fire.\"" Then he prayed it between the two evening prayers — between the Maghrib and the ʿIshāʾ.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated through a weak chain that he cancelled the first prayer and prayed the ʿAṣr"," then prayed the Maghrib. [Authentic. Preceded in the one before it.]"""
"3191","(3191) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Ibn Lahīʿah informed us from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Muḥammad ibn Yazīd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwf, from Abī Jumʿah Ḥabīb ibn Sibāʿ, who was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed the Maghrib on the Day of al-Aḥzāb and forgot the ʿAṣr. He said to his Companions: \Did you see me pray the ʿAṣr?\"" They said: \""No"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded the muʾadhdhin"," and he gave the adhān. Then he made the iqāmah for the prayer and prayed the ʿAṣr"," cancelled the first one"," and then prayed the Maghrib.\n\nAnd we have received in the authentic ḥadīth from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he prayed the ʿAṣr and then prayed the Maghrib after it. It is possible that he did this on one day"," and what we have received from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) pertains to another day"," and what we have received in the ḥadīth of Ibn Masʿūd and Abū Saʿīd pertains to yet another day. And it is possible that what is meant by the statement of ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) \""between the Maghrib and the ʿIshāʾ\"" is between the sunset and the time of the ʿIshāʾ"," in which case it would be in agreement with the narration of Jābir. And Allah knows best. [Munkar. Al-Ṭabarānī narrated it in al-Kabīr (3542).]"""
"3192","(3192) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us of it; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us from al-Zuhrī, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \When you come to the prayer"," do not come to it running; come to it walking"," and upon you is tranquillity. Pray what you have caught up with"," and make up what you have missed.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Sufyān. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī narrated it (866).]"""
"3193","(3193) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Bassām Abū Ibrāhīm al-Tarjumānī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever forgets a prayer and does not remember it except while he is with the imām"," let him pray with the imām. When he finishes his prayer"," let him repeat the prayer he forgot"," and then let him repeat the prayer he prayed with the imām.\""\n\nAbū Ibrāhīm al-Tarjumānī is alone in narrating this ḥadīth as marfūʿ (raised to the Prophet). The correct position is that it is from the statement of Ibn ʿUmar"," mawqūf (stopped at the Companion). And thus others besides Abū Ibrāhīm narrated it from Saʿīd. [Munkar. Ibn al-Jawzī narrated it in al-Taḥqīq (1/439).]"""
"3194","(3194) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated to us from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, a similar narration, and he did not raise it (to the Prophet).\n\nAnd likewise Mālik ibn Anas and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-ʿUmariyy narrated it from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, as mawqūf. [Authentic. Mālik narrated it (406).]"
"3195","(3195) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us. He said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Mālik ibn Anas informed you, from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: \Whoever forgets one of his prayers and does not remember it except while he is behind the imām"," when the imām says the salām"," let him pray the prayer he forgot"," and then let him pray the other prayer after it.\""\n\nIbn Wahb said: And Mālik"," al-Layth ibn Saʿd"," and Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sālim said the like of it.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The repetition of the prayer that one prayed with the imām"," according to al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him)"," is recommended (mustaḥabb)"," not obligatory (wājib). And Allah knows best. [Authentic. And it has preceded in the one before it.]"""
"3196","(3196) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr narrated to us; Baqiyyah narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us from Makḥūl, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you forgets a prayer and remembers it while he is in an obligatory prayer"," let him begin with that which he is in. When he finishes"," let him pray the one he forgot.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ʿUmar ibn Abī ʿUmar is unknown (majhūl); I do not know anyone who narrates from him other than Baqiyyah.\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: The totality of rulings in which the woman differs from the man in matters of prayer relates to covering (al-satr)"," and it is that she is commanded with everything that provides greater concealment for her. The chapters that follow this one reveal its meaning and detail. And with Allah is success. [Munkar. Ibn ʿAdī narrated it (5/22).]"""
"3197","(3197) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād said that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When a woman prostrates"," let her draw her thighs together.\""\n\nTwo weak hadiths have been narrated on this matter whose likes cannot be used as evidence"," one of them being: [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 2777]"""
"3198","(3198) The hadith of ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-ʿAjlān from Abū Naḍrah al-ʿAbdī from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) that he said: \The best rows of men are the first rows"," and the best rows of women are the last row.\"" And he used to command the men to keep their arms away from their sides in their prostration"," and he used to command the women to draw themselves together in their prostration. And he used to command the men to spread out their left leg and erect their right leg in the tashahhud"," and he used to command the women to sit cross-legged. And he said: \""O company of women"," do not raise your gazes in your prayer"," looking at the private parts of the men.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Mazīd al-Bayrūtī informed us that Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Sulaymān informed us from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-ʿAjlān that he narrated to them"," and he mentioned it.\n\nThe first wording and the last wording of this hadith are well-known from the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," but what is between them is rejected (munkar). And Allah knows best. [Rejected (Munkar)]"""
"3199","(3199) The other is the hadith of Abū Muṭīʿ al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Balkhī from ʿUmar ibn Dharr from Mujāhid from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \When a woman sits in prayer"," she places her thigh upon her other thigh"," and when she prostrates"," she presses her belly against her thighs"," which is the most concealing for her. And indeed"," Allah the Most High looks at her and says: 'O My angels"," I bear witness to you that I have forgiven her.'\"" [False (Bāṭil). Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī"," 2/124]"""
"3200","(3200) Abū Saʿd al-Ṣūfī informed us that Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us that ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad al-Sarakhṣī narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn al-Qāsim al-Balkhī narrated to us that Abū Muṭīʿ narrated to us that ʿUmar ibn Dharr narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \Abū Muṭīʿ is clearly weak in his hadiths"," and most of what he narrates is not corroborated.\""\n\nThe Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""He was declared weak by Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and others"," and likewise ʿAṭāʾ ibn ʿAjlān is weak. And a disconnected hadith has been narrated on this matter which is better than the two connected ones before it.\"" [False (Bāṭil). Previously mentioned in the one before it]"""
"3201","(3201) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us that Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī narrated to us that Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed us from Sālim ibn Ghaylān from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed by two women who were praying and said: \When you two prostrate"," press some of your flesh to the ground"," for a woman is not in that regard like a man.\"" [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd in al-Marāsīl"," as in al-Talkhīṣ"," 1/242]"""
"3202","(3202) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us that Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl from Muslim al-Baṭīn from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah the Most High: \Take your adornment at every mosque\"" [al-Aʿrāf:31]. He said: \""When a woman performed ṭawāf around the House"," she would expose her chest and what was there"," so Allah the Most High revealed: 'Take your adornment at every mosque.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Jarīr in his Tafsīr"," 5/469]"""
"3203","(3203) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated to us from Salamah ibn Kuhayl. He said: \I heard Muslim al-Baṭīn narrating from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: 'A woman used to perform ṭawāf around the House in the Jāhiliyyah while naked"," with only a rag over her private part"," and she would recite:\n\nToday some of it or all of it appears","\nAnd whatever of it appears"," I do not permit it.\n\nSo this verse was revealed: \""Say: Who has forbidden the adornment of Allah?\"" [al-Aʿrāf:32].'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Nāfiʿ and Ibn Bashshār from Ghundar from Shuʿbah.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī said: \""And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'None of you should pray in a single garment with nothing of it upon his shoulder.' This indicates that it is not permissible for anyone to pray unless he is clothed"," if he has the ability to wear clothing.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 3028]"""
"3204","(3204) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed us from Abū al-Zinād from al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \None of you should pray in a single garment with nothing of it upon his shoulder.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿĀṣim from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 352]"""
"3205","(3205) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us that Mālik informed us. He mentioned it with his chain of narration, except that he said: \A man should not pray in a single garment with nothing of it upon his shoulder.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū ʿĀṣim from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned in the one before it]"""
"3206","(3206) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed us that al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed me that Ibn Shihāb informed him from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade ishtimāl al-ṣammāʾ (wrapping oneself in a garment with no opening for the arms)"," and that a man should wrap himself in a single garment with nothing of it covering his private part.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah from al-Layth"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Abū Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 360]"""
"3207","(3207) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yazīd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh narrated from Khubayb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Ḥafṣ ibn ʀāṣim from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited two types of garments: al-ṣammā' (wrapping oneself in a garment with nothing else underneath) and al-iḥtibā' (sitting wrapped in a single garment) in such a manner that one's private parts are exposed towards the sky. It was narrated in the two Ṣaḥīḥs from the ḥadīth of ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 559.]"
"3208","(3208) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated from Mālik from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited a man from eating with his left hand, walking in a single sandal, wrapping himself in al-ṣammā', and sitting wrapped in a single garment while exposing his private parts. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. Al-ṣammā', according to the jurists, refers to a person wrapping himself in a single garment with nothing else upon him, then lifting it from one of his sides and placing it over his shoulders, whereby his private parts become exposed. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim, 2099.]"
"3209","(3209) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated; al-Layth narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited al-ṣammā' (wrapping), al-iḥtibā' (sitting wrapped) in a single garment, and that a man should raise one of his legs over the other while lying on his back. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. It is likely that the prohibition against raising one leg over the other while lying down is due to the exposure of the ʿawrah (private parts), because when a person lying down raises one leg over the other while wearing a narrow lower garment, something of his thighs inevitably becomes exposed, and the thigh is part of the ʿawrah. However, if the lower garment is ample or the wearer is cautious against exposure, then there is no harm in it. This was stated by Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī, as it reached me from him, by way of deduction. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim.]"
"3210","(3210) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm from his paternal uncle, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the mosque lying on his back, placing one of his legs over the other. Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said: His paternal uncle was ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and a group, all of them from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, p. 463.]"
"3211","(3211) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm from his paternal uncle, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) lying on his back in the mosque, raising one of his legs over the other. Al-Zuhrī said: And Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab informed me—meaning concerning ʿUmar and ʿUthmān—regarding that, and he could not enumerate how often they did that. Al-Zuhrī said: The people have come with a grave matter. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the preceding ḥadīth.]"
"3212","(3212) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym and Muḥammad ibn Shādhān and Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad said: Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Umawī narrated to us; my father narrated to me; he said: ʿUthmān ibn Ḥakīm narrated to me; Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl ibn Ḥunayf informed me from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: I came carrying a stone which I was bearing, and I was wearing a light lower garment. My lower garment came undone, and I had the stone with me and was unable to set it down until I had placed it in its proper place. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Return to your garment and take it"," and do not walk about naked.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Yaḥyā al-Umawī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 341.]"""
"3213","(3213) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh and Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated from Bahz ibn Ḥakīm from his father from his grandfather, who said: \O Prophet of Allah"," our private parts—from whom should we conceal them and from whom should we leave them uncovered?\"" He (ﷺ) said: \""Guard your private parts except from your wife or what your right hand possesses (your female slave).\"" I said: \""What if the people are among one another?\"" He said: \""If you can ensure that no one sees it"," then let no one see it.\"" I said: \""What if one of us is alone?\"" He said: \""Allah has more right that one should feel shy before Him than before people.\"" Al-Bukhārī made reference to this ḥadīth in his chapter heading. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4017.]"""
"3214","(3214) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said regarding the verse: \And let them not display their adornment except that which appears thereof\"" [al-Nūr: 31]: He said: \""That which is in the palm and the face.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 17018.]"""
"3215","(3215) Abū ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us; Muslim al-Malāʾī narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His statement: \And let them not display their adornment\"" [al-Nūr: 31]—the verse—he said: \""Kohl and a ring.\"" [Ḥasan through other chains. Narrated by al-Ṭabarī"," 9/302.]"""
"3216","(3216) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; Rūḥ narrated to us; Ḥātim—who is Ibn Abī Ṣaghīrah—informed us; Khuṣayf narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His statement: \And let them not display their adornment except that which appears thereof\"" [al-Nūr: 31]. He said: \""Kohl and a ring.\"" And we have narrated something similar from Anas ibn Mālik. [Ḥasan through other chains. See the preceding ḥadīth.]"""
"3217","(3217) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn informed us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us: ʿUqbah al-Aṣamm narrated from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabaḥ from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: \What is apparent from her is the face and the two hands.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿUmar that he said: \""The apparent adornment is the face and the two hands.\"" And the same meaning has been narrated to us from ʬāʾ ibn Abī Rabaḥ and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," and this is the view of al-Awzāʿī. [Weak]"""
"3218","(3218) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Kaʿb al-Anṭākī and Muʾammal ibn al-Faḍl al-Ḥarrānī both said: al-Walīd — meaning Ibn Muslim — informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn ʿAbdūs informed us: Mūsā ibn Ayyūb al-Naṣībī informed us: al-Walīd narrated from Saʿīd ibn Bashīr from Qatādah from Khālid ibn Durayk from ʿĀʾishah that Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) wearing thin Syrian garments, so he turned away from her and then said: \What is this"," O Asmāʾ? When a woman reaches the age of menstruation"," nothing should be seen from her except this and this.\"" And he pointed to his face and his two hands.\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Mālinī.\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: This is a mursal ḥadīth"," for Khālid ibn Durayk did not meet ʿĀʾishah.\n\nThe Shaykh said: Despite this being mursal"," it is supported by the statements of the Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) who have passed regarding the explanation of what Allah has permitted of apparent adornment. Thus the position becomes strengthened by it. And with Allah lies success. [Denounced (munkar). Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4101]"""
"3219","(3219) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maymūn informed us: al-Walīd informed us: al-Awzāʿī narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \When one of you gives his slave woman or his hired servant in marriage to his male servant"," let him not look at her private parts.\"" He said: \""At her private parts.\"" [Good (ḥasan). Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4113]"""
"3220","(3220) And Abū ʿAlī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb informed us: Wakīʿ informed us: Dāwūd ibn Sawwār al-Muzanī narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: \When one of you gives his servant girl in marriage to his male servant or his hired servant"," let her not look at what is below the navel and above the knee.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd said: The correct form is Sawwār ibn Dāwūd.\n\nThe Shaykh said: When this narration is compared with the narration of al-Awzāʿī"," it indicates that the meaning of the ḥadīth is the prohibition upon the master from looking at her private parts when he has given her in marriage"," and that the private parts of a slave woman are what is between the navel and the knee.\n\nThe other routes of this ḥadīth indicate — and some of them explicitly state — that the intended meaning is the prohibition upon the slave woman from looking at the private parts of the master after she has been given in marriage"," and the prohibition upon the male servant or the hired servant from looking at the private parts of the master after the marriage has taken place. Thus the report pertains to clarifying the extent of the private parts of a man"," not the extent of the private parts of a slave woman. We shall mention the evidences for this in the following chapter"," if Allah the Most High wills. [Good (ḥasan). Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4114]"""
"3221","(3221) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd informed us: Abū Usāmah narrated from al-Walīd — meaning Ibn Kathīr — from Nāfiʿ that Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd narrated to him, saying: A woman came out wrapped in a veil and covered in a jilbāb. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Who is this woman?\"" It was said to her: \""She is the slave girl of so-and-so"," a man from his tribe.\"" So he sent to Ḥafṣah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said: \""What compelled you to veil this slave woman and cover her in a jilbāb and make her resemble the free women"," to the point that I was about to seize her and punish her? I do not think she is anything but one of the free women. Do not make the slave women resemble the free women.\"" [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ). Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq as quoted in Naṣb al-Rāyah"," 1/241]"""
"3222","(3222) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ḥurfī in Baghdad informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Kūfī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Zayd ibn al-Ḥubbāb narrated from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, who said: Thumāmah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Anas narrated to me from his grandfather Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The slave women of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to serve us with their heads uncovered"," their breasts exposed.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: The reports from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) on this matter are authentic"," and they indicate that her head"," her neck"," and what becomes apparent from her during the course of her service are not considered private parts.\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb"," there is disagreement regarding its text; therefore"," it should not be relied upon regarding the private parts of a slave woman. However"," it may be used as evidence — along with other narrations that will come — regarding the private parts of a man. And with Allah lies success.\n\nSome of our companions have cited as evidence a ḥadīth that he narrated with its chain. [Good (jayyid). Al-Albānī mentioned it in al-Arwāʾ"," 6/204]"""
"3223","(3223) From ʿĪsā ibn Maymūn from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Whoever wishes to sell a slave girl or purchase her"," let him look at her entire body except her private parts. Her private parts are what is between the fastening of her waist wrapper and her knees.\""\n\nAbū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated it to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Fārisī in Ṣūr informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Madanī narrated from Muḥammad al-Taymī from ʿĪsā ibn Maymūn"," and he mentioned it. Abū Aḥmad (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He is Muḥammad ibn Nūḥ.\n\nThe Shaykh said: This is a chain of narration by which no proof can be established.\n\n(c) And ʿĪsā ibn Maymūn is weak (ḍaʿīf). It has also been narrated from Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar from Ṣāliḥ ibn Ḥassān from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb"," and he is also weak. [Denounced (munkar). Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Kabīr"," 10773]"""
"3224","(3224) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī narrated it to us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: ʿUmar ibn Sinān informed us: ʿAbbās al-Khallāl informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ṣāliḥ informed us: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar informed us: Ṣāliḥ ibn Ḥassān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \There is no harm in a man examining a slave girl when he wishes to purchase her"," looking at her except for her private parts. Her private parts are what is between her knees and the fastening of her waist wrapper.\"" [Denounced (munkar). It has been mentioned in the preceding ḥadīth]"""
"3225","(3225) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Shīrāzī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Maymūnī informed us: Rūḥ informed us: Zakariyyā ibn Isḥāq informed me: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār said: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to carry stones with them for the Kaʿbah, wearing his lower garment. His uncle al-ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: \O son of my brother"," if you were to untie your lower garment and place it upon your shoulders beneath the stones.\"" He said: So he untied it and placed it upon his shoulders"," whereupon he fell unconscious. He said: After that day"," he was never seen naked. The wording of their ḥadīth is the same.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Maṭar ibn al-Faḍl"," and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb"," both from Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ). Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 357]"""
"3226","(3226) Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAmr, and he said in the ḥadīth: \He fell to the ground and his eyes gazed toward the sky"," then he stood up and said: 'My lower garment! My lower garment!' So he fastened his lower garment upon himself.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr said: Ibn Jurayj informed us"," and he mentioned its meaning.\n\nMuslim narrated it from Isḥāq"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Ibn Jurayj. [Authentic (ṣaḥīḥ). It has been mentioned in the preceding ḥadīth]"""
"3227","(3227) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Muhammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad narrated from 'Abdullah ibn Shaddad from Abu 'Udhrah from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade entering the public baths, then later permitted men to enter them while wearing a waist-wrapper (izar). [Weak. Narrated by Abu Dawud, 409.]"
"3228","(3228) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal informed us; al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us; Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us; Malik narrated from al-Nadr, the freedman of 'Umar ibn 'Ubayd Allah, from Zur'ah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jurhad from his father, that Jurhad, who was among the People of the Bench (Ahl al-Suffah), said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sat with us while my thigh was exposed"," and he said: 'Cover it. Do you not know that the thigh is part of the 'awrah (area of the body that must be concealed)?'\"" Its meaning was also narrated by al-Qa'nabi from Malik. [Weak. Narrated by Abu Dawud"," 4014.]"""
"3229","(3229) 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran informed us in Baghdad; Abu Muhammad Da'layj ibn Ahmad ibn Da'layj informed us; Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Tha'labah ibn Suwa' narrated to us; my uncle narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jurhad from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by him while he was exposing his thigh, and he said: 'Cover it, for it is part of the 'awrah.' [Weak. Referred to in the preceding hadith.]"
"3230","(3230) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan informed us in Baghdad; 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to me; Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir said: al-'Ala' ibn 'Abd al-Rahman informed me; Abu Kathir, the freedman of Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Jahsh, informed me from his freedman Muhammad, who said: \I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when he passed by Ma'mar"," who was sitting near his house in the market with both his thighs uncovered. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'O Ma'mar"," cover your thighs"," for the thighs are part of the 'awrah.'\"" Isma'il ibn Ja'far also narrated it from al-'. [Weak. Narrated by Ahmad"," 5/290.]"""
"3231","(3231) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Bakr al-Marwazi narrated to us in Bayt al-Maqdis while residing in Ramla; Muhammad ibn Sabiq al-Kufi narrated to us; Isra'il narrated from Abu Yahya from Mujahid from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The thigh is part of the 'awrah.\"" Al-Bukhari mentioned in the translation the hadith of Ibn 'Abbas"," Jurhad"," and Muhammad ibn Jahsh without a chain. The Sheikh said: \""These are sound chains by which evidence may be established.\"" [Weak. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi"," 2796.]"""
"3232","(3232) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar al-Hafiz informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Bahlul narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Habib al-Shaylamani narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us; Sawwar Abu Hamzah narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Command your children to pray at seven years of age"," and strike them for it at ten"," and separate them in their beds. And when one of you marries his slave or his hired servant to his bondsman"," let him not look at what is between his navel and his knee"," for what is between the navel and the knee is part of his 'awrah.\"" [Hasan. Its grading was discussed earlier"," 3220.]"""
"3233","(3233) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Umar informed us; Muhammad ibn Makhlad informed us; Ahmad ibn Mansur Zajj informed us; al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us; Abu Hamzah al-Sayrafi, who is Sawwar ibn Dawud, narrated from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Command your children to pray at seven years of age"," and strike them for it at ten"," and separate them in their beds. And when one of you marries his bondsman to his slave woman or his hired servant"," let the bondsman not look at anything of his 'awrah"," for what is beneath the navel to his knee is part of the 'awrah.\"" It was also said that Sawwar narrated from Muhammad ibn Juhaadah from 'Amr"," but this is not correct. [Hasan. Referred to in the preceding hadith.]"""
"3234","(3234) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Isfara'ini informed us in Bukhara; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id al-Hafiz informed us; 'Isa ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa al-Marwazi narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn al-Jarrah al-Khwarizmi narrated to us; Mughirah ibn Musa narrated to us; Sawwar ibn Dawud narrated from Muhammad ibn Juhaadah from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Command your children to pray at seven years of age"," and strike them for it at ten"," and separate them in their beds. And when one of you marries his servant from among his slaves or his hired servants"," let him not look at anything of his 'awrah"," for everything below his navel to his knee is part of his 'awrah.\"" [Hasan li-ghayrihi. See hadith 3220.]"""
"3235","(3235) Abu Sa'id al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adi informed us; Isma'il ibn Dawud ibn Wardan al-Qazzaz narrated to us in Egypt; Zakariyya ibn Yahya, the scribe of al-'Umari, narrated to us; Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated from Yahya ibn Ayyub from al-Khalil ibn Murrah from al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib from his father from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Teach your children prayer at seven years of age"," and discipline them for it at ten"," and separate them in their beds. And when one of you marries his bondsman to his slave woman or his hired servant"," let him not look at his 'awrah"," for the 'awrah is what is between the navel and the knee.\"""""
"3236","(3236) Abu Sa'd al-Malini informed us, Abu Ahmad ibn Adiyy narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Dawud ibn Wardan al-Qazzaz narrated to us in Egypt, Zakariyya ibn Yahya, the scribe of al-'Umari, narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from al-Khalil ibn Murrah, from al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from 'Amr ibn Shu'aib, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Teach your children Salah at the age of seven years"," and discipline them regarding it at the age of ten years"," and separate them in their beds. And when one of you marries his female slave to his male servant or hired servant"," let him not look at her 'awrah"," and the 'awrah of a female slave is that which is between the navel and the knee.\"""""
"3237","(3237) Saʿīd ibn Rāshid al-Baṣrī — and he is weak — narrated from ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr from Zayd ibn Aslam from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār from Abū Ayyūb (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \Whatever is above the two knees is from the ʿawrah (nakedness)"," and whatever is below the navel is from the ʿawrah.\""\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq ibn Bahlūl narrated to us: my grandfather narrated to us: my father narrated to us from Saʿīd ibn Rāshid"," and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd what has preceded is sufficient"," and by Allah is the granting of success. [Weak. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī"," 1/231]"""
"3238","(3238) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn Mahdī al-Ḥāfiẓ in Baghdād informed us: al-Qāḍī al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl and ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Aḥmad ibn Naṣr both said: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) raided Khaybar. He said: We prayed the morning prayer there at the time of early dawn. Then the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) mounted, and Abū Ṭalḥah mounted, and I was riding behind Abū Ṭalḥah. The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) hastened his mount through the narrow alleys of Khaybar, and my knee was touching the thigh of the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ). Then he pulled up his lower garment from his thigh, until I could see the whiteness of the thigh of the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ). When he entered the village, he said: \Allāhu Akbar! Khaybar is ruined. Indeed"," when we descend upon the courtyard of a people"," evil is the morning of those who have been warned.\"" And he mentioned the hadith in its full length.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm with this wording.\n\nAnd Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah"," except that he said: \""And the lower garment slipped from the thigh of the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\nAnd Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated it from Ismāʿīl"," and he said in the hadith: \""And his thigh became exposed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 364]"""
"3239","(3239) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: my father narrated to us: Ismāʿīl narrated to us, and he mentioned it.\n\nAnd in his statement \it slipped\"" or \""it became exposed\"" is an indication that that was not by his (ﷺ) intention. A person's ʿawrah may become exposed by the wind"," a fall"," or other such causes"," and thus it would not be attributed to deliberate exposure.\n\nAnd his statement in the first narration: \""Then he pulled up his lower garment from his thigh\"" — it is possible that what is meant is that the narrowness of the alley in which he hastened his mount pulled his lower garment away from his thigh"," so the action would be attributed to the wall of the alley"," not to the Prophet (ﷺ). This would be in agreement with the narration of others from Ismāʿīl"," and in agreement with what has preceded from the hadiths stating that the thigh is ʿawrah"," without contradicting them. And by Allah is the granting of success.\n\nAnd Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated it from Anas"," and he said in one of the two narrations from him: \""And my knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)","\"" and he did not mention the exposure of the thigh."""
"3240","(3240) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr all said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Hishām ibn Mullās al-Numayrī al-Dimashqī narrated to us: Marwān, meaning ibn Muʿāwiyah, narrated to us: Ḥumayd narrated to us from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) reached Khaybar at night. When morning came, he mounted and the Muslims mounted with him. The people of Khaybar came out with their spades and baskets as they used to do every day. When they caught sight of the Prophet (ﷺ), they said: \Muhammad"," by Allah! Muhammad and the army!\"" Then they fled in retreat. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Khaybar is ruined! Indeed"," when we descend upon the courtyard of a people"," evil is the morning of those who have been warned.\"" Anas said: I was riding behind Abū Ṭalḥah that day"," and my knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). And in the other narration he said: \""And my foot was touching the foot of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3241","(3241) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ʿAbdūs ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī narrated to us: al-Anṣārī narrated to me: Ḥumayd narrated to us from Anas ibn Mālik, and he mentioned something similar to it.\n\nAbū Ḥātim said: I said to al-Anṣārī: \What does al-khamīs mean?\"" He said: \""The soldiers"," the army.\""\n\nAnd those who claim that the thigh is not ʿawrah cite as evidence something they narrate in that regard from the story of ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him). And what is established from the story of ʿUthmān in that regard is [as follows]. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3242","(3242) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥarmalah from ʿAṭāʾ and Sulaymān, the two sons of Yasār, and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was lying down in his house, having exposed his thighs or his shins. Abū Bakr sought permission, and he was given permission while he was in that state, and he conversed. Then ʿUmar sought permission, and he was given permission while he was likewise, and he conversed. Then ʿUthmān sought permission, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat up and adjusted his garments. Muḥammad said: \And I do not say that this was on a single day.\"" Then he conversed. When he left"," ʿĀʾishah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," Abū Bakr entered and you did not stir for him nor pay him any attention. Then ʿUmar entered and you did not stir for him nor pay him any attention. Then ʿUthmān entered and you sat up and adjusted your garments.\"" He said: \""Should I not feel modest before a man before whom the angels feel modest?\"" The wording is from the ḥadīth of Qutaybah.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā and Qutaybah and others with this wording: \""having exposed his thighs or his shins\"" — with the doubt (i.e."," the narrator was uncertain which word was used).\n\nAnd such a narration is not contradicted by a saḥīh"," explicit narration from the Prophet (ﷺ) commanding the covering of the thigh"," and the text stating that the thigh is ʿawrah. And Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī narrated it"," and he was the most precise of them (in memorization)"," and he did not mention anything of that in the story. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 2402]"""
"3243","(3243) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us: my father narrated to us from Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān, who said: Ibn Shihāb said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ informed me that Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ informed him that ʿUthmān and ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with them both) related that Abū Bakr sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was lying on his bed, wearing ʿĀʾishah's cloak. Permission was given to Abū Bakr while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in that state. He fulfilled his need and departed. Then ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission, and he was given permission while he was in that state. He fulfilled his need and departed. ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Then I sought permission from him"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat up and said to ʿĀʾishah: 'Gather your garments over yourself.'\"" He said: \""I fulfilled my need and departed.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I did not see you alarmed for Abū Bakr and ʿUmar as you were alarmed for ʿUthmān.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," ʿUthmān is a very modest man"," and I feared that if I gave him permission while I was in that state"," he would not convey his need to me.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAmr al-Nāqid and others from Yaʿqūb. And he narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿUqayl ibn Khālid from Ibn Shihāb"," and in it there is no mention of the thigh or the shin. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 2402]"""
"3244","(3244) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿUmar ibn Burhān, and others said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿArafah narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbadah narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abū Khālid informed me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Madanī, who said: Ḥafṣah ibn ʿUmar narrated to me, she said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was one day sitting, having placed his garment between his thighs. Abū Bakr came and sought permission, and he was given permission, while the Prophet (ﷺ) was in his state. Then ʿUmar, with a similar story. Then ʿAlī. Then some of his companions, while the Prophet (ﷺ) was in his state. Then ʿUthmān came and sought permission, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took his garment and covered himself with it. ʿĀʾishah said: \They conversed and then left.\"" She said: \""So I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," Abū Bakr"," ʿUmar"," ʿAlī"," and the rest of your companions came"," and you were in your state. But when ʿUthmān came"," you covered yourself with your garment.'\"" She said: He said: \""Should I not feel modest before a man before whom the angels feel modest?\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: And likewise Abū Yaʿfūr narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 6/288]"""
"3245","(3245) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāriq al-ʿAṭṭār both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Shaybān narrated to us from Abī Yaʿfūr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Madanī from Ḥafṣah ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me one day and had placed his garment between his thighs, and he mentioned its meaning.\n\nAnd what is most likely is that he (ﷺ) took the edge of his garment and placed it between his thighs, for nothing else is thought of him. And what would become exposed in most cases by that would be his knees, not his thighs.\n\nAnd the narration of Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī has made that explicit, I think, in another story. [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. And it was mentioned in the one before it.]"
"3246","(3246) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us in a mention he made from Ayyūb from Abī ʿUthmān from Abū Mūsā. Ḥammād said: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥakam and ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated to me that they both heard Abī ʿUthmān narrating to him from Abū Mūsā something similar to this, except that ʿĀṣim added in it: \That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in a place in which there was water"," and he had exposed his knees. When ʿUthmān approached"," he covered them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb.\n\nAnd this is no proof for those who hold the view that the thigh is not ʿawrah. And his exposing them before the entry of ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) only indicates that the two knees are not ʿawrah. And likewise the ḥadīth of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb and ʿAlī indicates that the navel is not ʿawrah. Rather"," the ʿawrah of the man is what is between the two (i.e."," between the navel and the knees). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 2492]"""
"3247","(3247) Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Faqih al-Rawzdbari informed us; Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih informed us; 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi informed us; Abu Salamah informed us; Hammad ibn Salamah informed us; Ibn 'Awn narrated from Muhammad — that is, Ibn Sirin — that Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said to al-Hasan: \Raise your shirt from your belly so that I may kiss where I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing.\"" So he raised his shirt"," and he kissed his navel.\n\nThus Hammad narrated it"," while others narrated from Hammad and from Ibn 'Awn"," from Abu Muhammad"," who is 'Umair ibn Ishaq.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad 2/427]"""
"3248","(3248) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us; Abu 'Amr ibn Matar informed us; Ibrahim ibn 'Ali narrated; Yahya ibn Yahya informed us; Azhar al-Samman narrated from Ibn 'Awn, from 'Umair ibn Ishaq, who said: \I was with al-Hasan when Abu Hurayrah met him and said: 'Show me"," so that I may kiss you where I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissing.' He indicated with his lips"," and he placed his mouth upon his navel.\""\n\n[Qawi (strong). A similar narration has preceded via another route.]"""
"3249","(3249) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated; Bahr ibn Nasr narrated; Ibn Wahb narrated; Anas ibn 'Iyad narrated from Muhammad ibn Abi Yahya al-Aslami, from Abu al-'Ala', the freedman of the Aslamites, who said: \I saw 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," wearing his waist-wrapper above the navel.\""\n\nThis does not contradict the statement of those who claimed that the navel is not part of the 'awrah"," because the one who made that claim tied the waist-wrapper above the navel in order to encompass the entire 'awrah with covering. And success is through Allah.\n\n[Da'if. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah 4852]"""
"3250","(3250) Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya and Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated; Bahr ibn Nasr narrated; it was recited to Ibn Wahb: \Malik"," Ibn Abi Dhi'b"," Hisham ibn Sa'd"," and others informed you that Muhammad ibn al-Qurashi narrated to them from his mother"," that she asked Umm Salamah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: 'What garments may a woman pray in?' She said: 'In a head-cover (khimar) and a full-length chemise (dir') that conceals the tops of her feet.'\""\n\nSimilarly"," Bakr ibn Mudar"," Hafs ibn Ghiyath"," Isma'il ibn Ja'far"," and Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated it from Muhammad ibn Zayd"," from his mother"," from Umm Salamah"," as a mawquf narration.\n\nAnd 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated it from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar"," from Muhammad ibn Zayd"," as a marfu' narration.\n\n[Da'if. Narrated by Malik 324"," Abu Dawud 639]"""
"3251","(3251) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz, Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, and Abu Sadiq Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-'Attar informed us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated; al-'Abbas Muhammad al-Duri narrated; 'Uthman ibn 'Umar informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that she asked the Prophet ﷺ: \Can a woman pray in a chemise and a head-cover without a waist-wrapper?\"" He said: \""If the chemise is full-length and covers the tops of her feet.\""\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by Abu Dawud 640"," al-Daraqutni 2/62]"""
"3252","(3252) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated; Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated; Sulayman —\n\n(And) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever drags his garment out of arrogance"," Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Umm Salamah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," then what about women?\"" He said: \""A hand's breadth (shibr).\"" She said: \""Then their shins will become exposed\"" — or she said"," \""their feet.\"" He said: \""Then a forearm's length (dhirā')"," and they should not exceed that.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Ahmad 2/5]"""
"3253","(3253) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad narrated; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated; Yazid ibn Harun informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubayd, from Umm Salamah, from the Prophet ﷺ: \The hem of a woman's garment is a hand's breadth.\"" I said: \""Then her feet will become exposed.\"" He said: \""Then a forearm's length"," and they should not exceed that.\""\n\nIn this is evidence for the obligation of covering her feet.\n\n[Sahih through other chains. Narrated by al-Darimi 2644]"""
"3254","(3254) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Umar al-Hamami in Baghdad informed us; Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated; 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad narrated; Abu al-Walid narrated; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated —\n\n(And) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated; 'Ali ibn Hamshadh al-'Adl narrated; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated; Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated; Hammad narrated from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Safiyyah bint al-Harith, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he said: \The prayer of a woman who has reached puberty is not accepted without a head-cover (khimar).\"" This is the wording of Hajjaj's narration.\n\nAnd Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated it from Qatadah"," from al-Hasan"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by Abu Dawud 641]"""
"3255","(3255) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ya'qub narrated; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Sa'id narrated from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The prayer of a woman who has reached puberty is not accepted without a head-cover (khimar).\""\n\n[Sahih through other chains. Preceded in the narration before it.]"""
"3256","(3256) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Faddal al-Qattan in Baghdad informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh narrated; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated; Ibn Bukayr narrated; 'Abd Allah ibn Lahia' narrated to me; Bukayr narrated from Bishr ibn Sa'id, from 'Ubayd Allah al-Khawlani — and he had been an orphan under the care of Maymunah — who said: \I saw Maymunah praying in a full-length chemise and a head-cover"," with no waist-wrapper upon her.\""\n\n[Sahih. Narrated by al-Harith 139; Zawa'id al-Haythami]"""
"3257","(3257) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from al-Thiqah, from Bukayr ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Ashajj, and he mentioned it similarly.\n\nHe said: And she used to pray in a dirʿ (shift) and a khimār (head-covering), with no izār (lower garment) upon her.\n\nHe said: And Mālik narrated to us that it reached him from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she used to pray in a dirʿ and a khimār.\n\n[Weak. Reported by Mālik, 323.]\n\n---"
"3258","(3258) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ, Sulaymān ibn Dāwūd al-Mahrī, Ibn al-Sarḥ, and Aḥmad ibn Saʿīd al-Hamdānī said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Qurrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Maʿāfirī informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \May Allah have mercy on the first women of the Muhājirāt. When Allah"," the Most High"," revealed: {And let them draw their head-coverings over their bosoms} [al-Nūr: 31]"," they tore — Ibn Ṣāliḥ said: they doubled — their wrappings and covered themselves with them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī reported it from the ḥadīth of Yūnus ibn Yazīd from Ibn Shihāb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by al-Bukhārī"," 4481.]\n\n---"""
"3259","(3259) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Zāhid in Baghdād narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar ibn al-Zibriqān narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us. He said: I heard al-Ḥasan ibn Muslim narrating from Ṣafiyyah ibn Shaybah, from ʿĀʾishah, Umm al-Muʾminīn, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \When this verse was revealed: {And let them draw their head-coverings over their bosoms} [al-Nūr: 31]"," the women of the Anṣār took their lower garments and tore them from the edges"," and covered themselves with them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym from Ibrāhīm ibn Nāfiʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Muslim"," 2128.]\n\n---"""
"3260","(3260) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī, Tamīm ibn Muḥammad, and al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān said: ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated from Suhayl, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Two types of people from the inhabitants of the Fire I have not yet seen: people with whips like the tails of cattle"," with which they strike the people; and women who are clothed yet naked"," inclined and inclining others"," their heads like the humps of leaning camels. They will not enter Paradise"," nor will they find its fragrance"," though its fragrance can be found from such and such a distance.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Jarīr. [Ḥasan for other than it. Reported by Abū Dāwūd"," 4116.]\n\n---"""
"3261","(3261) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Jubayr narrated to me that ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib narrated to him from Khālid ibn Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah, from Ḥumayd ibn Khalīfah who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Heraclius. When I returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a Coptic garment and said: \Make one half of it into a shirt"," and give the other half to her companion (i.e."," your wife) to use as a khimār (head-covering).\"" When I turned to leave"," he called me back and said: \""Tell her to place something underneath it"," so that it does not reveal (the shape of the body).\""\n\nSome of them said: ʿAbbās ibn ʿUbaydullāh. Al-Bukhārī said: Those who said Ibn ʿUbaydullāh are more numerous"," and among those who said ʿUbaydullāh are Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and Ibn Jurayj.\n\nThe Shaykh said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Lahīʿah narrated it from Mūsā ibn Jubayr that ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbbās narrated to him. [Ḥasan for other than it. See the one before it.]\n\n---"""
"3262","(3262) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿUqayl, from Muḥammad ibn Usāmah ibn Zayd, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me a thick Coptic garment that Ḥumayd al-Kalbī had presented to him. I gave it to my wife to wear. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \What is the matter with you? Why do you not wear the Coptic garment?\"" I said: \""I gave it to my wife.\"" He said: \""Tell her to wear an undergarment beneath it"," for I fear it may reveal her bones.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. Reported by another chain by Ibn Abī Shaybah"," 24792.]\n\n---"""
"3263","(3263) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to me from Muslim ibn Abī Maryam and Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Salamah, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, clothed the people with Coptic garments, then said: \Let your women not wear them as shifts (durūʿ).\"" A man said: \""O Amīr al-Muʾminīn"," I have already given it to my wife"," and she has been walking back and forth in the house"," and I have not seen anything transparent in it.\"" ʿUmar said: \""If it is not transparent"," then it is revealing (the shape).\""\n\nMuslim al-Baṭīn also narrated it from Abī Ṣāliḥ from ʿUmar.\n\nAnd for the meaning of this mursal narration there is a witness with a connected isnād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Reported by Ibn Manīʿ as in Kanz al-ʿUmmāl"," 21713.]\n\n(3264) Abū Manṣūr ʿAbd al-Qāhir ibn Ṭāhir"," the Faqīh"," informed us from his original book"," and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah"," and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥamdān al-Fārisī"," and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ṣaffār said: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us"," Abū Muslim narrated to us"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us"," Sulaymān"," meaning al-Taymī"," narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," from Abū Hurayrah"," from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who said: \""A woman may pray in three garments: a dirʿ (shift)"," a khimār (head-covering)"," and an izār (lower garment).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Umm Salamah that she prayed in a dirʿ and a khimār"," then said: \""Bring me the milḥafah (covering sheet).\""\n\nAnd from ʿĀʾishah something similar.\n\nAnd from ʿĀʾishah: She was asked about the khimār and said: \""The khimār is only that which conceals the skin and the hair.\""\n\n[Weak. Reported by Mālik"," 1625.]\n\n---"""
"3264","(3263) ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Salamah narrated that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, clothed the people with Coptic garments, then said: \Let your women not wear them as shifts.\"" A man said: \""O Amīr al-Muʾminīn"," I have given it to my wife"," and she has been walking back and forth in the house"," and I have not seen anything transparent in it.\"" ʿUmar said: \""If it is not transparent"," then it is revealing (the shape).\""\n\n(3264) Abū Manṣūr ʿAbd al-Qāhir ibn Ṭāhir"," the Faqīh"," informed us from his original book"," and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah"," and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAlī ibn Ḥamdān al-Fārisī"," and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ṣaffār said: Abū ʿAmr Ismāʿīl ibn Nujayd al-Sulamī informed us"," Abū Muslim narrated to us"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Anṣārī narrated to us"," Sulaymān"," meaning al-Taymī"," narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn"," from Abū Hurayrah"," from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who said: \""A woman may pray in three garments: a dirʿ (shift)"," a khimār (head-covering)"," and an izār (lower garment).\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Umm Salamah that she prayed in a dirʿ and a khimār"," then said: \""Bring me the milḥafah (covering sheet).\""\n\nAnd from ʿĀʾishah something similar.\n\nAnd from ʿĀʾishah: She was asked about the khimār and said: \""The khimār is only that which conceals the skin and the hair.\""\n\n[Weak. Reported by Mālik"," 1625.]\n\n---"""
"3265","(3265) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from ʿAlqamah ibn Abī ʿAlqamah, from his mother, who said: Ḥafṣah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān came to ʿĀʾishah, Umm al-Muʾminīn, and Ḥafṣah was wearing a thin khimār. ʿĿʾishah tore it and clothed her with a thick khimār.\n\n[Weak. Reported by Abū ʿUbayd in Gharīb al-Ḥadīth, 4/312.]\n\n---"
"3266","(3266) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us from Abī ʿUbayd, in the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah: That she used to tighten a waist-wrapper beneath the dirʿ during prayer.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Ḥajjāj narrated it from Ḥammād ibn Salamah from Umm Shabīb from ʿĀʾishah.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: Al-iḥtibāk is the fastening and securing of the izār (lower garment).\n\nMeaning: She would not pray except while wearing an izār (lower garment) fastened at the waist. [Ḥasan for other than it. Reported by Abū ʿUbayd in Gharīb al-Ḥadīth, 4/333.]"
"3267","(3267) And with this chain of narration from Abū ʿUbayd, in the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾishah: she disliked that a woman should pray without any adornment, even if she were to hang a thread around her neck.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: al-Fazārī narrated it to me from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yasār from ʿĀʾishah bint Ṭalḥah from ʿĀʾishah, that.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: His statement \ʿuṭulan\"" means one who has no jewellery upon her.\n\nAnd it is established from ʿĀʾishah regarding some of the believing women that they used to attend the prayer wrapped in their outer garments.\n\n[Authenticated. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 365.]"""
"3268","(3268) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed me — as I read to him — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb informed us from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would perform the Fajr prayer"," and women from among the believers would attend it with him"," wrapped in their outer garments. Then they would return to their homes and no one from among the people would recognize them.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Authenticated. Narrated by al-Ṭaḥāwī in Sharh al-Maʿānī"," 1/377. al-Bukhārī with another chain"," 365.]"""
"3269","(3269) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Muḥammad ibn Jabalah Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Simnānī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar informed us; both said: ʿUbaydullāh ibn Muʿādh informed us; my father informed us; Shuʿbah informed us from Tawbah al-ʿAnbarī, who heard Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\When one of you prays"," let him wrap a waist-cloth (izār) and wear a garment (ridāʾ).\""\n\n[Authenticated. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3270","(3270) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us; Ibn Abī Qumāsh informed us; Muthannā ibn Muʿādh informed us; my father informed us from Shuʿbah, and he mentioned it with its meaning and its chain of narration. [Authenticated. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Awsaṭ, 9368.]"
"3271","(3271) Abū al-ḿasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Madanī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Musayyibī informed us; Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ informed us from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah from Nāfiʿ from ʿAbdullāh — and Nāfiʿ is not seen as narrating except from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — who said:\n\n\When one of you prays"," let him wear his two garments"," for Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," is more deserving that one should adorn oneself for Him. If he does not have two garments"," then let him wrap a waist-cloth when he prays"," and let none of you wrap himself in his prayer as the Jews wrap themselves.\""\n\n[Authenticated through other chains. Narrated by Ibn Khuzaymah"," 766.]"""
"3272","(3272) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī informed us; Saʿid ibn ʿĀmir al-Ḍubaʿī informed us from Saʿid from Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ, who said:\n\nIbn ʿUmar saw me while I was praying in a single garment. He said: \Did I not clothe you?\"" I said: \""Yes"," indeed.\"" He said: \""If I had sent you on an errand"," would you go out like this?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then Allah is more deserving that one should adorn oneself for Him.\"" Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""When one of you prays in a single garment"," let him fasten it at his waist"," and do not wrap yourselves as the Jews wrap themselves.\""\n\n[Authenticated. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3273","(3273) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us from Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ, who said:\n\nI was held back one day attending to the feeding of the mounts. Ibn ʿUmar came upon me while I was praying in a single garment. He said to me: \Were you not given two garments?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Tell me"," if I were to send you to some of the people of Madīnah"," would you go in a single garment?\"" I said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Then Allah is more deserving that one should adorn oneself for Him"," or the people?\"" Then he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ — or ʿUmar — said: \""Whoever has two garments"," let him pray in them both"," and whoever has only one garment"," let him wrap it as a waist-cloth"," and do not wrap yourselves as the Jews wrap themselves.\""\n\n[Authenticated. It has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3274","(3274) Abū al-Ḥasan informed us; al-Ḥasan informed us; Yūsuf informed us; Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us; Ayyūb informed us from Nāfiʿ, who said:\n\nI was held back for him attending to the feeding of the mounts. And he mentioned the ḥadīth, and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ — or ʿUmar — said, and I think he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let one of you pray in two garments. If he finds only one garment"," let him wrap it as a waist-cloth"," and do not wrap yourselves as the Jews wrap themselves.\""\n\nAnd al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated it from Nāfiʿ thus"," with the doubt. [Authenticated. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 358.]"""
"3275","(3275) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī informed us; Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us from Ayyūb from Muḥammad — that is, Ibn Sīrīn — from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nA man stood before the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about praying in a single garment. He said: \Do all of you find two garments?\"" Then a man stood before ʿUmar and asked him about praying in a single garment. He said: \""When Allah grants abundance"," then be generous. A man should gather his garments upon himself. A man may pray in a waist-cloth and a cloak; in a waist-cloth and a shirt; in a waist-cloth and a long coat; in trousers and a cloak; in trousers and a shirt; in trousers and a long coat; in underpants and a long coat; in underpants and a shirt; and I think he said: in underpants and a cloak.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. [Weak. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 636.]"""
"3276","(3276) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Mukharramī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Muḥammad al-Jurmī informed us; Abū Tumaylah Yaḥyā ibn Wāḍiḥ informed us; Abū al-Munīb informed us from ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah from his father, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to pray in a blanket without draping it over his shoulders, and he forbade a man to pray in trousers without having a cloak upon him.\n\n[Authenticated. Narrated by al-Bukhārī, 351.]"
"3277","(3277) Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us: Abū Sahl Ziyād ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslama ibn Qaʿnab narrated to us, from Mālik ibn Anas.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ṣaffār informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us, he said: I read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah: that a questioner asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying in a single garment, and he said: \Do each of you have two garments?\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," from Mālik; and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. This is the wording of Aḥmad (2/238)]"""
"3278","(3278) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī in al-Ahwāz informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī informed us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us: Layth ibn Saʿd informed us, from ʿUqayl, from Ibn Shihāb, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard a man asking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Should one of us pray in a single garment?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do each of you have two garments?\"" Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," used to say: I would leave my cloak on the hook and pray wrapped in a single garment.\n\nMuslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of Layth ibn Saʿd"," without mentioning the action of Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him. And Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn also narrated it from Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī extracted it (345)]"""
"3279","(3279) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Mawālī informed us, from Ibn al-Munkadir, that he said: We entered upon Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh while he was standing, praying in a single garment wrapped in it. When he turned [from prayer], we said: \O ʿAbd Allāh"," do you pray in a single garment wrapped in it while your cloak is laid aside?\"" He said: \""Yes. I would like one such as you"," who is ignorant"," to see me. Indeed"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray like this.\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from Ibn Abī al-Mawālī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim extracted it (518)]"""
"3280","(3280) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr said: It was read to Ibn Wahb: Usāmah ibn Zayd al-Laythī and ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed you, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh: that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in a single garment, placing its two ends crossed upon his shoulders, while his cloak was on the hook.\n\nMuslim extracted it from Ḥarmalah, from Ibn Wahb, from ʿAmr, with the same meaning.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim extracted it (284)]"
"3281","(3281) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Bakhtarī informed us: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad informed us: Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd informed us: al-Aʿmash informed us, from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir, who said: Abū Saʿīd narrated to me, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying in a single garment, wrapped in it.\n\nMuslim extracted it from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī extracted it (348)]"
"3282","(3282) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Mahrūyah ibn ʿAbbās ibn Sinān al-Rāzī informed us: Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām informed us, from his father, from ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah: that the Prophet ﷺ prayed in a single garment, having placed its two ends crossed upon his shoulders.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned in the one before it]"
"3283","(3283) Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓufur ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAlawī in Biyhaq informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah informed us: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā both said: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed us, from his father, from ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a single garment, placing its two ends upon his shoulders. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā; and Muslim extracted it through various routes from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned in the one before it]"
"3284","(3284) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Abū Usāmah informed us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah informed us, from his father, from ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in the house of Umm Salamah in a single garment, wrapped in it. Both [al-Bukhārī and Muslim] extracted it from the ḥadīth of Abī Usāmah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Ibn Abī Shaybah extracted it (3188)]"
"3285","(3285) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm al-Wāsiṭī informed us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Dāwūd informed us, from Abī Naḍrah, from Abī Saʿīd, who said: Ubayy ibn Kaʿb and Ibn Masʿūd disagreed regarding praying in a single garment. Ubayy said: \A single garment.\"" And Ibn Masʿūd said: \""Two garments.\"" ʿUmar passed by them and rebuked them both"," saying: \""It displeases me that two of the Companions of Muḥammad ﷺ should disagree over a single matter"," such that the people would issue rulings according to whichever of your two fatwās [they follow].\"" Regarding Ibn Masʿūd"," [no action was taken]; and the correct position is what Ubayy said.\n\nAnd Abū Masʿūd al-Jarīrī narrated it from Abī Naḍrah"," without mentioning ʿUmar"," and he said: Ibn Masʿūd said: \""That was only when garments were scarce. But when Allah has expanded [one's means]"," then praying in two garments is more complete.\""\n\nThis and the one before it both indicate that what ʿUmar and Ibn Masʿūd enjoined regarding praying in two garments is a matter of recommendation (istiḥbāb)"," not obligation (ījāb).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim extracted it (516). al-Nasāʾī (769)]"""
"3286","(3286) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in his later works: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us: My grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Sufyān informed us, from Abī al-Zinād, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let none of you pray in a single garment when there is nothing of it upon his shoulders.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Sufyān.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. al-Bukhārī extracted it (353)]"""
"3287","(3287) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Aḥmad b. Maḥbūb in Marw informed us; Saʿīd b. Masʿʿūd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh b. Mūsá narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan b. ʿAbdān informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad b. Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī narrated to us; Jaʿfar b. Muḥammad narrated to us; Ādam narrated to us; both saying: Shaybān narrated to us from Yaḥyá b. Abī Kathīr from ʿIkrimah, who said: I heard Abū Hurayrah — may Allāh be pleased with him — testify that he heard the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ say: \Whoever prays in a single garment"," let him drape its two ends over his shoulders.\""\n\nʿUbayd Allāh added in his narration: \""over his two shoulders.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym from Shaybān"," using the wording of the ḥadīth of Ādam b. Abī Iyās.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 354.]"""
"3288","(3288) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad b. al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; Yūnus b. Muḥammad narrated to us; Fulayḥ b. Sulaymān narrated to us from Saʿīd b. al-Ḥārith: that he came to Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh along with a group of people whom he named. He said: When we entered upon him, we found him praying in a single garment wrapped around him, while his cloak was near him — had he reached for it, he would have been able to take it. He said: When he completed the prayer, we asked him about praying in a single garment. He said: \I do this so that the foolish among you may see me and thus spread from Jābir a concession that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ granted. I went out with the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ on one of his journeys. I came to him one night for a personal matter and found him praying"," while I was wearing a single garment. I wrapped myself in it and prayed beside him. When he finished"," he said: 'What brings you at night"," O Jābir?' I informed him of my need. He said: 'O Jābir"," what is this wrapping that I saw?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," it was a single"," narrow garment.' He said: 'When you pray and you have a single garment"," if it is wide"," wrap yourself in it; and if it is narrow"," tie it around your waist as an izār.'\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: In my book it is Saʿīd b. Sulaymān b. al-Ḥārith"," in the handwriting of al-Shīrāzī"," but the correct version is Saʿīd b. al-Ḥārith.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyá b. Ṣāliḥ from Fulayḥ from Saʿīd b. al-Ḥārith.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 3006.]"""
"3289","(3289) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥusayn Aḥmad b. ʿUthmān b. Yaḥyá al-Adamī in Baghdād narrated to us; Aḥmad b. Ziyād b. Mihrān al-Simsār narrated to us; Hārūn b. Maʿrūf narrated to us; Ḥātim b. Ismāʿīl narrated to us from Yaʿqūb b. Mujāhid Abī Ḥazrah from ʿUbādah b. al-Walīd b. ʿUbādah b. al-Ṣāmit, who said: We came to Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh in his mosque and he was praying in a single garment, wrapped in it. I stepped over the people until I sat between him and the qiblah. I said: \May Allāh have mercy on you — do you pray in a single garment while your izār is beside you?\"" He said: \""I wanted a fool like you to come to me and see how I act"," so that he may do the same.\"" Then he narrated a long ḥadīth in which he said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ stood to pray"," and I had a striped cloak. I tried to drape its two ends over my neck"," but they did not reach. It had fringes"," so I folded it up"," then I crossed its two ends over each other"," then I bent it over my neck to hold it in place. I came and stood to the left of the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ. He took my hand and turned me until he placed me to his right. Then Ibn Ṣakhr came and stood to his left. He took both of us by his hands and pushed us back until he placed us behind him. The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ kept glancing at me while I was unaware. Then I became aware of it"," and he gestured to me — meaning: fasten your waist-wrapper. When the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ finished"," he said: \""O Jābir.\"" I said: \""Here I am"," O Messenger of Allāh.\"" He said: \""If the garment is wide"," drape its two ends over your shoulders; and if it is narrow"," fasten it around your waist.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn b. Maʿrūf and others.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥumaydī"," 313.]"""
"3290","(3290) Abū Zakariyyá b. Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ b. Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated to us from Abī Isḥāq from ʿAbd Allāh b. Shaddād from Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ used to pray in a cloak"," part of it upon me and part of it upon him"," while I was menstruating.\""\n\nSimilarly"," it is established from ʿĀʾishah — may Allāh be pleased with her.\n\nIn this is evidence of the permissibility of praying in a single garment even if none of it rests upon the person's shoulders.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 633.]"""
"3291","(3291) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad b. Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muḥammad b. Ḥātim b. Bazīʿ narrated to us; Yaḥyá b. Abī Bukayr narrated to us from Isrāʾīl from Abī Ḥawmal al-ʿĀmirī from Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Bakr from his father, who said: Jābir b. ʿAbd Allāh — may Allāh be pleased with them both — led us in prayer wearing a shirt with no cloak over it. When he finished, he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ praying in a shirt.\""\n\n[Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4026.]"""
"3292","(3292) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad b. Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqrīʾ informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad b. Yaʿqūb narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh b. Muḥammad b. Shākir narrated to us; Zayd al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Muʾmin b. Khālid narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh b. Buraydah narrated to us. He said: I heard Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, say: \There was no garment more beloved to the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ than the shirt (qamīṣ).\""\n\nIt has also been narrated from him — from ʿAbd Allāh b. Buraydah from his mother from Umm Salamah.\n\n[Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. And it has been mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3293","(3293) Abū Naṣr b. Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbdah informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad b. Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī narrated to us; Aḥmad b. Ḥanbal narrated to us; Abū Tumaylah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Muʾmin b. Khālid al-Sadūsī narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh b. Buraydah from his mother from Umm Salamah, who said: \There was no garment more beloved to the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ than the shirt (qamīṣ).\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd narrated it from Ziyād b. Ayyūb from Abū Tumaylah.\n\nIt has also been narrated from him — from ʿAbd Allāh b. Buraydah from his father from Umm Salamah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Mujāhid that he said: I said to Ibn ʿUmar: \""Which single garment is most beloved to you to pray in?\"" He said: \""The shirt (qamīṣ).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 622; al-Nasāʾī"," 765.]"""
"3294","(3294) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī b. Muḥammad al-Muqrīʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan b. Muḥammad b. Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf b. Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Muḥammad b. Abī Bakr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz b. Muḥammad al-Dārawardī narrated to us; Mūsá b. Ibrāhīm narrated to us from Salamah b. al-Akwaʿ, who said: I said: \O Messenger of Allāh"," I am a man who hunts — may I pray in a single shirt?\"" He said: \""Yes"," and fasten its buttons"," even with a thorn.\""\n\nAbū Uways narrated it from Mūsá b. Ibrāhīm b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Rabīʿah al-Makhzūmī from his father from Salamah.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Aḥmad"," 2/472; Abū Dāwūd"," 32369.]"""
"3295","(3295) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Maḥbūbī informed us; Saʿīd b. Masʿūd narrated to us; al-Naḍr b. Shumayl informed us; Shuʿbah narrated to us from Yazīd b. Khumayr, who said: I heard a client of Quraysh say: I heard Abū Hurayrah narrating to Muʿāwiyah that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ forbade a man from praying until he ties a waist-wrapper (ḥizām) around his waist.\n\nʿAbd Allāh b. al-Mubārak narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was narrated from Yaḥyá b. Abī Kathīr that the Prophet ﷺ forbade a man from praying in a shirt whose buttons were undone, out of fear that his ʿawrah might be exposed when he bows, until he fastens its buttons. Yaḥyá said: This is when he has no izār on him.\n\nAlthough this narration is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous), it agrees with the preceding connected narration.\n\n[Munkar. Narrated by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt, 4/175.]"
"3296","(3296) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Yaḥyá b. Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad b. Muḥammad b. Rajāʾ narrated to us; Ṣafwān b. Ṣāliḥ al-Dimashqī narrated to us; al-Walīd b. Muslim narrated to us; Zuhayr b. Muḥammad al-Tamīmī narrated to us; Zayd b. Aslam narrated to us, who said: I saw Ibn ʿUmar praying with his buttons undone. I asked him about that and he said: \I saw the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ do it.\""\n\nZuhayr b. Muḥammad is the only one who narrated this.\n\nAnd it has reached me from Abū ʿĪsá al-Tirmidhī that he said: I asked Muḥammad — meaning al-Bukhārī — about this ḥadīth of Zuhayr"," and he said: \""I am cautious about this shaykh; it is as though his ḥadīth is fabricated. This is not in my opinion from Zuhayr b. Muḥammad.\"" Aḥmad b. Ḥanbal used to weaken this shaykh and say: \""This is a shaykh whose name they appear to have altered.\"" Al-Bukhārī alluded to some of this in al-Tārīkh.\n\nThat has also been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar through other routes but without this chain of narration.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrihi. And it has another route at al-Bukhārī in al-Tārīkh"," 8/174"," and its chain is also weak.]"""
"3297","(3297) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan both narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Bahr ibn Nasser narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub informed me, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: I never saw 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar except with his lower garment unfastened.\n\nSa'id said: and Zurrah ibn Ma'bad al-Qurashi narrated to me, he said: I saw Ibn al-Musayyib, Abu Hazim, and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir praying with the lower garments of their shirts unfastened.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn 'Abbas the same as what was narrated to us from Ibn 'Umar himself.\n\nAnd it [the unfastened garment] during prayer is considered tolerable by us when the opening [of the garment] is narrow. And Allah knows best."
"3298","(3298) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Mulazim ibn 'Amr narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn 'Ali, who said: We went out as a delegation to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ until we came to him. We pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him. Then a man came and said: \O Prophet of Allah"," what do you think of praying in a single garment?\"" The Prophet of Allah ﷺ unfastened his lower garment and cast his upper garment over it"," wrapping himself with it"," and stood and prayed with us. When he had completed the prayer"," he said: \""Do you all possess two garments?\""\n\nAnd the hadiths that have been narrated to us regarding the Prophet's ﷺ praying in a single garment while wrapping himself therein"," the intended meaning thereby is the upper garment (rida') or that which resembles the upper garment. And Allah knows best."""
"3299","(3299) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, al-Sari ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Waqid ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: Jabir prayed in a lower garment which he had tied from the nape of his neck, while his clothes were hanging on a peg. Someone said to him: \Do you pray in a single garment?\"" He said: \""Did I not do this only so that a fool like you might see me? And who among us possessed two garments during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Yunus."""
"3300","(3300) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Lakhmi informed us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and al-Qadi Yusuf both said: Ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: They used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ while their lower garments were fastened around their necks due to their smallness. So it was said to the women: \Do not raise your heads until the men are fully seated.\"""""
"3301","(3301) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us, Abu 'Abdullah al-Shaybani informed us verbally, Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: I have seen men fastening their lower garments around their necks like children, due to the narrowness of their lower garments, behind the Prophet ﷺ. So someone said: \O assembly of women"," do not raise your heads until the men raise theirs.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Kathir"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah."""
"3302","(3302) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil al-'Asqalani narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muslim, the brother of al-Zuhri, from a freed slave of Asma' bint Abi Bakr, from Asma' bint Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \Whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day"," let her not raise her head until the men raise their heads\"" — lest they see the nakedness of the men."""
"3303","(3303) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-Abbas al-Qasim ibn al-Qasim al-Sayyari in Marw informed us, Abu al-Muwajjih Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Fazari informed us, Yusuf ibn 'Isa informed us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, from his father, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw seventy people of the People of the Bench, not a single man among them wearing an upper garment (rida') — whether a striped cloak (burdah) or a wrap (kisa') — which they had tied around their necks. Some of them reached halfway down the shin, and some reached the ankles, and he would gather it with his hand lest his nakedness become exposed.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Yusuf ibn 'Isa."
"3304","(3304) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar informed us, Abu Isma'il al-Tirmidhi informed us, Musa ibn Isma'il informed us, Aban ibn Yazid al-'Attar informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir informed us, from Abu Ja'far, from 'Ata' ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: While a man was praying with his lower garment hanging below [his ankles], the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Go and perform ablution.\"" So he went and performed ablution"," then came back. He [the Prophet ﷺ] said: \""Go and perform ablution.\"" So he went and performed ablution"," then came back. A man said to him: \""O Prophet of Allah"," why did you command him to perform ablution and then remain silent about him?\"" He said: \""He was praying while his lower garment was hanging below [his ankles]"," and indeed Allah"," the Almighty and Majestic"," does not accept the prayer of a man whose lower garment hangs below [his ankles].\""\n\nThus did Aban al-'Attar narrate it from Yahya.\n\nAnd Harb ibn Shaddad differed from him in its chain of narration"," narrating it similarly."""
"3305","(3305) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Hisham ibn 'Ali informed us, Ibn Raja' informed us, Harb narrated to us, from Yahya, who said: Ishaq ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah narrated to me that Abu Ja'far al-Madani narrated to him that 'Ata' ibn Yasar narrated to him that a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated to him, saying: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man began to pray. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Go and perform ablution.\"" He performed ablution"," then returned to praying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \""Go and perform ablution.\"" A man said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is the matter with you — you command him to perform ablution and then remain silent about him?\"" He said: \""I only commanded him to perform ablution because he was letting his lower garment hang below [his ankles]"," and Allah does not accept the prayer of a man who lets his lower garment hang below [his ankles].\""\n\nHisham ibn 'Abdullah al-Dastawa'i narrated it from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir"," from 'Ata' ibn Yasar"," that a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to him — so [the narrator] fell between Yahya and 'Ata'."""
"3306","(3306) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us, Yunus ibn Habib informed us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi informed us, Abu 'Awanah and Thabit — Abu Zayd — narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu 'Uthman, from Ibn Mas'ud. Abu 'Awanah raised it [to the Prophet] and Thabit did not raise it: that he saw a Bedouin wearing a cloak which he had let trail down while he was praying. He said: \Indeed"," the one who lets his garment trail out of pride in prayer is not from Allah in what is lawful or forbidden.\""\n\nAbu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us"," Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us"," Abu Dawud al-Sijistani said: A group narrated this from 'Asim"," stopping it at Ibn Mas'ud"," among them Hammad ibn Salamah"," Hammad ibn Zayd"," Abu al-Ahwash"," and Abu Mu'awiyah.\n\nThe Shaykh said: And in the firmly established hadiths concerning the prohibition of letting the lower garment trail"," there is evidence for its reprehensibility in prayer and otherwise."""
"3307","(3307) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Halim al-Marwazi informed us; Abu al-Muwajjih informed us; 'Abdan informed us; 'Abd Allah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid al-Saffar informed us; Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Mutawakkil, Abu al-Hasan al-Bazzar, narrated to us; Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated from al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan from Sulayman al-Ahwal from 'Ata' from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, prohibited *al-sadl* (letting garments hang loosely) during prayer, and that a man should cover his face. [Munkar. See the hadith before it.]"
"3308","(3308) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us, saying: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Salman ibn al-Hasan al-Faqih informed us by dictation; 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi narrated to us; Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us; Shu'bah and Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated from 'Isl ibn Sufyan from 'Ata' from Abu Hurayrah that he disliked *al-sadl* (letting garments hang loosely) and attributed that to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. [Munkar. See the hadith before it.]"
"3309","(3309) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab, i.e., ibn 'Ata', informed us; Sa'id, i.e., Ibn Abi 'Arubah, narrated from 'Isl from 'Ata' from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, prohibited *al-sadl* (letting garments hang loosely) during prayer. Al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan connected it from Sulayman from 'Ata', and from 'Isl from 'Ata'. And 'Amir al-Ahwal sent it as a mursal narration from 'Ata'. [Da'if]"
"3310","(3310) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed him; Abu al-Hasan al-Karizi informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us; Abu 'Ubayd narrated to us; Hushaym informed us; 'Amir al-Ahwal informed us, saying: I asked 'Ata' about *al-sadl* (letting garments hang loosely) and he disliked it. I said: \Is this from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him?\"" He said: \""Yes.\""\n\nAlthough this chain of narration is munqati' (disconnected)"," it strengthens the two connected narrations before it.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah that he prayed while letting his garment hang loosely (*saadil*).\n\nIt is as though he forgot the hadith"," or he interpreted it to mean that it is not permissible when done out of arrogance (*khuyala'*)"," and he himself did not do it out of arrogance. And Allah knows best.\n\nIt has also been narrated from the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," through other routes. [Munkar. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq.]"""
"3311","(3311) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Ali al-Sana'ani in Makkah narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-A'la ibn Ibrahim al-Bawsi in Sana'a narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Bishr ibn Rafi' narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu 'Ubaydah from Ibn Mas'ud that he disliked *al-sadl* (letting garments hang loosely) during prayer, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to dislike it.\n\nBishr ibn Rafi' is the sole narrator of this hadith, and he is not strong (in hadith).\n\nAnd Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from an unnamed man from Abu 'Atiyyah al-Wadi'i that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by a man who had let his garment hang loosely during prayer, so the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, took his garment and folded it over him. This narration is munqati' (disconnected). [Munkar. The discussion on it preceded in hadith 3307.]"
"3312","(3312) And Hafs ibn Abi Dawud — who is Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Qari' al-Kufi — narrated it from al-Haytham ibn Habib from 'Awn ibn Abi Juḥayfah from his father, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by a man praying who had let his garment hang loosely, so he folded it over him.\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us of it; Abu al-Husayn ibn Abi 'Amr al-Sammak narrated to me; Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi narrated to us; Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us; Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated it.\n\nHowever, Hafs is weak in hadith.\n\nAnd we recorded it from the hadith of Ibrahim ibn Tahman from al-Haytham; if it is preserved correctly, then it is better than the narration of Hafs al-Qari'. And 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, also disliked it, as reported. [Very Da'if. Narrated by al-Quti'i in \Al-Alf Dinar","\"" 121.]"""
"3313","(3313) Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami informed us; Abu al-Hasan al-Karizi informed us; 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated from Abu 'Ubayd; Hushaym informed us; Khalid al-Hadha' informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'id ibn Wahb narrated from his father from 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he went out and saw a people praying who had let their garments hang loosely, so he said: \It is as though they are Jews who have come out of their place of worship.\""\n\nAbu 'Ubayd said: \""It is their place of assembly where they gather.\"" He said: \""*Al-sadl* is when a man lets his garment hang without gathering its two sides together between his hands. If he gathers them"," then it is not *sadl*.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Ibn 'Umar"," in one of the two narrations from him"," that he disliked it. Mujahid and Ibrahim al-Nakha'i also disliked it. And it is narrated from Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah"," and then from al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin"," that they saw no harm in it.\n\nIt is as though they only permitted it for one who does it without arrogance (*makhilah*). As for one who does it out of arrogance (*batar*)"," then it is prohibited. And Imam al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," alluded to this meaning in the book of al-Buwayti.\n\nHe cited as evidence the text of the hadith which... [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq"," 1423.]"""
"3314","(3314) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Whoever lets his garment hang out of arrogance"," Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nAbu Bakr al-Siddiq"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," one side of my lower garment tends to loosen unless I take care of it.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""You are not — or: Indeed"," you are not — among those who do it out of arrogance.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ahmad ibn Yunus. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Bukhari"," 3465.]"""
"3315","(3315) And Abu al-Han al-Muqri' informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; 'Amr narrated from Tawus and Musa ibn 'Uqbah from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah from his father that when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, mentioned regarding the lower garment what he mentioned, Abu Bakr said: \O Messenger of Allah"," my lower garment falls from one side.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," you are not among them.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Ali ibn al-Madini from Sufyan from Musa ibn 'Uqbah.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn 'Umar"," and then from Salim ibn 'Abd Allah"," Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab"," al-Sha'bi"," 'Ikrimah"," and Ibrahim al-Nakha'i that they all disliked *al-talaththum* (covering the face) during prayer. And the narration of al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan explicitly states the prohibition of it. [Sahih. See the hadith before it.]"""
"3316","(3316) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Bahr ibn Nasr narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us; 'Umar ibn Muhammad informed me from 'Abd Allah ibn Waqid from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, while my lower garment was hanging loosely, and he said: \O 'Abd Allah"," raise your lower garment.\"" So I raised it. He said: \""More.\"" So I raised it more. I continued to be careful thereafter. Some of the people said: \""To where?\"" He said: \""To the middle of the shins.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu al-Tahir from Ibn Wahb. [Sahih. Narrated by Muslim"," 2086.]"""
"3317","(3317) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us; Sufyān narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yaʿqūb.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; Ibn Wahb informed us; Mālik ibn Anas and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed me, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, who said: I asked Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī about the izār (lower garment), and he said: \I shall inform you of what I heard directly. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The izār of the believer reaches to the middle of the shanks"," and there is no sin in what lies between that and the ankles. Whatever falls below that shall be in the Fire — whatever falls below that shall be in the Fire. Allah will not look"," on the Day of Resurrection"," at the one who trails his izār out of arrogance.'\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Mālik and ʿAbd Allāh. [Ḥasan. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4093.]"""
"3318","(3318) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Faqīh al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawyah al-ʿAskarī informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī informed us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās informed us. Both (chains) said: Shuʿbah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated to us, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whatever of the izār falls below the two ankles shall be in the Fire.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Ādam. In the narration of ʿAbd al-Ṣamad"," it is from the Prophet ﷺ"," who said: \""Whatever of the izār is beneath the two ankles shall be in the Fire.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 5450.]"""
"3319","(3319) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; Hannād informed us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us, from Abī al-Ṣabbāḥ, from Yazīd ibn Abī Sumayyah, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the izār applies equally to the qamīṣ (shirt).\"" [Jayyid. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 4095.]"""
"3320","(3320) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāriṣ al-ʿAṭṭār both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us; Muʿāwiyah ibn Hishām informed us — I think from Sufyān — from ʿAmr ibn Qays al-Mulāʾī, from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The garment of Adam and Ḥawwāʾ"," upon them both be peace"," was (like) the fingernail. When they ate of the tree"," nothing of it remained except the measure of a fingernail"," and so they began to cover themselves with leaves of Paradise\"" — he said: \""leaves of the fig tree.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ḥākim"," 2/350.]"""
"3321","(3321) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us; al-Ḥumaydī informed us; Sufyān informed us; al-Zuhrī informed us; Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib informed me, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: \When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his head from the rukūʿ of the last rakʿah of the Fajr prayer"," he said: 'O Allah"," grant safety to al-Walīd ibn al-Walīd"," Salamah ibn Hishām"," ʿAyyāsh ibn Abī Rabīʿah"," and the weak ones in Makkah. O Allah"," intensify Your grip upon Muḍar"," and make it upon them years like the years of Yūsuf.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 961.]\n\n(3322) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Daqīqī informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Sulaymān informed us"," from Abī Mijlaz"," from Anas ibn Mālik"," that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt in the Fajr prayer for a month"," invoking (curse) upon Riʿl and Dhakwān"," and he said: \""ʿUṣayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nBoth (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sulaymān al-Taymī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 307.]"""
"3322","(3322) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Daqīqī informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Sulaymān informed us, from Abī Mijlaz, from Anas ibn Mālik, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunūt in the Fajr prayer for a month, invoking (curse) upon Riʿl and Dhakwān, and he said: \ʿUṣayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nBoth (al-Bukhārī and Muslim) narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sulaymān al-Taymī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 307.]"""
"3323","(3323) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrah informed us; Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān informed us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr informed us. Both (chains) said: al-Layth narrated to us, from ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas, from Ḥanẓalah ibn ʿAlī, from Khufāf ibn Īmāʾ al-Ghifārī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said in the Ṣubḥ prayer: \O Allah"," curse Banū Liḥyān"," Riʿl"," and Dhakwān"," and ʿUṣayyah — they disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. And Ghifār — may Allah forgive them. And Aslam — may Allah grant them peace.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Layth ibn Saʿd."""
"3324","(3324) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr al-ʿIrāqī informed us; Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Dārabajirdī informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maʿqil, that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib, may Allah be pleased with him, performed qunūt in the Maghrib prayer, invoking (curse) upon certain people and upon their followers, and he performed the qunūt after the rukūʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq, 4976.]"
"3325","(3325) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad informed us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Muʿādh informed us; my father informed us; Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿUbayd ibn al-Ḥasan, who heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Maʿqil say: I witnessed ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, performing qunūt in the ʿAtamah prayer — or he said, the Maghrib prayer — after the rukūʿ, and he invoked (curse) in his qunūt upon five persons and named them. [Ṣaḥīḥ. This is a ṣaḥīḥ, connected chain, and it is similar to what preceded.]"
"3326","(3326) Abū Manṣūr al-Ẓafar ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAlawī informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mātī informed us in Kūfah; Ibn Abī Gharzah informed us; Qabīṣah informed us; Sufyān narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from Abī Iyās, from Abī al-Dardāʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I supplicate for thirty of my brothers while I am in prostration"," mentioning them by their names and the names of their fathers.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"," 1098.]"""
"3327","(3327) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — 'Ali ibn Hamshadh al-'Adl narrated to us — Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us — Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Hamid narrated to us — Sharik narrated from 'Imran ibn Zubyan — from Abu Tuhya, meaning Hakim ibn Sa'd, who said: A man from among the Ghulat (extremists) called out to 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was in the Fajr prayer, and he recited: **\And indeed"," it has been revealed to you and to those before you: if you associate partners with Allah"," your deeds will surely become void"," and you will be among the losers\""** [al-Zumar: 65]. So 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) responded to him while still in the prayer: **\""So be patient; indeed"," the promise of Allah is true. And let not those who have no certainty make you careless\""** [al-Rum: 60].\n\n[Weak. Reported by al-Hakim (3/158)]"""
"3328","(3328) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furk informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated —\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh narrated to me — Muhammad ibn Yunus narrated to us — Abu 'Amir narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman — from 'Abd al-A'la ibn al-Hakam — from Kharijah ibn al-Salt, who said: We entered the mosque with 'Abd Allah (ibn Mas'ud) while the imam was in rukū'. So 'Abd Allah performed rukū', and we performed rukū' with him, and he began walking to the row while we were still in rukū'. A man passed by and greeted him (with salam), and he said: **\Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.\""** When he completed the prayer"," he said: \""It used to be said among the signs of the Hour that a man would greet another man out of personal recognition"," that mosques would be taken as thoroughfares"," that a man and his wife would engage in trade"," and that horses and women would become expensive and then become cheap"," and then would not become expensive again until the Day of Resurrection.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Abu 'Abd Allah"," and the hadith of Abu Bakr is abridged.\n\nIt has also been narrated from Tariq ibn Shihab from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud with a similar meaning"," and he raised its ending to the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," with some additions and omissions.\n\n[Weak. Reported by al-Hakim (4/493)]"""
"3329","(3329) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us in the Akhirin — they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us — al-Shafi'i narrated to us — Malik narrated —\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed me — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih narrated to me — Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us — he said: I read to Malik — from Abu Hazim — from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) went to Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf to reconcile between them. The time of prayer came, and the mu'adhdhin came to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and said: \Will you lead the people in prayer so that I may call the iqamah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So Abu Bakr began to lead the prayer. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) came while the people were in prayer"," and he made his way through until he stood in the row. The people began to clap"," and Abu Bakr would not turn around during the prayer. When the people increased in clapping"," he turned and saw the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) gestured to him to remain in his place. So Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) raised his hands and praised Allah for what the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) had commanded him to do in that regard. Then Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stepped back until he stood in the row"," and the Prophet (peace be upon him) came forward and led the prayer. Then he turned and said: \""O Abu Bakr"," what prevented you from remaining when I commanded you?\"" Abu Bakr said: \""It was not fitting for the son of Abi Quhafah to lead the prayer in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: **\""Why did I see you increase in clapping? Whoever is afflicted by something in his prayer"," let him say 'Subhan Allah","' for when he says 'Subhan Allah","' attention is turned toward him. Clapping is only for women.\""**\n\nThis is the wording of the hadith of Yahya ibn Yahya.\n\nMuslim reported it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and al-Bukhari reported it from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik.\n\n[Sahih. Reported by al-Bukhari (652) and Muslim (421)]"""
"3330","(3330) Abu 'Amr al-Adib informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili narrated to us — Ja'far al-Faryabi narrated to us — Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us — Ya'qub ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated — from Abu Hazim — from Sahl ibn Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was informed that there was a dispute among Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, so he went out to reconcile between them. He mentioned the hadith until he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: **\O people"," what is the matter with you that when something befalls you in the prayer"," you resort to clapping? Clapping is only for women. Whoever is afflicted by something in his prayer"," let him say 'Subhan Allah","' for no one hears him when he says 'Subhan Allah' except that he turns toward him.\""**\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim both reported it in their Sahih from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. They also reported it from Qutaybah from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abu Hazim from his father"," except that he said **\""al-tasfih\""** instead of **\""al-tasfiq.\""** And Sahl said: **\""Al-tasfih is al-tasfiq.\""**\n\n[Sahih. Previously referenced in the hadith before it]"""
"3331","(3331) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed him — Abu Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us — Qutaybah narrated to us — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abu Hazim narrated — from Abu Hazim — from Sahl ibn Sa'd. He mentioned it but did not include his words: **\For no one hears him\""** until the end of what we have transmitted.\n\n[Sahih. Previously referenced in the hadith before it]"""
"3332","(3332) Abu 'Ali al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Faqih in Nishapur and Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bushran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us — Sufyan narrated — from al-Zuhri — from Abu Salamah — from Abu Hurayrah — from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: **\Tasbih in the prayer is for men"," and tasfiq is for women.\""**\n\nAl-Bukhari and Muslim reported it in their Sahih from the hadith of Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah"," without the words **\""in the prayer.\""**\n\n(t) Al-Humaydi and a group narrated it from Ibn 'Uyaynah and included this wording.\n\n[Sahih. Reported by al-Bukhari (1145) and Muslim (422)]"""
"3333","(3333) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari in Baghdad informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us — Ma'mar narrated — from al-Zuhri — from Abu Salamah — from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: **\Tasbih is for men"," and tasfiq is for women in the prayer.\""**\n\n[Sahih. Previously referenced in the hadith before it]"""
"3334","(3334) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — 'Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Nasawi narrated to us — Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us — Ibn Wahb narrated to me — Yunus narrated to me — from Ibn Shihab — who informed me: Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman both informed me that they heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: **\Tasbih is for men"," and tasfiq is for women.\""**\n\nIbn Shihab said: \""And I have seen men of knowledge performing tasbih and making gestures.\""\n\nMuslim reported it in his Sahih from Harmalah. And Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated it from Ibn Shihab from both of them and said: **\""In the prayer.\""**\n\n[Sahih. This is the wording of Muslim (422); see the hadith before it]"""
"3335","(3335) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Yusuf narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us — Ma'mar narrated — from Hammun ibn Munabbih, who said: This is what Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: **\Tasbih is for the men"," and tasfiq is for women in the prayer.\""**\n\nMuslim reported it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi' from 'Abd al-Razzaq.\n\n[Sahih. Previously referenced in the hadith before it]"""
"3336","(3336) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Abu 'Umar Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-'Ataridi narrated to us — Abu Mu'awiyah Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us — al-A'mash narrated — from Abu Salih — from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: **\Tasbih is for men"," and tasfiq is for women.\""**\n\nMuslim reported it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayb from Abu Mu'awiyah.\n\n[Sahih. Previously referenced in the hadith before it]"""
"3337","(3337) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar informed us that Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us that Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us that al-Aʿmash narrated it with its like. Al-Aʿmash said: \I mentioned it to Ibrāhīm"," and he said: 'My mother used to do it.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim from Isḥāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3338","(3338) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us orally that Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Farrāʾ, and Qaṭn ibn Ibrāhīm said: Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to me from Sulaymān al-Aʿmash from Dhakwān from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When permission is sought from a man while he is praying"," his permission is to say 'Subḥān Allāh' (glorification)"," and when permission is sought from a woman while she is praying"," her permission is to clap.\""\n\nAs for the ḥadīth narrated from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," who said: \""I had a time during the last part of the night in which I would enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. If he was in prayer"," he would say 'Subḥān Allāh","' and that was his permission for me.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth differs in its chain of narration (isnād) and its text (matn). In one narration it says \""sabbaha\"" (he glorified)"," and in another it says \""taḥanḥaḥa\"" (he cleared his throat).\n\nIts chain revolves around ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy al-Ḥaḍramī. Al-Bukhārī said regarding him: \""There is doubt about him","\"" and others weakened him. What has preceded is sufficient regarding his narration. And with Allah is success. [Ḥasan. The ḥadīth has another chain in Aḥmad 2/290.]"""
"3339","(3339) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us that Abū Zakariyyā al-Ḥinnāʾī and Abū ʿImrān al-Tustarī said: Muḥammad, meaning Ibn ʿUbayd, narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us that ʿUmārah ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ narrated to us from al-Ḥārith al-ʿUkhlī from Abū Zurʿah ibn ʿAmr ibn Jarīr from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said to me: \I had a time during the last part of the night in which I would enter upon the Prophet ﷺ. If he was in prayer"," he would say 'Subḥān Allāh","' and that was his permission for me. And if he was not in prayer"," he would grant me permission.\"" Then he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\n\nMusaddad followed him on the authority of ʿAbd al-Wāḥid regarding the glorification (tasbīḥ)"," without mentioning al-Ḥārith in his chain. [Ḍaʿīf. It was narrated by al-Nasāʾī 1211.]"""
"3340","(3340) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Musaddad informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us that ʿUmārah ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ narrated to us from Abū Zurʿah from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I had a time during the last part of the night in which I would enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If he was in prayer"," he would say 'Subḥān Allāh","' and that was his permission. And if he was not in prayer"," he would grant me permission.\""\n\nMusaddad ibn Musarhad did not mention al-Ḥārith al-ʿUkhlī in his chain"," and he agreed with the first narration regarding the glorification (tasbīḥ). [Ḍaʿīf. It was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3341","(3341) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān, Abū al-Shaykh, informed us that Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim informed us that Abū Kāmil informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated it, and he mentioned al-Ḥārith al-ʿUkhlī in his chain, except that he said in its text: \If he was in prayer"," he would clear his throat (taḥanḥaḥa)"," and that was his permission.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. It was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3342","(3342) Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated it from Mughīrah from al-Ḥārith from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy regarding the throat-clearing (taḥanḥuḥ), without mentioning Abū Zurʿah in his chain.\n\nAbū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah narrated to us that al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥakam al-Ḥibarī narrated to us that Abū Ghassān narrated to me that Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to me.\n\nShuraḥbīl ibn Muddarak narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy from his father from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the glorification (tasbīḥ), and he added his father in the chain.\n\nHowever it may be, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nujayy is not a valid authority. [Ḍaʿīf. It was mentioned in the one before it.]"
"3343","(3343) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us that Muḥammad ibn Naṣr informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us that Hushaym informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us that Abū al-Muthannā informed us that Musaddad informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us—all of them—from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid from al-Ḥārith ibn Shubayl from Abū ʿAmr al-Shaybānī from Zayd ibn Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \One of us would speak to his companion beside him in prayer"," until {And stand before Allah in devout obedience} [Al-Baqarah: 238] was revealed"," and we were commanded to observe silence and forbidden from speech.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Hushaym.\n\nAnd he said: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us from al-Ḥārith ibn Shubayl.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān from Ismāʿīl: al-Ḥārith ibn Shubayl narrated to us"," and he said in its text: \""We used to speak in prayer; one of us would speak to his brother about his need"," until {Guard strictly your prayers"," especially the middle prayer"," and stand before Allah in devout obedience} [Al-Baqarah: 238] was revealed"," and we were commanded to observe silence.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 1142"," Muslim 539.]"""
"3344","(3344) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Abū Badr narrated to us from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī in Ṭūs informed us that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Shawdhab al-Muqriʾ in Wāsiṭ informed us that Aḥmad ibn Rashīd ibn Khuthaym al-Kūfī in Wāsiṭ informed us that Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us from al-Aʿmash from Ibrāhīm from ʿAlqamah from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \We used to greet the Prophet ﷺ during prayer"," and he would respond to us. When we returned from the presence of the Negus"," we greeted him"," but he did not respond to us. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we used to greet you in prayer"," and you would respond to us.' He said: 'Indeed"," in prayer there is occupation (preoccupation).'\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Ibn Fuḍayl.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Abī Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd"," we said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," you used to respond to us; what is the matter with you today that you did not respond to us?\"" He said: \""Indeed"," in prayer there is occupation (preoccupation).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī 1185.]"""
"3345","(3345) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak narrated to us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us that Abū Dāwūd informed us that Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿĀṣim from Abū Wāʾil from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him"," but he did not respond to me. I was seized by anxiety over what had passed and what was new. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," has something new occurred?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," decrees for His Prophet from His affair what He wills"," and indeed among what He has decreed is that you should not speak in prayer.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd 924.]"""
"3346","(3346) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us that Zāʾidah narrated to us from ʿĀṣim from Shaqīq from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: \We used to speak in prayer"," and some of us would greet one another"," and one of us would make requests of his need.\"" He said: \""So I came one day while the Prophet ﷺ was praying"," and I greeted him"," but he did not respond. I was seized by anxiety over what had passed and what was new. When he finished"," he said: 'Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," decrees from His affair what He wills"," and indeed He has decreed that you should not speak in prayer.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains. It was mentioned in the one before it.]"""
"3347","(3347) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn Saʿīd narrated from Kathīr ibn Shindhīr, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Prophet ﷺ sent me on an errand of his. I came back having fulfilled it, and I greeted him while he was praying, but he did not return my greeting."
"3348","(3348) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf the jurist informed us, Ibn Rajāʾ—meaning Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ ibn al-Sindī—informed us, Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Kathīr ibn Shindhīr narrated to us, ʿAṭāʾ narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand. I set out and then returned having fulfilled it. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. There fell into my heart what Allah knows best of [anxiety]. I said to myself: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is upset with me because I was slow in returning. Then I greeted him again, but he did not return my greeting. There fell into my heart something even stronger than the first time. Then I greeted him a third time, and he returned my greeting and said: \Indeed"," nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I was praying.\"" He was upon his mount"," facing other than the direction of the qiblah."""
"3349","(3349) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr the judge, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū ʿUtbah Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj al-Ḥijāzī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥumayr narrated to us, al-Awzāʿī narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Ibn Abī Maymūnah, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, and Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam al-Sulamī narrated to me, who said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer, a man from the people sneezed, so I said, \Yarḥamuka Allāh (May Allah have mercy on you).\"" The people glared at me with their eyes. I said"," \""Woe to your mothers! Why are you looking at me?\"" They struck their hands upon their thighs. When I saw them silencing me"," I fell silent. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer"," he called me. By my father and my mother"," I have never seen a teacher before him or after him better in teaching than him. By Allah"," he did not rebuke me"," nor strike me"," nor revile me. He said: \""Indeed"," in this prayer of ours"," nothing of the speech of people is proper. It is only takbīr"," tasbīh"," and recitation of the Qurʾān.\"""""
"3350","(3350) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yūnus al-Nasāʾī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, Fulayḥ narrated from Hilāl ibn ʿAlī, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam al-Sulamī, who said: When I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I was taught matters of Islam. Among what I was taught was that it was said to me: \When you sneeze"," praise Allah"," and when a sneezer sneezes and praises Allah"," say"," 'Yarḥamuka Allāh (May Allah have mercy on you).'\"" He said: While I was standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer"," a man sneezed and praised Allah"," so I said"," \""Yarḥamuka Allāh","\"" raising my voice with it. The people glared at me until that [glaring] overwhelmed me. I said"," \""What is the matter with you? Why are you looking at me with sharp eyes?\"" They made tasbīh. When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer"," he said: \""Who was the one speaking?\"" It was said: \""This Bedouin.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and said: \""Indeed"," the prayer is for the recitation of the Qurʾān and the remembrance of Allah. When you are in it"," let that be your concern.\"" I have never seen a teacher more gentle than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."""
"3351","(3351) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd ibn Yazīd informed us, my father informed me, al-Awzāʿī narrated to me, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to me, Hilāl ibn Abī Maymūnah narrated to me, ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār narrated to me, and Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam al-Sulamī narrated to me, who said: I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \We were recently in a state of Jāhiliyyah"," and then Allah brought Islam"," and among us are those who practice ṭiyarah (omen-taking).\"" He said: \""That is something they find in their hearts; let it not deter them.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and among us are those who visit the soothsayers.\"" He said: \""Then let them not visit them.\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," and among us are those who draw lines (for divination).\"" He said: \""There was a prophet among the prophets who drew lines; so whoever's line coincides with his"," then that is it.\"" He said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in prayer"," a man from the people sneezed"," so I said"," \""Yarḥamuka Allāh.\"" The people glared at me with their eyes. I said"," \""Woe to your mothers! Why are you looking at me?\"" The people struck their hands upon their thighs. When I saw them silencing me"," I fell silent. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer"," he called me. By my father and my mother"," I have never seen a teacher before him or after him better in teaching than him. By Allah"," he did not strike me"," nor rebuke me"," nor revile me. He said: \""Indeed"," in this prayer of ours"," nothing of the speech of people is proper. It is only tasbīh"," takbīr"," and recitation of the Qurʾān.\"" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith.\n\nAnd Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir informed us"," my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr the judge narrated to us"," Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us"," Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us"," ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us"," al-Awzāʿī narrated from Yaḥyā"," and he mentioned it similarly"," except that he did not mention his words: \""We were recently in a state of Jāhiliyyah"," and then Allah brought Islam.\"" Rather he said: \""I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Among us are men…'\"""""
"3352","(3352) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us, Yūnus narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Ḥarb ibn Shaddād and Abān ibn Yazīd narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr, from Hilāl ibn Abī Maymūnah, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār, from Muʿāwiyah ibn al-Ḥakam al-Sulamī, who said: I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and a man beside me sneezed, so I said, \Yarḥamuka Allāh.\"" The people glared at me with their eyes. I said"," \""Woe to your mothers! Why are you looking at me while I am praying?\"" They began striking their hands upon their thighs to silence me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer—by my father and my mother"," I have never seen before him or after him a teacher better in teaching than him—by Allah"," he did not rebuke me"," nor revile me"," nor strike me. But he said to me: \""Indeed"," in this prayer of ours"," nothing of the speech of people is proper. It is only prayer"," tasbīh"," taḥmīd"," and recitation of the Qurʾān.\"" Or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. Then he mentioned what al-Awzāʿī mentioned regarding ṭiyarah and other matters.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: It has not been reported that the Prophet ﷺ commanded him to repeat the prayer"," and it has been narrated that he spoke out of ignorance of that."""
"3353","(3353) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hamadhānī informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us, Ādam narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rakʿahs of Ẓuhr or ʿAṣr. Dhu al-Yadayn said to him: \Has the prayer been shortened"," O Messenger of Allah"," or did you forget?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his Companions: \""Is what he says true?\"" They said: \""Yes.\"" So he prayed two more rakʿahs and then performed the two prostrations of sahw. Saʿd said: I saw ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr pray two rakʿahs of Maghrib and then give salām"," then speak"," and then pray what remained. He said: \""Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"""""
"3354","(3354) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAnbarī and Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar informed us. They said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," when Abū Bakr stands in your place"," the people will not hear [the recitation] on account of his weeping. Command ʿUmar to lead the people in prayer.\"" He said: \""Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\"" ʿĀʾishah said: I said to Ḥafṣah: \""Say to him: 'When Abū Bakr stands in your place"," the people will not hear [the recitation] on account of his weeping. Command ʿUmar to lead the people in prayer.'\"" Ḥafṣah did so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," you are the companions of Yūsuf. Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\"" Ḥafṣah said to ʿĀʾishah: \""I have never received any good from you.\"""""
"3355","(3355) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the littérateur informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed me, Abū Saʿīd Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Juʿfī narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed me, Yūnus informed me from Ibn Shihāb, from Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from his father, who said: When the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became severe, he said: \Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\"" ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said to him: \""O Messenger of Allah"," Abū Bakr is a tender-hearted man. When he stands in your place"," the people will not hear [the recitation] on account of his weeping.\"" He said: \""Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\"" She repeated her words to him"," and he said: \""You are the companions of Yūsuf. Tell Abū Bakr to lead the people in prayer.\"""""
"3356","(3356) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān the jurist in Baghdad informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzār narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Thābit, from Muṭarrif, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying, and in his chest was a humming like the humming of a millstone on account of weeping."
"3357","(3357) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Darābjardī narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān informed us; ʿAbdullāh — that is, Ibn al-Mubārak — informed us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it with his chain of narration, except that he said: \And his belly produced a gurgling sound like the gurgling of a cooking pot.\"" [Authentic. It was referenced in the one before it. An-Nisāʾ 1214]"""
"3358","(3358) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ḥajjāj said: Ibn Jurayj said: \I heard Ibn Abī Mulaykah say: ʿAlqamah ibn Waqqāṣ informed me"," saying: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāllāh — may Allah be pleased with him — used to recite Sūrah Yūsuf in the ʿIshāʾ prayer"," and I was in the rear of the rows. When the mention of Yūsuf came"," I heard his sobbing from the rear of the row.\"" [Authentic. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 2703]"""
"3359","(3359) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us; Abū Aḥmad al-Zubayrī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir, who said: \Smiling does not invalidate the prayer"," but cackling does.\"" This is the preserved version"," as a mawqūf (stopped) narration. It was raised (marfūʿ) by Thābit ibn Muḥammad al-Zāhid"," and it is an error on his part. [Authentic. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 4774]"""
"3360","(3360) Abū Saʿīd Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us; Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Mahdī narrated to us; Thābit ibn Muḥammad — meaning al-Zāhid — narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \Smiling does not invalidate the prayer"," but cackling invalidates it.\"" Another ḥadīth has been narrated regarding smiling in prayer"," but the likes of it cannot be used as evidence. [Denounced (Munkar). It was referenced in the one before it]"""
"3361","(3361) Abū Saʿd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣūfī informed him; Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Yaʿlā informed us; ʿAmr al-Nāqid narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Thābit al-Jazarī narrated to us; al-Wāziʿ ibn Nāfiʿ narrated from Abū Salamah from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh — may Allah be pleased with them both — who said: \We were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during an expedition when he smiled during his prayer. When he completed his prayer"," we said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we saw you smile.' He said: 'Mīkāʾīl passed by me with traces of dust on his wing"," returning from pursuing the people"," so he smiled at me"," and I smiled back at him.'\"" Al-Wāziʿ ibn Nāfiʿ al-ʿUqaylī al-Jazarī — the scholars have spoken critically about him. Al-Wāqidī also related it in al-Maghāzī. We have also narrated in the Book of Purification from Abū Sufyān from Jābir regarding the one who laughs in prayer: he repeats the prayer but does not repeat the wuḍūʾ. And we have narrated from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī that he said in a story attributed to him: \""Whoever among you laughs"," let him repeat the prayer.\"" Something similar is also narrated from Ibn Masʿūd. [Very weak. Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā 2060]"""
"3362","(3362) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from his father from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: \The solar eclipse occurred during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" He then mentioned the prayer of the Prophet ﷺ and said: \""Then he blew in his final prostration and said: 'Uff"," uff.' Then he said: 'My Lord"," did You not promise me that You would not punish them while I am among them? Did You not promise me that You would not punish them while they seek forgiveness?'\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer"," and the sun had cleared. The Shaykh — may Allah have mercy on him — said: \""What is likely is that this blowing resembled snoring"," due to what was presented to him of the punishment of some of those upon whom punishment was due. No one else is permitted to say 'uff' in prayer as he ﷺ did — may my father and mother be sacrificed for him — just as no one else is permitted to see what he saw of their punishment.\"" ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ and said: \""He began to blow in his final prostration of the second rakʿah and wept","\"" and he did not mention the saying of 'uff.' Abū Isḥāq narrated it from al-Sāʾib ibn Mālik from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr and mentioned the blowing without the saying of 'uff.' Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī — may Allah have mercy on him — claimed that his saying 'uff' does not constitute speech unless the fāʾ is emphasized (mushaddada)"," in which case it would be three letters of disapproval. He said: \""The one who blows does not produce the fāʾ emphasized in his blowing"," nor can he produce a true fāʾ from its proper point of articulation.\"" [Authentic. Its detailed verification will come"," Allah willing"," in the Book of the Eclipse Prayer]"""
"3363","(3363) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawīyah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr al-Azdī narrated to us; Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; Zāʾidah narrated from Abū Ḥamzah from Abū Ṣāliḥ, who said: \I was with Umm Salamah when a young relative of hers with thick hair on his forehead entered. He stood to pray and began to blow. She said: 'O my son"," do not blow"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to our black slave: \""O Rabāḥ"," dust your face (i.e."," place your forehead on the ground in prostration).\""'\"" A group of imams narrated it similarly"," such as Ḥammād ibn Zayd and others"," from Maymūn"," Abū Ḥamzah. I have not recorded it from anyone else's ḥadīth"," and it is weak — and Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. It has also been narrated in another ḥadīth from Zayd ibn Thābit as a marfūʿ narration"," and it is weak beyond doubt. [Hasan through other chains. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī 381]"""
"3364","(3364) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn al-Khaḍir al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abū al-Ḍuḥā from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he used to fear that it might constitute speech — meaning blowing in the prayer. The Shaykh said: \Blowing does not constitute speech unless discernible speech with identifiable letters emerges from it. If no discernible speech with identifiable letters is understood from it"," then it is not speech.\"" [Authentic. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 3018]"""
"3365","(3365) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us; Salamah al-Abrash narrated to us; Ayman ibn Nābil narrated to us, saying: \I said to Qudāmah ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmmār al-Kilābī"," a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'We are bothered by the feathers of pigeons in the Masjid al-Ḥarām when we prostrate.' He said: 'Blow them away.'\"" [Weak. Narrated by Ibn Maʿīn in al-Tārīkh: 3/48]"""
"3366","(3366) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb: \Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim and al-Ḥārith ibn Nabhān informed you from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah"," the wife of the Prophet ﷺ"," that her slave Dhakwān used to lead her in prayer from the muṣḥaf during Ramaḍān.\"" Except that al-Ḥārith said in the ḥadīth: from Ayyūb from al-Qāsim from ʿĀʾishah. [Authentic. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 3825]"""
"3367","(3367) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) counting the tasbīḥ (on his fingers).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 1502]"""
"3368","(3368) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Mayṣarah and Muḥammad ibn Qudāmah, among others, said: ʿUththām narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) counting the tasbīḥ.\"" Ibn Qudāmah said: \""With his right hand.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: Ibn al-Bāghandī narrated it from Abū al-Ashʿath — Aḥmad ibn al-Miqdām al-ʿIjlī — from ʿUththām"," and he said in the hadith: \""He counted the tasbīḥ during the prayer.\""\n\nA scholar of ours in Bākhrūjard"," known as Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī"," of sound hearing"," narrated it from the Sheikh Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī in his Amālī"," from the hadith of al-Aʿmash"," from Ibn al-Bāghandī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the one before it]"""
"3369","(3369) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Khusrūjardī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Ḥaḍramī — Muṭayyin — narrated to us; Mālik ibn Fudayk narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: that he used to count the verses during the prayer and count with his fingers. This is the statement of Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. [Ḍaʿīf. It is the own statement of Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.]"
"3370","(3370) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sarrāj informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Ḥaḍramī — Muṭayyin — narrated to us; Mālik ibn al-Fudayk narrated to us; al-Aʿmash narrated to me from Ibrāhīm: that he used to count the verses during the prayer and count with his fingers. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"3371","(3371) And with his chain, he said: al-Aʿmash narrated to me from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father: that he used to count the verses during the prayer and count with his fingers. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"3372","(3372) Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Wakīʿ narrated — or Sufyān narrated — from al-Aʿmash, who said: \I saw Yaḥyā"," that is"," Ibn Waththāb"," counting the verses during the prayer.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"3373","(3373) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb informed us; al-Dabarī narrated from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, from al-Thawrī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl, from Ibn al-Ḥanafiyyah, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who attributed it to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \The key to prayer is purification"," its consecration is the takbīr"," and its release is the taslīm.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in its shorter form. Its extraction preceded in hadith 2261]"""
"3374","(3374) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us; Abū al-Walīd narrated to us; Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbbād ibn Tamīm, from his uncle, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) — meaning that a man complained to him about finding something in his prayer — he said: \He should not turn away until he hears a sound or detects an odor.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd"," and Muslim narrated it from the hadith of Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 137]"""
"3375","(3375) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq in Baghdad informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us; Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ informed us, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you is in doubt during his prayer as to whether something has passed from him or not"," he should not turn away until he hears a sound or detects an odor.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Muslim"," 362]"""
"3376","(3376) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād informed us; Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ informed us, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you is in prayer and feels movement in his posterior"," and he is uncertain whether he has broken his wudu or not"," and it is unclear to him"," he should not turn away until he hears a sound or detects an odor.\""\n\nIn this there is evidence that he turns away when he hears a sound or detects an odor"," with no distinction between it being intentional"," inadvertent"," or premature"," and Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū Dāwūd"," 177]"""
"3377","(3377) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Isḥāq informed us in Baghdad — Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Fākihī narrated to us in Makkah — Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarra narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Jārī informed us — ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Thawr, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet ﷺ:\n\n\Indeed"," Shayṭān comes to one of you and blows near his posterior"," so let him not leave [the prayer] until he hears a sound"," or finds an odor"," or does so deliberately.\""\n\n[Ḥasan in its grade. Al-Daqqāq recorded it in his Majlis"," no. 116.]"""
"3378","(3378) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Qāsim ibn al-Qāsim al-Sayyārī informed us in Marw — ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAlī al-Ghazzāl narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us — al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us — from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\When one of you has a minor ablution break [ḥadath] while in prayer"," let him place his hand over his nose"," then let him withdraw.\""\n\n[Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad followed him in connecting it"," from Ibn Jurayj"," from Hishām; and ʿUmar ibn ʿAlī al-Muqaddamī"," from Hishām; and Jubārah ibn Mughallis"," from ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak"," from Hishām.]\n\n[And al-Thawrī"," Shuʿbah"," Zā'idah"," Ibn al-Mubārak"," Shuʿayb ibn Isḥāq"," and ʿAbadah ibn Sulaymān narrated it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," as a mursal (disconnected) hadith.]\n\n[Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: \""This is more authentic than the ḥadīth of al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā.\""]\n\n[The Shaykh said: Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated it from al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā"," connected thus"," except that he said in its text: \""When one of you has a minor ablution break in his prayer"," let him hold his nose"," withdraw"," and then perform ablution.\""]\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Abū Dāwūd recorded it"," no. 1114.]"""
"3379","(3379) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed him — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us — Nuʿaym narrated to us — al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated it, mentioning it [as above].\n\n[And we have already narrated in the Book of Purity (Kitāb al-Ṭahārah) from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he ﷺ said: \The prayer of any one of you is not accepted when he has a minor ablution break until he performs ablution.\""]\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. (The reference mentioned above.) Preceded in the one before it. Abū Dāwūd"," no. 60.]"""
"3380","(3380) Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAlawī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Dalwīh narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me — Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to us — from Simāk ibn Ḥarb, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\There is no prayer without purification"," and charity from stolen wealth is not accepted.\""\n\n[Muslim recorded it from the ḥadīt"""
"3381","(3381) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Muḥammad ibn Bakr informed us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah informed us — Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd informed us from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal from ʿĪsā ibn Ḥiṭṭān from Muslim ibn Salām from ʿAlī ibn Ṭalq, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you passes wind during the prayer"," let him leave"," let him perform wuḍūʾ"," and let him repeat his prayer.\""\n\nThis explicitly indicates the repetition of the prayer"," and upon this position al-Miswar ibn Makhramah"," one of the Companions"," also held. [Ḍaʿīf. Abū Dāwūd narrated it (205)]"""
"3382","(3382) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh, both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, reading upon him while I was listening, that Dāwūd ibn Rushayd informed them — Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh informed me — ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Jurayj from his father, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you passes wind or has a belch during his prayer"," let him leave"," let him perform wuḍūʾ"," then let him build upon what has passed of his prayer"," so long as he has not spoken.\""\n\nIbn Jurayj said: \""If he speaks"," he begins anew.\""\n\nA group narrated it from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh from Ibn Jurayj from his father from the Prophet ﷺ as a mursal ḥadīth"," and from him from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah as a mawṣūl ḥadīth. [Munkar. Its takhrīj has preceded in Ḥadīth 669"," in the first part]"""
"3383","(3383) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — Abū ʿĀmir Mūsā ibn ʿĀmir informed us — al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed me — Ismāʿīl from Ibn Jurayj from his father from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever has a nosebleed during his prayer"," let him leave"," let him perform wuḍūʾ"," then let him build upon what he has prayed.\""\n\nThis ḥadīth is among the most objectionable narrations attributed to Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh. The preserved narration is what the group narrated from Ibn Jurayj from his father from the Prophet ﷺ as a mursal ḥadīth. Likewise"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī"," Abū ʿĀṣim al-Nabīl"," ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ"," and others narrated it from Ibn Jurayj.\n\nAs for the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," only Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh and Sulaymān ibn Arqam narrate it from Ibn Jurayj. Sulaymān ibn Arqam is matrūk (abandoned)"," and whatever Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrates from other than the people of Shām is ḍaʿīf and not reliable.\n\nIt was also narrated from Ismāʿīl from ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Jallān from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. Both ʿAbbād and ʿAṭāʾ are ḍaʿīf"," and Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. [Munkar. It preceded in the one before it]"""
"3384","(3384) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us. And Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, saying: It was read upon Ibn Wahb — ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān al-Jumaḥī and Mālik ibn Anas and al-Layth ibn Saʿd and Usāmah ibn Zayd informed you that Nāfiʿ informed them that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, when he had a nosebleed during the prayer, would leave, perform wuḍūʾ, then return and build upon what he had prayed, without speaking. This from Ibn ʿUmar is ṣaḥīḥ, and it has also been narrated from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Mālik narrated it (77)]"
"3385","(3385) Abū ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Bayyāʿ al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh, in what I read upon him — Muḥammad ibn Yūnus informed us — Rūḥ informed us — Shuʿbah informed us — Abū Isḥāq from ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \Whoever finds a rumbling in his stomach or vomits"," let him leave and perform wuḍūʾ. If he has not spoken"," he counts what he has prayed; if he has spoken"," he begins the prayer anew.\""\n\nAnd it was also narrated from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḍaʿīf. Aḥmad narrated it (1/88)]"""
"3386","(3386) Al-Ḥasan ibn Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Shādhān in Baghdad informed us — Ḥamzah ibn Muḥammad ibn al-ʿAbbās informed us — al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us — ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us — Isrāʾīl from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: \Any man who enters into the prayer and is afflicted by a rumbling in his stomach"," or vomiting"," or a nosebleed"," and fears that he will have a ritual occurrence before the imām delivers the salām"," let him place his hand upon his nose. If he wishes to count what has already passed"," let him not speak until he performs wuḍūʾ"," then let him complete what remains. If he speaks"," let him begin anew. And if he has already recited the tashahhud and fears that he will have a ritual occurrence before the imām delivers the salām"," let him deliver the salām"," for his prayer has been completed.\""\n\nAl-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī with part of its meaning. Al-Ḥārith al-Aʿwar is ḍaʿīf"," and ʿĀṣim ibn Ḍamrah is not strong.\n\nIt was also narrated from a third route from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and it too contains weakness"," and Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"3387","(3387) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn 'Ali narrated to us, saying: 'Abd Allah ibn Raja' narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Sa'id narrated from his father, from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Whoever feels a rumbling in his stomach or has the urge to urinate"," let him place his garment over his nose"," then let him turn away and perform wudu"," and let him not speak to anyone. If he speaks"," he must begin the prayer anew.\""\n\nAnd in all of this"," if it is authentic"," there is an indication of the permissibility of leaving the prayer due to the rumbling before the occurrence of hadath (nullification of wudu)"," and then building upon what has already been performed of the prayer. (Tirmidhi) And something similar has also been narrated from Salman al-Farisi (may Allah be pleased with him). [Da'if]"""
"3388","(3388) And Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Malik narrated to us, having received the report that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas used to experience a nosebleed, whereupon he would leave, wash off the blood, and then return and build upon what he had already prayed. [Da'if. Reported by Malik, 78]"
"3389","(3389) He said: And Malik narrated to us from Yazid ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Qusayt, that he saw Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib experiencing a nosebleed while he was praying. He went to the chamber of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and water for wudu was brought to him. He performed wudu, then returned and built upon what he had already prayed. [Sahih. Reported by Malik, 79]"
"3390","(3390) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us, saying: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, saying: al-Walid narrated from Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, from 'Ata' ibn Qays, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, who said: \He should return and build upon what he has already prayed\"" — meaning in the case of a nosebleed. 'Ata' said: And Ibn 'Umar and Abu Salamah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman wrote to Umayyah ibn Khalid ibn Asid"," and he read their letter to us confirming that. [Da'if]"""
"3391","(3391) He said: And al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Amr informed me that he heard 'Ata' saying: \He should leave"," perform wudu"," and not speak to anyone"," then return and build upon what he has already prayed.\"" And this has also been narrated from Tawus"," Sulayman ibn Yasar"," and others. [Sahih. Reported by 'Abd al-Razzaq"," 572]"""
"3392","(3392) And Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us, saying: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Amir narrated to us, saying: al-Walid said: Abu 'Amr — that is, al-Awza'i — informed me from Wasil, from Mujahid, who said: \If you turn your face away from the qiblah"," then repeat the prayer.\"" [Hasan. A good chain of narration]"""
"3393","(3393) He said: And Abu 'Amr — that is, al-Awza'i — said: Yazid ibn Abi Malik informed me that he heard 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz saying: \If you turn your face away from the qiblah"," then repeat it.\"" [Sahih]"""
"3394","(3394) And with this chain of narration, al-Walid narrated to us: Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed me from 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz and al-Hasan, something similar to that. [Da'if]"
"3395","(3395) al-Walid said: And al-Layth ibn Sa'd and 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Namir informed me from Ibn Shihab, who narrated to them from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah that he used to say: \He should begin the prayer anew.\""\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The most preferable of opinions to me in this matter is that it breaks the prayer. And this is the statement of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah.\"" He said: \""And the statement of al-Miswar is more akin to the statement of the generality of scholars regarding one who turns his back to the qiblah deliberately — that he should start over.\""\n\nHe said: \""It is not permissible for a person to be in a state in which prayer is not valid for him"," and then build upon his prayer. And Allah knows best.\""\n\nHe said: \""In the earlier period"," he used to say: 'He builds upon it.'\""\n\nAnd he said in al-Imla': \""Were it not for the positions of the fuqaha"," I would have held the view that whoever turns away from the qiblah due to a nosebleed or otherwise"," upon him is the obligation to repeat the prayer. However"," the narrations only mention the salam.\"" He said: \""That is regarding this issue and other issues.\"" And he retracted in his later position to the view of al-Miswar ibn Makhramah. And with Allah lies success. [Sahih]"""
"3396","(3396) Abu Salih ibn Abi Tahir al-'Anbari narrated to us, saying: My grandfather, Yahya ibn Mansur al-Qadi, narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id al-Thaqafi narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sent me on an errand. Then I caught up with him while he was praying. I greeted him with salam"," and he gestured to me. When he finished"," he called me and said: 'You just greeted me with salam while I was praying.'\"" And at that time he was facing toward the east.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. [Sahih. Reported by Muslim"," 540]"""
"3397","(3397) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub and Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Ziyad said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to me: Abu al-Zubayr narrated from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me while he was heading toward Banu al-Mustaliq. I came to him and he was praying upon his camel. I spoke to him, and he gestured to me with his hand in such a manner — and Zuhayr gestured with his hand. Then I spoke to him again, and he gestured to me in such a manner — and Zuhayr likewise gestured with his hand toward the ground. I could hear him reciting, nodding with his head. When he finished, he said: \What did you accomplish regarding that for which I sent you? Nothing prevented me from speaking to you except that I was praying.\"" Zuhayr said: Abu al-Zubayr was sitting with him facing the Ka'bah"," and he gestured with his hand toward Banu al-Mustaliq"," that is"," with his hand toward other than the Ka'bah.\n\nNarrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Yunus. [Authentic. Refer to the hadith before it.]"""
"3398","(3398) Abu Salih ibn Abu Tahir informed us: My grandfather, Yahya ibn Mansur, narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand. I came to him while he was praying. I greeted him with salam, and he responded to me with a gesture.\n\nOthers narrated from Sufyan and said in the hadith: \He did not respond to me.\""\n\nWhat is meant is that he did not respond to me verbally; rather"," he responded to me with a gesture. And success is by Allah.\n\nYazid ibn Ibrahim combined both narrations in his report. [Authentic. Refer to the hadith before it.]"""
"3399","(3399) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us: Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir: that the Prophet ﷺ sent him on an errand of his. He came and the Prophet ﷺ was praying, so he greeted him with salam. He did not respond to him and gestured with his hand. When he finished the prayer, he said: \Nothing prevented me from responding to you except that I was praying.\"" [Authentic. Refer to the hadith before it.]"""
"3400","(3400) 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdun informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: al-Asfati — that is, 'Abbas ibn al-Fadl — narrated to us: Abu al-Walid narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to me: Bukayr ibn 'Abdullah narrated from Nabil, the companion of the cloaks, from Ibn 'Umar, from Suhayb, who said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, so I greeted him with salam, and he responded to me with a gesture. Layth said: I think he said: \With his finger.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated in this account through a chain containing a mursal narration that he gestured with his hand without doubt. [Authentic. Narrated by al-Tirmidhi (367).]"""
"3401","(3401) Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdun informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam at Mina.\n\n'Abdullah ibn 'Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to the mosque of Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf in Quba' to pray in it. Men of the Ansar came to him greeting him with salam. I asked Suhayb, who was with him: \How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ respond to them when they greeted him while he was praying?\"" Suhayb said: \""He would gesture to them with his hand.\"" Sufyan said: I said to a man: \""Ask him: Did you hear this from Ibn 'Umar?\"" He said: \""O Abu Usamah"," did you hear it from Ibn 'Umar?\"" He said: \""Indeed"," I spoke to him and he spoke to me"," but Zayd did not say: 'I heard it from him.'\""\n\nIt has also been narrated from another route from Ibn 'Umar. [Authentic. Refer to the hadith before it.]"""
"3402","(3402) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr al-Qadi said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bakr al-Marwazi informed us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Hisham — that is, Ibn Sa'd — narrated from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Quba'. The Ansar came greeting him with salam while he was praying. They began greeting him with salam. Ibn 'Umar said: \O Bilal"," how did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ responding to them while he was praying?\"" He said: \""Like this","\"" and he spread his entire hand"," meaning he would gesture.\n\nWaki' ibn al-Jarrah and Ja'far ibn 'Awn likewise narrated it from Hisham ibn Sa'd.\n\n'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated from Hisham and said: \""Bilal or Suhayb.\"" [Authentic for other than this chain. Narrated by Abu Dawud (927).]"""
"3403","(3403) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi — and Abu Zakariyya — Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Muzakka — said: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — narrated to us: Bahr ibn Nasr narrated. He said: It was recited to Ibn Wahb: Hisham ibn Sa'd informed you from Nafi'. He said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Quba'. The Ansar heard of him and came greeting the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with salam. He said: I said to Bilal or Suhayb: \How did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ responding to them while they were greeting him with salam and he was praying?\"" He said: \""He would gesture with his hand.\"" He said: \""And it reached me in other than this hadith that it was Suhayb whom Ibn 'Umar asked — Ibn Wahb says it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Abu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi said: \""Both hadiths are authentic in my view"," as Ibn 'Umar narrated them from both Bilal and Suhayb.\"" [Authentic for other than this chain. The people of hadith have preceded it.]"""
"3404","(3404) Abu al-Husayn — 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran — informed us in Baghdad: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn 'Affan narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar: that he greeted a man who was praying, and the man responded to him verbally. He said: \When one of you is greeted with salam while he is praying"," let him not speak; rather"," let him gesture with his hand.\"" [Authentic. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq (3495).]"""
"3405","(3405) Abu Sa'id al-Isfarayini informed us: Abu Bahr al-Barbahari narrated to us: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Humaydi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: 'Amr narrated from 'Ata': that Musa ibn 'Abdullah ibn Jamil al-Jumahi greeted Ibn 'Abbas while he was praying, so he took hold of his hand. [Authentic. Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaybah.]"
"3406","(3406) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Husayn ibn 'Isa al-Khurasani al-Damaghani narrated to us: Ja'far ibn 'Awn narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us: Nafi' narrated. He said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Quba' to pray there. He said: The Ansar came to him and greeted him with salam while he was praying. He said: I said to Bilal: \How did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ responding to them when they were greeting him with salam while he was praying?\"" He said: \""He would say like this","\"" and he spread his palm. Ja'far ibn 'Awn spread his palm"," placing its inner surface downward and its outer surface upward. [Authentic for other than this chain. Its authentication preceded in hadith 3402"," recently.]"""
"3407","Ibn Sirin narrated that 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) greeted the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying, and he responded with a gesture of his head, meaning a reply.\n[Weak. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq 3493]"
"3408","Muhammad said: I was informed that Ibn Mas'ud said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ when I returned from Abyssinia to greet him, and I found him standing in prayer. So I greeted him, and he gestured with his head.\nMuhammad used to act upon this.\nThis is the preserved version, and it is mursal.\n[Weak. Its narrators are trustworthy, but it is disconnected]"
"3409","Abu al-Hasan ibn 'Abdan informed us; Ahmad ibn 'Ubaid informed us; Tamtam narrated to us; Abu Ya'la al-Tuzi narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Raja' narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: When I returned from Abyssinia, I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying. I greeted him, and he gestured with his head.\nThis is narrated exclusively by Abu Ya'la, Muhammad ibn al-Salt al-Tuzi.\n[Weak]"
"3410","Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Aban narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from 'Abdullah, who said: We used to greet one another during prayer and convey our needs. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was praying, and I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. I was overcome by anxiety over what had passed and what was new. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: \Indeed"," Allah decrees from His affair what He wills"," and indeed Allah has now decreed that you should not speak during prayer.\"" Then he returned my greeting.\n[Authentic through other chains. Narrated by Abu Dawud 928]"""
"3411","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh and Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i both said: 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \There should be no negligence (ghirar) in prayer nor in returning the greeting of peace.\""\nAhmad ibn Hanbal said: As I understand it"," he meant that you should not give the greeting of peace while someone is praying"," nor should it be given to you. The negligence (gharr) of a man in his prayer is that he should give the greeting of peace while he is doubtful about his prayer. Thus it is in my book.\nAbu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated it with his chain"," except that he said: \""There should be no negligence in prayer nor in returning the greeting of peace.\""\nAhmad ibn Hanbal said: He meant"," as I understand it"," that you should not give the greeting of peace while someone is praying"," nor should it be given to you"," and that a man should not be negligent in his prayer by departing while he is doubtful about it. This wording is closer to the explanation of Ahmad ibn Hanbal.\nAbu Dawud said: Ibn Fudayl narrated it from Abu Malik with the wording of Ibn Mahdi"," and he did not raise it (to the Prophet).\nMu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated it from Sufyan with his chain; he said: I think he raised it"," and he said: \""There should be no negligence in returning the greeting of peace nor in prayer.\""\n[Authentic. Narrated by Abu Dawud 928]"""
"3412","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Muhammad ibn Musa ibn 'Imran al-Faqih narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Sufyan, and he mentioned it.\nThis wording negates negligence in both prayer and the greeting of peace entirely. The preceding hadiths permit greeting the one who is praying and responding with a gesture, and these are more deserving of being followed. And with Allah is success.\n[Authentic. See the one before it]"
"3413","Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Hamid ibn Bilal narrated to us; Abu al-Azhar said: 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us; Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed during his illness while sitting, and behind him people were standing. He gestured to them to sit. When he finished his prayer, he said: \The Imam is appointed only to be followed. So when he bows"," bow; and when he raises his head"," raise your heads; and if he prays sitting"," pray sitting.\""\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih.\n[Authentic. Narrated by al-Bukhari 656"," Muslim 412]"""
"3414","From Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Numayr, from his father. Hammad said, from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, in this hadith: \He gestured to them with his hand to sit.\""\nAbu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Isma'il ibn Najid narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us; Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us; Hammad narrated it.\nMuslim narrated it from Sulayman ibn Dawud.\nAnd in the hadith of Jabir ibn 'Abdullah in this story"," he said: \""He turned toward us and saw us standing"," so he gestured to us.\""\n[Authentic. See the one before it]"""
"3415","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn 'Umar narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill, and we prayed behind him while he was sitting, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was calling out the takbir so that the people could hear his takbir. He said: He turned toward us and saw us standing, so he gestured to us, and he mentioned the rest of the hadith.\n[Authentic. Narrated by Muslim 413, Abu Dawud 602]"
"3416","Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Wahb informed me; 'Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Kurayb, the freedman of Ibn 'Abbas, that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah sent him to 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), and he mentioned the hadith about the two rak'ahs after 'Asr, and that they referred the matter to Umm Salamah. Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid them, but then I saw him praying them. As for when he prayed them, he prayed 'Asr and then entered while I had with me some women from Banu Haram of the Ansar, and he prayed them. So I sent the maidservant to him and said: Stand beside him and say to him: Umm Salamah says, \O Messenger of Allah"," I hear you forbid these two rak'ahs"," and I see you praying them.\"" If he gestures with his hand"," then move away from him. She said: The maidservant did so"," and he gestured with his hand"," so she moved away from him. When he finished"," he said: \""O daughter of Umayyah"," you asked about the two rak'ahs after 'Asr. Indeed"," some people from 'Abd al-Qays came to me with the matter of Islam from their people"," and they occupied me from the two rak'ahs after Dhuhr"," so these are those two.\""\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Yahya ibn Sulayman"," and Muslim narrated it from Harmalah"," both from Ibn Wahb.\n[Authentic. Narrated by al-Bukhari 1176"," Muslim 834]"""
"3417","(3417) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-Azhar narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar reported from ʿUbayd Allāh — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would gesture with his hand during the ṣalāh."
"3418","(3418) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dāwūd narrated to us — Salama ibn Shabīb, Muḥammad ibn Masʿūd, and Khushaysh ibn Aṣram narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar reported from al-Zuhrī — from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would gesture during the ṣalāh."
"3419","(3419) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik reported from Hishām — from ʿUrwah — from Fāṭimah bint al-Mundhir — from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: I came to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when the sun was eclipsed, and lo, the people were standing performing ṣalāh, and lo, she was standing. I said: What is the matter with the people? She gestured with her hand toward the heavens and said: \Subḥān Allāh.\"" I said: A sign? She gestured: \""Yes\"" — and she mentioned the ḥadīth."""
"3420","(3420) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Ibn Abī Dāwūd, that is, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dāwūd al-Sijistānī, narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us — from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — from Yaʿqūb ibn ʿUtba ibn al-Mughīra ibn al-Akhnas — from Abī Ghaṭafān al-Murrī — from Abī Hurayrah, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Tasbīḥ is for the men"," and taṣfīq is for the women. Whoever makes a gesture during his ṣalāh that is understood from him"," let him repeat it.\"" ʿAlī said: Ibn Abī Dāwūd said to us: \""Abū Ghaṭafān — this is an unknown man.\"" And the last part of the ḥadīth is an addition to the ḥadīth; perhaps it is from the words of Ibn Isḥāq. The authentic narration from the Prophet ﷺ is that he would gesture during the ṣalāh"," as narrated by Anas"," Jābir"," and others from the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAlī said: And Ibn ʿUmar and ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," also narrated it."""
"3421","(3421) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us — from Mālik — from ʿĀmir ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr — from ʿAmr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqī — from Abī Qatādah al-Anṣārī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be performing ṣalāh carrying Umāmah bint Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the daughter of Abū al-ʿĀṣ ibn Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbd Shams. When he performed sujūd, he would set her down, and when he stood up, he would carry her."
"3422","(3422) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and others informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us — from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān and Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, both of whom heard ʿĀmir ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr narrating from ʿAmr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqī — from Abī Qatādah al-Anṣārī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ leading the people in ṣalāh, and Umāmah bint Abī al-ʿĀṣ, the daughter of Zaynab bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was on his shoulder. When he performed rukūʿ, he would set her down, and when he had completed the sujūd, he would return her to his shoulder."
"3423","(3423) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us — Wahb ibn Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Yaʿqūb narrated to us — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād ibn al-Hād — from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us carrying one of his two grandchildren, al-Ḥasan or al-Ḥusayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped forward and placed him near his right foot. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then performed a sujūd and prolonged it. My father said: I raised my head from among the people, and lo, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in sujūd, and the boy was riding on his back. I returned and performed sujūd. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concluded his ṣalāh, the people said: \O Messenger of Allah"," you performed a sujūd in your ṣalāh that you do not usually perform. Was you commanded with something"," or was revelation being sent to you?\"" He said: \""None of that occurred. Rather"," my son mounted upon me"," and I disliked that I should hasten him before he fulfilled his need.\"""""
"3424","(3424) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār in Baghdad informed us — al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Mujashshir narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us — from ʿĀṣim — from Zir ibn Ḥubaysh, who said: One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was performing ṣalāh with the people, when al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, came forward, and they were young boys. They began climbing onto his back when he performed sujūd. The people came forward to remove them from that. He said: \Leave them. May my father and mother be his ransom — whoever loves me"," let him love these two.\"" This mursal narration serves as corroboration for what has preceded. The Shaykh said: And Anas ibn Mālik"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""I have not seen anyone more merciful with children than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"""""
"3425","(3425) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him — Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ṭaʿī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Ismāʿīl narrated to us — from Ayyūb — from ʿAmr ibn Saʿīd — from Anas ibn Mālik. And this is recorded in the book of Muslim along with all that has been authentically established from him ﷺ of his noble character traits and beautiful descriptions, the recognition of which would not make one far from what we have narrated in these two chapters of his compassion and mercy, in conjunction with the statement of Allah, the Most High: {And He is, to the believers, Kind and Merciful} [At-Tawbah: 128]."
"3426","(3426) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl, that is, Ibn Mihrān, narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Salamah al-Murādī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated to us — from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ — Rabīʿah ibn Yazīd narrated to me — from Abī Idrīs al-Khawlānī — from Abī al-Dardāʾ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up to perform ṣalāh, and we heard him saying: \I seek refuge in Allah from you\"" — three times. Then he said: \""I curse you with the curse of Allah\"" — three times. And he extended his hand as though he were reaching for something. When he had completed the ṣalāh"," we said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," we heard you saying something in your ṣalāh that we had never heard you say before"," and we saw you extend your hand.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," the enemy of Allah"," Iblīs — may Allah curse him — came with a firebrand to place it in my face. I said: 'I seek refuge in Allah from you' — three times. Then I said: 'I curse you with the complete curse of Allah.' He did not retreat — three times. Then I intended to seize him. By Allah"," were it not for the supplication of our brother Sulaymān"," he would have been bound"," and the children of the people of Madīnah would have played with him.\"""""
"3427","(3427) Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-Daqqāq in Baghdād — informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Khiraqī — informed us: Abū Qilābah — narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Khalīfah and Saʿīd ibn ʿĀmir — both said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \While I was praying"," a Satan confronted me"," so I seized him and choked him. Were it not for the supplication of my brother Sulaymān"," I would have tied him to one of these pillars so that the people would see him — or so that you would see him.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us in the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding the prayer of the eclipse (al-Kusūf)"," that he said: \""I saw Paradise — or I was shown Paradise — and I reached out to take a cluster of grapes from it.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 449.]"""
"3428","(3428) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah — narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh, i.e. Ibn Maslamah, from Mālik, from Abū al-Naḍr, the mawlā of ʿUbayd Allāh, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), that she said: \I used to sleep in front of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with my legs in his qiblah. When he prodded me"," I would draw in my legs"," and when he stood"," I would extend them. And the houses at that time had no lamps.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah"," and narrated by Muslim from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Its grading has been given previously in ḥadīth 615"," 616.]"""
"3429","(3429) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī — informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-ʿAbdī — narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr — narrated to us: Mālik, from Makhramah ibn Sulaymān, from Kurayb, the mawlā of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who informed him: \He spent a night with Maymūnah"," the Mother of the Believers (may Allah be pleased with her).\""\n\nHe then mentioned the ḥadīh concerning the standing of the Prophet (ﷺ)"," his ablution"," and his prayer. ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās said: \""I stood up and did as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had done"," and I stood at his side. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) placed his right hand upon my head"," then took hold of my right ear and twisted it.\""\n\nBoth al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Mālik.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 181.]"""
"3430","(3430) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān — informed us: Abū Muḥammad Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad — narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī — narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā — informed us: Hushaym — narrated to us: from Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAbd al-Malik, from ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to place the right hand upon the left hand during prayer"," and occasionally he would touch his beard while praying.\""\n\nThus narrated Hushaym ibn Bashīr. And Shuʿbah narrated it similarly.\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā"," 1462.]"""
"3431","(3431) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us: Abū al-Muthannā — narrated to us: my father — narrated to us: Shuʿbah.\n\nHe said: And Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us: ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAbd al-Malik, the brother of ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth, from a man, that the Prophet (ﷺ) was praying and occasionally touched his beard during his prayer.\n\nIt was also narrated from Muʾammal ibn Ismāʿīl from Shuʿbah, and he mentioned the unnamed man, who was ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth.\n\nAnd Sulaymān ibn Kathīr narrated it from Ḥuṣayn, from ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Ḥurayth al-Makhzūmī, the brother of ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥurayth, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ)…\""\n\nIt has also been narrated through another weak chain"," and in one of them it was said: \""without fidgeting (min ghayr ʿabaṯ).\""\n\nIt is mentioned that Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī said: \""It used to be said: touching the beard in prayer is 'once or leave it' (wāḥidah aw daʿ).\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""This is analogous to what is narrated regarding touching pebbles: 'once.'\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf. Preceded in the ḥadīth before it.]"""
"3432","(3432) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith — informed us: Abū al-Shaykh — narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḍabbī — narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Mūsā al-Khaṭmī, who said: I heard al-Walīd ibn Muslim say: I heard ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥakam ibn al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr narrating from Nāfiʿ, though he did not hear it directly from him."
"3433","(3433) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī — informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Shahryār — informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Ḥafṣ al-Aylī — narrated to us: al-Walīd, i.e. Ibn Muslim, from ʿĪsā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥakam ibn al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would occasionally place his hand upon his beard during prayer without fidgeting.\n\nIt has also been narrated through another weak chain, and it is from the ḥadīth of Abū Dharr.\n\nIt is mentioned that Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī said: \It used to be said: touching the beard in prayer is 'once or leave it.'\""\n\nAnd this is analogous to what is narrated regarding touching pebbles: \""once.\""\n\nAbū Aḥmad (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Most of what this ʿĪsā narrates is not corroborated.\""\n\n[Very weak (Ḍaʿīf jiddan). Narrated by Ibn ʿAdī in al-Kāmil"," 5/253.]"""
"3434","(3434) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar al-Muqriʾ in Baghdād — informed us: Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān al-Faqīh — informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad — I read to him: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubārak — narrated to us: Yūnus, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, who said: ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \The sun was eclipsed"," so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood and recited a lengthy sūrah"," then bowed and prolonged the bowing"," then raised his head"," then began another sūrah"," then bowed — when he had completed it — and prostrated. Then he did the same in the second rakʿah"," and then said: 'They are two signs among the signs of Allah. When you see that"," pray until it is dispelled from you. Indeed"," I have seen in this station of mine everything you have been promised"," until I saw myself wanting to take a cluster from Paradise when you saw me moving forward. And I saw Hellfire"," some parts of it consuming others"," when you saw me drawing back. And I saw therein ʿAmr ibn Luḥayy"," and he is the one who set free the sāʾibah camels.'\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil from ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak"," and narrated by Muslim from the ḥadīth of Ibn Wahb from Yūnus.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Its grading has been given previously in the book of Ṣalāt al-Kusūf.]"""
"3435","(3435) Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir — informed us: my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī — narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār al-ʿAbdī — narrated to us: Yaḥyā — narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī Sulaymān — narrated to us: ʿAṭāʾ, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" He then mentioned the ḥadīth concerning the prayer of the eclipse (al-Khusūf)"," and said therein: \""Then he moved back in his prayer"," and the rows moved back with him. Then he moved forward"," and the rows moved forward with him.\""\n\nThe complete ḥadīth is recorded in the book of Ṣalāt al-Khusūf. And with Allah lies all success.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded in the ḥadīth before it.]"""
"3436","(3436) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān — informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Miṣrī — narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Nāṣiḥ — narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim, from Burd ibn Sinān.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr — narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal — narrated to us: Burd, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \I came while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was praying in the house"," and the door was closed upon him. He walked until he opened it for me"," then returned to his place.\"" She said: \""And the door was in the qiblah.\""\n\nThis is the wording of the ḥadīth of Bishr. And in the ḥadīth of ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim"," she said: \""The door was in the qiblah of our mosque. I knocked upon the door"," and the Prophet (ﷺ)"," while praying"," walked until he opened the door"," then returned to his place.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Tirmidhī"," 60.]"""
"3437","(3437) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi in Hamadan narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us — Adam narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated to us — al-Azraq ibn Qays said: We were in al-Ahwaz fighting the Haruriyyah, when, as we were upon the bank of a river, a man was praying while holding the bridle of his mount in his hand. The mount began pulling against him, and he began following it. Shu'bah said: He was Abu Barzah al-Aslami. A man among the Kharijites began saying, \O Allah"," do something to this old man!\"" When the old man completed his prayer"," he said"," \""I heard your words. I have participated in military campaigns alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — six"," seven"," or eight campaigns — and I witnessed the leniency of the Prophet ﷺ. I would rather return with my mount than leave it to go to its familiar place and then have it become a burden upon me.\"""""
"3438","(3438) 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — 'Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us — Shu'bah informed us — from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: We were fighting the Azariqah in al-Ahwaz alongside al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufrah. Abu Barzah came and took hold of the leading rein of his she-camel — or his mount. While he was praying, it escaped from his hand, and the mount went off in the direction of the qiblah. Abu Barzah went after it until he caught it, then he turned back. A man who held the doctrine of the Kharijites said, \Look at this old man — he has abandoned his prayer and gone after his mount.\"" When Abu Barzah completed his prayer"," he came forward and said"," \""I have fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seven campaigns\"" — or he said \""several\"" — \""and I am an advanced old man. Were my mount to go off to its familiar place"," that would be a hardship upon me"," so I did what you saw.\"" We then said to the man"," \""I think Allah will requite you — you have insulted a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ.\"""""
"3439","(3439) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir. And 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Bishran informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us — 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us — Ma'mar narrated from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir — from Damdam — from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to kill two black creatures during the prayer: the snake and the scorpion."
"3440","(3440) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Susi both said — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid ibn Mazayid narrated to us — my father narrated to me — al-Awza'i narrated from Umm Kulthum bint Asma' bint Abi Bakr al-Siddiq — from 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying in the house when 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah the Most High ennoble his face, entered. When he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying, he stood beside him and prayed. Then a scorpion came until it reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then left him and went toward 'Ali. When 'Ali saw that, he struck it with his sandal. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not disapprove of his killing it."
"3441","(3441) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman al-Muradi narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Maslamah ibn Qa'nab narrated to us — Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated from Muhammad ibn 'Amr — from Abu Salamah — from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \It suffices you to strike a snake with a single lash of the whip"," whether you hit it or miss it.\"" This"," if authentic"," indicates — and Allah knows best — that the intended meaning is the fulfillment of sufficiency in performing what has been commanded"," for he ﷺ commanded its killing. And Allah knows best"," when it resists by itself upon a single strike"," the intention is not to prohibit additional strikes beyond one."""
"3442","(3442) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed us — Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us — Yahya ibn Yahya informed us — Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Suhayl. And Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Sabah narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated from Suhayl — from his father — from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \Whoever kills a gecko with the first strike shall have such and such hasanat"," and whoever kills it with the second strike shall have such and such hasanat"," fewer than the first"," and whoever kills it with the third strike shall have such and such hasanat"," fewer than the second.\"" In the hadith of Khalid"," the phrase \""fewer than the first\"" is omitted"," and it says \""fewer than the second\"" — the rest being the same."""
"3443","(3443) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us — Abu Bakr narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Muhammad ibn al-Sabah narrated to us — Isma'il ibn Zakariyya narrated from Suhayl, who said — my brother or my sister narrated to me — from Abu Hurayrah — from the Prophet ﷺ that he said, \With the first strike"," seventy hasanat.\"""""
"3444","(3444) Abu Sa'id Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Khatib al-Isfaranin informed us — Abu Bahr al-Barbahari narrated to us — Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us — al-Humaydi narrated to us — Sufyan narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar said: I saw 'Abd Allah ibn 'Umar see a feather during his prayer and strike it with his foot, saying, \I thought it was a scorpion.\"""""
